(117, 'Biggest Technology Trends in 2025', 'biggest-technology-trends', 'Project Service Automation', 'project-service-automation', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768049933757524.png', 'In today’s dynamically changing world, technology can only bring a revolutionary change and can even support the inevitable situation, for instance, looking forward to a post-pandemic situation.', '<p>In today’s dynamically changing world, technology can only bring a revolutionary change and can even support the inevitable situation, for instance, looking forward to a post-pandemic situation. Through this blog, we are going to reveal the 10 biggest technology trends to reinvent your business capabilities, support your growing processes, and uplift your business model with improved revenue outcomes and reduced operational costs.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>If we consider the recent 2-years of the market situation due to covid-19, the market scenario has changed. Let’s understand how these emerging yet strategic technology trends can help businesses to find their path, support their growing business model, and enlarge their global capabilities with high-end data security and potential reliability.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Now, it’s time to unwrap the top Tech Trends 2025 while covering all the potential aspects and opportunities for modern businesses.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h2>Top Tech Trends 2025 and Beyond&nbsp;\r\n</h2><h3>1. Business Intelligence\r\n</h3><p>Business Intelligence is one of the topmost technology trends that is being leveraged by most enterprises these days. To drive advanced business intelligence, several tools are available in the market to drive business intelligence practices including advanced reporting, data mining, predictive analysis, ensuring secured transactions, and even gaining device performance notifications in real-time when integrated with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/azure-iot-internet-of-things/\">IoT solutions</a>.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Leveraging business intelligence has become a necessity for modern enterprises today to analyze data, predict process results, forecast operations, identify specific customer needs, and make informed decisions.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>2. AI (Artificial Intelligence)&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>In the past few years, AI-based business intelligence has emerged as an essential need for every scale of businesses to discover hidden insights leveraging past data to ensure productive analysis, gain real-time reports, and make informed decisions in real-time when combined with cloud solutions.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Initially, AI is used to consider speech recognition, virtual or Chatbot assistance, or to ensure improved navigational experience. With time, AI emerged to gain in-depth business insights, data gathering, and more. According to the research report of Marketsandmarkets, the AI market share is anticipated to match $190 billion by the end of 2025.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>3. Edge Computing&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768049609710298.Edge-Computing.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">Edge Computing is referred to as distributed computing that helps to improve data-driven efficiency by bringing computation data and data storage closure to the involved source data. Edge computing can help you to improve your speed while reducing latency.&nbsp;<br></p><p>When it comes to user adaption, Edge Computing is ensuring its gradual contribution. Global market leaders like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-azure/\">Microsoft Azure</a>, Amazon Web Services, and Google Cloud are taking advantage while serving one step ahead solution i.e., Edge Computing.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Enterprises are leveraging Edge computing to ensure seamless data processing even in case of low connectivity. Making effective use of this one of the emerging technology trends, you securely process time-dominating data even from the distance. Further, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/azure-iot-edge/\">Edge computing</a> is also reserving market opportunities for IoT (Internet of Things).&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>4. Industrial Clouds&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Another suitable name that reserves its place on the list of strategic technology trends is Industrial Cloud, which is used to streamline data, operational efficiency, faster the production line, and more in real-time. Nowadays, medium to large scale organizations are leveraging Industrial cloud rather than just a SaaS-based solution as Industrial cloud can be customized and configured according to your specific industrial needs.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Businesses are availing of industry-specific cloud environments to ensure real-time process optimization as well as to control, manage, and drive their operational effectiveness. Cloud industry solution helps businesses to drive agile practices while reducing IT costs, system downtime, and other IT environment costs.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>When it comes to rolling your eyes on leading global cloud vendors, few names come ahead such as Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud Platform, and Amazon Web Services. Enterprises seeking to drive secured data-driven practices can ensure seamless integration with their existing ERP, CRM, or business solution.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>5. Internet of Things&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768049619968340.Internet-of-Things-.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\"><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/azure-iot-internet-of-things/\" style=\"background-color: white; font-family: sans-serif; font-weight: 400;\">Internet of Things</a> is the next one of the booming technology trends designed to connect devices, exchange data, and optimize devices performance to prevent system downtime, save maintenance costs, and secure your data-driven strategies. With the help of IoT, you can ensure highly secure and protected data distribution across the global market space.&nbsp;<br></p><p>By the end of 2022, the global market investment in IoT is expected to reach $1.1 trillion as per <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.statista.com/statistics/668996/worldwide-expenditures-for-the-internet-of-things/\" target=\"_blank\">Statista</a>.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>For businesses, there could be several compelling reasons to integrate IoT, for instance, gaining data analytics, driving process automation, ensuring predictive maintenance, and preventing last-moment system downtime. IoT can help businesses to monitor their device performance, send &amp; retrieve data, and ensure secure connectivity between devices and valuable data to drive productive and profitable results.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>6. Virtual Reality and Augmented Reality&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Virtual Reality and Augmented Reality are the next-generation technology solutions that are emerging in almost all industries to serve improved, engaging, and intuitive user experience. These technologies can be leveraged either independently or can be combined to serve integrated experience which is technically known as <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/mixed-reality/\">Mixed Reality</a>.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Virtual Reality is used to provide and ensure real-world user experience which is created and exhibited as a computer-generated environment. When it comes to Augmented Reality, enterprises can make effective use of AR to demonstrate real-world objects using digital visual experience to ensure serving improved customer experience even from remote locations.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>As per one of the market researchers, AR and VR market may reach $209.2 billion by the end of 2022.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>7. Metaverse&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768049628592414.Metaverse-.jpg\" style=\"width: 100%;\">Metaverse is another trending name ensuring its contribution to the list of tech trends 2022. Metaverse is used to ensure a user-engaging, intuitive, and interactive experience. It can be leveraged to enable your users for 3D virtual world experience focusing social connections as digital avatars which are facilitated by Mixed reality.&nbsp;<br></p><p>Industries involved in entertaining services or serving B2C are taking recourse of Metaverse to deliver an optimum level of user experience. Metaverse is becoming popular among the gaming industry as well to serve Metaverse gaming experience comprising including MSFT HoloLens, Epic Games, Play station\'s VR helmets, and more.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>8. Robotic Process Automation&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768049636886705.Robotic-Process-Automation.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">When enterprises anticipate more than <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-ai/\" style=\"background-color: white; font-family: sans-serif; font-weight: 400;\">AI</a> and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/azure-machine-learning/\" style=\"background-color: white; font-family: sans-serif; font-weight: 400;\">Machine Learning</a>, Robotic Process Automation (RPA) is the term that reserves its extensive contribution to the automation industry. RPA is leveraged by modern enterprises to automate the business processes, automatically manage assigned repetitive tasks, and interpret the business applications.&nbsp;<br></p><p>RPA can be implemented and configured to automatically receive invoices, extract the data, and ensure backend tasks are being performed successfully all through automation. RPA empowers enterprises to increase their speed, ensure quality practices, and drive a highly consistent approach while minimizing investment costs and improving the production line.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>RPA also serves improved data security and prevents your sensitive data from unauthorized access. For instance, financial services providers can gain and drive highly secured data models with the help of Robotic Process Automation.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>9. Quantum Computing&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Quantum Computing is the next breakthrough trending technology spreading its legs in the global market to leverage quantum phenomena such as superposition and quantum entanglement. This technology trend is emerging globally with its highly integrated capability of monitoring, analyzing, and applying the query to retrieve required results.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>It simplifies the way of predicting, monitoring, and controlling the data comprising privacy or sensitive values. Enterprises can seamlessly forecast circumstances and can even detect fraud. It can also be leveraged by the stock and trading industry to securely manage and control the high frequency of data transition. As per the market report shared by Statista, the global quantum computing market is expected to cover $2.5 billion by 2029.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>10. Next Generation End-Point Detection and Response (EDR)&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>One of the next technology trends that proudly takes part in this list is Next-Generation EDR (End-Point Detection and Response). EDR provides primary cyber security solutions to enterprises that deal in sensitive data or are concerned about their data security. With the help of EDR when integrated with AI and ML, businesses can ensure high-end data security and maximize their visibility into threat detection while ensuring faster response time.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>By comprising emerging technologies such as AI, ML, and behavioral monitoring, this Next-Generation EDR solution enables spot threat detection as well as ensures prompt response to unauthorized attacks. It also serves improved visibility into various types of Cyber-attacks.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h2>Summing Up!</h2><p>Since growing businesses cannot deny the rising adoption of trending technologies to survive, sustain, and gain competitive advantage. These technology trends in 2022 can truly help to support and uplift modern enterprises to enlarge high with global scalability.</p><p>To take your business operations to the next level, you should also familiarize yourself with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a>, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics ERP</a>, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a>, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance-operations/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations</a>, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Finance</a>, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</a>, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-sales/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Sales</a>, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-nav-to-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\">NAV Upgrade</a> and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\">Business Central Partner</a>.</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', '10 Biggest Technology Trends in 2025', 'Technology trends', 'We are going to reveal the 10 biggest technology trends to reinvent your business capabilities, support your growing processes, and uplift your business model with improved revenue outcomes and reduced operational costs.', 'IoT Solutions,Microsoft Azure,Mixed Reality,ERP', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768049933759061.png', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '07:07:54pm', '2023-06-07', '9 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-12-18 19:07:54'),
(119, 'Why do SMBs need CRM Software Solutions?', 'why-do-smbs-need-crm-software-solutions', 'CRM', 'crm', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768050927601282.jpg', 'CRM or Customer Relationship Management Software is an essential tool for SMBs. It empowers customer experiences & gives companies a competitive edge. CRM Software for SMBs is designed to collect details of your customers and store them in one place.', '<p>CRM or Customer Relationship Management Software is an essential tool for SMBs. It empowers customer experiences and gives companies a competitive edge. CRM Software for SMBs is designed to collect details of your customers and store them in one place. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Microsoft\'s leading CRM software, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-sales/\">Dynamics 365 for Sales</a>, helps small to medium firms build strong relationships with their clients and improve their interactions based on collected data. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>CRM system centralizes all data concerning the future, past, and present customers. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>According to stats, the global CRM market could reach $129 billion by 2028 (Fortune Business Insights, 2021). It shows that some businesses have already understood the importance of Customer Relationship Management. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>However, many SMBs are still confused about whether they need CRM software or not. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>We have compiled the top 5 reasons SMBs need CRM software solutions to grow to make things easier. &nbsp;</p><p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" src=\"//www.youtube.com/embed/4_mQBvLTGp8\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" class=\"note-video-clip\"></iframe><br></p><p>\r\n</p><h2>Top 5 Reasons SMBs need CRM Software Solutions\r\n</h2><h3>1. Streamline The Sales Process&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>The main reason to use Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales software is it streamlines your sales process. You can explore all opportunities from acquiring a lead, transforming it into a customer, and providing the necessary options. You can understand that the tool will help build and manage customer relationships right from the name. After obtaining this system, sales teams who handle many different things can be stress-free. &nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>2. Improving Sales At Least By 30% &nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Which business does not want to increase its sales? Every company\'s main criterion is to increase sales as much as possible. A CRM system will help create new opportunities and target the right audiences. Also, as per the wide range of factors, like market sector, spending, activities, etc., a marketing team can create opportunities that will help to increase sales. But without technology like Customer Relationship Management, it won\'t be possible. &nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>3. Increases Productivity By 50%&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a> can perform several activities, and the most important is automation. Automated actions created using the tool will increase productivity by 50%. It eliminates confusion and unnecessary manual tasks and reduces stress. CRM system introduces efficient business processes, and the sales department does not have to wait for a long time to collect updated details. &nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>4. Saves Company\'s Resources&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>CRM technology can save a company\'s resources like time and money. It can streamline several steps through automation and avoid manual tasks. As a result, professionals can invest their time in nurturing new leads. CRM is a one-stop solution for businesses operating within a specified marketing budget. This solution will help maximize the return on investments, and you can navigate a considerable profit margin. &nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>5. Handling Sales to Data Analytics Processes &nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Many companies still use excel sheets, which puts limitations on the company\'s insights, data, and even exposes them to potential security risks. Learning <a href=\"https://surfshark.com/blog/how-to-prevent-data-breaches\" target=\"_blank\">how to prevent data breaches</a> is essential in today\'s digital landscape. By switching to one of the efficient CRM Systems, companies can not only gain in-depth analytics, and details on sales but also ensure robust data security. As a result, there is a higher chance to generate maximum revenue and make critical decisions in favor of the business.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><h3>6. Centralized information database&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Furthermore, CRM software lets you create a centralized database with all your customer information so that it can be accessed by anyone in your company who needs it. For example, a sales representative can easily find out what products a specific customer is interested in. The CRM will include records of previous interactions with the customer, helpful in future marketing and sales efforts. It saves your employees time by eliminating the need to dig through old files and records and making for a better customer experience.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>7. Effective Communication with potential leads&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Lead nurturing can be a complex and arduous process, involving many steps and opportunities for communication. Your CRM manages the process automatically, notifying your employees when to reach out to the prospect and tracking the interaction from email to phone calls.&nbsp;</p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 57, 63); font-size: 2rem;\">Summing Up &nbsp;</span></h2><p>Customer Relationship Management is a go-to tool that every business needs to have. After getting CRM system, SMBs can avoid recruiting extra staff and win more deals by approaching the right customers. As one of the fastest-growing industries, the CRM software market is forecast to grow at a rate of 14.27% from 2020 to 2027, thanks to consumer demand for better customer service, automating engagement, and creating a more refined customer experience. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Therefore, many small to medium businesses are looking forward to availing Microsoft dynamics 365 sales to get the system deployed. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>If you\'re looking for a dedicated Microsoft Partner to <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">implement Dynamics 365</a> Sales CRM, consider Dynamics Square, your trusted <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a>. Our Microsoft consultants will assist you in the overall implementation process.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>See Also -\r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-vs-salesforce/\">Dynamics 365 vs Salesforce</a>\r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-scm-cloud-vs-on-premise/\">Dynamics 365 SCM – Cloud vs On-premise</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/crm-implementation-services/\" target=\"_blank\">CRM Implementation Services</a></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'CRM Software for SMBs - All you need to know!', 'CRM Software', 'CRM or Customer Relationship Management Software is an essential tool for SMBs. It empowers customer experiences and gives companies a competitive edge.', 'dynamics crm,microsoft dynamics crm,dynamics 365 crm,microsoft dynamics 365 crm,crm software', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768050927601861.jpg', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '01:51:36pm', '2023-06-07', '5 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-04-18 13:51:36'),
(123, 'Migrate Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365', 'migrate-dynamics-ax-to-dynamics-365', 'Comparison', 'comparison', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768052005645237.jpg', 'If you are still using Dynamics AX, it’s the time when you are required to Migrate Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365. Since users with Dynamics AX 2012 and Dynamics AX R2 will not be able anymore to avail of any sort of support services from Microsoft soon', '<p>If you are still using Dynamics AX, it’s the time when you are required to Migrate Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365. Since users with Dynamics AX 2012 and Dynamics AX R2 will not be able anymore to avail of any sort of support services from Microsoft soon.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>As we know Microsoft regularly comes up with product and feature updates to ensure market relevancy and empower businesses to leverage the technology up to maximum potential. When it comes to <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-nav/\">Dynamics NAV</a>, it has been already announced that Microsoft will not continue providing support to Dynamics NAV users which is effective from October 2021. Later to give comfort to existing NAV users, it has been extended till 12th April 2022.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>AX was designed as a business transforming ERP to manage finance and operations wrapped with embedded intelligence to be optimized whether for on-premises systems, on-cloud, or even Hybrid. Considering the recent announcement of Microsoft, it becomes obligatory to ensure upgrading from <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-ax/\">Microsoft Dynamics AX</a> to <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Dynamics 365</a>&nbsp;to stay current with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics ERP</a> advancements.</p><p>Upgrading your system with the new version will help enterprises to leverage modern features, advanced functional navigation, and expansion capabilities. Using upgraded capabilities, businesses can start optimizing their processes more efficiently, improve their production line, plan capacity, and uplift their business outcomes.</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768051043239753.dynamics-ax-dashboard.jpg\" style=\"width: 100%;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 57, 63); font-size: 2rem;\">Moving from Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365 in the Cloud&nbsp;</span><br></p><p>So, if you are planning to Migrate from Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365, you need to consider a few factors to ensure a seamless and successful upgrade. In this blog, we are going to unfold essential factors being considered impacting your growth potential from the very initial days.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Before we migrate from Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365, let’s understand how upgrading from Microsoft Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365 could be a high-end fruitful deal for your business.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>When you are ready to upgrade your NAV system, a logical call goes to <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance</a> and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain</a>. These advanced solutions are designed for modern enterprises with continuously growing operational flow to seamlessly manage and drive advanced finance processes, improved operational flow, and transparent supply chain practices.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Before you make a final call to your decision, let’s perceive the capabilities of these two:&nbsp;\r\n</p><h2>Capabilities of Dynamics 365 Finance&nbsp;\r\n</h2><h3>1. Improved Financial Visibility&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Improve your real-time visibility with accuracy across your financial practices, monitor your finance operations, control your finance flow, and drive an agile approach while enlarging your growth rate. With the help of key visuals, reporting analytics, and built-in business intelligence, empower your organization to make real-time decisions.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>2. Data and Process Automation&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Dynamics 365 Finance enables you to integrate your processes, centralize your data, bring process automation, and drive operational continuity. Automation in your processes and data helps to access and process the data seamlessly and efficiently.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>3. Improved Planning &amp; Analysis&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>With the help of the upgraded system, you can start optimizing your costs across your global space. Features like automation, budget &amp; control, financial planning, and analytics can help to ensure so.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>4. Global Risk &amp; Compliance Management&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Upgrade to Microsoft Dynamics 365 can help to ease and support your global expansion in terms of regulatory reporting and global compliances. You can monitor and take control of your electronic processing, automated invoicing, and global payments.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h2>Capabilities of Dynamics 365 Supply Chain&nbsp;\r\n</h2><h3>1. Faster Time to Market&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Upgrading from Microsoft Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365 Supply Chain can help to upgrade your supply chain flow in terms of monitoring the production line, responding to quality issues in real-time, bringing agility in distribution, and mitigating delays.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>2. Bring Agility &amp; Ensure Customer Fulfilment&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>When you upgrade from Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365 for the Supply chain module, you can achieve real-time monitoring, drive agility, and ensure customer fulfillment. Enterprises can improve their end-to-end production flow by preventing stockout and overstocking conditions.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>3. Optimize Inventory, Resources, and Logistics&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Businesses can optimize their inventories, increase their resource utilization, and improve their logistics flow all through leveraging built-in business intelligence that helps to keep your real-time eyes on your warehousing, distribution &amp; logistics, material sourcing, and more.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>4. Intelligent Manufacturing Operations&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Boost your operational efficiency and improve your manufacturing capability combined with agility across your practices at the edge with AI, IoT, and AR/VR. Support not merely your current manufacturing flow even your planned or futuristic manufacturing flow.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>5. Improve Your Asset Uptime&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Monitor and control your processes, improve your device performance, reduce your equipment downtime, and maximize longevity by leveraging the proactive approach to your maintenance part. Moving from Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365 in the cloud can help modern firms to improve their overall process flow and impact operational effectiveness.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>After gaining such sort of feature overview, you can have a clear understanding of your current system limitations and how such limitations can be fulfilled once you migrate from Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h2>How are your customizations and reports are migrated during the upgrade process?&nbsp;\r\n</h2><p>Customizations are managed differently in both systems. When it comes to Dynamics AX, you will be required to perform coding on the top of the base to ensure app customization whereas, in Dynamics 365, you can code customizations by simply extending the base code leveraging LCS.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>When you migrate from Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365, you may also require doing manual coding so that your customizations can demonstrate compatibility with your new system.&nbsp;</p><p>Similarly, migrating your AX reports to the newly configured system may not show compatibility. However, newer versions of AX may allow you to migrate some of your vital reports using the code upgrade tool.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>We understand how it feels to lose your customized reports. Leveraging the newly configured system, you can quickly create high-end customized reports. If you want, we can create highly customized and powerful reports for your business.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>How much does it cost to upgrade to Dynamics 365?&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>So, if you are decided to move from Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365 in the cloud, you will cost in both terms – migration cost and licensing cost. Apart from this, the complexity level of your project always matters. Usually, system upgrade cost varies from project to project. Connect with us, by reviewing your system upgrading needs, we can share your exact cost.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Now, when it comes to licensing cost, it starts with $180 per user/per month whether for Dynamics 365 Finance upgrade or Dynamics 365 Supply Chain upgrade per user/per month. If you are planning to avail a migration solution combining both the finance and supply chain capabilities, your pricing may go differently. Further, your actual licensing cost can be calculated depending on your user requirement as well.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h2>Summing Up!&nbsp;\r\n</h2><p>To support your growing and scaling business needs, businesses are required to upgrade their system with new system capabilities. For enterprises driving their process flow using Dynamics AX are required to support their continuity and this can be made possible by upgrading from Microsoft Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365. This upgrade can bring a proven transformation in your business and ensure a smoother operational flow wrapped with maximized outcomes. For expert advice and support, reach out to Dynamics Square, your trusted <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics partner</a>.</p><p>So, Contact for migrating - &gt;\r\n</p><p>Call - <a href=\"tel:+1 213 784 0845\">+1 213 784 0845</a>\r\n</p><p>Email - <a href=\"mailto:info@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">info@dynamicssquare.com</a></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Why to Migrate Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365?', 'Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365', 'If you are still using Dynamics AX (Axapta), it’s the time when you are required to Migrate Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365. You need to consider a few factors to ensure a seamless and successful upgrade.', 'dynamics ax,microsoft dynamics ax,dynamics 365,Dynamics AX to Dynamics 365', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768052005645858.jpg', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '03:54:43pm', '2023-06-07', '7 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-08-22 15:54:43'),
(127, 'Business Central Vs Dynamics 365 CRM', 'business-central-vs-dynamics-365-crm', 'Comparison', 'comparison', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768053663064358.jpg', 'Sooner or later, every business is to adopt a business solution upgrading their system capabilities and improving their operational flow to grow at scale.', '<p>Sooner or later, every business is to adopt a business solution upgrading their system capabilities and improving their operational flow to grow at scale. Often deciding the right technology becomes difficult especially when it comes to Dynamics 365 Business Central Vs Dynamics 365 CRM.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Since every business could have different business practices and require different business solutions demonstrating the specific needs. So, this blog is curated for enterprises seeking to upgrade their system capabilities with the right solution to impact their overall business flow and production line.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>We can’t deny the specific features and functional navigation offered by Dynamics 365 Business Central and Dynamics 365 CRM. However, there are some overlapping features that often create hassles for businesses seeking a business solution out of these two.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Now, let’s make things easy for the enterprises to ensure a smarter decision by deriving Dynamics 365 Business Central Vs Dynamics 365 CRM. Initially understand their core concepts and then, let\'s navigate through the difference.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h2>Dynamics 365 Business Central Vs Dynamics 365 CRM&nbsp;\r\n</h2><h3>1. Dynamics 365 Business Central\r\n</h3><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> can be defined as a complete business solution package to control, manage, and drive overall business processes in SMBs. Leveraging Business Central, enterprises can automate their data, streamline their practices, and can acquire operational efficiency.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>It allows enterprises to manage end-to-end business capabilities such as finance management, customer relationship, supply chain, inventory &amp; warehousing, project automation, sales, customer service, and more to join this list. Leveraging all such capabilities, businesses can support their ongoing practices, optimize their resource utilization, and enlarge productivity levels while ensuring seamless global regulation and compliance.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>2. Dynamics 365 CRM&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\">Dynamics 365 CRM</a> is a full-fledged customer relationship management solution designed for small to mid-scale enterprises seeking to manage their day-to-day operational flow from customer engagement to service part, sales &amp; marketing to field service, and project automation.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Curated for businesses that are more focused on managing customers, sales, services, and project operations, Dynamics 365 CRM acts as a bundle of applications that comprises Dynamics 365 modules such as <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-sales/\">Dynamics 365 Sales</a>, Marketing, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-customer-service/\">Customer Service</a>, Project Operations, and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-field-service/\">Field Services</a>. It helps business to effectively engage their customers, support them in timely accordance, and efficiently drive sales to impact revenue.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>After getting familiar with both these solutions, it can be easily seen that both the D365 Business Central and D365 CRM come with similarity in features, and this often brings decision-makers in dilemma. Now, let’s understand what those common features are and based on how distinctively, users can make a smarter choice out of Dynamics 365 Business Central and Dynamics 365 CRM.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Common Functional Navigation Between These Two&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Considering the above-mentioned, it’s clear that Business Central and Dynamic 365 CRM come with a few similar capabilities. Here it is essential to perceive which solution would be a specific solution for your business.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Business Central serves application modules such as sales, customer service, and project operations which are quite similar to Dynamics 365 CRM. However, Dynamics 365 CRM comprises all these modules with in-depth functionality along with a field service module that helps customers proactively serve customers in their preferred locations.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Let’s explore more facts about what should be chosen whether Dynamics 365 Business Central or Dynamics 365 CRM.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h2>Does Business Central Offers Scope for CRM Practices?&nbsp;\r\n</h2><p>Business Central comes with its set of modules to drive your overall business practices. However, due to a few modules’ similarities with Dynamics CRM, it can help to drive basic customer relationship management practices such as contact management, customer engagement &amp; interaction, sales &amp; services, and marketing.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Furthermore, Business Central can be leveraged to turn your potential prospects into customers, entering quotes and converting them into order completion. It also serves supply chain capabilities to manage and drive your supply chain pipeline but again with limited functionality. You cannot drive advanced functionalities using Business Central.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>If your requirement goes driving customer relationships and sales practices with high-end capability, Business Central will not be able to serve so. Again, Business Central will not help you to drive a major level of sales and marketing practices. To ensure the fulfilment of these practices, Dynamics CRM could be a quite suitable deal for your business.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Still, things are messing up. Let’s understand how Dynamics 365 Business Central and Dynamics 365 CRM are isolated from each other by clearly knowing when to implement Business Central and when Dynamics 365 CRM.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h2>When to Choose Dynamics 365 CRM?&nbsp;\r\n</h2><p>When your customer relationship management imbibes complex processes that are not served by Business Central, for instance, lead distribution, field service management, and more.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>If your business domain needs to carry out advanced terms such as marketing automation, customer service, field service, and project operation management services.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>When there is a need to empower your team with seamless access yet an advanced set of CRM features to be leveraged via mobile devices.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>If your need arises to connect your field service technicians with in-house employees to access and gain the required information in real-time.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>When you need to strengthen your field service executives’ capability with advanced tools and application solutions to proactively serve customers in their preferred locations.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>When all the above-mentioned terms are favorable situations for you, going with Dynamics 365 CRM could be a quite suitable solution for your business.&nbsp;</p><p>Explore <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/crm-implementation-services/\" target=\"_blank\">CRM implementation services</a> designed to scale and grow businesses</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 57, 63); font-size: 2rem;\">When to Choose Dynamics 365 Business Central?&nbsp;</span><br></p><p>When your requirement is just not fulfilling customer relationship management part even it incorporates practices such as finance, logistics &amp; warehousing, supply chain, manufacturing, etc.,&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>When your business demands to scale on a global level, and you need regulatory, global compliance management requirements.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>If your business requirement is to improve your financial visibility, financial reporting, and closing.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>When there is a need to leverage business insights and analytics but not limited to customer management, sales, marketing, etc., to gain visibility into project status, finance &amp; operations, and resources.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>When you need to optimize, control, and manage resource utilization, ensure capacity planning, track invoicing against planned or actual costs.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>When you need to control and manage advanced supply chain capability. Moreover, accessing inventory status and predictive inventory replenishment is your primary requirement.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Do you think that you need to create bills of materials, require registering consumption, and output for all your bills of material?&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Thus, if your requirement addresses the above-given requirement facts, you certainly need <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-business-central-implementation/\" target=\"_blank\">Business Central implementation</a> to simplify, manage, and drive your business processes while ensuring profitability and scalability.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h2>Summing Up!&nbsp;\r\n</h2><p>Every business domain comprises distinct business practices and requires different business solutions depending on current business practices and desired scalable objectives, thereby, it becomes essential to make the right decision while choosing a business solution for your enterprise.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>We hope, this blog – Dynamics 365 Business Central Vs Dynamics 365 CRM is involving all the information that can help you to make a strategic yet productive decision for your business. If you have queries or need expert consultation, contact Dynamics Square, your trusted <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics partner</a>. We can reveal the best solutions for you.</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Dynamics 365 Business Central Vs Dynamics 365 CRM', 'Business Central Vs Dynamics 365 CRM', 'Dynamics 365 Business Central Vs Dynamics 365 CRM : Initially understand their core concepts and then, let\'s navigate through the difference.', 'business central,dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics business central,dynamics 365 crm,microsoft dynamics 365 crm,d365 crm,dynamics crm,microsoft dynamics crm', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768053663065336.jpg', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '01:50:59pm', '2023-06-07', '7 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-04-18 13:50:59');
