(138, 'Which Is The Best CRM Platform For Businesses?', 'best-crm-platform-for-businesses', 'CRM', 'crm', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768129699904270.jpg', 'Find the perfect CRM platform for your businesses! Compare features, benefits, and make an informed decision to enhance productivity and drive sales.', '<p>“Searching for a cloud CRM solution that can give you the most comprehensive and a unified view of your business? Read this blog and discover which CRM software can be the best fit for your business.”</p><p>To derive business growth, companies look for easy ways to provide exceptional customer experiences.\r\n</p><p>For businesses exploring CRM solutions, platforms like Freshdesk or a <a href=\"https://crisp.chat/en/alternatives/freshdesk/\" target=\"_blank\">Freshdesk Alternative</a> such as Crisp, offer robust features tailored to enhance communication and customer engagement. Crisp, in particular, stands out for its specialized focus on improving customer interactions and support.</p><p>Let’s dig deep and figure out:</p><ul><li>What CRM is\r\n</li><li>Which is the best CRM software in today’s digital space\r\n</li><li>How can a CRM application help a business stay connected to customers\r\n</li><li>How can a CRM platform unify sales processes and improve profitability, and more</li></ul><h2>What is CRM (Software or System)?</h2><p>CRM refers to ways (using a tool like a CRM system) of managing a company’s relations and interactions with current and prospective customers.\r\n</p><p>The goal of CRM technology is simple: “improve business relations to advance the growth of an organization“.\r\n</p><p>CRM software usually consists of contact management and sales management and helps with marketing, service (or customer service), lead ranking, and customer case management.\r\n</p><p>For example, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-sales/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 for Sales</a> is an amazing CRM platform for big-size companies and includes functionalities to foster teamwork, accelerate revenue growth, predict and manage pipelines, sales tracking, improve customer experience (CX), and more.</p><h2>Why do Small Businesses need CRM Software?</h2><p>Small businesses often struggle to find a “low-cost, high productivity” CRM solution to drive desired sales.\r\n</p><p>Here are some ways in which a company can use CRM software to:\r\n</p><ul><li>Monitor sales funnel to drive more sales\r\n</li><li>Monitor real-time sales data\r\n</li><li>Gain insights for planning the next steps\r\n</li><li>Enable automation for workflow optimization\r\n</li><li>Learn about customer journeys to make an impact\r\n</li><li>Unify multiple platforms for strong customer engagement</li><li>Use modern networking tools like <a href=\"https://www.uniqode.com/digital-business-card\" target=\"_blank\">Uniqode’s business card</a>, Calendly links, or embedded lead forms to seamlessly connect with prospects and store interactions directly in the CRM</li><li>Gain a competitive edge and agility to grow</li></ul><h2>The List of Best CRM Software for Businesses In 2023</h2><p>Here are the top CRM solutions for your businesses:&nbsp;</p><p><b>Dynamics 365 Sales:</b> It is a cloud-based, highly secure CRM platform. This CRM solution is the best for large enterprises that operate their operations in multiple locations (since it’s available in more than 130 countries and regions)\r\n</p><p><b>Salesforce:</b> Comprehensive CRM solution for small and medium size businesses (SMBs)\r\n</p><p><b>Zoho CRM:</b> Best for Startups and companies that are starting out\r\n</p><p><b>Monday:</b> Best suited for small and creative teams\r\n</p><p><b>Zendesk Sell:</b> Best for small organizations that strive to provide better CX</p><h2>Which is the best CRM Software for Businesses?</h2><p>Anything becomes best for you or your businesses if it can solve your most critical issues.\r\n</p><p>The same is with choosing a CRM platform that can show you the ways of doing business in smarter ways such as helping sales teams accelerate revenue using data-driven insights in a collaborative sales workspace.\r\n</p><p>Plus, you also need to keep your business size in mind since it matters a lot when there’s a ton of money at stake.\r\n</p><p>For instance, if your business is into automobile manufacturing and operates in multiple locations with different breeds (supply chain, distribution, finance, and more), investing in Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales can be the best choice.\r\n</p><p>If your businesses is of small and medium size but deals with complex sales processes, Salesforce might be the best fit. And for startups and other small teams, there are several options like Zoho CRM, Zendesk Sell, Monday, and more.\r\n</p><p>Note: If you find it difficult to make an informed decision to select a CRM from plethora of options, talk to your cloud solution provider (CSP) like<a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\"> Dynamics Square</a>. They keep a strong team to solve all your queries.<a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\"> Contact Now</a>!</p><h2>How can Dynamics CRM or Dynamics 365 Sales Help Businesses?</h2><p>The choice between D365 Sales (formerly Dynamics CRM) and other CRM platforms will deviate towards the specific use case your business may have. If you are a company or a firm looking to grow its products and reach out to untapped potential, Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales can be the better choice.\r\n</p><p>That said, you may still have questions like why should I choose Dynamics CRM and how it can help boost my business’ growth?\r\n</p><p>Let’s answer your why in this way –\r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-365/business/sales-support\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft</a> has invested billions of dollars in its cloud-computing ecosystem that hosts Dynamics 365 Suite. This business suite has 11 core business management modules built on Azure platform and powered by Artificial Intelligence (AI) and<a href=\"https://blog.dynamicssquare.com/microsoft-introduces-dynamics-365-copilot/\" target=\"_blank\"> Dynamics 365 Copilot</a> (OpenAI’s GPT4-based language model). \r\n</p><p>With these powerful business modules, you can manage every aspect of your business. You can manage your sales, service, and marketing, and bring automation to talent management, finance and operations, supply chain management, and retail.</p><p><b>Why select Dynamics 365 Sales:</b></p><ul><li>Easy learning curve\r\n</li><li>Seamless integration with other Microsoft products such as Office 365, Outlook, OneNote, Microsoft Teams, Microsoft Loop, Microsoft Viva Sales, and other third-party add-ons (on Microsoft AppSource) and integrations.\r\n</li><li>Built-in AI for context-driven suggestions, data analytics, and report-sharing options.\r\n</li><li>Highly secure for any businesses.\r\n</li><li>Helps with customer insights, customer invoices, marketing, and order management.\r\n</li><li>Allows easy customization, extensibility, and more tools to scale growth</li></ul><h2>Dynamics 365 Sales Pricing</h2><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a> offers three main sales plans and two main customer service plans. Microsoft designed these plans to cover all breeds of business management:</p><h3><b>Main Sales Plans</b></h3><p>Sales Professional: Available at $65 per user/month and offers core sales force automation and Microsoft 365 Automation.\r\n</p><p>Sales Enterprise: At $95 per user/month and offers industry-leading sales force automation with contextual insights and business-centric customization options.\r\n</p><p>Sales Premium: At $135 per user/month and adds prebuilt, customizable intelligence solutions designed for your business’s sellers and admins.\r\n</p><p>Customer Service Plans\r\n</p><p>Customer Service Professional: At $50 per user/month and offers core customer service capabilities.\r\n</p><p>Customer Service Enterprise: At $95 per user/month and provides more advanced customer service capabilities.\r\n</p><p>Note: If your business is already using Dynamics 365 products, this plan is discounted to $20 per user/month and these plans are billed annually.</p><p>\r\n</p><h2>CRM Software FAQs for Businesses</h2><h3>How do Dynamics 365 and Salesforce vary from one another?</h3><p>Though CRM products like Salesforce are sleek and have a modern interface; Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales is an upgrade of Dynamics CRM and comes with intuitive, yet classic interface.\r\nMoreover, Salesforce is designed to help small to</p><div> medium-sized businesses, while Dynamics 365 Sales is for larger businesses spread across the globe.</div><div><br></div><h3>Why choose Dynamics 365 Sales?</h3><p>Dynamics 365 Sales uses Microsoft Viva Sales (a powerful combination of Copilot and generative AI) to enhance the seller experience.\r\n</p><p>If you are looking for an edge in your sales team, this cloud-based sales platform can be your final destination for years of resolution.\r\n</p><p>An innovative CRM solution like D365 sales that is flexible to customize can help you to:\r\n</p><ul><li>Determine and engage with right customers\r\n</li><li>Improve interaction with existing customers\r\n</li><li>Thoroughly learn about the customer journey\r\n</li><li>Increase the productivity of your sales and marketing team\r\n</li></ul><p>Get in touch with your <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a> to reveal the best suited CRM module from Dynamics 365 apps.</p><h3>Is Dynamics the same as Salesforce?</h3><p>No. Dynamics CRM (now Dynamics 365 sales) is a tried-and-true product of hard work from the top 5 companies in the world, while Salesforce is a Silicon Valley success story. Both cater to different sizes of businesses. Dynamics 365 sales can be the best selection for big organizations, whereas Salesforce may be a good fit for small and medium sized enterprises (SMEs).</p><h3>What is the easiest CRM?</h3><p>It is difficult to answer since it depends on the sizes of a business, complexity of sales operations, and use cases. For instance, CRMs like Zoho, Salesforce, or alike can go with small and medium size organizations, while Dynamics 365 Sales is for organizations that are searching for ways to grow their product.\r\n</p><p>Thus, it is recommended to get in touch with your Microsoft Dynamics 365 Partner like Dynamics Square, share your business needs, and make an informed decision.</p><h3>Can small businesses use CRM?</h3><p>&nbsp;Yes. CRM software is a backbone to win new customers and make strong interaction with the current customers. Solutions like Dynamics 365 Sales, Marketing, and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-customer-engagement/\" target=\"_blank\">Customer Engagemen</a>t are specially designed to manage <a href=\"https://generect.com/blog/business-contact-database/\" target=\"_blank\">contacts </a>and marketing campaigns, identify sales opportunities, monitor sales related activities on a unified interface.\r\n</p><p>CRM solutions are key to informed decision-making for anyone at your company who might need it anytime.\r\n</p><p>Contact your Dynamics 365 Partner for a suitable CRM solution for your enterprise.</p><h3>How to choose CRM for small business?</h3><p>Small startups run on a confined budget and require a highly efficient yet cost-effective CRM solution like Salesforce, Zoho, Monday, Zendesk Sell, or HubSpot CRM. However, if you want basic capabilities for your startup business, you can opt for <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central</a>.  \r\n</p><p>Remember, if you have a complex set of operations with a large customer base, Dynamics 365 Sales may be the right option.\r\n</p><p>Schedule a 1:1 meeting with our Microsoft Consultants for a strategic decision.</p><h3>Bottom Line</h3><p>CRM solutions from Microsoft Dynamics 365 are well-built and well-designed and are extensively integrated with third-party applications, hundreds, if not thousands, of apps/add-ons available on AppSource. Other cloud CRM solution providers do not offer the same. Plus, the learning curve is easy because of its easy-to-understand user interface. Even an inexperienced individual can learn to use Dynamics 365 within a few days. \r\n</p><p>Further, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-sales/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales</a> is the best CRM application for larger and more established organizations. In addition to that, businesses that already use the Microsoft Office suite extensively can avail themselves of amazing discounts on subscriptions.  \r\n</p><p>Finally, if you’re looking for a CRM solution that makes it easier for your employees to do more with less by easily accessing data to collaborate and increase productivity, get in touch with us and reveal a business-centric CRM for your business.</p><p>Explore <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/crm-implementation-services/\" target=\"_blank\">CRM implementation services</a> designed to scale and grow businesses</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><div>\r\n</div><p><b>\r\n</b></p><p><b>\r\n</b></p><p><b>\r\n</b></p><p><b>\r\n</b></p><p><b>\r\n</b></p><p><b>\r\n</b></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Which is the best CRM Platform for Businesses?', 'businesses', 'Find the perfect CRM platform for your businesses! Compare features, benefits, and make an informed decision to enhance productivity and drive sales.', 'dynamics crm,microsoft dynamics crm,dynamics 365 sales,microsoft dynamics 365 sales,d365 sales,microsoft d365 sales', NULL, 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', '.', '[]', '03:30:44pm', '2023-06-13', '10 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-09-11 15:30:44'),
(139, 'What is Dynamics 365 Finance? An Overview', 'dynamics-365-finance-an-overview', 'Dynamics 365 Finance', 'dynamics-365-finance', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768130317157292.jpg', 'Get enlightened how Dynamics 365 Finance ERP can help you maximize financial visibility and profitability and accelerate your finance and operations for your business.', '<p>Get enlightened how <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance/\">Dynamics 365 Finance ERP</a> can help you maximize financial visibility and profitability and accelerate your finance and operations for your business.\r\n</p><p>Let\'s ask basic questions first before going any further.\r\n</p><p>What is Finance?\r\n</p><p>Finance is the “<b>Art and Science of managing money!</b>” It\'s that simple.\r\n</p><h2>Why is Financial Management so important in Business?\r\n</h2><p>Finance is the life cycle of your business, or more precisely - it is a critical function for the survival of the organization.\r\n</p><p>Financial decisions involve qualitative and quantitative factors that further require both art and science.\r\n</p><p>The art of finance involves human skills, creativity, risk-taking, and effective communication, while science involves observing and experimenting to understand the environment and create value for shareholders using proven theories and concepts.\r\n</p><p>Corporate finance involves managing assets and liabilities to generate a fair rate of return for shareholders.\r\n</p><p>Familiarity with the three financial statements (income statement, balance sheet, and cash flow statement) is crucial for your finance team.\r\n</p><p>A less complex financial management strategy is to use a minimum amount of assets and the right mix of liabilities and equity to meet risk tolerance while maximizing revenues.\r\n</p><p>Thus, your finance management department should focus on increasing revenues while minimizing costs and expenses to generate a fair rate of return (or return on investment – ROI).\r\n</p><p>And to accelerate your finance management, employ the right finance software system like Microsoft\'s Dynamics 365 Finance (earlier; <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance-operations/\">Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations</a>). Such systems help your finance team win.\r\n</p><p>If you are concerned that your current finance system is finding it hard to manage the increasing flow of financial activity, it may be time to get started with upgrading your existing finance ERP software to Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance - an all-in-one cloud solution for your company\'s finance.\r\n</p><p>By <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-finance-implementation/\">implementing Dynamics 365 Finance</a>, you can effectively manage multiple processes simultaneously, while also supporting your expanding financial practices to fuel innovation and enhance productivity.\r\n</p><p>So, let\'s know about this finance ERP from Microsoft.\r\n</p><h2>What is Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance?\r\n</h2><p>Dynamics 365 Finance is a comprehensive finance management application to help you streamline all your financial processes and enhance your financial decision-making.\r\n</p><p>This powerful finance tool enhances your ability to seamlessly and effectively manage crucial practices such as budgeting, planning, forecasting, and AI analytics, as well as aiding you with key reporting capabilities.\r\n</p><p>Additionally, D365 Finance enables enterprises like yours to efficiently manage global compliance and regulatory services while keeping costs under control.\r\n</p><p>With such an advanced finance ERP solution, you can optimize your financial operations and ensure compliance with ease.\r\n</p><p>Now that you know what <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a> is and how capable it is. Let\'s explore how Dynamics 365 Finance can help you achieve these goals.\r\n</p><h2>Benefits Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance\r\n</h2><p>Rolling out a cloud solution like Microsoft Dynamics 365 for finance can bring several benefits to your organization, including:\r\n</p><p><b>Streamlined Financial Processes:</b> With Dynamics 365 Finance, you can streamline and automate your financial processes, reducing the time and effort needed to complete financial tasks.\r\n</p><p><b>Greater Financial Visibility:</b> This cloud ERP solution gives you real-time financial insights, enabling you to make data-driven decisions and manage your finances more effectively and efficiently.\r\n</p><p><b>Enhanced Productivity:</b> With features such as automated workflows and approvals, Dynamics 365 Finance can help you improve productivity and reduce manual errors.\r\n</p><p><b>Better Compliance:</b> The solution includes built-in compliance features, allowing you to stay compliant with relevant regulations and avoid penalties.\r\n</p><p><b>Enhanced Scalability:</b> Dynamics 365 Finance is highly scalable and can support the growth of your organization, enabling you to manage financial operations across multiple locations and business units.\r\n</p><p><b>Advanced Data Analytics and Insights:</b> The solution includes advanced analytics capabilities, such as <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-ai/\">artificial intelligence</a> and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/azure-machine-learning/\">machine learning</a>, providing deeper insights into your financial data and supporting more informed decision-making.\r\n</p><p><b>Reduce Costs:</b> Achieve cost minimization and best spending across business geographies through process automation, budget control measures, and financial intelligence, planning, and analysis tools with Dynamics 365 Finance.\r\n</p><p>Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance is a sure help if you are willing to get up and improve the efficiency, accuracy, and compliance of your financial operations while driving&nbsp;the growth and success of your organization.\r\n</p><h2>Features of Dynamics 365 Business Central\r\n</h2><p>Microsoft Dynamics 365 for Finance is a comprehensive financial management application&nbsp;that offers you a range of features to help your team manage your financial operations.\r\n</p><p>With this finance ERP software, you can unify and automate your business processes by integrating financials into core processes and automating repetitive tasks to boost productivity, support evolving business models, and maximize financial performance.\r\n</p><p>You can drive agility and growth with Dynamics 365 Finance’s powerful financial reporting, embedded analytics, and AI-driven insights.\r\n</p><p>Some of the key features of Dynamics 365 Finance include:\r\n</p><ul><li><b>Budgeting and Forecasting:</b> You can use the budgeting and forecasting capabilities provided by D365 F&amp;O (formerly known as Dynamics 365 Finance) to better plan and make informed decisions.\r\n</li><li><b>General Ledger:</b> D365 Finance assists you with a centralized view of all financial transactions and supports multiple currencies, budgets, and financial dimensions.\r\n</li><li><b>Accounts Payable:</b> This feature in Dynamics 365 Finance helps you manage vendor invoices, payments, and credit memos, and enables you to automate invoice processing and approvals.\r\n</li><li><b>Accounts Receivable:</b> This advanced finance solution is powered by Microsoft’s latest tech and enables you to manage customer invoices, payments, and credit memos, and supports features such as collections, customer credit limits, and sales tax calculations. Platforms complement this by helping businesses <a href=\"https://monk.com/platform/automation\" target=\"_blank\">automate accounts receivables</a> through streamlined collections and follow-up workflows.</li><li><b>Cash and Bank Management:</b> Dynamics 365 for finance allows you to manage your cash and bank accounts, bank reconciliations, and cash forecasting, and supports features such as electronic bank statement imports and payment reconciliation.\r\n</li><li><b>Fixed Assets:</b> Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance helps you manage your fixed assets, including acquisition, depreciation, and disposal, and supports multiple depreciation methods.\r\n</li><li><b>Project Management and Accounting:</b> D365 Finance helps you to manage project finances, including project budgeting, tracking costs and revenues, and project invoicing.\r\n</li><li><b>Financial Reporting and Analytics:</b> This feature in Dynamics 365 finance offers you a range of financial reporting and analytics tools to help you gain insights into your financial data, including financial statements, business intelligence, and artificial intelligence capabilities.\r\n</li><li><b>Global Compliance:</b> The built-in regulatory and compliance features in Dynamics 365 Finance, including tax and audit management, help you meet local and global regulatory requirements with super ease.\r\n</li></ul><p>Moreover, a&nbsp;study conducted by Forrester Consulting in 2022 on behalf of Microsoft found that <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://tools.totaleconomicimpact.com/go/microsoft/D365Finance/\" target=\"_blank\">deploying Dynamics 365 Finance resulted in a substantial return on investment (ROI) of 122% over a three-year period</a>.\r\n</p><p>The study also reported legacy cost savings of over $3.5 million, and finance personnel productivity improvements of 55%.\r\n</p><p>These are just some of the many features of Dynamics 365 Finance.\r\n</p><p>With this game-changing solution, you can seamlessly manage your financial operations more effectively, while gaining deeper insights into your financial data to quickly make informed decisions.\r\n</p><h2>Why use Dynamics 365 Finance to Maximize Outcomes?\r\n</h2><p>As an organization grows and expands, managing financial operations can become increasingly complex.\r\n</p><p>Dynamics 365 Finance is a finance-centric solution for your business. It helps you flawlessly streamline your financial processes, enhance productivity, improve compliance, and maximize financial insights.\r\n</p><p>See how Dynamics 365 finance solution helps you hone your financials:\r\n</p><h3>Streamlining Financial Processes\r\n</h3><p>1. Automating financial tasks\r\n</p><p>2. Centralizing financial data\r\n</p><p>3. Improving financial visibility\r\n</p><h3>Enhancing Productivity\r\n</h3><p>1. Automating workflows and approvals\r\n</p><p>2. Reducing manual errors\r\n</p><p>3. Enabling self-service capabilities\r\n</p><h3>Improving Compliance\r\n</h3><p>1. Meeting regulatory and compliance requirements\r\n</p><p>2. Minimizing the risk of penalties and fines\r\n</p><h3>Maximizing Financial Insights\r\n</h3><p>1. Analyzing financial data with advanced analytics tools\r\n</p><p>2. Supporting data-driven decision-making\r\n</p><p>3. Showing trends and opportunities for further optimization\r\n</p><h3>Supporting Business Growth at Scale\r\n</h3><p>1. Scalability of the cloud ERP - Dynamics 365 for Finance\r\n</p><p>2. Supporting global financial operations\r\n</p><p>3. Prop up mergers and acquisitions\r\n</p><h2>How Can Dynamics 365 Finance help make my business grow at scale?\r\n</h2><p>Dynamics 365 Finance is a powerful business software tool that can help businesses to streamline their operations and optimize their financial management.\r\n</p><p>Here are some of the key benefits that Dynamics 365 Finance can offer to businesses looking to get started at full throttle and make waves:&nbsp;\r\n</p><p><b>Enhanced Financial Visibility:</b> Dynamics 365 Finance provides increased real-time visibility into your financials, allowing you to monitor your cash flow, track expenses, and manage budgets with ease.\r\n</p><p>With advanced reporting and analytics capabilities, you can gain insights into your financial performance and make informed decisions to improve your profitability.\r\n</p><p><b>Improved Cash Flow Management:</b> This finance application enables businesses to augment their cash flow by automating financial processes such as invoicing, payment collection, and accounts payable.\r\n</p><p>This helps to reduce the time and effort needed to manage financial transactions and ensure that your cash flow still is healthy and predictable.\r\n</p><p><b>Simplified Financial Reporting:</b> Dynamics 365 Finance offers a range of pre-built financial reports that can help you quickly generate correct financial statements, balance sheets, and cash flow statements.\r\n</p><p>It can save businesses significant time and effort and guarantees that they still are compliant with regulatory requirements.\r\n</p><p><b>Streamlined Financial Processes:</b> D365 Finance can help businesses to streamline their financial processes by automating tasks such as bank reconciliation, financial close, and intercompany accounting.\r\n</p><p>This can reduce the risk of errors and make sure that financial processes are completed accurately and on time.\r\n</p><p><b>Scalability and Flexibility:</b> Dynamics 365 Finance is a cloud-based solution that can be customized to meet the unique needs of your business.\r\n</p><p>Meaning, as your business grows and evolves, this solution grows too!\r\n</p><p>That is, you can add new features and functionality to your Dynamics 365 Finance system to support your changing needs.\r\n</p><h2>Who can use Dynamics 365 Finance?\r\n</h2><p>Designed and developed by Microsoft, Dynamics 365 Finance is for organizations of all sizes across various industries.\r\n</p><p>You can use it to manage financial operations, such as accounting, financial planning, and cash flow management.\r\n</p><p>Dynamics 365 Finance is suitable for finance professionals, accountants, and people who manage the financial aspects of your business.\r\n</p><p>Your finance decision-makers who need to have access to the right financial data to make informed business decisions can use&nbsp;this software in many ways.\r\n</p><h3>List of the Global Leaders Using Dynamics 365 for Finance\r\n</h3><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 for Finance</a> is used by many companies across various industries.\r\n</p><p>Here are a few examples of companies that use Dynamics 365 Finance:\r\n</p><p><b>1. Bel Fuse Inc. -</b> An Electronic connector manufacturing company in the USA.\r\n</p><p><b>2. Coca-Cola Beverages Africa -</b> The popular soft drink manufacturer and an American multinational beverage corporation founded in 1892.\r\n</p><p><b>3. Hitachi, Ltd. -</b> A Japanese multinational conglomerate corporation that drives Social Innovation Business by creating a sustainable society with data and technology.\r\n</p><p><b>4. Fieldfisher LLP -</b> A multinational law firm headquartered in London.\r\n</p><p><b>5. Dah Chong Hong Holdings Limited (DCH Ltd.) -</b> A Hong Kong-based conglomerate engaged in motor vehicle sales and repair, air cargo equipment distribution, cosmetic, airport ground support equipment maintenance, food, logistics, and warehouse services.\r\n</p><p><b>6. HP Inc. -</b> an American multinational information technology company.\r\n</p><p><b>7. Airbus Group -</b> a European multinational aerospace corporation.\r\n</p><p><b>8. The Adecco Group -</b> a Swiss multinational human resource consulting firm.\r\n</p><p><b>9. LEGO Group -</b> a Danish multinational toy company.\r\n</p><p><b>10. The Hershey Company -</b> an American multinational food company.\r\n</p><p><b>11. Trek Bicycle Corporation –</b> USA’s bicycle and cycling product manufacturer.\r\n</p><p><b>12. Big Brothers Big Sisters of America -</b> a nonprofit organization that gives mentorship programs for children.\r\n</p><p><b>13. GEA Group -</b> a German multinational technology group that specializes in process engineering.\r\n</p><p><b>15. KIND -</b> a healthy snack bar and granola company based in the United States.\r\n</p><p><b>16. Williams-Sonoma, Inc. -</b> an American home goods retailer.\r\n</p><p><b>Note:</b> This is not an exhaustive list and there are many other companies that use Dynamics 365 Finance.\r\n</p><h2>The Wrap Up!\r\n</h2><p>Dynamics 365 Finance is an ideal solution for businesses looking to get started at full throttle and make waves. This single solution provides you with a comprehensive suite of financial management features.\r\n</p><p>This finance cloud ERP solution enables you to gain a deeper understanding of their financial situation and make data-driven decisions that can help you achieve your business goals and objectives.\r\n</p><p>D365 finance gives you enhanced financial visibility, improved cash flow management, simplified financial reporting, streamlined financial processes, and scalability and flexibility.\r\n</p><p>With this solution, you can help your business operations to re-invent your finances and achieve what you want, and the way you want.\r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Get in touch with Dynamics 365 experts</a> at Dynamics Square to get started with the implementation of Dynamics 365 Finance. Or if you’re a small business looking for an all-in-one ERP solution, consider implementing <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central</a>.</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Dynamics 365 Finance: An Informative Overview', 'dynamics 365 finance', 'Discover how Dynamics 365 Finance can improve financial operations for businesses. Our blog provides an informative overview of its features and benefits.', 'dynamics 365 finance,microsoft dynamics 365 finance,d365 finance,microsoft d365 finance', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768130317157843.jpg', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', '.', '[]', '06:51:49pm', '2023-06-08', '13 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2026-01-28 01:51:49');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(140, 'Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: What Is It?', 'what-is-dynamics-365-supply-chain-management', 'supply chain management', 'supply-chain-management', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768130615989095.jpg', 'Streamline your operations with Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management. Enhance efficiency, improve visibility, and optimize your supply chain with AI-powered insights and real-time data.', '<p>If you’re looking for a centralized approach to managing your supply chain, you need <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</a> (or D365 SCM). It is an integrated supply chain ERP solution. D365 SCM makes your supply chain more intelligent and helps you overcome current and future challenges with ease. Explore this blog for more.”</p><p>Your business is growing like never before, but your operational efficiency is not as you expected. Why? Maybe you lack an adequate system, support, or functional capability that can do magic.\r\n</p><p>Or maybe you’ve outgrown your current ERP system and you have no idea that it needs an upgrade.\r\n</p><p>Today, businesses need highly connected business applications like Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management (formerly, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance-operations/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations</a>).</p><p></p><p>For growing businesses, it is essential to have real-time visibility to optimize their end-to-end processes and resources to drive profitability at scale. Dynamics 365 for Supply Chain Management comes with built-in business intelligence (BI) and process automation capability. It helps enterprises to optimize their process flow and resource utilization.\r\n</p><p>To support an organization’s business continuity, this supply chain solution from Microsoft could be a proven, efficient deal. This robust solution enables businesses to drive operational success and bring agility into their manufacturing &amp; distribution processes.\r\n</p><p>Further, it empowers your employees to quickly solve customer issues and ensure satisfactory customer fulfillment by bringing transparency into the warehousing and service department.\r\n</p><p>If you’re a business that caters to thousands of transactions per day and involves complex operations to handle, this blog is worth a read. Let’s get to the bottom of what Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management really is!</p><h2>What is Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management?</h2><p>Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management or D365 SCM (formerly <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-ax/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics AX</a>) is a cloud-based, enterprise-scale supply chain solution. With its help, operations leaders can transform the ways of managing their manufacturing and supply chain processes.</p><p></p><p>This supply chain ERP acts as a single source of information that uses AI-driven predictive insights and the <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/azure-iot-internet-of-things/\" target=\"_blank\">Internet of Things</a> (IoT) across planning, production, stock, warehouse, and transportation management. If you’re looking to maximize operational efficiency, product quality, and profitability for your business, Dynamics 365 SCM can be the answer to your quest.</p><h2>What are the Capabilities of Dynamics 365 SCM?</h2><p>Dynamics 365 SCM is the successor to both Dynamics AX and Dynamics 365 F&amp;O. Thus, it is more powerful than its predecessors, and other similar ERP solutions in the market.</p><h3><b>Core functions and capabilities of Dynamics 365 for Supply Chain Management</b></h3><ul><li><b>Maximized Asset Uptime and Accelerate Time to Market: </b>With Dynamics 365 SCM, you can bring the power of AI and IoT intelligence to automate your manufacturing processes, reduce machine downtime, and accelerate the time to market your products. You can perform production planning in real-time with the Planning Optimization Preview feature in D365 SCM.\r\n</li><li><b>Enhanced warehouse management:</b> Supply Chain Management isn’t merely about inventory and logistics. You need solutions to go beyond that. Use machine learning models to quickly figure out out-of-stock or overstock situations to effectively manage stock management.\r\n</li><li><b>AI-Embedded Manufacturing for Optimized Production Performance:</b> Using the IoT Intelligence Preview feature in D365 SCM, manufacturers can identify potential machine issues, prevent machine downtime, and enhance product quality.\r\n</li><li><b>Increase the lifespan of Your Assets:</b> Maximize equipment lifespan and enhance performance by utilizing Asset Management Preview, which employs IoT and mixed reality to predict, schedule and conduct maintenance.\r\n</li><li><b>Employ Automation for Simplified Supply Chain:</b> With predictive analytics features, businesses can enhance their supply chain at par. Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management can automate core SCM tasks such as fulfillment, material sourcing, logistics processes, and more. It ultimately leads to optimized planning and product delivery.\r\n</li><li><b>On-the-go Business Management with Cloud Services:</b> Access real-time information on any device, simplify business process changes, streamline integration with legacy systems, ensure global compliance, easily scale up or down as needed, and manage your business on-the-go.</li></ul><h2>Pricing and Licensing Options for Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</h2><p>Microsoft cares for every business out there and has come up with industry-specific licensing options.\r\n</p><p>Here is the per user/per app or per business process pricing model for Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management:</p><p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" data-filename=\"image.png\" style=\"width: 1248px;\"><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p></p><blockquote><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Get in touch with your Microsoft Dynamics Partner like Dynamics Square for more information regarding the pricing and licensing of Dynamics 365.</b></a></p></blockquote><h2>Conclusion\r\n</h2><p>When it comes to managing your continuously growing supply chain, logistics, and manufacturing &amp; distribution practices, Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Solution could be the best investment – not for today but for tomorrow too.</p><p>If you want your supply chain the way you have imagined, D365 SCM can be a highly productive solution for your business to support your current market adoption and globally expand your business capabilities with seamlessness, reliability, and agility.</p><p>Curious to see this next-gen SCM ERP application in action?</p><p>Connect with our Dynamics 365 Experts to <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/schedule-a-demo/\" target=\"_blank\">schedule a FREE demo</a>.</p>', 'What is Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management?', 'Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management', 'Optimize your supply chain with Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management for improved efficiency and real-time insights.', 'dynamics 365 finance,dynamics 365 supply chain management,microsoft dynamics 365 supply chain management,d365 supply chain management', NULL, 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '04:56:01pm', '2023-06-13', '43 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-02-13 16:56:01');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(141, 'When Does Your Business Need ERP Software?', 'when-does-your-business-need-erp-software', 'ERP', 'erp', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1783095383674186.ERP Software.png', 'Find out if your business needs an ERP system with our blog. Learn the benefits of ERP software and how to determine if it\'s right for your organization.', '<p>Thinking about a business idea is one thing and seldom easy, but running a whole business around that idea is another. Plus, keeping up with every business operation and compiling a ton of data becomes tough as the business grows.\r\n</p><p>This is why businesses of all sizes deploy Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) system. An ERP system is an <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365\" target=\"_blank\">integrated business management solution</a> that acts as the backbone of an organization. It makes your enterprise more efficient, resilient, and intelligent enough to strike the chord with evolving markets.\r\n</p><p>If you’re into running a business, you might need help from an ERP solution (whether on-premises, cloud, or hybrid).\r\n</p><p>But do you know what an ERP is? What does an ERP system do? How does an ERP solution benefit your company? We’ve assembled easy-to-digest keynotes to help you discover the basics of ERP and why you should deploy it. Let’s get rolling!</p><p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" src=\"//www.youtube.com/embed/EIK7QNmQloQ\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" class=\"note-video-clip\"></iframe><br></p><h2>What is Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP)?</h2><p>ERP refers to ways of managing the back-end operations and resources to run an enterprise and the software that makes it easy, known as ERP software.\r\n</p><p>Today, there are <a href=\"https://blog.dynamicssquare.com/microsoft-dynamics-365-erp-for-smes/\" target=\"_blank\">numerous ERP solutions </a>available in all shapes and sizes to help organizations of all sizes spread across industries bolster their operational efficiency, avoid unnecessary costs, and scale their business at par.\r\n</p><p>These solutions assist companies with simple tasks like accounting and procurement to complex operations such as financials, supply chain management, inventory, <a href=\"https://www.peoplehum.com/payroll-software\" target=\"_blank\">HR-payroll</a>, and scheduling.\r\n</p><p>More precisely, an ERP system is a centralized program designed and developed to run essential functions of an organization.</p><h2>What is the Purpose of an ERP for a Company?</h2><p>Many use cases can prompt you to employ an ERP system.\r\n</p><p>The more important one is when businesses look for ways to bring all their precious data into one place and keep it flowing to preserve business continuity, especially when turning a growing <a href=\"https://redandwhitemagz.com/sustainable-ideas-for-starting-a-business-kickstart-your-eco-friendly-online-venture-today/\" target=\"_blank\">business idea</a> into a structured and scalable company.\r\n</p><p>Companies strive to do it since it keeps their data safe, and organized, and can be accessed anytime, anywhere.\r\n</p><p>An ERP system provides the flexibility to help business admins keep track of all the moving parts of their organization and get a 360-degree view of day-to-day operations.</p><h2>Do companies of all sizes use an ERP system?</h2><p>Yes. More than 70% of large groups use an ERP or a similar business management solution.\r\n</p><p>Any company – no matter what the size is – needs an ERP system. It is projected that the <a href=\"https://www.alliedmarketresearch.com/press-release/global-ERP-software-market-is-expected-to-reach-41-69-billion-by-2020.html\" target=\"_blank\">ERP market size will hit</a> $117.09 billion by 2030. That’s about $360 per person in the US. This data is enough to see the value an ERP system can generate for businesses.\r\n</p><p>Earlier models of ERP software (<a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics ERP</a>) were incorporated to manage large manufacturing companies. However, as technology evolved over the years, <a href=\"https://blog.dynamicssquare.com/cloud-erp-best-choice-for-small-businesses/\" target=\"_blank\">cloud-based ERP solutions</a> are making it more accessible.\r\n</p><p>Businesses of all sizes and budgets can implement an ERP system to better manage their supply chain, improve financial control, and generate custom proposals and reports.\r\n</p><p>One of the popular <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/case-studies/nav13-business-central-upgrade/\" target=\"_blank\">aviation fluid handling component designer and manufacturer</a>&nbsp;near Niagara Falls experienced soaring profit post implementing a cloud ERP solution – Microsoft Dynamics Business Central. This comprehensive ERP helped this manufacturing company expand its manufacturing capabilities and do more with less.</p><h2>What are the benefits of Deploying an ERP for my business?</h2><p>Investing in an ERP solution is a long-term decision, and it will help you now and, in the future, to make informed choices.\r\n</p><p>Today, <a href=\"https://www.brandveda.in/blog/top-it-companies-in-hyderabad\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">IT companies</a> want a business management system that is comprehensive; meaning, a solution that breaks data silos into meaningful insights, and makes it easy and quick to share reports between departments. To achieve this efficiently, many organizations opt for <a href=\"https://www.n-ix.com/outsourcing-software-development/\" target=\"_blank\">outsource software development</a>, ensuring tailored ERP solutions that meet their specific business needs.</p><p><b>Here are the benefits of an ERP your business can reap, they include:</b></p><ol><li>Get a clear, real-time picture of your financial data to gain better financial visibility and maximize profitability.\r\n</li><li>Seamlessly manage budgets, record transactions, and expenses, oversee assets and collections, and measure cash flows.\r\n</li><li>A better ERP solution helps a company keep its financial data safe and compliant.\r\n</li><li>Cloud ERP solutions offer advanced data security features, automatic backups, and disaster recovery options, which leads to mitigating most security concerns of business owners.\r\n</li><li>Helps businesses make their supply chain more resilient and sustainable. It is one of the many reasons why ERP was first created.\r\n</li><li>A best-of-breed ERP suite can help organizations monitor the progress of various projects at one time.\r\n</li><li>According to successful business leaders, ERP is a synonym for “managing human capital effectively“. In other words, any ERP can be the best if it gives importance to people working in an organization. Hence, an ERP is essential to manage the core functions of an enterprise, such as time management and payroll.</li></ol><p>Further, an ERP can also help a company automate HCM (Human Capital Management) tasks like scheduling, employee absences, and vacations to save time, money, and other tasks like providing a clear overview of hiring data.\r\n</p><p>Cloud ERP solutions can provide business intelligence features to help you track progress, measure performance, and create in-depth reports. With an integrated ERP solution, stakeholders of a business can empower their organization to quickly make informed decisions.\r\n</p><p>Customer relationships management (CRM) like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a> is another field in which an ERP like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> can help an organization deal with basic customer service needs.\r\n</p><p>If you want to see how an ERP like D365 BC works, you can opt for a free trial here:<a href=\"https://blog.dynamicssquare.com/get-start-business-central-free-trial/\" target=\"_blank\"> How to get started with Dynamics 365 Business Central FREE Trial</a></p><h2>When does your company need an ERP solution?</h2><p>For most companies, it is not the matter of “why should they” implement an enterprise resource planning software, but “when is the right time.”\r\n</p><p>The right time to deploy is when you are going through one or more of the following situations:\r\n</p><ul><li><b>You’ve outgrown your existing software: </b>Your current ERP system can no longer process the data and lacks automation capabilities.\r\n</li><li><b>You’re having inefficient processes:</b> Constantly switching among ERP software to find the right fit.\r\n</li><li><b>When you are spending a ton of money on software integrations:</b> You are trying to integrate multiple applications and add-ons to streamline data and access it cross-departmentally. This isn’t cheap!\r\n</li><li><b>Your current ERP system is not able to meet customer demands</b>: It means, you are no longer in a position to live up to your promises and having difficulty managing and tracking inventory.\r\n</li></ul><p><b>There may exist other reasons why a company needs modern ERP software.\r\n</b></p><p>If you’re a small size business looking for a comprehensive business management solution, you can always get in touch with Dynamics Square (<a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a>). Our ERP solution experts are always there for you! <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\">Contact now</a>.</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'When does your Business need ERP Software?', 'business', 'Find out if your business needs an ERP system with our blog. Learn the benefits of ERP software and how to determine if it\'s right for your organization.', 'business central,dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics business central,dynamics erp,microsoft dynamics erp,dynamics 365 erp,erp solutions', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1783095383674193.ERP Software.png', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', '.', '[]', '01:25:20pm', '2023-11-20', '7 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2026-03-20 20:25:20'),
(142, 'Feature Update 2023 for Microsoft Power BI: Transform Your Data into Immediate Impact', 'new-feature-update-for-power-bi', 'Power BI', 'power-bi', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768132987400486.png', 'As a Microsoft Power BI enthusiast at Dynamics Square, I am pleased to introduce you to Power BI, Microsoft’s cloud-based business analytics service.', '<p>As a <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">Microsoft Power BI</a> enthusiast at Dynamics Square, I am pleased to introduce you to Power BI, Microsoft’s cloud-based business analytics service.\r\n</p><p>With the goal of empowering your business intelligence needs, Microsoft Power BI offers a suite of tools that enable you to collect, analyze, and visualize data from a wide range of sources, even from your <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM</a>.\r\n</p><p>Whether you are a small business owner or part of a large enterprise, Power BI is a Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) and provides you with a scalable, cost-effective solution that helps you make informed decisions based on real-time data.\r\n</p><p>With Microsoft Power BI, you can easily create customized dashboards and reports that allow you to gain insights into your data, identify trends, and monitor key performance indicators (KPIs) from one location.\r\n</p><h2>Are you excited to see what\'s latest in Power BI in 2023?\r\n</h2><p>The Power BI February 2023 feature update includes several new features and enhancements that make it easier for businesses to transform their data into actionable insights.\r\n</p><p>Moreover, with this popular business intelligence (BI) tool, you can connect to popular SaaS solutions like Salesforce and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a>, making it an ideal tool for businesses that are already using these applications.\r\n</p><p>Let\'s see the key features of this new update in Microsoft Power BI. Continue reading for more details.\r\n</p><h3>1. Data Analysis Expressions (DAX) Enhancements\r\n</h3><p>One of the major highlights of the Microsoft Power BI February 2023 release is the enhancements to Data Analysis Expressions (DAX).\r\n</p><p>DAX is a powerful formula language that is used in Microsoft Power BI to create calculations and custom measures.\r\n</p><p>For the following examples, the data includes Sales Amount and gross national product (GNP) per capita:\r\n</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768131823095541.Data Analysis Expressions (DAX).png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">These new enhancements include support for time intelligence and new DAX functions, “<b>LINEST</b>” and <b>“LINESTX</b>” that make it easier to work with hierarchical data, as shown in the above image.<br></p><p>This makes it easier for users to perform complex calculations and analyze their data in real-time.\r\n</p><h3>2. Visual Data Preparation\r\n</h3><p>Power BI also introduces a new feature called \"<b>Visual Data Preparation</b>.\"&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>This feature allows users to prepare and clean their data directly within the visualization, without having to switch between the visualization and the data model.\r\n</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768131836853206.Visual Data Preparation.jpeg\" style=\"width: 100%;\">With Visual Data Preparation, users can perform data cleansing, transformation, and wrangling tasks on their data, making it easier to prepare their data for analysis.<br></p><h3>3. Data Flow Enhancements\r\n</h3><p>Another major enhancement in the Microsoft Power BI February 2023 release is the improvements to Data Flows.\r\n</p><p>Data Flows is a cloud-based data preparation tool that lets users extract, transform, and load data from various sources.\r\n</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768131848047982.Data Flow Enhancements.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">The new enhancements include support for incremental refresh and enhanced support for data transformations. These enhancements make it easier for users to work with large datasets and perform data transformations more efficiently.<br></p><h3>4. AI Capabilities\r\n</h3><p>Microsoft Power BI also introduces new AI capabilities that make it easier for users to gain insights from their data. The new AI capabilities include an intelligent assistant that can help users to discover insights in their data and suggest new visuals to use in their reports.\r\n</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768131859560713.AI Capabilities.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">The intelligent assistant can also help users to create natural language queries and get quick answers to their questions.<br></p><h3>5. Enhanced Integration with Microsoft Teams\r\n</h3><p>In addition to the new features and enhancements, Microsoft Power BI also introduces improved integration with Microsoft Teams.\r\n</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768131870527899.Enhanced Integration with Microsoft Teams.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">With the new integration, users can share their Power BI reports and dashboards directly within Microsoft Teams channels, making it easier to collaborate with team members and share insights with others.<br></p><h3>6. Improved Security and Compliance Features\r\n</h3><p>Microsoft Power BI also introduces new security and compliance features that make it easier for businesses to protect their data.\r\n</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768131882170223.Improved Security and Compliance Features.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">The new features include support for Azure Active Directory authentication, which allows users to authenticate using their organizational credentials, and enhanced data protection features, such as sensitivity labels and data loss prevention policies.<br></p><h2>What is the major advantage of using Power BI in 2023?\r\n</h2><p>One of the major advantages of using Microsoft Power BI is its ability to connect to a wide range of data sources.\r\n</p><p>From Excel spreadsheets to cloud-based applications, Power BI allows you to collect data from virtually any source.\r\n</p><p>This makes it easier for you to integrate your data source and generate a comprehensive view of your operations.\r\n</p><p>In addition to its wide range of connectivity options, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">Power BI</a> offers a suite of data analysis tools that enable you to analyze your data in real-time.\r\n</p><p>With features like Quick Insights, you can quickly generate data visualizations and uncover insights that may have gone unnoticed.\r\n</p><p>Moreover, with its powerful AI capabilities, Power BI can help you discover hidden patterns and relationships in your data.</p><p>All these features could be used for in-house and <a href=\"https://alcor-bpo.com/offshore-power-bi-development/\" target=\"_blank\">offshore Power BI development</a>, data analytics, etc.</p><h2>Drill Down Donut PRO: Power BI Visuals by Zoom Charts\r\n</h2><p>“<b>Experience the power of Drill Down Donut PRO by ZoomCharts for Microsoft Power BI and take your data analysis to the next level.</b>”\r\n</p><p>Drill Down Donut PRO by <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://zoomcharts.com/en/\" target=\"_blank\">ZoomCharts</a>, is a powerful visualization tool for Microsoft Power BI that enables users to effortlessly explore and analyze data with visually appealing donut charts.\r\n</p><p>With this visualization tool, all chart interactions take place directly on the chart itself, providing an intuitive user experience that guides the eye and allows for easy data exploration.\r\n</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768131893022551.Drill Down Donut PRO.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">Customize the look of your chart with advanced formatting options and choose from different chart types to create the perfect visualization for your data.<br></p><p>The adjustable \"<b>Others</b>\" slice feature lets you set the number of visible slices and group the rest, while the cross-chart filtering capability enables the chart to function as a filter for the rest of the report.\r\n</p><p>Additionally, Drill Down Donut PRO supports multi-level drill down, allowing you to drill down up to 9 levels for a deeper understanding of your data.\r\n</p><p>With full customization options for slices, labels, and the legend, you can create a chart that is uniquely tailored to your data. Plus, enjoy seamless navigation on both desktop and mobile devices, making it easy to explore your charts on any device.\r\n</p><h2>Why Drill Down Donut PRO?\r\n</h2><p>This tool is ideal for a variety of use cases, including sales and marketing, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-human-resources/\">human resources</a>, accounting and finance, and project management.\r\n</p><p>You can use it to measure campaign performance and research results in sales and marketing, track staff composition and performance data in human resources, conduct income, expense analysis, and manage billings and debtors in accounting and finance, and distribute risks and allocate resources in project management.\r\n</p><h3>A couple of quick recaps of this article:\r\n</h3><p>This article is about time-to-time feature updates for Power BI from <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://powerbi.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft</a>, which include -\r\n</p><h4>Reporting:</h4><ul><li>String fields can be conditionally formatted.\r\n</li><li>Smart Narrative visual summary icon added.\r\n</li><li>Table and matrix <a href=\"https://www.adobe.com/express/feature/image/resize\" target=\"_blank\">images can be resized</a> and formatted to adjust width.</li><li>Power BI’s base theme can now be updated.\r\n</li><li>Custom report themes can now be validated.\r\n</li><li>Text box visual indentation is now available.\r\n</li><li>New accessible report themes have been added.\r\n</li><li>Page navigator visual now allows visible pages to be customized.\r\n</li><li>Sensitivity labels now supported in PDF export from Desktop Preview.\r\n</li><li>Enhanced row-level security editor Preview now available.\r\n</li></ul><h4>Analytics:\r\n</h4><ul><li>Quick Create SDK (software development kit) is now available.\r\n</li></ul><h4>Modeling:\r\n</h4><ul><li>LINEST and LINESTX are new DAX functions available.\r\n</li></ul><h4>Data Connectivity:\r\n</h4><ul><li>Denodo (Connector Update) now available.\r\n</li><li>Digital Construction Works Insights (Connector Update) is now available.\r\n</li><li>Profisee (Connector Update) now available.\r\n</li><li>Cosmos DB V2 (Connector Update) now available.\r\n</li></ul><h4>Service:\r\n</h4><ul><li>A new ‘Get Data‘ experience is now available in the Power BI Service (SaaS version of Power BI).\r\n</li><li>Compact view is now available.\r\n</li><li>Linked metrics are now available.\r\n</li><li>Follow metric now available.\r\n</li></ul><h4>Paginated Reports:\r\n</h4><ul><li>Paginated Reports Formatted Table authoring experience has been added.\r\n</li><li>Users can now create a Paginated Report from a datamart.\r\n</li><li>Capacity Planning for Paginated Reports is now available.\r\n</li></ul><h4>Embedded:\r\n</h4><ul><li>TypeScript support is now available in the playground developer sandbox.\r\n</li></ul><h4>Visualizations (third-party visuals):\r\n</h4><ul><li>Editor’s pick of the quarter has been added.\r\n</li><li>New visuals are now available in AppSource.\r\n</li><li>Milestone Trend Analysis Chart by Nova Silva is now available.\r\n</li><li>Multiple Sparklines are now available.\r\n</li><li>Inforiver Charts 2.1 is now Microsoft Power BI certified.\r\n</li><li>accoPLANNING by Accobat is now available.\r\n</li><li>Drill Down Donut PRO by ZoomCharts is now available.\r\n</li></ul><p>For more information about these features, be sure to check out our informative blog posts about Power BI here.\r\n</p><p>And if you’re ready to get started with Drill Down Donut PRO? You can download it now from Microsoft AppSource or <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">get in touch with Power BI experts</a> at Dynamics Square.</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Microsoft Power BI 2023 Feature Update: What\'s new?', 'microsoft power bi', 'Microsoft Power BI\'s 2023  Update includes (DAX) & Data Flow Enhancements, Visual Data Preparation, new AI Capabilities, Teams Integration and more.', 'power bi,microsoft power bi,cost of microsoft power bi,power bi pricing,power bi for mac', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768132987402261.png', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '01:40:19pm', '2024-03-13', '10 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-06-03 13:40:19'),
(143, 'New Update 21.4 to Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central (Online) from 2022 release wave 2', 'new-update-to-dynamics-365-business-central', 'Business central', 'business-central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768135980737738.jpg', 'Learn more about Dynamics 365 Business Central\'s new features and capabilities from 2022 release wave 2. This blog insight will help you explore about hot fixes, as well as regulatory feature updates for March 2023.', '<p>\"Learn more about Dynamics 365 Business Central\'s new features and capabilities from 2022 release wave 2.&nbsp;This blog insight will help you explore about hot fixes, as well as regulatory feature updates for March 2023.\"</p><p>Formerly popular as Dynamics NAV or Navision, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> is a new software-as-a-solution (SaaS) ERP leader in the market that offers various enterprise resource planning (ERP) offerings for small and medium-sized businesses (SMEs).</p><p>Its direct competitors are SAP Business One, Sage Intacct, Oracle NetSuite, and Odoo ERP.</p><p>Many businesses across a wide range of industries prefer using Dynamics 365 Business Central because of its powerful features and capabilities.</p><p>Let\'s know a bit about this all-in-one-cloud ERP solution from Microsoft.</p><h2>What is Dynamics 365 Business Central?</h2><p>If you want the power of <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-nav/\">Dynamics NAV</a> to a cloud solution, Dynamics 365 Business Central is the answer you were waiting for.</p><p>Business Central was first announced as Dynamics 365 \'Tenerife\' back in 2017, and then got released as Dynamics 365 Business Central in Oct. 2018. Since then, the platform is continually being updated with new capabilities and compliance with new regulations such as GDPR and MTD (also popular as Making Tax Digital by the Govt. of the United Kingdom).</p><h2>What is Update 21.4 for Dynamics 365 Business Central?</h2><p>Microsoft releases timely updates for Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central products and is categorized as - <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365-release-plan/2022wave2/smb/dynamics365-business-central/planned-features\" target=\"_blank\">new and planned updates</a>.</p><p>Hence, walking in these footsteps, the 2023 update for Business Central has something for you, which includes hotfixes, feature changes, localization updates, a release plan for scheduled updates, and some \"Good to know information\" that you can utilize to take full advantage of your customized version of Business Central.</p><p>Let\'s uncover each hotfix one by one and bit by bit.</p><p><b>Hotfixes:</b> These are the small codes that are used to quickly correct bugs or faults in Business Central.</p><p>Applying <a href=\"https://mackeeper.com/blog/a-critical-software-update-is-required-for-your-mac/\" target=\"_blank\">critical software updates</a> ensures your Business Central system operates securely and without interruption.</p><p>Thus, to install the hotfix, you must update your customer license to access new objects released (or present in the previous update).</p><p>For the lists of updates, see: <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://support.microsoft.com/topic/8efa5bbb-3cd5-4445-ba3a-0752694bf46f\" target=\"_blank\">Related Updates for Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central 2022 Release Wave 2</a>.</p><p>Note: Because of third-party products integrated with your system, it is not recommended to move forward in installing hotfixes or any updates without a trusted <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a> like Dynamics Square. Microsoft Partners will help you identify whether your environment is compatible with the released updates or hotfixes. <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Contact me now</a>!</p><h2>Resolution to your Problems with this 21.4 Update for Business Central</h2><p>The Following are the problems that Microsoft\'s development team has fixed:</p><h3>1. Platform Hotfixes</h3><h3><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768133301191659.Platform Hotfixes.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">2. Application Hotfixes</h3><h3><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768133310631180.Application Hotfixes.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">3. Local Application Hotfixes</h3><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768133327065813.Local Application Hotfixes.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">Note: Above are the screenshots of the full detailed description of update 21.4 for Dynamics 365 Business Central. To read or learn more, follow this link: <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/topic/update-21-4-for-microsoft-dynamics-365-business-central-on-premises-2022-release-wave-2-application-build-21-4-52785-platform-build-21-0-52534-52761-ec46967d-2718-470b-9033-78417dbc1441\" target=\"_blank\">Latest updates to Dynamics 365 Business Central.</a></p><h2>How to get Started with the release wave 2 files for Dynamics 365 Business Central update 21.4?</h2><p>To manually download files and begin installations, go to <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/download/details.aspx?id=104945\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Download Center</a>, and follow the instructions.</p><h3><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768133349938555.Dynamics 365 Business Central update 21.4 2022 release wave 2.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">Which hotfixes should you download?</h3><p>Update 21.4 consists of multiple hotfix packages. So, select your hotfix package based on your country, and the 2022 database of your Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central.</p><h2><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768133360798762.Hotfix Package.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">How to install the on-premises 2022 Release Wave 2 update for Business Central?</h2><p>Prerequisites to begin with this update:</p><p>First, you must install D365 Business Central 2022 Release Wave 2 on your system. Then, begin applying the above-mentioned hotfix from update 21.4.&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768133380032780.install D365 Business Central 2022 Release Wave 2.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">See: <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/upgrade/upgrading-cumulative-update-v21\" target=\"_blank\">A simplified way to install Business Central 2022 Release Wave 2 update from Microsoft</a>.</p><p>And if you want more help, do not hesitate to call, or email us.</p><p>We, at Dynamics Square are always eager to help you out with any problem you may have about the upgrade to your Business Central ERP or any <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a> product, such as Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management, Dynamics 365 Finance, or D365 Sales, and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">Microsoft Power BI</a> (Business Intelligence software).</p><p>You can also send your requirements to us if your looking for a trusted Microsoft Partner to <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-nav-to-business-central/\">upgrade your Dynamics NAV to Business Central</a>. We have a suitable and affordable plan for you.</p><p>Get in touch today!</p><h2>What is the Good to know information about the 21.4 update for Business Central?</h2><p>To ensure that you keep your delegated admin access to your customers, make sure to regularly check our blog section and act before March 1, 2023.</p><p>Earlier this year, Microsoft Partner Center introduced Granular Delegated Administration Privileges (GDAP) as a replacement for Delegated Administration Privileges (DAP), offering more fine-grained access rights and time-bound partner-customer relationships.</p><p>“<b>The deadline to migrate your current DAP relationships to GDAP has been extended to March 1, 2023.</b>”</p><p>Remember, if you do not act by this date, you will lose access to your customers\' Business Central environments.</p><p>Thus, keep following us, and the Partner Center announcement page from Microsoft which is available at this link: <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/partner-center/announcements/2022-october#17\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Partner Center Announcements</a></p><p>Read more: <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-business-central-implementation/\" target=\"_blank\">Business Central Implementation</a></p>', 'New Update 21.4 to Dynamics 365 Business Central (Online)', 'dynamics 365 business central', 'Upgrade your Dynamics 365 Business Central Online with Update 21.4 in 2023. Experience improved performance and enhanced features for your business.', 'business central,dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics business central,business central partner,business central implementation,business central support,microsoft dynamics business support', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768135980738773.jpg', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '06:27:07pm', '2023-06-08', '6 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-05-19 18:27:07');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(144, 'Comparing Working in Dynamics GP vs. Dynamics 365 Business Central (Online)', 'comparing-dynamics-gp-vs-business-central', 'Comparison', 'comparison', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768137329010536.jpg', 'Both Dynamics 365 GP (Great Plains) and Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central offer a diverse range of business capabilities. Choosing between them depends on factors like organization size, budget, functionality needs, and future growth plans.', '<p>Both <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-gp/\">Microsoft Dynamics GP </a>(Great Plains)&nbsp;and Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central offer a diverse range of business capabilities. Choosing between them depends on factors like organization size, budget, functionality needs, and future growth plans.\r\n</p><p>Though both ERP solutions are equipped with tools tailored to your specific business requirements, including high-end features, custom configurations, and scalability, they each have their pros and cons. However, it\'s worth noting that Business Central has fewer cons than Dynamics GP.\r\n</p><p>Additionally, Microsoft has discontinued selling Dynamics GP licenses, so existing GP users can only obtain support services directly from Microsoft Gold Partners like Dynamics Square.\r\n</p><p>With <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central</a>, the potential to grow your business is significant, and it is accessible to everyone. This cloud-based ERP solution is less complicated to deploy/implement and costs much less than on-premises ERP software.\r\n</p><p>Now that you have a general idea of the differences between these business management solutions, let\'s explore them in more detail.\r\n</p><h2>Dynamics 365 Business Central vs. Dynamics GP: Basics\r\n</h2><p>Dynamics 365 GP forms an ERP solution and accounting, sales, and services modules. When we talk about Dynamics 365 Business Central, this all-in-one ERP solution also has various business management modules rather than basic capabilities.\r\n</p><p>So, from the first principles’ POV, let\'s explore both ERP solutions:\r\n</p><h2>What is Microsoft Dynamics GP?\r\n</h2><p>Microsoft Dynamics GP was specifically designed to support not only your ERP needs but also to aid in accounting and other essential business activities.\r\n</p><p>It is a great solution&nbsp;for businesses that seek reliable solutions to automate:\r\n</p><ul><li>Data\r\n</li><li>Streamline&nbsp;workflows\r\n</li><li>Optimize the use of resources\r\n</li><li>Manage the financial flow efficiently and effectively, and related tasks.\r\n</li></ul><p>Dynamics GP includes&nbsp;both sales and services modules wrapped with built-in business intelligence to make decision-making better and more productive across your organization.\r\n</p><p>Note: To ensure the best database maintenance and availability, certain guidelines must be followed when <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics-gp/installation/microsoft-sql-server-configuration\" target=\"_blank\">configuring Microsoft SQL Server disk support for Dynamics GP</a>, as it relies on SQL Server for these tasks.</p><h2>What is Microsoft Dynamics Business Central?\r\n</h2><p>Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central as compared to Dynamics GP is developed as a powerful business management solution with endless features, vast configuration capability, and deployment flexibility (whether on-premises, hybrid, or on-cloud).\r\n</p><p>Business Central allows enterprises or companies with up to&nbsp;300 named users to manage end-to-end business practices including:\r\n</p><ul><li>Customer relationships (using CRM integration like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a>)\r\n</li><li>Finance &amp; Supply Chain (with SCM module)\r\n</li><li>Human resourcing (using HRM plug-ins)\r\n</li><li>Warehousing (with WMS add-ons)\r\n</li><li>Sales\r\n</li><li>Planning &amp; budgeting\r\n</li><li>Regulatory &amp; global compliance and more.\r\n</li></ul><p><b>Know More Here:</b>  <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-business-central-features/\">Features of Dynamics 365 Business Central</a>\r\n</p><h2>Benefits of Rolling out Dynamics GP vs Business Central\r\n</h2><p>Dynamics GP has long been a popular enterprise resource planning solution, offering extensive functionality and customizable options. However, it is now only available to existing users, limiting access for newcomers.\r\n</p><p>As a business management software application designed for mid-sized businesses across various industries, Dynamics GP remains a wise choice. Its numerous add-ons, available through Microsoft AppSource, enable businesses to expand their capabilities and enhance profitability.\r\n</p><p>Dynamics GP facilitates the growth of your business practices while providing seamless management capabilities.\r\n</p><p><b>Businesses can effectively manage and drive practices, such as:\r\n</b></p><ul><li>Finance &amp; procurement\r\n</li><li>Field service\r\n</li><li>Inventory\r\n</li><li>Supply Chain\r\n</li><li>Business intelligence (BI) &amp; reporting\r\n</li><li>Project automation, and more.\r\n</li></ul><p>GP’s excellent BI&nbsp;capabilities assist&nbsp;enterprises to promptly make informed decision-making better.\r\n</p><p>Business owners or administrators can streamline core business practices, simplify process flows, enable efficient remote operations, and maintain business continuity with Dynamics GP.\r\n</p><p>For businesses handling sensitive data, Dynamics GP can be an effective solution, as it can be deployed on-premises and securely store data using SQL Server.\r\n</p><h2>Advantages of Deploying Dynamics 365&nbsp;Business Central vs Dynamics GP\r\n</h2><p>Business Central is designed with small to mid-sized enterprises (SMEs) in mind, offering a quick return on investment (ROI), typically achieved within 12 months following implementation.\r\n</p><p>As a business management application, it helps SMEs streamline processes, automate data, and enhance efficiency through real-time decision-making capabilities that support overall operational performance.\r\n</p><p>Dynamics 365 Business Central may be the better choice for businesses seeking a solution to improve productivity and increase profitability.\r\n</p><p>Managing your end-to-end operational flow becomes as effortless as spreading butter on bread.\r\n</p><p>With AI-powered Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central’s latest version - 21.4, you can seamlessly manage:&nbsp;\r\n</p><ul><li>Finance &amp; supply chain\r\n</li><li>Manufacturing &amp; distribution\r\n</li><li>Resourcing &amp; project automation\r\n</li><li>Regulatory &amp; global compliance, and more.\r\n</li></ul><p>Business Central\'s advanced business intelligence capabilities empower enterprises with real-time decision-making efficiency and enhanced control over their operational processes.\r\n</p><p>Equipped with essential functionalities, Business Central\'s core version supports the growth of organizations. As it provides continuous upgrades and feature releases, you can keep your ERP system up-to-date and accessible, enabling remote work—a sought-after feature for many employees.\r\n</p><p>Furthermore, implementing Business Central is simple and straightforward. By partnering with Dynamics Square, you can deploy a tailored business-centric model (on-premises, cloud-based, or hybrid) that best suits your organization\'s needs.\r\n</p><h2>Pricing and Licensing: Dynamics GP vs Dynamics 365 Business Central\r\n</h2><p>Before committing to any ERP solution, budget considerations are always a concern, as each enterprise has unique financial plans and constraints. Let\'s explore how Dynamics GP and Business Central can fit into your budget.\r\n</p><p>Dynamics GP is an on-premises solution that requires additional upfront costs for hardware installation and related infrastructure, along with a subscription plan. However, it is no longer available for new users, as Microsoft has stopped selling new GP licenses.\r\n</p><p>If you\'re still utilizing Dynamics GP, you can seek trusted, hassle-free support from a reliable Microsoft Gold Partner, like Dynamics Square.\r\n</p><p>On the other hand, D365 Business Central runs on the cloud and includes Azure facilitation, which Dynamics GP lacks. This feature makes Business Central one of the most secure and reliable business management applications in today\'s digital landscape.\r\n</p><p>With its cloud-based deployment, you can access your Business Central account from anywhere, at any time, and on any portable device, such as a mobile phone, tablet, or laptop.\r\n</p><p>As a new Business Central user, you can choose from flexible licensing plans tailored to your specific business needs and requirements.\r\n</p><h2>Latest Licensing and Pricing for Business Central\r\n</h2><p>Initially, it starts at $80 per user/month and Microsoft named this license as Business Central Essential Plan.\r\n</p><p><b>The Essential plan includes:\r\n</b></p><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-ai/\">Artificial Intelligence (AI)</a>\r\n</li><li>Financial Management\r\n</li><li>Advanced Financial Management\r\n</li><li>AI-enabled Forecasting\r\n</li><li>Project Management\r\n</li><li>Supply Chain Management (SCM)\r\n</li><li>Warehouse Management &amp; Inventory Management\r\n</li><li>Customer Relationship Management (CRM) - Advanced Capabilities of Dynamics CRM\r\n</li><li>Human Resources Management\r\n</li><li>E-Services\r\n</li><li>Analysis Reports\r\n</li><li>Embedded Power BI\r\n</li><li>Workflow\r\n</li><li>Word Reporting/Document Reporting\r\n</li><li>Reason Codes\r\n</li><li>User Management and User Tasks\r\n</li><li>Access to an Unlimited number of Companies, and more.\r\n</li></ul><p>Here are other Business Central plans for you to consider if you want more advanced business management:\r\n</p><p><b>Business Central Premium Plan:</b> $110 per user/month\r\n</p><p><b>Includes:</b> All Essentials license capabilities plus Service Order Management and Manufacturing.\r\n</p><p><b>Additional Capabilities of Business Central Premium License:\r\n</b></p><ul><li>Planning and Dispatching\r\n</li><li>Service Item Management\r\n</li><li>Service Contract Management\r\n</li><li>Service Order Management\r\n</li><li>Agile Manufacturing\r\n</li><li>Finite loading\r\n</li><li>Sales and Inventory Forecasting\r\n</li><li>Production Bill of Materials\r\n</li><li>Version Management\r\n</li><li>Production Orders\r\n</li><li>Basic Capacity Planning\r\n</li><li>Basic Supply Planning\r\n</li><li>Machine Centers\r\n</li></ul><p><b>Note:</b> There’s also a basic plan for Business Central, known as Team Member, which starts at $8 per user/month. This plan is already included in the Essentials and Premium plans with unrestricted access. <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Get in touch with our Dynamics 365 experts</a> to explore its features and benefits.\r\n</p><p>Hence, this will be your only licensing cost. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>However, if you want a customized or specially configured solution, or any sort of integration for add-ons like an integrated <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/mobile-wms-dynamics-365-business-central/\">WMS solution from Insight Works</a>, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/sana-ecommerce-add-ons-business-central/\">Sana Commerce</a> for eCommerce, or <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/payroll-for-business-central-nav/\">NaviPayroll</a> to simplify your HR Payroll process to maximize your functional and financial capability, your pricing will be revised accordingly.\r\n</p><h2>Functional Capability: Dynamics GP vs Dynamics 365 Business Central\r\n</h2><p>In terms of functional capabilities, Business Central effortlessly outperforms Dynamics GP, as it offers not only the same features as Dynamics GP, but also additional ones.\r\n</p><p>With its essential plan, you gain access to exclusive modules such as Dynamics 365 Finance, inventory, project management, order management, and more.\r\n</p><p>If the Team Member plan doesn\'t suit your needs or if you want to add more modules like service management, sales order management, manufacturing, or others, you can opt for the premium plan.\r\n</p><p>Furthermore, if you start with the essential plan, you can easily upgrade to a more advanced version, such as the premium or higher plans (including the Team Member plan), whenever you wish.\r\n</p><h2>Why Business Central Could Be the Best ERP Choice for Your Business\r\n</h2><p>Choosing Microsoft Dynamics Business Central over Dynamics GP can be a wise decision due to several key factors that can propel your business to new heights:\r\n</p><ul><li><b>Cloud-based:</b> Business Central, or BC for short, is a cloud-based solution, meaning it is accessible from anywhere, at any time, and on any device with an internet connection. In contrast, Dynamics GP is an on-premises solution that requires installation and maintenance on a physical server.\r\n</li><li><b>Subscription-based or Pay-as-you-Go Model:</b> Dynamics 365 Business Central offers a Pay-as-you-Go service, allowing you to pay monthly for only what you use. This approach simplifies budgeting and expense planning for businesses. Dynamics GP, however, demands a large upfront investment in licensing and implementation.\r\n</li><li><b>Integration with other Microsoft products:</b> Business Central integrates seamlessly with other Microsoft products, such as Office 365, Power BI, and PowerApps from the Power Platform suite. This integration enables a cohesive experience across various applications and tools. In comparison, Dynamics GP may necessitate more customizations for integration with other Microsoft products.\r\n</li><li><b>Modern User Interface:</b> D365 Business Central features a modern, intuitive user interface (UI) that enhances user adoption and productivity. Dynamics GP\'s traditional interface might require more training and may not be as user-friendly for today\'s users.\r\n</li><li><b>Advanced features:</b> D365 BC includes advanced features like machine learning and artificial intelligence, helping businesses make data-driven decisions and automate processes. Dynamics GP may not offer the same level of advanced features.\r\n</li></ul><p>Ultimately, choosing between Business Central and Dynamics GP depends on your business\'s specific needs. Carefully evaluate your requirements and compare the features, functionality, and cost of both solutions before making a decision. Alternatively, let our experts at Dynamics Square guide you in making the best choice for your business.</p><p>Read more: <a href=\"/dynamics-gp-to-business-central-migration/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics GP to Business Central Migration</a></p><p>\r\n</p><h2>Final Words</h2><p>Now that you know how different Dynamics 365 Business Central and Dynamics GP are, you can make a smarter decision.\r\n</p><p>If you need expert advice, contact our&nbsp;Dynamics 365 consultants that have years of industry expertise in deploying <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Dynamics 365 products</a>.\r\n</p><p>Experts at Dynamics Square&nbsp;are ready to reveal and suggest to you the best solution for your business. Send us your requirements so that we can review your current ERP system, and let you know whether you need an upgrade.</p><p>Read more: <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-business-central-implementation/\" target=\"_blank\">Business Central Implementation</a></p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Comparing Dynamics GP vs Dynamics 365 Business Central', 'dynamics gp', 'Compare the benefits and differences of Dynamics 365 Business Central vs Dynamics GP. Find the best fit for your business needs and streamline operations.', 'dynamics gp,microsoft dynamics gp,great plains,business central,dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics business central,business central implementation,business central support', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768137329011587.jpg', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', '.', '[]', '06:14:59pm', '2023-06-08', '11 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-11-06 01:14:59'),
(145, 'Microsoft Dynamics 365 Copilot: A Next-Generation AI for Every Business Size', 'microsoft-introduces-dynamics-365-copilot', 'Microsoft Dynamics 365', 'microsoft-dynamics-365', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768138959564226.png', 'Microsoft brings an AI-powered Copilot - Microsoft Dynamics 365 Copilot to its business app suite - Microsoft Dynamics 365 and calls it the \"next generation\" of AI products for its business apps portfolio.', '<p>Microsoft brings an AI-powered Copilot - Microsoft Dynamics 365 Copilot to its business app suite - <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a> and calls it the \"<b>next generation</b>\" of AI products for its business apps portfolio.\r\n</p><p>On March 6, 2023, Charles Lamanna, CVP of business apps and platform at Microsoft <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://cloudblogs.microsoft.com/dynamics365/bdm/2023/03/06/introducing-microsoft-dynamics-365-copilot-bringing-next-generation-ai-to-every-line-of-business/?_gl=1*9kuv96*_ga*MTQxMTU0ODExNi4xNjc1ODQ4NTYw*_ga_NNH8F3SCG6*MTY3ODY5NTM1MS4zLjEuMTY3ODY5NTM4My4yOC4wLjA.\" target=\"_blank\">announced the launch of Dynamics 365 Copilot</a>, an AI-powered solution that promises to streamline and automate a variety of business processes, including financial management, supply chain operations, customer service, and sales.\r\n</p><p>In this blog, you will explore the key features and discover the benefits Dynamics 365 Copilot has for you, as well as its impact on the business world.\r\n</p><h2>Is there even a need for Business Automation?\r\n</h2><p>The straight answer is, Yes!\r\n</p><p>Let me help you think this way - Are you able to manage your business through your pocket-sized device/smart devices like mobile phones or tablets by individually operating on each app meant for every business operation?\r\n</p><p>Probably NOT. And even if you\'re doing it, be ready for accelerated aging and get dementia for FREE. The same goes for everyone at your workplace. And no human wants that to happen. Period!\r\n</p><p>Moreover, in today\'s fast-paced business environment, it is easy to get into facing increased pressure to improve efficiency, reduce costs, and enhance customer experience (CX).\r\n</p><p>To achieve business management efficiency, organizations seek cost-effective business automation solutions. These low-cost business automation solutions leverage the latest advances in artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) like <a href=\"https://imagine.art/blogs/imagine-ai-art-generator-all-that-you-need-to-know-before-you-start\" target=\"_blank\">AI art generators</a> and Microsoft Dynamics 365.</p><p>Furthermore, for any business (whether related to manufacturing or an enterprise for the distribution of manufactured products), enterprise resource planning (ERP) and customer relationship management (CRM) systems are the key assets for the business-continuity.\r\n</p><p>CRM and ERP systems (<a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics ERP</a>) are designed to help companies like yours to manage key aspects of your operations (like accounting, inventory, order processing, and customer service) at scale.\r\n</p><p>However, legacy ERP and CRM systems like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-nav/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics NAV</a>, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-ax/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics AX</a>, or <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\">Dynamics CRM</a> are often complex and inconvenient to operate. These systems require significant resources for their implementation and maintenance.\r\n</p><p>Such outgrown systems are limited in their ability to adapt to changing business needs and customer preferences.\r\n</p><p>As a result, many small to medium-sized businesses (SMBs) have struggled to fully realize the benefits of these systems.\r\n</p><p>But the wait and the complexities are now seeming to be over because of Microsoft\'s latest offering in the field of business automation - \"Dynamics 365 Copilot, designed to help organizations automate routine tasks, identify patterns and insights, and drive better decision-making across the business.\"\r\n</p><p>Let’s see its features.\r\n</p><h2>What are the Key Features of Microsoft Dynamics 365 Copilot?\r\n</h2><p>Are you curious to know what exactly Dynamics 365 Copilot does? And how does it work?\r\n</p><p>Here I have simplified the complex info from Microsoft\'s blog post in easy-to-understand key points.\r\n</p><p>Key Features of this Innovative Solution:\r\n</p><h3>1. Natural Language Processing (NLP)\r\n</h3><p>One of the fascinating features of Dynamics 365 Copilot is its ability to understand and respond to natural language queries. Meaning, you or its users at your premises can easily interact with the system using the language they feel comfortable speaking every day.\r\n</p><p>This helps your people at work avoid any need to learn complex commands or programming.\r\n</p><p>For example - you could ask Copilot to \"<b>create a new invoice for customer X</b>\" and the system would automatically create the appropriate document based on relevant data fetched in the chosen ERP system using Copilot for <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central</a>.\r\n</p><p>See how Copilot is making waves for Business Central users:\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align: center; \"><iframe frameborder=\"0\" src=\"//www.youtube.com/embed/RVXJaVUxGD4\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" class=\"note-video-clip\"></iframe><br></p><h3>2. Predictive Analytics</h3><p>Another impressive feature of Dynamics 365 Copilot is its advanced analytics capabilities. The use of machine learning algorithms to analyze vast amounts of data from multiple sources, including transactional data, customer feedback, and social media makes this product stand out.\r\n</p><p>Using this, Copilot can provide insights and recommendations to help you make your decision-making better and improve business outcomes.\r\n</p><p>For instance, Copilot could identify customer complaints\' trends about a particular product, prompting you to investigate and resolve the issue as it occurs.\r\n</p><p>Explore and discover how Dynamics 365 Copilot in Dynamics 365 Customer Insights is helping businesses of all sizes create impact by enhancing customer experiences: \r\n</p><p style=\"text-align: center; \"><iframe frameborder=\"0\" src=\"//www.youtube.com/embed/_a_hCCkk0L8\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" class=\"note-video-clip\"></iframe><br></p><h3>3. Customizable Workflows\r\n</h3><p>Finally, Dynamics 365 Copilot allows users to create and customize workflows that reflect their specific business processes and needs. This means that companies can tailor their CRM/ERP systems to their unique requirements, rather than being forced to conform to a one-size-fits-all solution.\r\n</p><p>For example, a manufacturing company could create a workflow that automates the process of scheduling production runs based on demand forecasts and inventory levels. This would help to minimize waste and optimize production efficiency.\r\n</p><p>Watch this short video to understand better how Copilot for Dynamics 365 can help you enhance your operations and user experience:\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align: center; \"><iframe frameborder=\"0\" src=\"//www.youtube.com/embed/GMwtXDx-JUI\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" class=\"note-video-clip\"></iframe><br></p><h2>What are the Benefits of Dynamics 365 Copilot for Your Business?\r\n</h2><p>Let\'s understand the potential benefits of Dynamics 365 Copilot for your businesses.\r\n</p><p>Here are the key advantages that you can leverage to advance the growth of your organization:\r\n</p><h3>1. Increased Efficiency\r\n</h3><p>By automating routine tasks and providing insights, you can help make decision-making better. Dynamics 365 Copilot can help you do that with little to no effort. This can free up your workforce\'s valuable time, and optimize resources that can be redirected to more strategic activities. And increase efficiency and productivity across the organization.\r\n</p><h3>2. Improved Customer Experience (CX)\r\n</h3><p>Dynamics 365 Copilot can analyze customer feedback and identify trends to help you address issues proactively and improve your overall customer service. This can lead to higher customer satisfaction, increased brand loyalty, and increased revenue and profitability.\r\n</p><p>Learn more about this amazing AI-powered integration here: \r\n</p><p style=\"text-align: center; \"><iframe frameborder=\"0\" src=\"//www.youtube.com/embed/Uv7hK6o4mXo\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" class=\"note-video-clip\"></iframe><br></p><p>Microsoft is also simplifying virtual agent creation for customer service departments using <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://aka.ms/GPT-PP\" target=\"_blank\">Power Virtual Agents with conversation boosters</a>. This will help you for fast access to answers from company websites and internal knowledge bases through <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/products/cognitive-services/openai-service\" target=\"_blank\">Azure OpenAI Service</a> and <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.bing.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Bing</a>. Your departments can now build <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-virtual-agents/\">virtual agents</a> within minutes.\r\n</p><h3>3. Enhanced Data Insights\r\n</h3><p>With Copilot\'s advanced analytics capabilities, Dynamics 365 Copilot can help companies like yours gain deeper insights into daily business operations and what customers are looking for. This can provide \"valuable intelligence\" that can be used to identify new opportunities, optimize processes, and keep you in the know.\r\n</p><h3>4. Greater Flexibility\r\n</h3><p>Microsoft Dynamics 365 Copilot\'s customizable workflows and its functionality to get integrated with different Microsoft products help you with greater flexibility and agility in responding to evolving business requirements. This can help organizations future-proof their operations and ensure they enjoy long-term success.\r\n</p><h2>Can Copilot be Integrated with Other Microsoft Products?\r\n</h2><p>Yes! Microsoft considered your consideration and designed Dynamics 365 Copilot to work with other Microsoft products, including Office 365, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">Power BI</a>, and Azure.\r\n</p><p>With this, you have access to a wide range of ERP and CRM tools and resources within a single, unified platform.\r\n</p><p>For instance, your sales rep could use Copilot to generate a sales quote, which would automatically be saved to the sales rep\'s SharePoint account and updated in real-time with any changes made by the customer.\r\n</p><p>This level of integration can help you counter duplicate data entry and lower the risk of errors (even those errors that might appear in the future).\r\n</p><h2>What is the Potential Impact of Dynamics 365 Copilot on the Business World?\r\n</h2><p>Dynamics 365 Copilot is a significant step forward in business automation, offering a powerful and flexible solution that uses trending AI and machine learning technologies.\r\n</p><p>Its potential impact on the business world is significant, with the ability to transform the way companies manage their operations and interact with customers.\r\n</p><p>As more companies adopt these types of solutions, you can see a shift in the ways business is conducted, with greater emphasis on data-driven decision-making, customer-centricity, and agility.\r\n</p><p>This could lead to a more dynamic and responsive business environment, as companies can adapt more quickly to changing market conditions and customer preferences.\r\n</p><h3>Is it worth investing your time, energy, and money to upgrade your existing CRM/ERP for Copilot?\r\n</h3><p>Dynamics 365 Copilot is an exciting development in business automation, offering a powerful and flexible solution that uses the latest AI, AI-powered language model like ChatGPT, and machine learning technologies.\r\n</p><p>With Copilot’s natural language processing, predictive analytics, integration with other Microsoft products, and customizable workflows, it has the potential to pave the way for companies to better manage their operations and make interaction with customers easy.\r\n</p><p>While Copilot may take some time for businesses to fully realize its benefits, the potential impact on the business world is significant.\r\n</p><p>As companies look to increase efficiency, improve customer satisfaction, and gain deeper insights into their operations, solutions like Dynamics 365 Copilot are likely to play an increasingly vital role in driving business success in the years ahead.\r\n</p><p>Connect with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a> solution reps at Dynamics Square to understand how you can utilize the power of Copilot like many organizations are taking advantage of OpenAI’s ChatGPT.</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Microsoft Dynamics 365 Copilot: AI for Every Business Size', 'dynamics 365 copilot', 'Microsoft Dynamics 365 Copilot is an AI-powered assistant that helps businesses of all sizes improve productivity and make smarter decisions.', NULL, 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768138959565909.png', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '03:55:32pm', '2023-06-08', '10 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 15:55:32'),
(146, '5 Easy Steps to Migrate from Dynamics GP to Business Central', 'steps-to-migrate-gp-to-business-central', 'Comparison', 'comparison', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768141421566019.png', 'If you\'re looking to migrate from Dynamics GP to Dynamics 365 Business Central, this blog post is for you. Learn about the crucial steps, reasons, and best practices for Dynamics GP to Business Central Migration.', '<p>\"If you\'re looking to migrate from Dynamics GP to Business Central, this blog post is for you. Learn about the crucial steps, reasons, and best practices for <a href=\"/dynamics-gp-to-business-central-migration/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics GP to Business Central Migration</a>.”\r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-gp/\">Microsoft Dynamics GP</a> helps businesses keep track of money and other important stuff. Sometimes, businesses want to switch to a cloud-based program called Business Central – an all-in-one ERP solution for all your business needs.\r\n</p><p>But how to make sure that all business data/old information gets moved over to the new program?\r\n</p><p>First, let me elaborate, moving all that information is called \"<b>migrating.</b>\"\r\n</p><p>Second, this blog gets you to learn how you can migrate your crucial data from Dynamics GP to Dynamics 365 Business Central.\r\n</p><p>Third, the article also introduces you to a step-by-step GP to Business Central migration process, so you don\'t lose any information important to you.\r\n</p><p>Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;Let’s begin with something about Dynamics GP.\r\n</p><p>The initial version 1.0 of Dynamics GP was released back in Feb. 1993 by <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Plains_Software\" target=\"_blank\">Great Plains Software</a>.\r\n</p><p>Since then, Dynamics GP has been a backbone software application for many organizations across different industries to fulfill their enterprise resource planning (ERP) needs for many years.\r\n</p><p>But there\'s a new smart kid around the corner making waves.\r\n</p><p>It\'s <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> – a popular cloud-based ERP software used by businesses in various industries to manage their daily operations, including Business Intelligence (BI), financials, warehouses, and inventory.\r\n</p><p>Business Central\'s popularity can be attributed to the surge in cloud technology adoption.\r\n</p><p>“There is no question that providing consumers with secure and reliable financial services means greater demand for cloud-based technologies.”\r\n</p><p>Deputy Secretary of the United States Treasury, Wally Adeyemo\r\n</p><p>Compared to Dynamics GP, Business Central offers more flexibility, scalability, and integration with other Microsoft products like Office 365, Outlook, and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">Power BI</a>.\r\n</p><p>Migrating from Dynamics GP to Business Central involves data migration, customization, and training and it can be a decisive move for a more sustainable future.\r\n</p><p>Let\'s see what the potential reasons can be to migrate from Dynamics GP to Business Central.</p><p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" src=\"//www.youtube.com/embed/_6Q0eIBYSA4\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" class=\"note-video-clip\"></iframe><br></p><p>\r\n</p><h2>What can be the reasons to Migrate from Dynamics GP to Dynamics 365 Business Central?\r\n</h2><p>Here are some crucial reasons to consider when migrating your data from legacy&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\">ERP systems</a> like Dynamics GP to Business Central:\r\n</p><ul><li><b>Cloud-Based Solution -</b> Helps keep the business up to date with features and functionalities&nbsp;that meet users\' expectations.\r\n</li><li><b>Personalized User Interface -</b> Allows users to move around with ease and provides a customizable user experience with easy-to-use and role-based functionalities.\r\n</li><li><b>Online Data Processing -</b> It helps you avoid hung batches or interrupted posting used for simultaneous transactions and promotes automatic system integrations.\r\n</li><li><b>Office 365 Integration -</b> It can integrate with a wide range of office 365 products such as an Outlook integration which makes recipient searches, and more.\r\n</li><li><b>Flexibility -</b> Users can access the application from any device (laptop, tablet, or mobile), and across several operating systems such as Windows, Apple, and Android.\r\n</li></ul><h2>What are the Benefits of moving to Business Central?\r\n</h2><p>Upgrading your business\'s legacy system from Dynamics GP to Dynamics 365-based ERP platforms like Business Central offers a host of benefits that can have a positive impact on your operations.\r\n</p><p>From automatic upgrades and streamlined processes to integrated Microsoft tools and improved data analysis, Dynamics 365 Business Central is a comprehensive business management solution that can transform the way you do business.\r\n</p><h3>Benefits of Upgrading GP to Dynamics 365:\r\n</h3><ul><li>Availability of automatic upgrades for improved functionality and security.\r\n</li><li>Anytime, anywhere access for enhanced productivity and flexibility.\r\n</li><li>Empowering you to operationalize valuable data and optimize processes.\r\n</li><li>Helping you to unify accounting and finance with the rest of the business for more streamlined operations.\r\n</li><li>Assists you in avoiding challenges and risks associated with fragmented ERP solutions.\r\n</li><li>Helps your teams eliminate costs associated with managing third-party solutions.\r\n</li><li>Easily gets integrated with your familiar Microsoft tools like Excel, Teams, Outlook, and eCommerce plus warehouse management solutions like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/sana-ecommerce-add-ons-business-central/\">Sana Commerce</a> and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/mobile-wms-dynamics-365-business-central/\">Insight Works WMS</a> add-on, respectively.\r\n</li><li>Syncs data among all connected business management modules and apps for seamless workflows.\r\n</li><li>Enables you to perform daily tasks in one place, minimizing errors and non-compliance risks.\r\n</li><li>Frees up your team’s time for strategic tasks like analyzing data in context.\r\n</li><li>Includes Power BI for building customizable dashboards and creating interactive visual reports.\r\n</li><li>Improves sales, cash flow, and inventory forecasting with baked-in powerful BI.\r\n</li><li>Provides end-to-end visibility into company performance for better decision-making.\r\n</li></ul><p>Built on the low-code <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-platform/\">Power Platform</a>, Business Central makes it easy for non-technical users to create customized solutions and do more with less.\r\n</p><p>Now, before I move onto explaining the GP to Business Central Migration process, let’s know a bit how different these two ERP systems are.\r\n</p><h2>Dynamics GP vs Dynamics 365 Business Central\r\n</h2><p>Both GP and Business Central are ERP solutions developed by Microsoft, but differ in architecture, licensing, and functionality.\r\n</p><p>GP is an on-premises ERP system installed on local servers (that you purchase), while BC is cloud-based (that Microsoft offers and maintains all your hurdles and updates) and can be accessed via a web browser.\r\n</p><p>GP, on the other hand, requires a one-time payment for a perpetual license, whereas BC is licensed on a subscription basis (Pay-as-you-GO model).\r\n</p><p>Dynamics 365 Business Central offers more advanced features and benefits from being a newer cloud-based ERP solution, with enhanced automation, built-in AI and language models like ChatGPT, and better integration with other Microsoft products like Power BI and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-apps/\">PowerApps</a>.\r\n</p><p>Below is the key differences table for your reference:</p><h2><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768139202780815.Key-Differences-between-dynamics-gp-to-Business-Central.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">What does Dynamics GP to Dynamics 365 Migration involve?</h2><p>Migrating your business processes from GP to the cloud involves unifying all business tools, data, and processes into a single ERP platform, not just moving a few data sources from GP.\r\n</p><p>This includes merging GP data into a cloud-based system your team is already using or performing multiple migrations simultaneously.\r\n</p><p>And before beginning the migration, you must clarify the game plan.\r\n</p><p><b>In any case, let\'s look at the steps you need to take to get ready:\r\n</b></p><h3>Step 1: Carryout an Audit\r\n</h3><p>In case you\'re beginning with a fragmented system, expect to spend additional time and resources on the audit process. The objective is to assess the system holistically and create a map of all interconnected components of your current ERP system.\r\n</p><h3>Step 2: Analyze Your Operations\r\n</h3><p>Create a map and analyze your business processes, data flows, and applications. Determine the tools and processes that each team uses and identify what\'s effective and what\'s not!\r\n</p><h3>Step 3: Find out Business Requirements\r\n</h3><p>Collaborate with your different teams to comprehend their work processes, challenges, and desired improvements by migrating your business data to the Business Central.\r\n</p><h3>Step 4: Make Room for Improvement Opportunities\r\n</h3><p>Think about how new capabilities can address issues or seize potential opportunities. How can integrating financial data with other business areas (and vice versa) benefit your organization?\r\n</p><h3>Step 5: Assess External Solutions and Partners\r\n</h3><p>Look for a certified <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Partner</a> like Dynamics Square that is experienced in GP migrations and has a knowledgeable team. They can also assist in identifying the right cloud solutions and external applications or add-ons that increase the value of your D365 investment.\r\n</p><h2>Wizards to Migrate Data from Dynamics GP to Business Central\r\n</h2><p>To migrate to Business Central, GP users can use <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/administration/migrate-data\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft\'s inbuilt migration tools</a> to transfer data to the cloud.\r\n</p><p>The migration wizard is only compatible with GP versions 2015 or later, requiring an upgrade to migrate from older versions or choosing a complete implementation.\r\n</p><p>Also, it should be ensured that your on-prem system is using SQL Server 2016 or a later version and that your database\'s compatibility level is at 130 or higher.\r\n</p><p><b>Here\'s an overview of the GP data transfer process to BC:\r\n</b></p><h2>Migrating Data Using the Data Migration Wizard\r\n</h2><p>This tool eases the process of migrating GP data to the new system and is intended for companies looking to transition from on-prem to BC as their primary solution, in a one-time move.\r\n</p><p>The cloud migration tool transfers the following GP data to the cloud:\r\n</p><ul><li>Inventory items\r\n</li><li>Chart of Accounts master records\r\n</li><li>Checkbook master data\r\n</li><li>Outstanding transactions from the Payables module &amp; vendor master records\r\n</li><li>Excellent outstanding transactions via Receivables module and customer records\r\n</li><li>Payables, Receivables, PO processing, Historical data from Inventory, and Sales Order processing\r\n</li></ul><p><b>Note:</b> This tool doesn’t migrate everything from your on-prem system to BC, I\'ve explained the process to do that later in this blog.\r\n</p><p><b>For instance:</b> The migration wizard excludes data linked to closed transactions, POP, SOP (standard operating procedure), and manufacturing transactions. Additionally, it doesn\'t migrate the breakdowns of accounts, and totals are instead recorded in the account number. To allocate them across various segments, journal entries need to be created.\r\n</p><h2>Moving the remaining GP Data to Dynamics 365 Business Central\r\n</h2><p>Here are some alternatives to migrate important financial data to Business Central\'s cloud:\r\n</p><h3>1. Migrate with RapidStart\r\n</h3><p>Utilize “<b>RapidStart</b>”, import transactional data. Note that it is not in the migration wizard. This allows you to create Configuration Packages in Excel to migrate transactions and set up the new system more efficiently.\r\n</p><h3>2. Transfer Your Dynamics GP’s database to Azure Data Lake\r\n</h3><p>Move your GP database to Azure Data Lake to store historical data securely in the cloud for later use.\r\n</p><h3>3. Azure Data Factory\r\n</h3><p>Use Azure Data Factory to rehost data in the cloud and integrate data from ISV solutions with Dynamics 365 automatically.\r\n</p><h3>4. Replicate GP data with the intelligent cloud\r\n</h3><p>Replicate GP data with the intelligent cloud to temporarily access financial data in the cloud while finishing the migration process or deciding what to do with historical data.\r\n</p><p><b>Remember:</b> You can keep your GP data on-prem for historical records.\r\n</p><h2>What challenges you might face while moving your operations from GP to BC?\r\n</h2><p>Migrating to the cloud is a crucial step to support your business to evolve into a growing organization. However, it\'s not a smooth ride as it might seem.\r\n</p><p>Different obstacles may arise.\r\n</p><p>Below are some of the major hurdles you may find on your journey to <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/administration/migrate-dynamics-gp\" target=\"_blank\">migrate from Microsoft GP to Dynamics 365</a>.\r\n</p><h3>1. Alternate Solutions to Replace GP Features\r\n</h3><p>GP\'s 3rd-party integrations and customizations add complexity to the ERP system. Whereas Business Central eases this by providing streamlined customization development and a robust suite of tools.\r\n</p><p>However, unraveling existing customizations and integrations is necessary before reaping benefits.\r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a> may lack some core GP features, such as <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/payroll-for-business-central-nav/\">HR payroll processing</a> and Account Schedules, requiring investment in different solutions or 3rd-party ERP apps/add-ons.\r\n</p><h3>2. Giving Room to New Functionality\r\n</h3><p>Business apps from Dynamics 365 like Business Central simplify financial data analysis through dimensional accounting and embedded intelligence.\r\n</p><p>Dimensions provide a comprehensive overview to allocate resources, purchase inventory, and adjust strategy. However, it may be challenging for long-time GP users. A phased migration process from a certified cloud solution partner (CSP) may ease the transition for overwhelmed teams.\r\n</p><h3>3. Transforming Financial Records from GP to Dynamics 365\r\n</h3><p>Migrating your data from Dynamics GP to business management apps in Dynamics 365 suite is a complex process that occurs in multiple stages.\r\n</p><p>It involves two separate systems, and the data migration wizard only transfers open transactions and master records.\r\n</p><p>Critical information needs implementation through other methods. Though solutions like Azure Data Lake &amp; Data Factory simplify the process, it remains complicated and requires planning from the outset.\r\n</p><h2>Summary!\r\n</h2><p>Dynamics GP will continue to receive Microsoft support until 2024, allowing time for strategic planning and resource allocation for an upgrade. And continue to use the legacy system can cause long-term damage or losses, and inaction poses a significant risk to make progress.\r\n</p><p>To help you avoid all of that, you can <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">connect with Dynamics Square experts</a> and understand the GP upgrade process. The team will also provide rapid <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-business-central-implementation/\">Business Central implementation</a>.</p><p>\r\n</p>', '5 Easy Steps to Migrate from Dynamics GP to Business Central', 'Dynamics GP to Business Central Migration Steps', 'Learn how you can seamlessly migrate from Dynamics GP to Business Central in just 5 easy steps with our comprehensive blog. Simplify your migration today!', 'dynamics gp,microsoft dynamics gp,business central,dynamics 365 business cetral,microsoft dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics business central,business central implementation,business central partner,business central support', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768141421567284.png', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '02:13:00pm', '2023-06-08', '12 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-01-15 14:13:00');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(147, 'Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing: Solutions for Healthcare & Life Sciences', 'introducing-the-cloud-for-manufacturing', 'ERP', 'erp', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768143190207038.png', 'In order to navigate through disruptions in the MedTech sector, improve resiliency, and build a sustainable future, many medical device manufacturing, and distribution companies have moved their operations to the cloud solutions', '<p>“In order to navigate through disruptions in the MedTech sector, improve resiliency, and build a sustainable future, many medical device manufacturing, and distribution companies have moved their operations to the cloud solutions like Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing. This has allowed them to gain operational visibility, integrate data across various systems, and foster digital collaboration among those who are close to manufacturing facilities and supply chains.”\r\n</p><p>Today, people are aware and know what\'s happening in the business world. All they need is technology that can help them connect the dots, manage their operations, and run their business with minimum input – with regards to both tech and costs.\r\n</p><p>By minimum inputs, I mean - a low-cost technology that results in higher outputs/results and lowers the recall rate for manufactured medical devices.\r\n</p><p>This leads to say; increased efficiency and enhanced productivity, while also helping the workforce maintain a work-life balance.\r\n</p><p>And the way to achieve these goals is by investing in cloud solution(s) for manufacturing, like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/industries/microsoft-cloud-for-manufacturing/\">Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing</a> - a smart manufacturing solution to empower your workforce from all ends.\r\n</p><p>Let\'s see how this innovative technology can enable scalability, speed, and security for your medical devices so that your intent to help those in need blooms.\r\n</p><h2>What is Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing?\r\n</h2><p>Before I proceed to let you know what Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing is, let me write a bit about cloud technology and what companies have shifted their operations to <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">cloud-based business management applications</a>.\r\n</p><h3>1. Cloud Technology\r\n</h3><p>A collection of servers, storage, databases, networking, software, and analytics, over the internet to deliver computing resources at your fingertips is known as cloud technology, cloud computing, or cloud tech (to help you sound fancier!).\r\n</p><p>This tech is so powerful that it enables you to access and utilize these resources on demand without having to invest in expensive IT infrastructure and hardware.\r\n</p><p>All the resources needed for <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.globaldata.com/store/report/cloud-computing-market-analysis/\" target=\"_blank\">cloud computing</a> are hosted and managed by cloud service providers like Microsoft, or your cloud solution partners (CSP) like Dynamics Square as <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a> to help ensure the high availability, scalability, security, and performance of the resources.\r\n</p><p>One of the fascinating things about cloud technology is, you can access cloud technology through various models such as Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS), Platform as a Service (PaaS), and Software as a Service (SaaS), depending on your specific business needs.\r\n</p><p>The evolution of cloud technology has revolutionized not only the IT industry but almost every industry that requires scaled growth and a sustainable future.\r\n</p><p>Enabling access to this robust tech for your businesses, and individuals at your workplace to utilize powerful computing resources on demand, regardless of location, without having to incur significant capital expenditures can be a decisive move.\r\n</p><h3>2. Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing\r\n</h3><p>It is a PaaS offering from Microsoft and includes <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-azure/\">Azure Services</a>.\r\n</p><p>PaaS is a platform for developers to build, deploy, and manage their applications, without the need to manage the underlying infrastructure. This platform can help you streamline innovation and faster the time to market products.\r\n</p><p>Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing helps medical device manufacturers with a set of tools and services to build, deploy, and manage their manufacturing operations, including analytics, IoT (Internet of Things), business applications, and more, on top of Microsoft\'s cloud infrastructure.\r\n</p><p>Manufacturers can leverage this platform for a wide range of cloud-based services, including computing, storage, networking, analytics, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/azure-machine-learning/\">machine learning</a>, and more to build custom applications and solutions.\r\n</p><p>By integrating with other Microsoft technologies and connecting to your existing CRM (<a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a>) and ERP systems (<a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics ERP</a>) and data sources, you can manage your device manufacturing operations at scale.\r\n</p><p>For example, using <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/azure-iot-internet-of-things/\">Azure IoT services</a> you can enable remote monitoring, predictive maintenance, and real-time analytics of manufacturing equipment and processes.\r\n</p><p>It also uses <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/products/synapse-analytics/\" target=\"_blank\">Azure Synapse Analytics</a> to provide a powerful analytics and data warehousing solution for manufacturers to gain deeper insights into business operations and make data-driven decision-making better at every step. Hence, enhanced business intelligence (BI) for years to come.\r\n</p><p>Additionally, the cloud platform allows you to integrate with other Azure services, such as Azure Active Directory and Azure Security Center, to provide secure and compliant access to data and web applications.\r\n</p><h2>Benefits of Rolling out Cloud Infrastructure for Manufacturing\r\n</h2><p>Some of the benefits of implementing Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing include:\r\n</p><h3>Accelerate Time to Market\r\n</h3><p>Medical device companies can accelerate product development by utilizing product-specific cloud tools and partner networks.\r\n</p><h3>Enhanced Operational Efficiencies\r\n</h3><p>MedTech companies that have already rolled out cloud infrastructure can optimize their digital <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\">supply chain</a> by leveraging Microsoft Cloud\'s tools and Azure solutions for enhanced data visibility across the value chain.\r\n</p><h3>Patient-Focused Innovation\r\n</h3><p>Integrate downstream data into your R&amp;D to identify unmet patient needs and comprehend the care ecosystem by utilizing personalization services for patient-focused outreach.\r\n</p><p>There are many other benefits of rolling out Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing for Medical Devices such as enhanced efficiency, improved quality, regulatory compliance, cost savings, faster innovation, and more.\r\n</p><h2>How can Microsoft Cloud help transform your Manufacturing workforce?\r\n</h2><p>Microsoft Cloud provides insights into the challenges faced by manufacturers in attracting, retaining, and training skilled workers in the fast-paced digital manufacturing industry.\r\n</p><p>Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing can help manufacturers close the skill gap and increase employee productivity by transforming their workforce.\r\n</p><p>Industry-tailored cloud solutions provide end-to-end solutions that help workers to collaborate from anywhere, anytime. It assists you in building a safer work environment.\r\n</p><p>With Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing, manufacturers can connect and empower their frontline workers, enhance training, and improve worker wellness, health, and safety.\r\n</p><p><b>Through this platform, medical device manufacturers can:\r\n</b></p><ul><li>Improve employee engagement\r\n</li><li>Close the skill gap\r\n</li><li>Enhance productivity by using modern digital manufacturing tools\r\n</li><li>Automating processes\r\n</li><li>Providing better training and educational opportunities\r\n</li><li>Help you promote a safer work environment by reducing manual effort through automation\r\n</li><li>You can digitally empower your workforce, operate safe and agile factories, create more resilient supply chains, and unlock innovation and new services\r\n</li></ul><h2>Can Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing help reduce the recall rate?\r\n</h2><p>Medical Adoption of Cloud solutions can significantly reduce medical device recall rates.&nbsp; MedTech companies like BrightInsight, Euris, and Rackspace are leading Cloud vendors for medical devices, other than Microsoft.\r\n</p><p>Also, according to GlobalData, <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.globaldata.com/media/medical-devices/medical-devices-industry-headed-towards-ai-machine-learning-2023-says-globaldata/\" target=\"_blank\">the medical devices industry will be embracing AI/ML and cloud tech in 2023</a>, and beyond.\r\n</p><p>And device manufacturers like Edwards Lifesciences, 3M, and Johnson and Johnson are Cloud adopters. Cloud adoption enables scalability, speed, and security, leading to significant growth in the Cloud services market for medical devices, projected to reach $4.4bn by 2024 (at a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of 17.1%).\r\n</p><p>Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing is already helping manufacturing customers like Chevron and Alcoa transform their workforce and improve efficiency.\r\n</p><p>By investing in Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing, businesses can drive workforce transformation, close the skill gap and keep up with the complexities of digital manufacturing and manufacture a more resilient, sustainable future.\r\n</p><p>With Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing, you can improve employee engagement and boost manufacturing productivity.\r\n</p><p>To see how this platform works, you can avail it for preview, and businesses can explore how it can help them build a more resilient and sustainable future.\r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Get in touch</a> with our cloud solution experts, understand all your how\'s and whys, and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/schedule-a-demo/\">get a FREE quote</a>!</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing: Solutions for Healthcare', 'cloud for manufacturing', 'Transform your healthcare operations with Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing, offering industry-specific solutions for increased efficiency and innovation.', 'cloud erp systems,dynamics 365,cloud for manufacturing,microsoft dynamics,microsoft dynamics 365,microsoft cloud,microsoft cloud for manufacturing', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768143190209064.png', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '12:48:14pm', '2023-06-08', '8 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-08-22 12:48:14'),
(148, 'Power BI Pricing and Licensing: Free vs Pro vs Premium', 'power-bi-pricing-and-licensing-free-vs-pro-vs-premium', 'Power BI', 'power-bi', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1821139737388091.Power BI Pricing and Licensing.png', 'Microsoft offers cost-effective and value-for-money Power BI pricing that makes it the top choice for smart business owners. Power BI is the most reliable data analytics solution available for small and large businesses.', '<p>Microsoft offers cost-effective and value-for-money Power BI pricing that makes it the top choice for smart business owners. Power BI is the most reliable data analytics solution available for small and large businesses. It is helping such businesses utilize the power of data using AI-driven technologies.</p><p>In this blog, we are going to discuss Power BI pricing and licensing to understand why it is a top choice for growing businesses. Also, we will compare its different plans and capabilities with each other. </p><p>Before we deep dive into the pricing and compare the plans, let’s understand a bit about Microsoft Power BI.</p><p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" src=\"//www.youtube.com/embed/Evkj4zfpk0Q\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" class=\"note-video-clip\"></iframe><br></p><p> \r\n</p><h2>What is Power BI? \r\n</h2><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Power BI</a> is a powerful, interactive, and popular data analytics tool that empowers users to utilize the data at its best. Capable of collecting data from 500+ data sources, Power BI offers extensive data visualization of piles of data. It helps the users understand the treasure that’s hidden beneath the huge collection of data. \r\n</p><p>It comes with embedded visual analytics, which can help you refine and visualize the data to supercharge business growth. Based on data visualization, you can make data-driven decisions to support your business\'s growth. \r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.softwebsolutions.com/resources/ai-for-data-analytics.html\" target=\"_blank\">Embedded with AI</a> (artificial intelligence) and BI (business intelligence), Power BI provides realistic data to empower you to make fast and informed decisions with ease. It enables you to build personalized reports and dashboards to enhance the quality of data visualization. \r\n</p><p>As per <a href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics-365/blog/business-leader/2024/12/02/microsoft-is-recognized-as-a-leader-in-the-2024-gartner-magic-quadrant-for-cloud-erp-for-service-centric-enterprises/\" target=\"_blank\">Gartner</a> April 2023 Magic Quadrant for Analytics and Business Intelligence Platform, Microsoft is considered a leader based on Ability to Execute and Completeness of Vision. \r\n</p><p>When it comes to integration with Power BI, there is no match in the market, as you can connect any desired solution within minutes using APIs and direct connections. You can easily connect Power BI with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\">Business Central ERP</a> or a CRM solution (<a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a>) to build a consistent flow of data. \r\n</p><p>Data security is generally a major concern for all business owners as data becomes an asset for modern organizations. With Microsoft, you don’t need to be worried about data security as you are covered by the trust of <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-azure/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Azure</a>. \r\n</p><p>Power BI is basically a cloud-based solution offering global connectivity to users. However, you can also deploy it using on-premises data servers (Power BI Report Server), making it adaptable for different business requirements.</p><h2>Microsoft Power BI Pricing\r\n</h2><p>Microsoft is continuously changing the prices of its popular products after the release of new business solutions. Similarly, after the release of <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/microsoft-fabric-impact-on-data-and-bi/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Fabric</a>, Power BI pricing is offered in five plans for all businesses.</p><p>You can also access the <a href=\"https://app.powerbi.com/home?culture=en-in&amp;country=in&amp;experience=power-bi\" target=\"_blank\">Power BI trial</a> for 60 days by signing up for free using Microsoft Power BI homepage.</p><h2>Microsoft Power BI Licensing \r\n</h2><p>Microsoft offers a very flexible licensing plan for all businesses. Microsoft Power BI pricing is based on two subscription plans: \r\n</p><h4>1. User-Based Licensing Plan \r\n</h4><p>The Power BI licenses will be allotted based on the number of users. This plan will act like a shared access with shared capacity of resources based on server storage. \r\n</p><h4>2. Capacity-Based Licensing Plan \r\n</h4><p>You can avail yourself of a capacity-based licensing plan based on the capacity you are using. The capabilities and server strength cannot be shared with another user. \r\n</p><h3>Microsoft Power BI Licensing Plans</h3><h4>1. Microsoft Power BI Desktop/Free \r\n</h4><p>Power BI Free or Desktop version is freely available for all users to help them analyze and visualize the reports. It is a basic version that allows you to <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/how-to-generate-interactive-reports-in-power-bi/\" target=\"_blank\">create reports and dashboards</a> in PIX format. You can access this version with ease without even creating an account. You can download Power BI on your desktop and start data visualizations. \r\n</p><p>However, you cannot share the reports with other users or collaborate with other users with different licensing plans. Later, you can access the reports using a web browser or the Power BI Mobile app, but you will need to sign in to Power BI Desktop. \r\n</p><p>Since everything comes with it free of charge, you still need to get a Power BI Free license. Your Power BI Administrator can assign it to you, or you can get it yourself by signing up from the <a href=\"https://app.fabric.microsoft.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft website</a>. \r\n</p><p><b>Price: Free \r\n</b></p><p>Some of its features are: \r\n</p><ul><li>Create Reports \r\n</li><li>Data security \r\n</li><li>Encrypted data flow \r\n</li></ul><h4>2. Microsoft Power BI Pro \r\n</h4><p>Microsoft Power BI Pro offers all the features of Power BI Free and comes with a per-user licensing plan. The main difference when we do a comparison of Microsoft Power BI Free vs Power BI Pro is the ability to share the visualization in the form of reports. \r\n</p><p>You can access all types of sharing tools with this Power BI Pro licensing plan, other than the options that come with Power BI embedded licensing. \r\n</p><p>Based on the administrator\'s authorization, you can share the reports within or outside the organization. However, the other users must have a Power BI Pro or Premium license to access the shared reports and workspaces. \r\n</p><p>Another major benefit of purchasing the Pro license is the ability to integrate with other native and third-party applications to build a sustainable data flow. You can connect Power BI with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft ERP</a> or Office 365. This is especially beneficial in <a href=\"https://www.saasadviser.co/blog/marketing-reports-and-data-analysis-for-b2b-startups\" target=\"_blank\">data analysis for startups</a>, where quick integration and insights can lead to more agile business decisions.</p><p><b>Price: $10 per user/month \r\n</b></p><p>Some of its features are: \r\n</p><ul><li>All features of Power BI Free \r\n</li><li>Publish and share reports \r\n</li><li>Team collaboration on reports \r\n</li><li>1 GB Model Memory size \r\n</li><li>8/day Refresh Rate \r\n</li><li>10 GB/User storage (maximum) \r\n</li></ul><h4>3. Microsoft Power BI Premium \r\n</h4><p>The Power BI Premium licensing plan is built for organizations with heavy usage of data analysis and visualization and larger numbers of users. This licensing plan comes in two options: \r\n</p><h5>A. Microsoft Power BI Premium Per-User Licensing \r\n</h5><p>This is a per-user-based licensing plan with more capabilities and features when we compare it with the Power BI Pro license. With this license, you will get more capabilities, server power, and a lot more features to help you build more interactive reports. \r\n</p><p><b>Price: $20 per user/month \r\n</b></p><p>Some of its features are: \r\n</p><ul><li>All features of Power BI Pro \r\n</li><li>Comes with Advanced AI \r\n</li><li>Dataflows and Datamarts \r\n</li><li>XMLA endpoint read/write \r\n</li><li>100 GB Model Memory size \r\n</li><li>48/day Refresh Rate \r\n</li><li>100 TB total storage \r\n</li></ul><h5>B. Microsoft Power BI Premium Per Capacity Licensing \r\n</h5><p>This license is specifically designed for organizations with a greater number of users. Such companies require dedicated space to deal with all data analytics requirements, which cannot be fulfilled with per-user licensing. \r\n</p><p><b>Price: Varies \r\n</b></p><p>Some of its features are: \r\n</p><ul><li>You cannot publish and share reports outside the organization. \r\n</li><li>All features of Power BI Premium per user \r\n</li><li>All internal users can consume reports without any licensing \r\n</li><li>Access to all features of Microsoft Fabric. \r\n</li><li>400 GB Model Memory size \r\n</li><li>48/day Refresh Rate</li></ul><table class=\"table table-bordered\"><tbody></tbody></table><table class=\"table table-bordered\"><tbody><tr><td><b>Features</b></td><td><b>Power BI Free<br>\r\n</b></td><td><b>Power BI Pro<br>\r\n</b></td><td><b>Premium Per User<br>\r\n</b></td><td><b>Premium – Per Capacity</b><br>\r\n</td></tr><tr><td>Create Reports</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Data Security</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Publish and Share</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>Team Collaboration</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Advanced AI</td><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Dataflows</td><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>XMLA endpoint read/write</td><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Consume Power BI content without a paid per-user license</td><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Model Memory Size limit</td><td>0</td><td>1 GB</td><td>100 GB</td><td>Varies</td></tr><tr><td>Refresh Rate for Datasets</td><td>0</td><td>8/day</td><td>48/day</td><td>48/day</td></tr><tr><td>Maximum Storage</td><td>0</td><td>10 GB/license</td><td>100 TB</td><td>Varies</td></tr><tr><td>Pricing</td><td>Free</td><td>$10 per user/month</td><td>$20 per user/month</td><td>Varies</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>How can Dynamics Square help you with Power BI Implementation? \r\n</h2><p>Businesses have to deal with a lot of strange and unrefined data before processing it for data analytics. In such a scenario, you need to check the capabilities of Power BI to see whether it can be a perfect fit for your business or not. \r\n</p><p>In such a scenario, you can <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\">contact us</a> to book a free Power BI Demo with our Microsoft-certified Power BI consultants. In this demo, we will test Power BI considering your business data to test its efficiency in all complex processes. \r\n</p><p>With our years of experience, we have gained positive feedback on all <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/power-bi-implementation/\" target=\"_blank\">Power BI implementation</a> we have done in the USA. Such businesses have managed to maximize profit, lower ROI, and minimize IT costs while making data-driven decisions in real time. \r\n</p><p>In case of need, feel free to write us a mail at <a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a>, or you can call us directly at <a href=\"tel:+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a> for instant support.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blog-faq-style\">\r\n                    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions about Power BI</h2>\r\n                    <h3>1. How much does Power BI cost?</h3>\r\n                    <p>Power BI Desktop is available as a free download. Power BI Pro costs $10 per user/month, and Power BI Premium costs $20 per user/month.</p>\r\n                    <h3>2. What are the different subscriptions for Power BI?</h3>\r\n <p>Power BI offers three main subscriptions:</p>\r\n                    <ul>\r\n                        <li>Power BI Free: Basic features for individual use.</li>\r\n  <li>Power BI Pro: Enhanced features for collaboration, priced at $10 per user/month.</li>\r\n  <li>Power BI Premium: Advanced features for enterprise use, available as per-user ($20 per user/month) or capacity-based licenses.</li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n<h3>3. What are the key features of Power BI Pro?</h3>\r\n<p>Key features of Power BI Pro include: Certified and Shared Datasets, AI-Powered Data Visuals, Ad-hoc Analysis with Excel, Collaboration and Sharing, and Mobile Access.</p>\r\n<h3>4. Can I use Power BI for real-time data analysis?</h3>\r\n                    <p>Yes, you can use Power BI for real-time data analysis. Power BI supports real-time streaming, allowing you to stream data and update dashboards in real time. This feature is useful for monitoring data from sources like factory sensors, social media, and service usage metrics</p>\r\n</div>', 'Power BI Pricing and Licensing: Free vs Pro vs Premium', 'Power BI Pricing', 'Compare the latest Power BI pricing plans, Free, Pro, and Premium. Choose the best option for your needs and budget to unlock advanced features.', 'power bi,microsoft power bi, power bi pricing,microsoft power bi cost,cost of microsoft power bi', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1821139737388095.Power BI Pricing and Licensing.png', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/power-bi-pricing-and-licensing-free-vs-pro-vs-premium/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Power BI Pricing and Licensing: Free vs Pro vs Premium\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Microsoft offers cost-effective and value-for-money Power BI pricing that makes it the top choice for smart business owners. Power BI is the most reliable data analytics solution available for small and large businesses.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Ayush Jain\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Ayush-Jain\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"\"\r\n}', '[]', '01:25:50pm', '2023-09-15', '11 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-08-07 13:25:50'),
(149, 'How to Get Started with D365 Business Central FREE Trial?', 'get-start-business-central-free-trial', 'Business central', 'business-central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768147847979115.png', 'Are you looking for an easy way to start your FREE Business Central trial? Wait no more! This blog is for you. Explore the features, capabilities, and benefits of Business Central from Dynamics 365 Suite.', '<p>\"Are you looking for an easy way to start your FREE Business Central trial? Wait no more! This blog is for you. Explore the features, capabilities, and benefits of Business Central from Dynamics 365 Suite. Also discover how Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central goes beyond conventional ERP systems by signing up for a free trial.”\r\n</p><p>Curious to delve into the world of <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> and gauge its business management potential for your organization? Or\r\n</p><p>Does a Business Central trial seem like the perfect way to start your learning process?\r\n</p><p>Well!, you’re lucky, because this comprehensive blog offers you a step-by-step guide on how to set up your own Free Business Central ERP Trial Version (with similar features like any of its paid versions).</p><p>From creating your account and utilizing a demo database to launching a trial with your data and subscribing to your organization, this guide covers it all.<br></p><p>With this cloud ERP, you can unlock the full potential of your financial visibility and real-time operational monitoring by signing up for a free ERP software trial.\r\n</p><p>You\'ll also be discovering how to optimize your financial insights and track your business operations in real time through this immersive experience.\r\n</p><p>Get ready to discover the possibilities that Business Central has to offer!\r\n</p><h2>What will you achieve from this learning module?\r\n</h2><p>Upon completing this article, you will be able to:\r\n</p><ul><li>Establish a Business Central account.\r\n</li><li>Access Business Central through login.\r\n</li><li>Operate a demo database.\r\n</li><li>Initiate a trial period using your data.\r\n</li><li>Prolong your trial and opt-in or opt-out of your organization\'s subscription to Business Central.\r\n</li></ul><h2>What do you need before getting started with the free trial to Business Central?\r\n</h2><p>You need access to a Microsoft Dynamics Business Central trial account, or your Microsoft Office 365 account. The other way is to get in touch with your <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/microsoft-dynamics-365-partner\">Dynamics 365 Partner</a> for help.\r\n</p><p>Let\'s get started:\r\n</p><h3>1. Introduction to D365 Business Central\r\n</h3><p>This is the first step to getting started with Business Central. You can start by creating a Microsoft Business Central account, or if you already have a Microsoft Office 365 account, you can get started right away.\r\n</p><p>You can create your account using the link \"<b><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/#exampleModal\">Start Your Free Trial</a></b>\", which will redirect you to Business Central’s official web page.\r\n</p><h3>2. Signing into Business Central</h3><p>To connect your operations across your small or medium-sized business, you will have to login into Business Central using the following two options:\r\n</p><ul><li>Sign into Business Central with Office 365 Account\r\n</li></ul><p>To access Business Central through Microsoft 365, simply login to your Microsoft account and browse through the collection of business applications available. This way, you can easily access all your Microsoft apps in one convenient location.\r\n</p><p>To get started, visit the Microsoft 365 sign-in page and enter your login credentials. Once you\'ve logged in, you\'ll see a list of available apps on the left-hand side of the screen. Look for Business Central in the list, or use the Search feature to find it quickly:</p><p></p><ul><li>Accessing Dynamics 365 Business Central Directly<br></li></ul><p>Business Central offers you direct access to its dashboard:\r\n</p><ol><li>You do not want to sign in for the first time.\r\n</li><li>Your browser knows the login credentials that you already entered while accessing office 365 login details.\r\n</li></ol><h3>3. Using a Demo Database\r\n</h3><p>When you sign into Business Central for the first time, you\'ll enter the demo company CRONUS. You can manage multiple companies in Business Central and can add more yourself.\r\n</p><p>The company you\'re currently working in is shown on the top-left of the page, and the environment is displayed on the top-right.\r\n</p><p>You can switch to another company in the same environment or another environment from there.\r\n</p><p>From the My Settings menu, you have the option to switch to another company as well.<br></p><p>The demo company in Business Central provides functional domain coverage for exploring and confirming all features, including sales quotes, orders, and invoices. You can change data, implement available functions, and try out various scenarios. You can create a new company with sample data anytime to get a fresh demo experience.<br></p><p>Using the demo company you can make your Business Central exploration easier through various learning paths. Check the Company Information page to verify your trial subscription level and upgrade to premium to access manufacturing and service management functions.</p><p>\r\n</p><h3>4. Get Started with your own Data to Experience More\r\n</h3><p>The CRONUS demo company provides demo data and configurations for all functional domains in Business Central. In addition to that, you can set up your own company in Business Central using two methods:\r\n</p><ul><li>You can activate a 30-day trial company with your own company data.\r\n</li><li>Alternatively, you can create a new company.\r\n</li></ul><h2>How to use your own company data to activate a 30-day trial company?\r\n</h2><p>It is possible to begin a Business Central Trial company using your own data.</p><p>If you choose to \"<b>Configure a Company</b>\" from the message on your role center page, you will start a wizard that can help you create a new company with compatibility for your own company data.<br></p><p>Once you agree to the Terms and Conditions, you can begin your FREE trial.\r\n</p><p>To begin your first trial of business central, you will need to provide essential details about your company.<br></p><p>These details will appear on external documents like sales invoices and will include your company logo and bank information.\r\n</p><p>Thus, it is necessary to configure your fiscal/economic/budget year during this step.\r\n</p><p><b>Note:</b> You can upload your company logo now too.<br></p><p>The wizard prompts you to set your company\'s budget year start, which you may skip and configure later.\r\n</p><p>Next, specify your inventory costing method before beginning to use your company.\r\n</p><p>It comes with some setup, master, and supplemental data, including default G/L accounts and regional data.\r\n</p><p>However, you must manually “<b>add</b>” or “<b>import</b>” any other necessary data, using built-in tools like assisted setup or configuration packages.\r\n</p><h2>How to Create your New Company?\r\n</h2><p>Go to \"<b>My Settings</b>\" page and create a \"<b>new company</b>\" if needed.\r\n</p><p>By accessing this page, you can navigate to the Allowed Companies page, where you have the option to create a new company using a wizard. To initiate this process, simply select \"<b>New.</b></p><p>This wizard can create three unique types of companies:\r\n</p><ul><li>Evaluation – With Sample Data\r\n</li></ul><p>This creates a company like the demonstrated company with sample data and setup data.\r\n</p><ul><li>Production – With Setup Data\r\n</li></ul><p>This option creates a company like when you activated the 30-day trial, but with some setup data and without real sample data.\r\n</p><ul><li>Create new – With No Data\r\n</li></ul><p>This step helps you create a blank company, but without any setup data.\r\n</p><h2>How to Extend or Cancel your Organization\'s Trial Subscription?</h2><p>To extend or cancel your Dynamics 365 Business Central trial subscription, follow these steps:\r\n</p><p><b>Step – 1:</b> Sign-in to the Microsoft 365 admin center.\r\n</p><p><b>Step – 2:</b> In the left-hand menu, select \"<b>Billing &gt; Subscriptions</b>\".\r\n</p><p><b>Step – 3:</b> Find your Business Central trial subscription and click the \"<b>ellipsis (...)</b>\" to expand the options.\r\n</p><p><b>Step – 4:</b> To extend your trial subscription, click \"<b>Add seats</b>\" and follow the prompts to complete the purchase.\r\n</p><p><b>Step – 5:</b> To cancel your trial subscription, click \"<b>Cancel subscription</b>\" and follow the prompts to confirm the cancellation.\r\n</p><p><b>Note:</b> Canceling your trial subscription will remove access to Business Central and all associated data. Be sure to back up any valuable information before canceling.\r\n</p><p>Furthermore, to keep access to Business Central beyond the trial period, you must enroll your organization in a subscription. <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Business Central Partner</a> like Dynamics Square can help you with subscription inquiries.\r\n</p><p>Business Central offers three license models:\r\n</p><ul><li>Dynamics 365 Business Central Essentials; Starts at $80 per-user/month\r\n</li><li>Dynamics 365 Business Central Premium; from $110 per-user/month\r\n</li><li>Dynamics 365 Team Members; begins at $8 per-user/month\r\n</li></ul><p>Read more: <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-business-central-pricing-licensing/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central Pricing</a>\r\n</p><h3>Re-Cap of Free Business Central Trial\r\n</h3><p>Steps you need to follow for Free Business Central Trial:\r\n</p><ul><li>Create a Business Central Account\r\n</li><li>Go to - <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://dynamics.microsoft.com/business-central/overview/\" target=\"_blank\">https://dynamics.microsoft.com/business-central/overview/</a>\r\n</li><li>Select Get started.\r\n</li><li>Select Business Central.\r\n</li><li>Enter a work email address.\r\n</li><li>Enter a phone number.\r\n</li><li>Enter a phone number to confirm by text message or by phone call&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Enter the code that you receive\r\n</li><li>Complete your account setup and enter the verification code that was sent to your email address\r\n</li><li>Select Create\r\n</li></ul><p>Finally,&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Sign-in to your Business Central\r\n</h3><p>Based on the info at <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://dynamics.microsoft.com/en-us/business-central/overview/\" target=\"_blank\">Business Central Overview Page</a> on Microsoft’s official website, select your account in the top-right corner of the page, and select:\r\n</p><ul><li>Dynamics 365 Home\r\n</li><li>Or, Business Central</li></ul><h2>Final Thoughts!\r\n</h2><p>It is always a good idea to sign up for a free trial of <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a> products before you purchase a license. Microsoft Dynamics Business Central offers features such as financial management, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\" target=\"_blank\">supply chain management</a>, accounting, invoicing, and AI-powered project management, which can streamline operations and increase efficiency. Plus, with the inclusion of GPT4-based Copilot for Dynamics 365 and Microsoft Office 365, you can further lower the burden from the shoulders of people close to your business.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>The FREE Trial Period provides you with access to all the software\'s functionalities, allowing you to evaluate its benefits for your business. Sign up today and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">contact Dynamics Square Microsoft Dynamics partner</a> if you need any help during the trial.</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'How to Get Started with D365 Business Central FREE Trial?', 'trial', 'Learn how to kickstart your experience with D365 Business Central by signing up for a FREE trial. Follow simple steps to explore this powerful ERP solution.', 'business central,microsoft dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics business central,business central partner,business central implementation,business central trial', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768147847980924.png', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', '.', '[]', '06:12:18pm', '2023-06-08', '10 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-11-06 01:12:18');
