(155, 'Why it is Important to Clean Data in Power BI? How to clean and transform the data?', 'how-to-clean-irrelevant-data-in-power-bi-and-ways-to-transform-the-data', 'Power BI', 'power-bi', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768495783337723.jpg', 'Do you know if your data is unstructured or unmanaged while importing to Power BI, either it may give an error or may not deliver inaccuracy in your reports and analytics? Here, the need for Data Cleaning in Power BI takes place.', '<p>Do you know if your data is unstructured or unmanaged while importing to Power BI, either it may give an error or may not deliver inaccuracy in your reports and analytics? Here, the need for Data Cleaning in Power BI takes place.\r\n</p><p>So, this blog will give a complete overview of how to perform data cleaning and data transformation in Power BI to get accurate and actionable data to support the decision-making process within your organization.\r\n</p><h2>Why Data Cleaning in Power BI\r\n</h2><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">Power BI</a> enables everyone in your organization to make instant and growth-driven decisions with its powerful visualization and data analytics. When your data is irrelevant or confined at any level, this will not help to develop accurate reports. Eventually, no users will be able to make productive decisions with compromised data or reporting capabilities.\r\n</p><p>Now, let’s move forward and understand the ways to transform the data in Power BI:\r\n</p><h2>Ways to Clean &amp; Transform the Data In Power BI\r\n</h2><h3>Data Transformation Through Power Query\r\n</h3><p>When it comes to cleaning and structuring your data, all you need to start by selecting ‘Transform Data’ on the home page of your Power BI desktop. To understand visually, a reference image is given below:\r\n</p><p style=\"text-align: center; \"><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768494791916994.Data-Transformation-Through-Power-Query.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">Source: <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/learn/modules/clean-data-power-bi/media/02-open-query-editor-transform-button-ssm.png\" target=\"_blank\">Image Source</a><br></p><p>Whatever queries you apply, the leveraged data in your select query will be demonstrated in the middle part of the Power Query Editor and available queries can be easily seen in the queries setting pane. All the data changes and steps are taken to transform the data are seamlessly recorded in the Query Setting Pane.\r\n</p><h3>Data Structuring for Column Headers &amp; Names\r\n</h3><p>Now, the next step is to check whether the Column Headers &amp; Names are in a structured manner or not. You are required to evaluate your data and start transforming accordingly. Make sure that each column is at the correct place. Let’s understand it with sample images. Here we have two images. One is a CSV file – a data source and another is Power BI.\r\n</p><p>The first image is showing sample data for sales targets wherein you can see product categories along with sub-categories for months. So, the result is in front of you. It’s clearly visible how data is imported in case you have not managed column headers and names in the second image. It’s not imported as anticipated. You can see, it’s difficult to even understand the data, forget about analyzing it. Here you need to reorganize your data.</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768494802367669.Data-Structuring-for-Column-Headers-Names.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\"><br></p><p>\r\n</p><h3><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768494811742077.identify-Data-Structuring-for-Column-Headers-Names.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">Removing Irrelevant Rows</h3><p>When you drive data cleansing to get accurate Power BI reports, there could be blank or meaningless rows that are not required for your reports. For more clarification, consider the sample image. You can see it contains a blank row below the column header, which can be removed by applying Power Query:\r\n</p><p><b>Home tab-&gt; ‘Remove Rows’-&gt; ‘Remove Top Rows</b>.\r\n</p><p>There is another row that contains data, if you think that data is not relevant for your reporting visuals, simply remove them using the same query mentioned above.\r\n</p><p>Similarly, for column data, you can remove that too.\r\n</p><p>‘<b>Home tab-&gt; ‘Remove Columns’-&gt; ‘Remove Columns</b>’.\r\n</p><h3>Renaming the Columns\r\n</h3><p>Next, you need to check column headers. Make sure that no column contains wrong headers, misspelled data, or compromising in the header name series.\r\n</p><p>Now, let’s understand how to solve this part through the below-given image. It seems irrelevant when column names are column1, column2, and subsequently. Here, we need to correct the column names by selecting ‘Use First Row as Headers.\r\n</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768494822686385.Renaming-the-Columns.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">To rename this column header, you are required to right-click the header-&gt; select ‘<b>Rename</b>’-&gt; \'edit’ the name-&gt;press ‘<b>Enter</b>’.<br></p><p>After applying the Power Query, here is how it will look:\r\n</p><h3><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768494833305674.Use-First-Row-as-Headers.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">Unpivoting the Columns</h3><p>Unpivoting is the essential feature in Power BI for data cleansing. This feature can be used while importing your data from your data sources especially when it comes to importing data from your Excel files.\r\n</p><p>For Example, we have data in Excel File. See reference image:</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768494843562815.Unpivoting-the-Columns.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">Now, when this data is imported to Power Query, see how it looks in the given image:<br></p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768494854175386.Original-Power-Query-data.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">The above image is showing a year-wise sales report. Now, if you want data preparation demonstrating the sales report combining both the years, simply rename the first column to month. Thereafter, you need to highlight the year 2018 and 2019 columns. Lastly, select the ‘Transform’ tab and then ‘Unpivot’.<br></p><h2>Bottom Line\r\n</h2><p>To prevent data issues and to achieve accuracy in your reports, data preparation is always required. Once you are done with data sanitization, your system is ready to deliver actionable insights helping your workforce to make timely and productive decisions. In this blog, we covered all the basic tactics in terms of Power BI data cleansing. We hope this blog will help you adequately cleanse and structure your data. Further, we are always ready to provide you with more relevant information for your business. <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Contact Dynamics Square</a> to avail of Power BI consultation, Implementation, or maintenance services.\r\n</p><p>See Also - <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/power-bi-architecture-and-its-components-explained/\">Power BI Architecture and Its Components Explained</a></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'How to Clean Irrelevant Data in Power BI & Ways to Transform the Data?', 'power bi', 'A complete overview of how to perform data cleaning and data transformation in Power BI to get accurate and actionable data to support the decision-making process within your organization.', 'power bi,microsoft power bi,power bi cost,microsoft power bi cost,power bi pricing,microsoft power bi pricing', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768495783339198.jpg', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '04:53:27pm', '12-06-2023', '6 mins read', NULL, 1, NULL, '2023-06-12 11:24:29'),
(156, 'Why Businesses Need to Invest in Power BI – A Business Intelligence Tool', 'why-your-business-needs-power-bi', 'Power BI', 'power-bi', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768497237765077.jpg', 'If managing data has continuously been consuming most of your business hours and making timely decisions is a challenging deal for your business. Power BI can help to streamline your data with its business intelligence and data analytics capabilities', '<p>If managing data has continuously been consuming most of your business hours and making timely decisions is a challenging deal for your business. <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">Power BI</a> can help to streamline your data with its business intelligence and data analytics capabilities.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><h2>Now the question is - Why Power BI?&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</h2><p>Power BI is a complete suite of business intelligence for reporting, analytics, and key <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">data visualization</a>. Enterprises can make prompt and productive decisions to support the futuristic growth of their business by simply adopting Power BI services.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>When you drive numerous operational processes in your organization, it becomes difficult to manage data manually or by using basic system software. Thereby, you need an advanced software configuration to seamlessly manage &amp; distribute your data across your organization over a secured network. Rather than spending hours while making valuable reports and analytics, you need to focus more on core business.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Power BI comes with vast business transforming features that do not merely simplify your data-driven practices or even help you to lead your business toward the next level. Here we are unwrapping the compelling features of this business intelligence tool and such features can help you to uplift your business model:&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Customized Dashboards&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Power BI comes with interactive and customizable dashboards wherein users can choose the layout or personalize the dashboards as per their specific needs or preference. Again, it can be customized according to specific user roles or needs. For instance, a sales manager would love to view sales analytics whereas a project manager would love to represent the data that represents the project insights.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Visual Reports &amp; Analytics&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Visualization helps us to understand things more quickly and seamlessly. Power BI has powerful capability wherein users can access the reports and analytics in an interactive visualization. Users can choose the layout they feel comfortable with. One can also create their reporting visuals and can share the same with other users across their organization by leveraging R language or JavaScript Library.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Seamless Integration &amp; Customization&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>We understand your existing system setup and your concern about adopting a new system. Power BI is a quite comfortable platform designed while considering Excel-like features. Moreover, businesses can integrate the Power BI with their existing system and can drive like a pro.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>If your current system comprises other Microsoft applications or products, Power BI can be configured accordingly to drive parallel data efficiency. Further seamless and secured data integration can be performed with your existing system. For instance, it can be integrated with your existing CRM (<a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a>) software like Salesforce, accounting software like QuickBooks, web analytics like Google Analytics, and more.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>On-Premise &amp; Cloud Flexibility&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Power BI provides the flexibility of keeping and driving data defining your business requirements and values. With a cloud-based implementation, you synchronize and automate your data across your systems, platforms, and devices. If you want to drive your data intelligence implemented for the on-premises system, Power BI is embedded to be configured accordingly.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Data Intelligence with Machine Learning&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>To get predictive analysis, Power BI is powered by <a href=\"https://onlineexeced.mccombs.utexas.edu/online-ai-machine-learning-course\" target=\"_blank\">Machine Learning</a> algorithms. Users can create insightful visual reports and different data analyses serving a specific business need. Such reports can be leveraged to support and accelerate the decision-making process.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Often, it takes hours or even sometimes months to generate reports and this delays your decisions too. With Power BI, everyone in your firm can make decisions quickly and in real-time. For instance, such analytics can prevent you not to invest more in a project which is no longer a profitable deal for your business.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Flexible Implementation&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Considering your specific business needs, Power BI can be implemented to support your organizational practices and values. You can avail yourself of Microsoft Business Intelligence:&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><p><b>Power BI Desktop:</b> To drive data efficiently on your desktop. Create immersive and interactive visual reports and key analytics to discover the hidden insights helping users in your workspace to make productive decisions.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><p><b>Power BI Service:</b> Power BI Services is a SaaS-based model that is hosted on <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-azure/\">Azure</a> – Microsoft’s cloud platform. Through this, organizations can automatically synchronize their data across devices, systems, and platforms. Thereby, everyone in your organization can access, share, and utilize the visual reports and key metrics to make business-supportive decisions quickly using any device from anywhere.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><p><b>Power BI Mobile:</b> Power BI for business intelligence solutions can also be configured in terms of mobile apps. These apps can be integrated with your available data resources to be analyzed to unfold actionable insights supporting strategic business decisions.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><h2>Bottom Line&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</h2><p>Microsoft Power BI helps brands with powerful visual reports, data analytics, and predictive analysis that enable everyone in your organization to make instant smarter decisions. Thus, you can see how the Microsoft Business Intelligence solution can ease your reporting and data analysis tasks while saving time and efforts. To know more about how it can be customized and implemented for your distinct business, Dynamics Square <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a> can help. Connect with us today.\r\n</p><p>Check other Power BI Articles - \r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/how-to-generate-interactive-reports-in-power-bi/\">How to Generate Interactive Reports in Power BI?</a>\r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/how-to-clean-irrelevant-data-in-power-bi-and-ways-to-transform-the-data/\">Why it is Important to Clean Data in Power BI?</a>\r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/an-introduction-to-microsoft-power-bi/\">An Introduction to Microsoft Power BI</a>\r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/power-bi-architecture-and-its-components-explained/\">Power BI Architecture and Its Components Explained</a></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Why Businesses Need to Invest in Power BI?', 'power bi', 'Power BI for Business need: Power BI can help to streamline your data with its business intelligence and data analytics capabilities.', 'power bi,microsoft power bi,power bi cost ,cost of microsoft power bi', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768497237766861.jpg', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '05:32:18pm', '2023-06-12', '6 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-11-07 17:32:18'),
(157, 'What are the Benefits and Capabilities of Microsoft Dynamics 365 for Sales', 'what-are-dynamics-365-for-sales-benefits-and-capabilities', 'Dynamics 365 Sales', 'dynamics-365-sales', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768498184185840.jpg', 'Business leaders who use Microsoft Dynamics 365 for Sales realize the potential of this powerful tool to transform their ways of doing business, connect departments, simplify data reporting, and automate sales processes that lead to growth', '<p>Business leaders who use <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-sales/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 for Sales</a> realize the potential of this powerful tool to transform their ways of doing business, connect departments, simplify data reporting, and automate sales processes that lead to growth and sustainability. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>\"Utilize cloud computing for real-time data availability and intelligent decision-making with Dynamics 365 Sales.\"&nbsp;</p><p><iframe frameborder=\"0\" src=\"//www.youtube.com/embed/6J0TkxVb074\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" class=\"note-video-clip\"></iframe><br></p><p>\r\n</p><h2>Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales: What Is It?&nbsp;\r\n</h2><p>Microsoft Dynamics 365 for Sales (formerly known as <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\">Dynamics CRM</a>) helps organizations increase end-to-end sales practices, build better customer relationships, and close deals faster. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>With actionable sales insights configured for mobile devices, Dynamics 365 for sales helps to make instant productive decisions, engage customers, and drive effective sales strategy.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Aside from simplifying sales, Microsoft is also looking to redefine the user experience. In addition, Microsoft developed a cloud-based software solution with the mixed capabilities of ERP (Enterprise Resource Planning) and CRM - Dynamics 365 Sales.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p><b>Microsoft Dynamics 365 for Sales features that empower sellers to:</b>&nbsp;\r\n</p><ul><li>Seamlessly &amp; effectively manage sales. &nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Close sales deals faster.&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Drive personal engagement with customers.&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Use data to make data-driven decisions and communicate the actual data to sales teams.&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Take mature decisions to manage inventory &amp; revamp manufacturing.&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Establish strong CRM, ERP, and more. &nbsp;\r\n</li></ul><p>Since Microsoft Dynamics 365 for Sales is <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-azure/\">Microsoft Azure</a> Cloud-based (a cloud computing service operated and managed by Microsoft) business application. It can connect all SaaS (Software as a Service) apps and services to transform how organizations and customers communicate. &nbsp;\r\n</p><h2>Dynamics 365 for Sales benefits&nbsp;\r\n</h2><h3>Business Growth &nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Increase revenue while reducing acquisition costs by leveraging intelligent insights and business processes. Before talking to a supplier, customers are 57% halfway through the buying process.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Sales Focused&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Avoid distractions in a fast-paced sales environment. Approximately 70% of sales representatives consider their jobs highly complex.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Faster Wins&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Collaboration and productivity in sales can help close deals faster and generate more revenue. Nearly 67% of sales reps\' time goes on non-selling activities. &nbsp;\r\n</p><h2>Capabilities of Dynamics 365 for Sales &nbsp;\r\n</h2><h3>Actionable Insights&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Make sense of big and complex data with the Dynamics 365 for Sales functionalities. The Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales application uses data intelligently and provides sellers with actionable contextual insights they can understand. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Customer insights get converted into the context of customer relationships, so it\'s easy to focus on what\'s important and drive personal engagement.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Prospect and Lead Prioritization&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>The Versium Predict platform combines enterprise account and sales data with business and customer life data and machine learning, giving your sales teams the ability to: &nbsp;\r\n</p><ul><li>Deciding which leads are the most important to pursue.&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Identify and gather new prospects.&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Data accuracy and completeness are ensured for multichannel campaigns.&nbsp;\r\n</li></ul><h3>Relationship Health&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Get smarter about selling with Dynamics 365 for Sales by revealing true relationship health and risk data and adopting the next-best actions while allowing the sales team to focus on the most important prospects and customers.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Pre-built dashboards and reports from <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">Power BI</a> (Business Intelligence) provide drill-down, interactive, and visual capabilities to make actionable insights quickly accessible to sales teams.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Social Media Tracking&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Make the most of social selling to spot buying signals, evaluate competitive threats, build social authority, stay up to date with changing market conditions, find quality leads, build social authority, stay up to date with changing market conditions, find quality leads, and more. Visit <a href=\"https://socialthink.io/\" target=\"_blank\">SocialThink</a> for getting Social media platforms knowledge.</p><p>Additionally, keep an eye on buzz volume and trends, and perform sentiment analysis using Dynamics 365 for Sales features. &nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Customer Intelligence&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Build customer engagement more personal and effective using customer <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-sales-insights/\">insights from Dynamics 365 Sales</a>. A dedicated dashboard tailored for sales brings everyone in the organization to the same page.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Relationship Management&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Build relationships with buyers by engaging them authentically and personally. By unifying the sales experience around relationships, sellers can deliver one of the most attentive customer experiences on the market today.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>LinkedIn Sales Navigator Integration&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Discover the power of LinkedIn\'s over 500 million professional members. Take advantage of colleagues\' social networks to identify, understand, and connect with buyers. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>By continuously understanding and responding to customer needs, you can build trust. Manage relationships at scale with unified data and processes that make it easy to grow and expand relationships. Manage relationships at scale with unified data and processes that allow you to <a href=\"https://evaboot.com/blog/export-leads-linkedin-sales-navigator\" target=\"_blank\">export lead lists to Excel</a>, making it easy to grow and expand relationships&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><h3>Relationship Assistant&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>The relationship health score provides a clearer picture of each customer relationship based on the wealth of data gathered from CRM, email, and social networks, including transactions, customer sentiment, emails, and content exchanged. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Observe the strength and trend of each relationship to proactively focus on the relationships that need extra attention.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Email Intelligence&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Get insights about your customers by analyzing their email interactions. Knowing which contacts are most receptive to engaging with you, you can figure out which emails are opened, replied to, or attached.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Content Personalization&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p> Make personalized sales documents faster and easier by searching for and creating them online. As you work on different projects, relevant content is sent to you. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Create personalized content using familiar Office 365 tools. The opportunity you are working on should provide access to sales documents directly.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Sales Productivity&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Automate sales processes using an intuitive interface and Microsoft Office integration for greater revenue, increased productivity, and lower costs.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Sales Process&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Optimize the sales efforts by automating the sales process and implementing a guided sales process. Embedded business processes will help you close deals faster. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Help and guidance across the web and mobile apps that are rich, context-sensitive, and easy to use can increase user adoption.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Opportunity Management&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>From smartphones, tablets, PCs, and Macs manage customers and deals wherever and however, you like.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Salespeople can use familiar and preferred tools to carry out tasks in <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-sales/\">Dynamics 365 for Sales</a> using Office 365 apps. See contextual sales data, including activities, cases, and opportunities, with incoming emails in <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://outlook.live.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Outlook</a> and Outlook Web Access.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>When it\'s time to run a what-if analysis, open sales data in Excel, make changes and save them to Dynamics 365 for Sales. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Lead qualification or prepared for customer meetings with accurate 3rd party firmographics, news, and exciting events embedded in your accounts, contacts, leads, and opportunities.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Sales Mobility&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>It\'s smarter to sell anytime, anywhere, even offline. Get context-driven news, social data, and task flows for completing frequent tasks quickly with rich, modern mobile apps. Create records, schedule meetings, set reminders, and quickly find information with intuitive, natural voice commands. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>You can still get your work done even if your Internet connection is interrupted. Offline editing, updating, and deleting of records is possible. It is possible to synchronize local changes by automatically replaying offline actions. During connection and offline transitions, you\'ll experience seamless transitions.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Partner Management&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Engage, enable, and activate your partner channel to recruit and onboard new partners. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Develop a successful channel strategy by accelerating partnership revenue and meeting strategic goals. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>By providing partners with the dashboard, you can keep track of conversations across opportunities, cases, and other relevant information to which the vendor has granted access. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Vendors have early pipeline visibility through deal registration and are authorized to offer additional discounts, rebates, and benefits to help them win deals. Maximize selling and implementation expertise by allowing multiple partners to collaborate on the same opportunity. &nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Sales Performance&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Nurture success by creating a culture of success. With real-time analytics and predictive information, you can accelerate sales performance. Recruit, train, coach, and motivate your team with just a few clicks. &nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Seller Onboarding&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Using business process management and interactive help and documentation, ease onboarding and align sales behavior with best practices. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>In addition to learning how to use the Sales application, it\'s a great resource. It\'s also ideal for determining your organization\'s specific sales processes and immediate priorities. &nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Sales Effectiveness&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Providing feedback in real-time, monitoring results, and setting goals will help you achieve your numbers. Correct deviations from the plan with quota setting and analytical dashboards. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Utilize immersive Excel and pre-built templates without leaving the Sales application.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Reports and Dashboards&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Q&amp;As in natural language help you find answers quickly. Analyze all data independently, without requiring technical assistance. Getting started is a breeze with pre-built Power BI sales templates. &nbsp;\r\n</p><p>The at-a-glance dashboards, contextual charts, and graphs right inside Dynamics 365 for Sales helps sales managers get insights quickly about sales performance in addition to Power BI. It is also possible to create charts and graphs on the fly. &nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Gamification&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Increase productivity, performance, and adoption of business applications. Involving employees in fun and engaging team-based competitions motivates employees and engages all employees. Ensure accountability by placing web, mobile, and TV monitors in high-traffic areas. &nbsp;\r\n</p><h2>Ready for the change?&nbsp;\r\n</h2><p>Get more information about <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a> for Sales by contacting Dynamics Square. Being Microsoft Gold Partner, we help businesses with a stress-free D365 Sales implementation, training and support.</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Microsoft Dynamics 365 for Sales: Benefits and Capabilities', 'dynamics 365 for sales', 'Capabilities of Dynamics 365 for Sales benefit salespeople build strong customer relationships, follow actionable insights for sales productivity, and close and win deals faster.', 'dynamics 365 sales,microsoft dynamics 365 sales,d365 sales,dynamics 365 for sales,microsoft dynamics 365 for sales', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768498184188018.jpg', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/what-are-dynamics-365-for-sales-benefits-and-capabilities/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"What are the Benefits and Capabilities of Microsoft Dynamics 365 for Sales\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768498184185840.jpg\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"\",\r\n    \"name\": \"\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"\"\r\n}', '[]', '06:47:31pm', '2023-06-12', '10 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2026-04-01 01:47:31'),
(158, 'What is the Difference between Dynamics 365 Sales Professional vs Sales Enterprise?', 'dynamics-365-sales-professional-vs-sales-enterprise', 'Dynamics 365 Sales', 'dynamics-365-sales', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768499674241936.jpg', 'Compare Dynamics 365 Sales Professional vs Enterprise. Discover key differences in features, pricing, and scalability to find the best CRM solution for your business.', '<p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-sales/\">Dynamics 365 Sales</a> is powerful and one of the most popular CRM software solutions such as <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a> available to businesses today.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>It’s obvious to ask which variant of Dynamics 365 Sales – Professional or Enterprise – is suitable when thinking about rolling Dynamics 365 Sales for managing business processes.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Choosing between D365 Sales Enterprise and Sales Professional is a matter of one\'s business requirements. Meaning, features &amp; functionalities needed to smoothly run and manage business activities under budget. No other solution like Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales, a cloud-based software application, comes with various license types, packages and rates concerning the modules of the required solution.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>And about the difference between Dynamics 365 Sales Professional and Enterprise, D365 Sales Professional has core features, whereas D365 Sales Enterprise includes all features. Below are the key differences that you can refer to –\r\n</p><figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Features</strong>&nbsp;</td><td><strong>D365 Sales Professional</strong>&nbsp;</td><td><strong>D365 Sales Enterprise</strong>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Sales Execution&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;&nbsp;Limited&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;&nbsp;*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Forecasting&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Sales lead &amp; opportunity management&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Quick Campaigns &amp; Marketing Lists&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Products, price Lists and product bundles&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Quotes, Orders, &amp; Invoices&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Data enrichment solution discovery &amp; CPQ&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Live Org Charts&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Product, relationships, &amp; hierarchies&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Cases for Sales&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Business Card Scanner&nbsp;</td><td>Add-On&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Assistant (Standard Cards)&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Email intelligence (email engagement and auto-capture)&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Sales Playbooks&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Competitors, Sales Goals &amp; Territory Management&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Partner Relationship Management&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Microsoft Office 365 Integration&nbsp;</td><td>Limited&nbsp;&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Reporting &amp; Analysis&nbsp;</td><td>Limited&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Export to Excel, advanced analytics with separate Power BI license&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Real-time sales reports &amp; dashboards&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Portals&nbsp;</td><td>Add-On&nbsp;</td><td>Add-On&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Customization &amp; Extensibility&nbsp;</td><td>Add-On&nbsp;</td><td>*&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Contextual Insights&nbsp;</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td>Add-On&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Conversational Intelligence</td><td>&nbsp;</td><td><p>Add-On&nbsp;</p><p><br></p></td></tr></tbody></table>In general, keep the following three things in mind before choosing between D365 Sales Enterprise and D365 Sales Professional:&nbsp;</figure><ul><li>Requirement of the level of customizations and adaptations.&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>The need for the number of dashboards.&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>The type and the number of business processes.&nbsp;\r\n</li></ul><h2>What is common to both Sales Enterprise &amp; Sales professionals?&nbsp;\r\n</h2><p>Both the software applications provide entitlement to create and manage the below-mentioned processes, entities, and basic case creation capabilities in <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a> under their license types:&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><ul><li>Activities&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Leads&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Opportunities&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Accounts&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Contacts&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Dashboards&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Marketing Lists&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Campaigns&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Orders&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Products&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Price Lists&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Quotes&nbsp;\r\n</li></ul><p>Additionally, they both provide consistent capabilities to integrate <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Teams\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Teams</a>, Outlook, Excel, and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">Power BI</a> to Microsoft Dynamics 365.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h2>Pricing: Dynamics 365 Sales Professional Vs Enterprise&nbsp;\r\n</h2><p>Dynamics 365 Sales Professional: Users will have core sales force automation and Office 365 integration at $65 per user/month&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Dynamics 365 Sales Enterprise: Businesses will need to put in $ 95 per user/month for industry-leading sales force automation along with contextual insights, and advanced customization capabilities.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>In addition to that if you want the combined capabilities of \"Dynamics 365 Sales Enterprise\" and \"LinkedIn Sales Navigator\", you\'re advised to choose Microsoft Relationship Sales - starting from $130 per user/month.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h2>What\'s exclusively available to Dynamics 365 Sales Enterprise?&nbsp;\r\n</h2><p>If business leaders choose merely to go with D365 sales professionals, they will miss out on the following powerful functions and services that D365 Sales Enterprise comes with:&nbsp;\r\n</p><ul><li>Sales Goals&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Territory Management&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Forecasting&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Product Families &amp; Relationships&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Competitor Tracking&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Configure and Define Teams&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Sales Playbook&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Knowledgebase&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Embedded Intelligence&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Business Units&nbsp;\r\n</li></ul><p>Remember, D365 Sales Professional licenses provide (no additional per-user capacity entitlement) the same default cloud storage capabilities to users compared to D365 Sales Enterprise at the tenant level.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>D365 Sales Enterprise users will also get additional storage as follows:&nbsp;\r\n</p><ul><li>Common Data Service Database Capacity: 250MB per user license&nbsp;\r\n</li><li>Common Data Service File Capacity: 2GB per user license&nbsp;\r\n</li></ul><h3>License Rules&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>The tenant level is the only place mixing and matching for Sales Professional and Sales Enterprise licenses can occur. Also, there can be no simultaneous deployment of these app modules since most organizations prefer deploying a sales application in a single stroke - the choice will be whether to go for Sales Enterprises or Sales Professionals for a license.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Again, for light usage across all <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 apps</a>, businesses can opt for a Team Member license.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Moreover, Dynamics 365 Enterprise licenses are the only ones that allow businesses to use their licenses for on-premises purposes and in the cloud simultaneously. But there is only a single type of license available Dynamics 365 Sales Professional – for a cloud-based software application.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p><b>Note:</b> For D365 Sales Professional, businesses will require to get a named user license, while a named device license is needed for D365 Sales Enterprise.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Sales Hub&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>This app can only be installed on D365 Sales Enterprise licenses and every customization must be done using Sales Professional\'s dedicated app.&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Moving from Sales Professional to Enterprise&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Transitioning from Dynamics 365 Sales Professional to Dynamics 365 Sales Enterprise is quite easy. Users can upgrade the Sales Professional version to Sales Enterprise at any time whenever there are changes in the requirements.&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><h3>Promotional Offers from Microsoft&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p>Microsoft from time to time rolls out offers for qualifying customers. Keep reading our blogs for either Dynamics 365 Sales Professional or Enterprise, and other products under Microsoft Dynamics 365 like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-customer-service/\">Dynamics 365 Customer Service</a>, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\" target=\"_blank\">Supply Chain</a> and Operations, Human Resources, and more. Also, do not forget to ping us if you want to explore how our team at Dynamics Square (<a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a>) can help you successfully implement such a robust CRM automation project.</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Dynamics 365 Sales Professional vs Enterprise', 'Dynamics 365 Sales Professional vs Enterprise', 'Compare Dynamics 365 Sales Professional vs Enterprise. Explore key differences in features, pricing, and scalability.', 'dynamics 365 sales ,microsoft dynamics 365 sales,d365 sales,dynamics 365 for sales,microsoft dynamics 365 for sales', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768499674243590.jpg', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '03:01:29pm', '2023-06-12', '8 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-10-16 15:01:29');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(159, 'Why Creative Small Business Leaders Need Power BI to Succeed?', 'small-business-leaders-need-power-bi', 'Power BI', 'power-bi', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768500913349057.png', 'Small businesses have a higher risk of failing compared to bigger businesses. In fact, 20% of small businesses fail in their first year. By the second year, 30% would have failed.', '<p>Small businesses have a higher risk of failing compared to bigger businesses. In fact, <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.entrepreneur.com/starting-a-business/the-true-failure-rate-of-small-businesses/361350\" target=\"_blank\">20% of small businesses fail</a> in their first year. By the second year, 30% would have failed. The reason for this is small businesses have less capital to manage losses, meaning there\'s less room for improvement over a short period of time.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Fortunately, there is one-way small business leaders can avoid failure: creative leadership. <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.lhh.com/us/en/insights/why-creative-leadership-is-the-right-solution-for-todays-business-challenges/\" target=\"_blank\">Creative leadership is the right solution</a> for today’s business challenges as it promotes consistent flexibility. Leaders constantly need to make decisions that will help their small businesses adapt to whatever situation is at hand.&nbsp;</p><p>Below are the top 4 features of Power BI that can help small businesses thrive.\r\n</p><h2>Why do small business leaders need Power BI?\r\n</h2><h3>1. Power BI provides real-time information\r\n</h3><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768500442788394.Power BI provides real-time information.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\"><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">Microsoft Power BI</a> is a business intelligence service that allows users to see dashboards and reports related to their business. With it, there’s no need for you to manually collect and analyze data on your own, or even wait for a certain period of time to see specific information. Instead, Power BI can be set up to display real-time information. This way, you can identify issues and solve them immediately, such as when costly marketing efforts are ineffective for increasing sales. This is especially crucial for small businesses because even minor mistakes can result in huge losses.&nbsp;<br></p><p>Want to know how Power BI can help your business to transform your scattered data into useful insights? \r\n</p><p>Read our comprehensive <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/guides/power-bi-guide-for-sme/\">Power BI guide</a> which includes:&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n</p><ul><li>Importance of BI tools for your small business\r\n</li><li>How to make interactive reports using Power BI\r\n</li><li>Great Power BI Dashboard Examples\r\n</li><li>Power BI vs Other BI tools\r\n</li></ul><p>And lots more...\r\n</p><h3>2. Microsoft Power BI makes data easier to understand&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768500456336461.Microsoft Power BI makes data easier to understand.jpg\" style=\"width: 100%;\">Rather than simply showing you numbers, Power BI visualizes data using graphs, charts, and tables to make it easier to digest. This visualization is one of the reasons <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/why-your-business-needs-power-bi/\">why your small business needs business intelligence</a>. It helps you better understand your business and make fact-based decisions. For instance, seeing that one particular team member makes the most sales through data provided by Power BI, you can assign them a product that has the least number of sales. Doing so can improve your chances of increasing the product’s sales and help your small business grow further.&nbsp;<br></p><h3>3. Power BI improves customer relationship management&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768500470254521.Power BI improves customer relationship management.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">It’s no secret that businesses rely on their customers to stay afloat, but this is especially true for small businesses. A small business that loses even just one customer can greatly affect its revenue. Power BI can aid in this regard by <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/why-do-smbs-need-crm-software-solutions/\" style=\"background-color: white; font-family: sans-serif; font-weight: 400;\">helping small businesses improve customer relationship management</a>. Included in the data it collects and presents is customer information like their preferred products and services, where and what time they like to shop, and any points of improvement they have for your business. With this information at hand, you can tailor your products, services, and customer interactions to make sure that your customers remain satisfied with your small business.&nbsp;<br></p><h3>4. Power BI predicts the future of your small business&nbsp;\r\n</h3><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1768500479392742.power-bi-predictive-analysis.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">That being said, one of the reasons small businesses fail is due to finances such as a lack of capital or failure to set aside funds. This is why small businesses can’t ignore forecasting. This step is vital if you wish to gain insight into your present and future performance. Power BI helps predict this future by using data to show what the next few months or years will bring. For example, if it notices that the holiday season is associated with more sales, you can anticipate this by increasing your product supply and manpower to meet customer demands. Overall, it allows you to perform in accordance with your small business\'s long-term goals.<br></p><p>Power BI is a tool that can help small businesses succeed by improving customer relationships, forecasting, visualizing data, and providing real-time information. Utilize Power BI today for the benefit of your small business.&nbsp;\r\n</p><p>Are you looking for strategic ways to improve your reporting and analytics for your business? Contact our <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Power BI experts</a> today!</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Why Creative Small Business Leaders Need Power BI to Succeed?', 'Small Business Leaders Need Power BI', 'Why do small business leaders need Power BI to succeed? Let\'s uncover some interesting features & benefits of Power BI so that you can make smarter decisions.', 'power bi,microsoft power bi,cost of microsoft power bi,microsoft power bi pricing', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768500913716246.png', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '05:25:50pm', '13-06-2023', '5 mins read', NULL, 1, NULL, '2023-06-13 17:25:50'),
(160, '5 Trusted CRM Software For Real Estate Industry', 'crm-software-for-real-estate', 'CRM', 'crm', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768502264466728.png', 'Discover the trusted CRM software for real estate industry to streamline sales, leads, automate tasks, and enhance client relationships for growth.', '<p>A real estate agency, <b>Greenwich Properties</b>, manages hundreds of leads daily—buyers, sellers, and renters. Agents manually track inquiries, follow-ups, and property details in spreadsheets, which often leads to mistakes like overlooking important calls or mixing up client preferences. This results in frustrated clients, missed opportunities, and decreased sales.</p><p>One day, a client, interested in a luxury apartment, slips through the cracks because an agent forgot to follow up on an inquiry. By the time the client returns, the property is sold. \r\n</p><p>After implementing a CRM system, Greenwich Properties can track client interactions, schedule follow-ups, and store detailed client preferences. The CRM automates reminders, ensures timely responses, and gives agents access to a 360-degree view of each client’s journey. As a result, the agency improves customer satisfaction, boosts lead-conversion rates and significantly reduces the chances of missed opportunities. \r\n</p><p>This scenario highlights the critical need for CRM software in the real estate industry, offering better organization, personalized service, and greater business growth. </p><p>In this article we will discuss the 5 high-performing CRM Software for Real Estate Industry. </p><h2>What is CRM Software for Real Estate?</h2><p>CRM software for real estate is a must-have tool for agents and brokers. It helps them keep track of leads, manage interactions with prospects, organize property listings, and automate follow-ups, all in one place. \r\n</p><p>With a CRM, real estate professionals can stay on top of inquiries, build relationships, and close deals faster. Modern day CRMs are designed in such a way that they don’t let you forget any lead, so that every opportunity is taken advantage of.&nbsp;</p><p> \r\n</p><h2>Why does the Real Estate Industry need CRM Software? \r\n</h2><p>The real estate industry needs CRM software to efficiently manage client relationships and streamline operations. With CRM software, real estate agents can store and organize client information, track interactions, and automate routine tasks. </p><p>This leads to improved client satisfaction through personalized service and timely communication. Additionally, CRM software helps in capturing and nurturing leads, enhancing the chances of converting them into clients, and ultimately driving business growth. \r\n</p><p>Moreover, CRM software provides valuable insights through data analytics and reporting, enabling real estate professionals to make informed decisions and optimize their marketing strategies. By centralizing property listings and integrating with other tools, CRM software also reduces administrative overhead and increases overall efficiency, allowing agents to focus on high-value activities and close more deals. \r\n</p><h2>Key Features and Benefits of CRM software for Real Estate Industry \r\n</h2><p>CRM (Customer Relationship Management) software can be a game-changer for the real estate industry. Here are some key features and benefits: \r\n</p><h3>Key Features \r\n</h3><ul><li><b>Contact Management</b>: Store detailed information about clients, including contact details, preferences, communication history, and important dates. This helps in segmenting contacts based on criteria like location, budget, or property preferences. \r\n</li><li><b>Property Listings Management</b>: Easily upload, organize, and showcase available properties within the CRM platform. This centralizes property listings, streamlining the sales process and reducing administrative overhead. \r\n</li><li><b>Task and Appointment Reminders</b>: Stay organized with reminders for tasks and appointments, ensuring no important deadlines or meetings are missed. \r\n</li><li><b>Lead Management and Automation</b>: Capture, track, and nurture leads through automated workflows, improving efficiency and conversion rates. \r\n</li><li><b>Customizable Reporting and Analytics</b>: Generate reports and analyze data to gain insights into sales performance, client behavior, and market trends. \r\n</li><li><b>Mobile Accessibility</b>: Access CRM features on the go, allowing agents to manage their work from anywhere. \r\n</li><li><b>Integration with Third-party Tools</b>: Seamlessly integrate with other tools like email marketing platforms, social media, and property management systems. \r\n</li><li><b>Customer Support and Training</b>: Access to support and training resources to ensure effective use of the CRM software. \r\n</li></ul><h3>Benefits \r\n</h3><ul><li><b>Improved Client Relationships</b>: By maintaining a comprehensive database of contacts and interactions, agents can deliver personalized services, leading to increased client satisfaction and loyalty. \r\n</li><li><b>Increased Efficiency</b>: Automation of routine tasks and streamlined processes save time and reduce errors, allowing agents to focus on high-value activities. \r\n</li><li><b>Better Lead Management</b>: Efficiently capture and nurture leads, improving the chances of converting them into clients. \r\n</li><li><b>Enhanced Communication</b>: Centralized communication tools ensure timely and consistent interactions with clients and prospects. \r\n</li><li><b>Data-Driven Decisions</b>: Access to detailed analytics and reports helps in making informed decisions, optimizing marketing strategies, and improving overall business performance. \r\n</li><li><b>Scalability</b>: As your business grows, CRM software can scale with you, accommodating more clients, properties, and agents. \r\n</li></ul><p>Using CRM software tailored for the real estate industry can significantly enhance your business operations and client relationships. \r\n</p><h2>How to Choose the Right CRM Software for Real Estate Market? \r\n</h2><p>Choosing the right CRM software for the real estate industry involves considering several key factors to ensure it meets your specific needs. Here are some steps to guide you: \r\n</p><p><b>1. Identify Your Needs</b>: Determine what features are most important for your business. Common features for real estate CRMs include lead management, contact management, email marketing, and integration with other tools. \r\n</p><p><b>2. Evaluate Features</b>: Look for CRMs that offer features tailored to real estate, such as property management, automated follow-ups, and pipeline management. Some well-known options include: \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Dynamics 365 CRM</b>: Renowned for automation and data centralization. </li><li><b>Pipedrive</b>: Great for email marketing and project management.</li><li><b>Follow Up Boss</b>: Designed specifically for real estate agents. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>3. Consider Usability</b>: Ensure the CRM is user-friendly and easy to navigate. A complicated interface can hinder productivity. \r\n</p><p><b>4. Check Integration Capabilities</b>: The CRM should integrate seamlessly with other tools you use, such as email platforms, social media, and marketing automation tools. \r\n</p><p><b>5. Assess Scalability</b>: Choose a CRM that can grow with your business. It should accommodate an increasing number of users and data as your business expands. \r\n</p><p><b>6. Read Reviews and Testimonials</b>: Look for reviews from other real estate professionals to understand their experiences with different CRMs.  \r\n</p><p><b>7. Take Advantage of Free Trials</b>: Many CRM providers offer free trials. Use these to test the software and see if it fits your workflow. \r\n</p><p><b>8. Consider Cost</b>: Compare the pricing plans of different CRMs. Ensure the cost aligns with your budget while providing the necessary features. \r\n</p><p>By following these steps, you can find a CRM that enhances your efficiency and helps you manage your real estate business more effectively.  \r\n</p><h2>What are some Highly Preferred CRM Software for Real Estate?  \r\n</h2><p>Customer relationship management tools are increasingly becoming popular and as well as important for daily real estate work for agents. CRM tools help real estate agents and brokers achieve success every year. </p><p>The suitable real estate CRM software has industry-specific features like emailing, texting messages, <a href=\"https://phonexa.com/blog/real-estate-lead-generation-guide/\" target=\"_blank\">tools for following leads</a>, and click-to-call capabilities. Here is the list of the highly recommended CRM software for real estate agents:  \r\n</p><h3>1. Microsoft Dynamics CRM or Dynamics 365 Customer Engagement \r\n</h3><p>Microsoft Dynamics CRM (now known as <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-customer-engagement/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Customer Engagement</a>) includes a suite of applications to manage customer interactions, track property availability, maintenance, and pricing. It can help you gain insights into customer preferences and behavior. The real estate industry can automate sales, marketing, and customer service processes. </p><p>On top of that, they can use reports and dashboards to make data-driven decisions. Dynamics 365 CRM includes a whole host of features that are tailored to unique requirements of the real estate business. </p><p>Here are some detailed reasons: \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Comprehensive Lead Management</b>: Dynamics 365 CRM helps real estate firms track and manage leads from initial contact to closing deals. This ensures that no potential client is overlooked and helps in converting leads into sales more efficiently. \r\n</li><li><b>Enhanced Customer Engagement</b>: The platform allows for personalized communication and automated follow-ups, helping to build and maintain strong client relationships. It enables real estate agents to stay connected with their clients through various channels, including email, phone, and social media. \r\n</li><li><b>Efficient Property Management</b>: Dynamics 365 CRM centralizes property data, making it easier to manage listings, contracts, and maintenance schedules. This ensures that all property-related information is easily accessible and up-to-date. \r\n</li><li><b>Sales and Marketing Automation</b>: The system streamlines sales processes and enables targeted marketing campaigns. This automation reduces administrative tasks, allowing real estate professionals to focus more on client interactions and closing deals. \r\n</li><li><b>Field Service Management</b>: The platform optimizes field service operations, ensuring timely property maintenance and inspections. It helps in scheduling, dispatching, and tracking field service activities, which is crucial for maintaining property standards. \r\n</li><li><b>Advanced Analytics and Reporting</b>: With powerful analytics tools, real estate firms can gain insights into sales performance, customer behavior, and market trends. These insights help in making data-driven decisions and optimizing business strategies. \r\n</li><li><b>Integration with Microsoft Ecosystem</b>: Dynamics 365 CRM seamlessly integrates with other Microsoft products like Office 365, Power BI, and Azure. This integration enhances collaboration, data analysis, and overall productivity. \r\n</li><li><b>Scalability and Customization</b>: The platform is highly customizable and scalable, allowing real estate businesses to tailor it to their specific needs. Whether dealing with residential, commercial, or industrial properties, Dynamics 365 CRM can be adapted to fit various business models. \r\n</li></ul><p>These features collectively make <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a> a powerful and versatile tool for real estate professionals, helping them streamline operations, improve customer engagement, and drive more sales. \r\n</p><h4>Pricing \r\n</h4><h5>1.	Dynamics 365 Customer Service</h5><ul><li><b>Professional</b>: $50.00 per user/month \r\n</li><li><b>Enterprise</b>: $105.00 per user/month \r\n</li><li><b>Premium</b>: $195.00 per user/month \r\n</li></ul><h5>2.	Dynamics 365 Sales</h5><ul><li><b>Professional</b>: $65.00 per user/month \r\n</li><li><b>Enterprise</b>: $95.00 per user/month \r\n</li></ul><h5>3.	Dynamics 365 Customer Insights</h5><ul><li>Pricing varies based on specific needs and configurations. \r\n</li></ul><blockquote><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Want to explore more about Dynamics 365 CRM or Dynamics 365 Customer Engagement? Schedule a free call now! </b></a></blockquote><h3>2. Salesforce Sales Cloud  \r\n</h3><p>Real estate agents use Salesforce cloud to track property statuses, availability, track their performance, and process Key Performance Indicators (KPIs). Salesforce is a SaaS CRM solution and has the CPQ tool that helps agents create proposals and automates cost estimations. </p><p>These are some of the key features of Salesforce Sales Cloud that make Salesforce an ideal CRM for the real estate industry. \r\n</p><ul><li>Lead generation</li><li>Lead tracking</li><li>Event scheduling  \r\n</li><li>Task monitoring</li><li>Contract management, and other related functions</li></ul><h4>Pricing  \r\n</h4><ul><li><b>CPQ</b>: $75/user/month; billed annually</li><li><b>CPQ Plus</b>: $150 user/month; billed annually  \r\n</li><li><b>Essentials Edition</b>: $25/user/month; billed annually</li><li><b>Professional Edition</b>: $75/user/month; billed annually</li><li><b>Enterprise Edition</b>: $150/user/month; billed annually</li><li><b>Unlimited Edition</b>: $300/user/month; billed annually</li></ul><h3>3. HubSpot  \r\n</h3><p>HubSpot CRM (a part of Sales Hub) is an all-in-one CRM solution designed and developed by HubSpot for faster and better sales. It is an ideal CRM tool to help your real agents in growing your business with its effective features. HubSpot CRM is a unified CRM platform for real estate agencies that want to scale in no time. You can also bundle it with HubSpot\'s Marketing Hub, CMS Hub, and Service Hub for enhanced functionalities. </p><p>These features make HubSpot a key CRM solution for real estate businesses: \r\n</p><ul><li>Free option</li><li>Contact management</li><li>Email templates</li><li>Meeting scheduling</li><li>Call tracking</li><li>Sales automation</li><li>Pipeline management</li><li>Automate other sales and marketing-related tasks</li><li>Create a personalized appointment scheduler</li><li>Add live chat to your website</li><li>Integration capabilities with your company’s apps and tools through HubSpot\'s App Marketplace.  \r\n</li></ul><h4>Pricing  \r\n</h4><ul><li><b>Free</b>: Available \r\n</li><li><b>Starter</b>: $45/month</li><li><b>Professional</b>: $450/month  \r\n</li><li><b>Enterprise</b>: $1,200/month</li></ul><h3>4. Agile CRM   \r\n</h3><p>Agile CRM is not for realtors. Although, it has various features that real estate agents can benefit from. It is an ideal CRM tool for small size <a href=\"https://resimpli.com/real-estate-team/\" target=\"_blank\">real estate teams</a> looking for a collaborative platform. </p><p>Agile CRM includes a range of features that can significantly help real estate agents: \r\n</p><ul><li>Free for up to 10 users</li><li>Unlimited document storage</li><li>Easy collaboration</li><li>Task management  \r\n</li><li>Document tracking  \r\n</li><li>Sales tracking</li><li>Marketing campaign tracking</li><li>Service efforts tracking</li><li>Appointment setting</li><li>Integrates with Zendesk, Google Drive, Gmail, and different social media networks</li></ul><h4>Pricing  \r\n</h4><ul><li><b>Free</b>: Available \r\n</li><li><b>Starter</b>: $8.99/user/month</li><li><b>Regular</b>: $29.99/user/month</li></ul><h3>5. Apptivo  \r\n</h3><p>Apptivo CRM is a comprehensive solution tailored for real estate professionals, offering a suite of tools to manage client relationships, streamline operations, and enhance productivity. It provides features like client data access on the go, project management, targeted email campaigns, and automation to handle routine tasks. With inventory management, lead tracking, and email marketing capabilities, Apptivo helps real estate agents stay organized and efficient. </p><p>Here is a list of key features of Apptivo for real estate industry: \r\n</p><ul><li>Access to the client data on the go</li><li>Run targeted campaigns</li><li>Project management</li><li>Invoicing</li><li>Email campaigns</li><li>Create powerful automation rules to save time</li><li>Inventory management</li><li>Creating work orders</li><li>Assigning sales territories to real estate agents</li><li>Creating assignment rules that automatically assign leads and customers to your real estate reps</li><li>Integration with a wide tech stack - Google Workspace, Slack, QuickBooks, PayPal, Microsoft Office 365, RingCentral, and Dropbox</li></ul><h4>Pricing  \r\n</h4><ul><li><b>Lite</b>: $8/user/month</li><li><b>Premium</b>: $12/user/month</li><li><b>Ultimate</b>: $20/user/month</li></ul><p>Ready to take the next steps? </p><p>Choose any of the above-mentioned key CRM solutions for your real estate business and start making waves. </p><h2>FAQ\'s Related to CRM for Real Estate</h2><h3>1. What is real estate CRM, and how can it benefit my business?</h3><p>A real estate CRM (Customer Relationship Management) system is a tool designed to help real estate professionals manage their interactions with clients, leads, and contacts. It centralizes all client information, streamlines communications, and automates various tasks. Benefits include improved organization, enhanced client relationships, better lead management, and increased efficiency.&nbsp;</p><h3>2. What Features Should I Look for in a Real Estate CRM?&nbsp;</h3><p>Key features to look for in a real estate CRM include:&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Contact Management: Store and organize client details and communication history.&nbsp;</li><li>Property Listings Management: Upload, organize, and showcase properties.&nbsp;</li><li>Lead Management and Automation: Track and nurture leads through the sales funnel.&nbsp;</li><li>Task and Appointment Reminders: Stay on top of daily activities and deadlines.&nbsp;</li><li>Customizable Reporting and Analytics: Gain insights into your business performance.&nbsp;</li><li>Mobile Accessibility: Access CRM features on the go.&nbsp;</li><li>Integration with Third-party Tools: Connect with other software and platforms you use&nbsp;</li></ul><h3>3. How Does a CRM System Help in Managing Property Listings and Client Interactions?&nbsp;</h3><p>A CRM system helps manage property listings by centralizing all property information, making it easy to upload, organize, and search listings. For client interactions, it tracks communication history, sets reminders for follow-ups, and personalizes communication, ensuring no lead or client falls through the cracks.&nbsp;</p><h3>4. Can CRM Integrate with Other Tools and Platforms Commonly Used in Real Estate?&nbsp;</h3><p>Yes, most real estate CRMs can integrate with various tools and platforms such as Multiple Listing Services (MLS), email marketing tools, social media platforms, and accounting software. These integrations help streamline workflows and ensure all your tools work seamlessly together.&nbsp;</p><h3>5. What are the Costs Associated with Implementing a Real Estate CRM?&nbsp;</h3><p>The costs of implementing a real estate CRM can vary widely depending on the features and scale of the system. Basic plans can start as low as $12 per user per month, while more advanced systems can cost upwards of $69 per user per month. Some CRMs also offer free trials or freemium versions with limited features.&nbsp;</p><h3>6. How Secure is Client Data Within a Real Estate CRM System?&nbsp;</h3><p>Client data security is a top priority for real estate CRMs. They typically employ advanced security measures such as encryption, multi-factor authentication, and regular software updates to protect sensitive information. Additionally, many CRMs comply with data protection regulations like GDPR and CCPA to ensure data privacy and security.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p> \r\n</p><h2>Get Started with Dynamics 365 CRM for Real Estate Industry? \r\n</h2><p>With Dynamics 365 CRM or Dynamics 365 Customer Engagement you can leverage the benefits of unified data, powerful lead management, and accurate sales cycles. </p><p>With this premium CRM solution you can ensure that no leads fall through cracks. If you want to take your real estate business to the next level, then Dynamics Square can be a great help to you. We have a team of certified Dynamics 365 professionals. </p><p>We offer a flawless and risk-free implementation of Dynamics 365 products. If you need any help, please don\'t hesitate to contact us by phone at <a href=\"tel:+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a> or by email at <a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a>.</p><p>Explore <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/crm-implementation-services/\" target=\"_blank\">CRM implementation services</a> that grow your business.</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', '5 Trusted CRM Software for Real Estate Industry 2026', 'crm software for real estate', 'Discover the trusted CRM software for real estate industry to streamline sales, leads, automate tasks, and enhance client relationships for growth.', 'CRM,Real Estate', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768502264469423.png', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/crm-software-for-real-estate/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Top 5 CRM Software For Real Estate Industry\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Discover the top 5 CRM software for real estate industry to streamline sales, leads, automate tasks, and enhance client relationships for growth.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Ayush Jain\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Ayush-Jain\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"\"\r\n}', '[]', '03:04:57pm', '2023-06-13', '17 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2026-02-19 22:04:57'),
(161, 'What are the Features and Capabilities of Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central?', 'features-dynamics-365-business-central', 'Business central', 'business-central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768503684636975.png', 'Enhance your business operations, increase productivity, connect people and data with Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central – an all-in-one business management Software application.', '<p>Enhance your business operations, increase productivity, connect people and data with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> – an all-in-one business management Software application.\r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\">ERP Software</a> applications first appeared back in the early 90s. Based on the increasing needs and complexities of business operations, ERP (Enterprise Resource Planning) applications were further enhanced beyond just controlling inventory and manufacturing processes to manage other functions of an organization as well, such as finance, sales, and accounting.\r\n</p><p>Since then, ERPs have been upgraded many times and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-ax/\">Dynamics AX</a>, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-nav/\">NAV</a>, or <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-gp/\">GP (Great Plains)</a> have been the most popular ones. Today, because of the necessity to use data for prompt strategic decisions, ERPs are integrated with data visualization and AI (Artificial Intelligence) tools.\r\n</p><p>If your business is small or medium size (SME/SMB) and needs the help of actionable insights, Microsoft’s Business Central from the <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a> suite of business apps can be the right choice. Earlier this ERP tool was known as Dynamics NAV or Navision. But back in Oct. 2018, Microsoft renamed it as Business Central.\r\n</p><p>Today, Business Central is a part of countless businesses and industries across the globe. Since its release in 2018, <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft</a> has been releasing continuous feature updates for this cloud ERP to keep the application with new and enhanced capabilities and compliance regulations like GDPR and Making Tax Digital (MTD, UK).\r\n</p><h2>What is Microsoft Business Central?\r\n</h2><p>Bringing the power of Dynamics NAV to Microsoft Cloud.\r\n</p><p>Dynamics NAV can do almost everything that Business Central can do, but from 2022 businesses want their processes to be future-proof using cloud and automation, leading them to move to cloud-based ERPs.<br></p><p>Dynamics 365 Business Central is an all-in-one business management application that allows you to upgrade your legacy ERP system or accounting software to a comprehensive solution. By implementing this application, you can seamlessly manage your finances, operations, sales, and customer services.\r\n</p><h2>What are the Primary Features of Business Central?\r\n</h2><p>Since its launch, Business Central is helping organizations streamline their business processes, improve customer relations, and open doors for higher growth and new business opportunities, including:\r\n</p><ul><li><b>Breaking Data Silos:</b> Complex data gets broken down into easy-to-understand insights and helps connect people all your business ops while boosting your organization’s overall efficiency. By automating tasks and workflows with familiar apps Word, Excel, and Outlook, you can drive your business without silos.\r\n</li><li><b>Actionable Insights:</b> Accurate data and actionable insights are today’s need for a 360-degree view of your business operations to gain a competitive edge in the market. With Business Central, you get it all!\r\n</li><li><b>Cloud security:</b> Microsoft is a leader in cyber security. Its Azure platform is second to none when it comes to the security of your data and crucial information.\r\n</li><li><b>Designed to Evolve:</b> Microsoft-made Businesses can get started quickly and can adapt to evolving business environments.\r\n</li><li><b>Cost-effective:</b> Business Central is a SaaS ERP solution, and can be deployed on the cloud, according to the pay-as-you-go model, which costs you less and makes available more ERP functionality than an on-premises ERP application. Click here to know more about its pricing and implementation costs or contact us to discuss more.\r\n</li></ul><h2>What are the recent key changes in Business Central?\r\n</h2><ul><li><b>Refreshed User Experience:</b> With an updated layout that maximizes screen space and allows for simpler navigation throughout the whole program, the new Business Central UI (User Interface) helps users accelerate their productivity.</li><li><b>Availability:</b> Business Central can be deployed on-premises, in-cloud, or in a hybrid installation, allowing businesses to manage operations from anywhere, and at any time.<br></li><li>The \"<b>Tell Me</b>\" Feature: This feature evolved in response to search for pages or reports from users\' end, allowing you to discover what they need more quickly and with fewer clicks.\r\n</li><li><b>Filtering:</b> On the sides of panels, a new filtering pane is available in Business Central, allowing you to easily apply multiple predefined or custom filters to your lists, which will be kept as you navigate between pages.\r\n</li><li><b>Copy &amp; Paste Rows:</b> This new feature increases data efficiency by allowing users to copy and paste rows into the same or similar lists within the application.\r\n</li><li><b>Enhanced Experience with Embedded Power BI (Business Intelligence):</b> With a more seamless connection of <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">Microsoft Power BI</a> with Business Central, users can promptly share information right after logging in. They can customize and manage reports without ever leaving the app.\r\n</li><li><b>Changing Permission Sets:</b> Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central supplies customizable permission sets that allow you to add, remove or change based on changing business environments.\r\n</li><li><b>Integrations:</b> Intelligent platforms like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-apps/\">Power Apps</a>, Power BI, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-automate/\">Power Automate</a>, and technologies such as AI/ML help Business Central deliver actionable insights to efficiently run your business operations across the globe. For extra functionality, other Dynamics 365 apps can be integrated seamlessly.\r\n</li><li><b>Customization via Extensions:</b> No standard functionality is enough to fully meet business needs. Hence, the requirement to customize an app. With third-party customization and extensions, Business Central can provide you with enhanced features for business continuity even in challenging times.\r\n</li></ul><h3>Is Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central available in my area?\r\n</h3><p>On April 2nd, 2018, Dynamics 365 Business Central was made available for general availability (GA) as a SaaS solution. However, since Oct 1st of 2018, Business Central is available for on-premises and hybrid deployment options. Microsoft sells Business Central\'s cloud subscriptions in over 100 countries worldwide, including Dynamics Square - a trusted Microsoft Gold Partner.\r\n</p><h3>What are the hosting options for Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central?\r\n</h3><p>Microsoft designed and developed Dynamics 365 - a suite of business apps primarily for cloud deployment. And since Business Central is its part, it\'s available for cloud installations. However, in the light of current requirements from business owners, Microsoft made it possible to deploy its services in a variety of ways: On-premises, Cloud/Software as a Service (SaaS), or Hybrid.\r\n</p><p>Explore more about <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-business-central-implementation/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central Implementation</a> options.\r\n</p><h3>What is the scope of Dynamics 365 Business Central?\r\n</h3><p>Twice a year, Microsoft releases feature updates for Dynamics 365 Business Central. The first update is in February and the second one is in October. Microsoft has named these updates as release waves - 1, 2, 3, and so on. These updates not only improve BC’s features but also enhance its performance, helping users to be more productive and more efficient.\r\n</p><h3>How to implement Business Central in my business?\r\n</h3><p>It’s easy. By contacting or scheduling a meeting with a <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a> like Dynamics Square. These service providers can implement Business Central by examining your current ERP system, and business operations, among other needs to figure out whether Business Central needs to customize or implemented.\r\n</p><p>Note: When licensing <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-platform/\">Dynamics 365 with Power Platform solutions</a>, new Dynamics 365 clients Can save 40%. Contact your Dynamics 365 Service provider ASAP.</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Exploring What\'s New in Dynamics 365 Business Central?', 'dynamics 365 business central features', 'Want new features, additions, capabilities and availability of Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central? Read this blog that briefly explains.', 'business central,dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics business central,business central implementation,business central partner,microsoft business central support', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1768503684638647.png', 'Ayush Jain', 'ayush@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '04:48:36pm', '2023-11-22', '7 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-11-13 16:48:36');
