(179, 'Era of AI in Healthcare with Microsoft 365 Copilot', 'ai-in-healthcare-with-microsoft-365-copilot', 'Healthcare', 'healthcare', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1774468563040790.png', 'The introduction of AI in healthcare is one of the revolutionizing advancements witnessed by healthcare professionals in 2023.', '<p>The introduction of AI in healthcare is one of the revolutionizing advancements witnessed by healthcare professionals in 2023. AI (artificial intelligence) in healthcare industry has enormous potential to change patient care, advance administrative procedures, and improve decision-making. \r\n</p><p>One path breaking advancement offered by Microsoft 365 is <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://blogs.microsoft.com/blog/2023/03/06/introducing-microsoft-dynamics-365-copilot/\" target=\"_blank\">Copilot</a>. It has the power to completely transform the way you work, by working alongside, to empower healthcare professionals (HCPs) to concentrate more on treatment plans and less on administrative work. </p><p>In this article, we will discuss the <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://blogs.microsoft.com/blog/2023/03/20/breaking-new-ground-in-healthcare-with-the-next-evolution-of-ai/\" target=\"_blank\">applications of AI in healthcare with its integration in Microsoft cloud for healthcare</a> and review advantages and disadvantages of ai in healthcare, its ethical implications and potential. \r\n</p><p><b>Also read:</b> <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-ai/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 AI</a></p><h2>Applications of AI in Healthcare Industry \r\n</h2><p>Benefits of AI in healthcare industry, include massive changes in administrative work, patient involvement and adherence, and diagnosis and treatment. The progress is such that the value of AI healthcare market has been forecasted to be of $187 billion by 2030 as compared to $11 billion dollar in 2021, by <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.statista.com/statistics/1334826/ai-in-healthcare-market-size-worldwide/#:~:text=In%202021%2C%20the%20artificial%20intelligence,11%20billion%20U.S.%20dollars%20worldwide.\" target=\"_blank\">Statistia</a>.  \r\n</p><p>With seamless integration and support of AI <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/dynamics-365-for-healthcare-industry/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft cloud for healthcare</a> is one such solution that caters to all healthcare operations. With its all-in-one business intelligence tool - <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\" target=\"_blank\">power BI</a>, healthcare professionals (HCPs) can visually analyze patient data to predict outcomes. \r\n</p><h3>Diagnosis and Treatment Applications \r\n</h3><p>In terms of diagnosing and treating illnesses, AI has produced encouraging results. Machine learning algorithms can forecast treatment plans and outcomes based on patient characteristics and contextual data. Radiology increasingly uses deep learning algorithms to identify malignant tumors and boost the precision of image analysis.  \r\n</p><p>Despite these developments, it is still challenging to integrate AI into clinical operations and electronic health record (EHR) systems.</p><h3>Patient Engagement and Adherence Applications \r\n</h3><p>Enhancing patient engagement and compliance is essential for improving health outcomes. AI has an enormous potential to influence patient behavior, personalize and contextualize care, and deliver focused interventions. Machine learning and business rule engines can enable nuanced interventions along the care continuum by providing timely notifications and pertinent patient content.</p><p>AI-enabled virtual care and tools like Microsoft 365 Copilot can streamline patient triage, prescription follow-ups, and adherence tracking for chronic weight-management therapies. For example, GLP-1 medications are increasingly managed through telehealth workflows: eligible adults can complete online evaluations, receive ongoing coaching, and coordinate refills while clinicians monitor outcomes and side effects. To understand how an end-to-end digital pathway works, from eligibility to prescription support, <a href=\"https://www.weightwatchers.com/us/weight-loss-medication/wegovy\" target=\"_blank\">learn about wegovy</a>, including virtual consults and ongoing monitoring options.</p><p>  \r\n</p><p>AI systems can give patients, medical professionals, and care coordinators personalized recommendations by examining patient data and comparing it to successful treatment pathways. <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.antino.com/healthcare-app-development\" target=\"_blank\">Healthcare app development company</a> can ensure the integration of advanced AI technologies to optimize care delivery and patient management<br></p><h3>Administrative Applications \r\n</h3><p>AI has the potential to improve administrative procedures in the healthcare industry significantly. The maintenance of medical records, revenue cycle management, and claim processing are a few examples of jobs that <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.thestellify.com/transforming-role-of-ai-in-robots/1519/\" target=\"_blank\">robotic automation AI</a> can enhance through automation, making these tasks more efficient and less prone to errors.</p><p>Start off with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance-operations/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations</a> &amp; Take Control of Your Operations and Finances \r\n</p><p>Natural language processing (NLP)-enabled <a href=\"https://www.brainvire.com/blog/impact-of-ai-chatbots-on-customer-support/\" target=\"_blank\">chatbots</a> can manage straightforward patient interactions and support mental health and wellness. Machine learning techniques can reduce administrative work and improve claims accuracy by probabilistically matching data across databases. \r\n</p><h2>How is AI Helping in the Healthcare Industry? \r\n</h2><p>The use of AI in healthcare industry has many advantages, some of which are: \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Improved Diagnosis and Treatment \r\n</b></li></ul><p>Large-scale data analysis performed by AI systems can help medical personnel make precise diagnoses and treatment suggestions. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Enhanced Patient Engagement \r\n</b></li></ul><p>Generative AI in healthcare, combined with health coaching software, can offer patients individualized treatment plans, focused interventions, and real-time monitoring, enabling them to take an active role in their healthcare monitoring. Healthcare providers also collaborate with a <a href=\"https://growthpixelagency.com/\" target=\"_blank\">healthcare marketing company</a> to deliver clear digital communication, patient education, and engagement campaigns that support these AI-driven care initiatives.</p><ul><li><b>Streamlined Administrative Processes \r\n</b></li></ul><p>Automating repetitive administrative processes with AI technologies like RPA can lower expenses and increase productivity. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Advanced Imaging Analysis \r\n</b></li></ul><p>Deep learning algorithms can more accurately evaluate medical images, assisting in the early diagnosis of diseases and enhancing the effectiveness of treatment. Furthermore, clinical documentation often requires standardizing formats; using a <a href=\"https://www.canva.com/features/heic-to-jpg-converter/\" target=\"_blank\">heic to jpg photo converter</a> allows teams to upload and convert photos directly in Canva, ensuring medical imagery is accessible and compatible across all diagnostic platforms.</p><ul><li><b>Predictive Analytics \r\n</b></li></ul><p>AI models can identify at-risk patients, forecast population health trends, and assist healthcare companies in allocating resources efficiently.</p><p>As AI grows in healthcare, <a href=\"https://www.antino.com/artificial-intelligence\" target=\"_blank\">AI services</a> will be key to ensuring effective implementation, value maximisation, and alignment with industry standards.</p><h2>5 Top Challenges of AI in Healthcare \r\n</h2><p>Although AI has a lot of potential, there are a few issues that must be resolved before it can be successfully used in healthcare. Let us explore how AI is used in healthcare industry to meet these challenges:  \r\n</p><p><b>1. Healthcare Workflow Integration</b><br></p><p>Adding AI to current healthcare workflows and EHR systems can be difficult and time-consuming. But with D 365 customization, it can be integrated to EHR allowing comprehensive view of patient’s case history.</p><p><b>2. Limited Data Availability \r\n</b></p><p>Training AI systems requires access to big, labeled datasets, but aggregated sources of medical pictures and other healthcare data are scarce.  \r\n</p><p><b>3. Transparency and Interpretability \r\n</b></p><p>Deep learning algorithms are frequently challenging to understand, which can make it difficult to explain the justification for AI-generated diagnoses or treatment suggestions.  \r\n</p><p><b>4. Ethics \r\n</b></p><p>Using AI in healthcare raises questions about accountability, patient privacy, algorithmic bias, and the potential effects on the doctor-patient relationship. With <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-azure/\">Azure cloud</a>, no breach of sensitive data is now possible and can be accessed on various platforms with absolute standards of security maintained. \r\n</p><p><b>5. Implementation Costs  \r\n</b></p><p>The cost of implementing AI in healthcare is an expensive affair since it calls for significant infrastructure, staffing, and upkeep expenses. But at the same time, how does ai reduce costs in healthcare is equally significant to calculate the business metrics and ROI (return on investment). \r\n</p><h3>AI Ethics in Healthcare \r\n</h3><p>Critical ethical questions are raised when it comes to AI implementation in healthcare. As with some AI algorithms, profound learning algorithms are challenging to analyze and explain; transparency is a big challenge. Concerns exist around AI system errors, ai based patient sentiment analysis in healthcare industry and who is responsible for them.  \r\n</p><p>Another ethical problem is algorithmic prejudice, where AI systems may unintentionally reinforce biases based on race or gender. Ongoing attention, thoughtful regulation, and governance structures are necessary to address these ethical concerns and guarantee responsible AI use in healthcare. \r\n</p><h3>The Future of AI in Healthcare \r\n</h3><p>Despite these difficulties, the impact of AI in healthcare is path breaking. As machine learning and deep learning develop, more precise diagnoses and treatment suggestions will be possible. Improving integration with clinical procedures and <a href=\"https://www.curemd.com/top-ehr-vendors/\" target=\"_blank\">EHR systems</a> will facilitate the deployment of AI technologies. Instead of replacing human clinicians, AI will support them, freeing them to concentrate on tasks that call for human abilities like empathy and big-picture integration.<br></p><p>Although AI has the potential to save costs, its effects on healthcare employment are anticipated to be modest. The development of AI technology will lead to new occupations, fostering a cooperative approach to healthcare provision.  \r\n</p><h2>To Conclude \r\n</h2><p>The importance of <a href=\"https://www.imgglobalinfotech.com/ai-in-healthcare\" target=\"_blank\">AI in healthcare</a> companies has expanse in patient interaction, enhanced diagnosis, and treating ailments more effectively. The use of AI technology in healthcare has enormous potential to improve patient outcomes and transform healthcare delivery, despite difficulties and ethical concerns. To maximize advantages and reduce risks as technology develops, it is essential to ensure responsible and ethical AI use in healthcare.</p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\"><table class=\"table table-bordered\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"border:2px solid black;border-radius:5px;\">Leverage the highest potential of Microsoft’s solutions powered by AI to streamline your hospital’s workflow. Increase your patient satisfaction and double your word-of-mouth referrals!!<br>Avail yourself of free expert consultation to enhance your patient experience!</td></tr></tbody></table></a>', 'Era of AI in Healthcare with Microsoft 365 Copilot', 'ai in healthcare', 'The power of AI in healthcare is changing the scenario in terms of patient care, reduction of costs, and accessibility of affordable healthcare to everyone.', 'ai in healthcare,machine learning,azure cloud,microsoft cloud for healthcare', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1774468563044364.png', 'Samar Malik', 'samar.malik@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/ai-in-healthcare-with-microsoft-365-copilot/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Era of AI in Healthcare with Microsoft 365 Copilot\",\r\n  \"description\": \"The power of AI in healthcare is changing the scenario in terms of patient care, reduction of costs, and accessibility of affordable healthcare to everyone.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1774464920656891.AI in Healthcare Industry.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Harsh Nager\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Harsh-Nager/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2023-08-17\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2023-09-04\"\r\n}', '[]', '02:24:39pm', '2023-09-04', '8 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2026-05-14 21:24:39'),
(180, 'Implementing Dynamics 365 Human Resources - For Best Practices in Healthcare Hiring', 'best-practices-for-healthcare-hiring', 'Healthcare', 'healthcare', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1775195997724014.Best Practices For Healthcare Hiring.png', 'Healthcare hiring practices calls to be revamped by healthcare leaders to acquire high-performing individuals. Following healthcare hiring trends can build an apt talent pool, that might be overlooked by conventional recruitment.', '<p>Current Hiring Trends in Healthcare – Need of Hour \r\n</p><p>Healthcare hiring practices calls to be revamped by healthcare leaders to acquire high-performing individuals. Following healthcare hiring trends can build an apt talent pool, that might be overlooked by conventional recruitment. Although disrupting employment procedures is challenging, one can access healthcare hiring from adopting <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.myhealthtalent.com/article/5-compelling-uses-of-artificial-intelligence-in-recruitment\" target=\"_blank\">AI (Artificial Intelligence)</a> tools or <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-human-resources/\">microsoft solutions for human resources</a>.  \r\n</p><p>Infact, current hiring trends in healthcare are due for a \"<b><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://books.google.co.in/books/about/Moneyball_The_Art_of_Winning_an_Unfair_G.html?id=3DnUCWSnci0C&amp;redir_esc=y\" target=\"_blank\">Moneyball</a></b>\" revolution or an “<b><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.sportsadda.com/cricket/features/what-is-bazball-cricket-explained\" target=\"_blank\">Bazball</a></b>” approach. The transition to value-based payment has very well demonstrated the need to improve our system\'s ability to produce patient-centric outcomes, such as enhanced health and quality of life.</p><p>However, the efforts to accomplish this goal to change healthcare hiring process may be hampered by the employment procedures used in healthcare today.  \r\n</p><p>We may not be prejudiced against those who toss things funny. Still, we are very prejudiced against persons of certain races, social classes, and educational levels. Many of our traditions date back to when most of the healthcare was provided by elite-trained physicians and nurses whose effectiveness rested primarily on subject-matter knowledge. This model is no longer valid because we now understand the importance of diversity and inclusion to improve healthcare hiring.</p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\"><table class=\"table table-bordered\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"border:2px solid black;border-radius:5px;\">By implementing Dynamics 365 solution for Human Resources, enterprises can engage and onboard the right talent and build a productive workspace by utilizing AI insights.</td></tr></tbody></table></a>\r\n<h2>Factors Impacting Healthcare Hiring \r\n</h2><p>Healthcare leaders should question conventional scouting practices and instead concentrate on finding people who, regardless of looks, exhibit the attributes necessary for success.  \r\n</p><p>Billy Beane, the general manager of the Oakland A\'s, revolutionized baseball by questioning accepted scouting practices. He understood that unconscious prejudices were hindering scouts from identifying players with promises who could help the club succeed.</p><p>Similarly, healthcare institutions must adopt a fresh perspective and prioritize hiring healthcare candidates with the qualities required to provide holistic treatment.</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1775194974349153.Billy Beane.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">- Although technical expertise is unquestionably crucial, it is no longer the only aspect that determines whether a patient will have a successful outcome.<br></p><p>- It is crucial to address the biases that have long hampered hiring in the healthcare industry if we are to create a diverse and compassionate workforce. \r\n</p><p>- Organizations may be unable to recognize the most qualified applicants for a position due to unconscious biases based on background or appearance which sometimes lead to <a href=\"https://testlify.com/recruiter-burnout/\" target=\"_blank\">recruiter burnout</a>.</p><p>Here are a few instances of prejudices that may affect the hiring for healthcare industry and its solutions: \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Ageism  \r\n</b></li></ul><p>It is the prejudice towards people of a particular age. Even if the older applicants have more training and experience, this could result in the healthcare sector favoring younger candidates over older ones.</p><p>Healthcare organizations can combat ageism by writing job descriptions that do not include an age range and by refraining from questioning applicants about their age during interviews. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Gender Bias  \r\n</b></li></ul><p>It is prejudice against a particular gender. This may appear in the healthcare sector as a preference for female candidates over male candidates for positions, such as nursing. Healthcare organizations can write job descriptions that are inclusive of women to address gender bias. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Race or Ethnicity Bias \r\n</b></li></ul><p>This can show up in the healthcare sector as a preference for white candidates over individuals of color. Healthcare organizations can utilize blind recruiting practices, such as not revealing the applicant\'s name or photo on the resume, to diversify the pool of applicants for open positions and combat racial and ethnic bias. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Disability Bias \r\n</b></li></ul><p>This can show up in the healthcare sector as a preference for individuals without disabilities over candidates with disabilities. Healthcare organizations might avoid asking applicants about their disabilities and write job descriptions that are accessible to persons with disabilities to combat disability bias. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Sexual Orientation Bias \r\n</b></li></ul><p>This can show up in the healthcare sector as a preference for heterosexual candidates over LGBT prospects. Healthcare organizations can combat sexual orientation bias by publicizing their vacant posts in a variety of locations and by refraining from requesting candidates\' sexual orientations during interviews.</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1775194989329815.Hiring for Healthcare Industry.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 57, 63); font-size: 2rem;\">Healthcare Hiring Solutions</span></p><p>According to <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://dhigroupinc.com/home/default.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background-color: white; font-family: sans-serif; font-weight: 400;\">DHI</a> Group’s Hiring Indicators September 2017 report, the average time to employ was around 41 days, and in the medical space, it was around 49 days. The reason being that employment in the healthcare industry often takes longer because of specific regulatory procedures that deal with compliance issues.</p><p>However, we also know that the top 10% of applicants are usually chosen within ten days if they meet all criteria. So, let us explore the top 4 sources to healthcare hiring solutions for quick recruitment:</p><ul><li><b>Internal Recommendations  \r\n</b></li></ul><p>You may always find someone who knows someone or is a study group member. Internal referrals are typically the top source of hires in most larger firms, and these organizations usually have some internal referral scheme where they pay the doctor who makes the referral $5,000 or $10,000. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>LinkedIn and Indeed  \r\n</b></li></ul><p>Indeed, it is a message to candidates to not only post a job but also to search in the database. The same applies to LinkedIn; you can advertise jobs there, but messaging prospective employees is a better strategy. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Medical Colleges \r\n</b></li></ul><p>As the representatives at the medical schools or residency programs, it gets in there because you can plan meals and Zoom classes through the reps\' eyes. That\'s like recruiting a candidate you want to hire. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Medical Conferences in the State and Local Levels   \r\n</b></li></ul><p>You may find your purple squirrel unicorn amidst the pool of talented professionals who attend state and local conferences. It is an ideal platform to conduct recruitment here. \r\n</p><p>Additional strategies to combat bias in the healthcare hiring process include: \r\n</p><p><b>Use Structured Interviews:</b> A structured interview is one where the questions and criteria for scoring are pre-determined. As the interviewer is not permitted to ask their own questions or make subjective judgments, this can help to lessen the influence of prejudice. \r\n</p><p><b>Use Blind Hiring:</b> During the interview, the interviewer isn\'t shown the candidate\'s name, photo, or other identifying information. As the interviewer cannot draw conclusions about the candidate based on their name or looks, this can help to lessen the effects of unconscious prejudice. \r\n</p><p><b>Obtain Feedback from Others:</b> Examine your job descriptions, interview questions, and recruiting choices with the help of outsiders. This can assist you in determining relative biases. \r\n</p><p><b>Give your Hiring Team Training on Unconscious Bias:</b>&nbsp;Including how to spot it and deal with it during the healthcare hiring. This could contribute to a more equitable and fair recruiting procedure.</p><table class=\"table table-bordered\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"border:2px solid black;border-radius:5px;\">A multispeciality clinic based out of US, was running short of nurses. By <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">implementing Microsoft Dynamics 365</a> for human resources, they were able to offer flexible work arrangements. They offered candidates 4 day work a week and part time facilities, while easily maintaining the work sheets on cloud. So, the organization got back to it\'s main line of work, employee burn out rate decreased with reinstatement and trust of better work life balance!</td></tr></tbody></table>\r\n<h2>Implementing 5 Best Practices for Hiring in Healthcare</h2><p>Organizations must use best practices for hiring in healthcare industry to attract and retain healthcare workers who possess the appropriate attributes. These techniques consist of: \r\n</p><p><b>1. Growing the Pool of Candidates \r\n</b></p><p>Organizations should actively look for people from underrepresented groups to create a diverse workforce. Partnerships with academic institutions, trade associations, and community outreach initiatives can help achieve this. By widening the candidate pool, businesses improve their chances of discovering people with the qualities needed to provide holistic care. \r\n</p><p><b>2. Tools for Structured Interviews and Evaluation \r\n</b></p><p>Organizations should use structured interviews and evaluation tools to reduce biases during the interview process. These methods offer a consistent way of assessing candidates, emphasizing their competencies and behaviors rather than individual evaluations. Organizations should change healthcare hiring process by taking personal biases out of the equation.  \r\n</p><p>The HCM module of <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance-operations/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 for Finance and Operations</a>, which includes several add-ons, supports all HR activities and rules to make things easier. These add-ons improve the standard HCM module from mediocre to exceptional.</p><p>These upgrades allow for seamless integration of Workforce Planning, Benefits &amp; Compensation, Leave, Recruitment, and Talent Management into one module, giving you total visibility into your worldwide workforce. Managers, Employees, Payroll Admin, HR Staff, and HR Managers can all use the HCM/HRM module.</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1775195002078632.Implementing 5 Best Practices for Hiring in Healthcare.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\"><b>3. Programs for Training and Development</b><br></p><p>Healthcare personnel should have access to continued training and development opportunities after employment. These programs place equal emphasis on technical proficiency and the character qualities required for providing comprehensive care.</p><p>Healthcare practitioners may benefit from training in empathy, cultural competency, effective communication, cooperation, and adaptability to improve and meet the patients\' changing requirements continuously. \r\n</p><p><b>4. Mentoring and Assistance \r\n</b></p><p>Healthcare professionals can be retained and helped to succeed in their positions through <a href=\"https://www.robinwaite.com/blog/what-is-the-importance-of-business-coaching-and-mentoring\" target=\"_blank\">business mentoring</a> and support programs. Knowledge transfer, advice, and support are possible when new hires are paired with seasoned mentors. This helps healthcare practitioners overcome the difficulties of providing holistic treatment and improving their professional development. \r\n</p><p><b>5. A Culture of Inclusion in the Workplace \r\n</b></p><p>To recruit and keep a diverse staff, organizations must cultivate an inclusive culture. Organizations ought to promote a culture that values diversity and gives each employee a sense of worth and respect.</p><p>This entails supporting diversity and inclusion efforts, offering chances for employee input and feedback, and dealing swiftly and effectively with any incidents of bias or discrimination. \r\n</p><h3>Conclusion \r\n</h3><p>The old method of hiring for healthcare based primarily on technical abilities needs to be replaced by current hiring trends in healthcare. Healthcare organizations must adapt and prioritize the qualities required to provide holistic treatment.</p><p>Organizations can create a diverse and compassionate staff that responds to patients\' changing needs by addressing prejudices in the healthcare hiring process, putting best practices into place, and building an inclusive culture.</p><p>This change will be advantageous for businesses as well as patients and result in a more just and equal healthcare system.</p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\"><table class=\"table table-bordered\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"border:2px solid black;border-radius:5px;\">Consulting with ERP experts, like Dynamics Square, can help in finding the right solution for your healthcare organization. Connect with us to get started.<br>\r\n</td></tr></tbody></table></a>\r\n<h2>FAQs</h2><p><b>1. What are the specific qualities needed for success in healthcare hiring?  \r\n</b></p><p>- Compassion, communication, problem-solving, teamwork, attention to detail, flexibility, and work ethics are some of the specific qualities required for success in healthcare hiring. \r\n</p><p><b>2. What are the tools for structured interviews and evaluation mentioned in the document?  \r\n</b></p><p>- Competency-based interview questions, rating scales, and behavioral interview guides are the tools for organized interviews and evaluations. \r\n</p><p><b>3. How does Microsoft Dynamics 365 (Human Capital Management) support the new healthcare hiring processes and policies? \r\n</b></p><p>- With a cloud-based platform that can automate and streamline numerous hiring procedures, such as application monitoring, interviewing, and onboarding, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a> (Human Capital Management) supports the new healthcare employment practices and standards.</p>', 'Implementing Dynamics 365 Human Resources - For Best Practices in Healthcare Hiring', 'healthcare hiring', 'Master healthcare hiring with 5 essential practices for success. Elevate your team and deliver quality care. Explore the guide now!', 'healthcare hiring,hiring for healthcare,hiring in healthcare industry,dynamics 365 finance and operations,microsoft dynamics erp', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1775195997724019.Best Practices For Healthcare Hiring.png', 'Meha Khera', 'meha.khera@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/best-practices-for-healthcare-hiring/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Implementing Dynamics 365 Human Resources - For Best Practices in Healthcare Hiring\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Master healthcare hiring with 5 essential practices for success. Elevate your team and deliver quality care. Explore the guide now!\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1775194959698956.Best Practices For Healthcare Hiring.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Madhushree Agarwal\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Madhushree-Agarwal/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2023-08-25\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2023-08-25\"\r\n}', NULL, '11:27:10am', '2023-09-04', '11 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-01-07 11:27:10'),
(181, 'Role of Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain in Transportation Management', 'dynamics-365-supply-chain-in-transportation-management', 'supply chain management', 'supply-chain-management', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1776927210213020.Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain in Transportation Management.jpeg', 'Transportation management in Dynamics 365 supply chain lets you use your company’s transportation and identify vendor and routing solutions for inbound and outbound orders.', '<p>Transportation management in Dynamics 365 supply chain lets you use your company’s transportation and identify vendor and routing solutions for inbound and outbound orders. The many components used to plan transportation routes in <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\">Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</a> are discussed below. \r\n</p><p>The effectiveness and performance of organizations engaged in logistics and supply chain activities are significantly influenced by D365 transportation management. Route planning is a crucial component of transportation management since it has an immediate impact on costs, fuel usage, and delivery times.</p><p>This article will discuss how transportation management Dynamics 365, a potent business solution, aids in the <b>optimization of transportation routes</b>, ensuring that organizations can provide goods and services in the most effective and economical way possible. \r\n</p><p>So, say good-bye to delays and hello to a centralized hub to plan and optimize effective route plans to cut down travel time and unlock savings.</p><h2>Top 4 Components of Dynamics 365 Transportation Management</h2><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/supply-chain/transportation/transportation-management-overview\" target=\"_blank\">D365 transportation management</a> utilizes route planners and route guides for complicated transit routes with numerous stops. You can create a scheduled route if the same route will be taken frequently.</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1776942905323940.4 Components of D365 Transportation Management.jpeg\" style=\"width: 100%;\"><b>1. Route Plans</b><br></p><p>A route plan includes portions of the route that include the destinations visited along the route and the carriers utilized for each section. The stops on the route must be designated as hubs. A hub could be a supplier, a warehouse, a client, or even merely a spot to reload when switching carriers. You can specify \"<b>spot rates</b>\" for different costs for each segment. Here are a few instances: \r\n</p><ul><li>Travel costs to the specified segments \r\n</li><li>Costs associated with picking up the items \r\n</li><li>Fees for delivering the items \r\n</li></ul><p>A route guide must be connected to every route plan. \r\n</p><p><b>2. Route Guides \r\n</b></p><p>The standards for matching a load to a particular route plan are laid forth in a route guide. For instance, you can pick a shipping carrier, service, or group, as well as constraints for the container\'s volume or weight. On the Rate route workbench page, route recommendations are offered, and loads and routes can be matched manually or automatically. It is also accessible on the Load building workbench page if the route guide is for a scheduled route. \r\n</p><p><b>3. Scheduled Routes \r\n</b></p><p>A planned route plan with a schedule for the shipping dates is known as a scheduled route. The way loads are apportioned to planned routes and non-scheduled routes varies. Only the load and the route guidance are evaluated when you assign a non-scheduled route using the Rate route workbench.</p><p>The dates and addresses from the orders and hubs, along with the date on the route plan, are also considered when assigning a scheduled route. To manually assign loads to a scheduled route, you don\'t always need to use the Rate route workbench page.</p><p>Instead, you can suggest loads be generated based on customer addresses and delivery dates from sales orders for a certain planned delivery using the load building workbench. \r\n</p><p>The origin and destination hubs of the route plan for scheduled routes will be set. For all portions, the shipping carrier and service will often be the same, though they can vary. The postal codes of the consumers who are visited along the path are used to generate the destination hubs.</p><p>For a single route plan, various route schedules can be created. A route guide must be connected to the route plan. For planned journeys, the plan can only be connected to one route guide, though.</p><p>Only the actual routes on the Route schedule page are created using the route schedule. When you propose loads on the Load building workbench, you can use the default load template. \r\n</p><p><b>4. Load Building Workbench \r\n</b></p><p>The load building workbench proposes a load using the client addresses, delivery dates, and available scheduled routes from sales orders. On the workbench, the values from the route are automatically entered.</p><p>You can, however, use a \"<b>from</b>\" date that is earlier than the routes \"<b>from</b>\" date. The delivery address and date of all open sales orders are compared when a load is suggested. The sales order for the load is proposed if the delivery address\'s postal code coincides with that of a hub in the route plan and if the delivery date falls within the parameters that were chosen in the criteria. The load template\'s capacity is also taken into account.  \r\n</p><p>One load at a time is suggested. You might need to utilize an alternative load template (such as a load template for a larger truck or container) or schedule an additional delivery if you have a sales order that is not shown. \r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Contact our experts</a> to help you plan your freight transportation routes with multiple stops. \r\n</p><h2>The Importance of Route Optimization in Transportation Management \r\n</h2><p>For companies that depend on transportation to deliver their goods or services, effective route planning is essential. It enables them to improve customer happiness, cut expenses, and streamline processes.</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1776942920255476.Importance of Route Optimization in Transportation Management.jpeg\" style=\"width: 100%;\">Businesses may reduce travel time, avoid gridlock, and make the most of their resources by optimizing their routes. Dynamics 365\'s clever algorithms and sophisticated route optimization capabilities give enterprises the tools they need to realize these advantages.<br></p><h3>Leveraging Intelligent Algorithms in Dynamics 365 \r\n</h3><p>Utilizing clever algorithms, Dynamics 365 analyzes massive quantities of data and creates the best paths. These algorithms consider many variables, including past traffic patterns, current conditions, and delivery restrictions. <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a> can identify the most effective routes for each transportation activity by taking these factors into account. \r\n</p><p>Based on prior performance and current data, Dynamics 365\'s intelligent algorithms are always learning and adapting. To maximize efficiency, this enables organizations to make data-driven decisions and modify routes, as necessary. Businesses may cut down on travel time, use less fuel, and improve operational efficiency overall with Dynamics 365. \r\n</p><h3>Cost Savings through Reduced Fuel Consumption \r\n</h3><p>The decrease in fuel consumption is one of the major advantages of route optimization in transportation management. Businesses can reduce the distance traveled and, consequently, the quantity of gasoline consumed by figuring out the quickest and most effective routes. This results in cost savings and lessens the negative effects of transportation operations on the environment. \r\n</p><p>Businesses can determine the most fuel-efficient routes based on variables like traffic conditions, road quality, and vehicle specifications thanks to Dynamics 365\'s route optimization capabilities. Businesses can save a lot of money and help create a greener, more sustainable transportation ecosystem by including these factors in route design. \r\n</p><h3>Ensuring Timely Deliveries with Improved Delivery Times \r\n</h3><p>To keep customers happy and loyal, firms must adhere to delivery windows. Deliveries that are late may result in angry clients, ruined reputations, and even financial fines. By determining the quickest and most effective routes for each transportation activity, Dynamics 365 assists organizations in maximizing delivery times. \r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Dynamics 365</a> ensures that businesses can design routes that reduce travel time and optimize on-time deliveries by considering elements like traffic congestion, road conditions, and delivery limits. Businesses can constantly satisfy client expectations and establish lasting relationships because of this degree of efficiency and precision in route planning. \r\n</p><h3>Integration with Other Supply Chain Processes \r\n</h3><p>The transportation management features of Dynamics 365 go beyond route optimization. Other supply chain functions, such inventory control, order fulfillment, and warehouse management, are smoothly integrated with it. Through this connectivity, companies may gain a comprehensive understanding of their supply chain and use real-time data to optimize transportation routes. \r\n</p><p>Dynamics 365, for instance, can consider variables like inventory availability at various locations, customer order priority, and warehouse capacity when planning routes. Businesses may guarantee that transportation duties are in line with overall supply chain objectives by factoring these factors into route design. This in turn will increase operational efficiency and customer satisfaction. \r\n</p><h3>Streamlining Operations with Automation \r\n</h3><p>The transportation management capability of Dynamics 365 emphasizes automation. Businesses can streamline operations and free up important resources for more strategic endeavors by automating monotonous chores and procedures. Dynamics 365 automates processes like order aggregation, carrier selection, and load optimization, allowing companies to optimize routes swiftly and effectively. \r\n</p><p>Automation not only lowers human error and saves time, but it also enables firms to react quickly to changing circumstances. Dynamics 365 can automatically reroute goods, for instance, if there are unexpected delays or disruptions in the transportation network, reducing the effect on delivery times. In the fast-paced corporate climate of today, this level of agility and reactivity is essential. \r\n</p><h3>Real-Time Visibility and Collaboration \r\n</h3><p>Businesses can trace shipments throughout the entire transportation process thanks to Dynamics 365\'s real-time visibility into transportation operations. Through proactive problem-solving and proactive response, firms can keep transportation chores on schedule and deliver goods on time. \r\n</p><p>Additionally, Dynamics 365 makes it easier for the various parties engaged in transportation operations to collaborate and communicate. Businesses may communicate in real time with consumers, drivers, and carriers, ensuring that everyone has the information they need to work together efficiently. Collaboration and operational efficiency are improved at this level of transparency. \r\n</p><h3>Continuous Improvement through Data Analysis \r\n</h3><p>Transportation activities are the subject of a tremendous amount of data that Dynamics 365 collects and analyzes. Trends, patterns, and chances for improvement can be found using this data. Businesses may use this data to continuously improve and optimize their transportation procedures, which boosts productivity and lowers costs. \r\n</p><p>Businesses might, for instance, spot inefficient regions like recurrent bottlenecks or inefficient routes by looking at previous transportation data. Following that, they can take corrective action by revising carrier contracts, altering delivery timetables, or optimizing warehouse layouts. Businesses can remain adaptable and competitive in the evolving transportation industry with the support of this data-driven approach to continuous development.</p><h2>To Summarize</h2><p> \r\n</p><p>For companies engaged in transportation management, effective route planning and optimization are crucial. Dynamics 365 offers strong tools and capabilities to streamline routes, cut expenses, reduce fuel use, and accelerate deliveries.</p><p>Businesses may automate tasks, increase real-time visibility, and improve operational efficiency by utilizing intelligent algorithms, automation, and data analysis. Businesses can deliver goods and services in the most effective and economical way possible using Dynamics 365, thereby satisfying customers, and promoting corporate success.</p><h4><b>Witness a Scalable Transformation With our Team</b></h4><p> \r\n</p><p>Predict, optimize and boost profitability with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\">Microsoft Dynamics partner</a> and rest aside all your logistic worries!!</p><p><b><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Get in Touch</a></b></p>', 'Role of Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain in Transportation Management', 'supply chain in transportation management', 'Discover how Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain streamlines transportation management for efficiency and cost savings. Explore now!', 'dynamics 365 supply chain management,microsoft dynamics 365 supply chain management,d365 supply chain,dynamics 365 supply chain,microsoft dynamics 365 supply chain', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1776927210213027.Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain in Transportation Management.jpeg', 'Meha Khera', 'meha.khera@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/dynamics-365-supply-chain-in-transportation-management/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Role of Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain in Transportation Management\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Discover how Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain streamlines transportation management for efficiency and cost savings. Explore now!\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1776927210213027.Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain in Transportation Management.jpeg\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Madhushree Agarwal\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Madhushree-Agarwal/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2023-09-13\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2023-09-13\"\r\n}', NULL, '01:11:23pm', '2023-11-18', '10 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-09-10 13:11:23');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(182, 'Chief Experience Officer (CXO) - The C-Suite Edit', 'chief-experience-officer-c-suite', 'Dynamics 365 Marketing', 'dynamics-365-marketing', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1776926760777477.Chief Experience Officer (CXO).jpeg', 'Chief Experience Officer (CXO) has been identified as the forerunner in today\'s competitive business landscape. The value of experiences is how the C-suite values customer experience in the digital age.', '<p>Chief Experience Officer - Chief Customer Experience Officer + Chief Employee Experience Officer   \r\n</p><p>Chief Experience Officer (CXO) has been identified as the forerunner in today\'s competitive business landscape. The value of experiences is how the C-suite values customer experience in the digital age.</p><p>Companies are constantly seeking new ways to gain a sustainable competitive advantage.  One often <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://hbr.org/2019/06/why-every-company-needs-a-chief-experience-officer\" target=\"_blank\">overlooked solution</a> is the integration of customer experience (CX) and employee experience (EX). \r\n</p><p>While the experience of the customer is the new marketing, it is incomplete without employee experience. When managed together, CX and EX can create a unique and powerful advantage for organizations. This is what is a Chief Experience Officer (CXO) all about.</p><p>In this article, we will explore what is chief experience officer, the meaning of CXO in business, and why it matters in the modern business world.</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1776926681626031.Team working together in the office.jpeg\" style=\"width: 100%;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 57, 63); font-size: 2rem;\">What is a CXO’s Role?</span></p><p>A CXO is a senior executive who is in charge of managing and integrating an organization\'s employee and customer experiences. The Economist Intelligence Unit <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.ceo-review.com/2018-the-rise-of-the-chief-experience-officer/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background-color: white; font-family: sans-serif; font-weight: 400;\">reports</a> that 59% of businesses achieve faster turnover when they prioritize investments in the customer experience.</p><p>This position extends beyond the typical responsibilities of human resources or customer service. Instead, the CXO focuses on getting everyone in the company working together to provide outstanding experiences for both consumers and employees. \r\n</p><p>&nbsp;“<b>There is only one boss – the customer</b>,” Sam Walton \r\n</p><p>The chief executive officer (CXO) serves as a link between a company\'s employee- and customer-facing operations. They help company executives comprehend the requirements and driving forces of their staff and increase employees\' comprehension of consumers. The CXO establishes a unified and comprehensive approach to business by concentrating value on people-centered functions. \r\n</p><h2>Why Every Company Needs A CXO? \r\n</h2><p>The CXO is the chief customer experience officer who is responsible for fostering a people-centered culture and making sure that employee and customer experiences are in line with the organization\'s overarching strategy and objectives.</p><p>In other words, the following are the key responsibility areas to include in chief experience officer job description.</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1776926694462646.Every Company Needs CXO.jpeg\" style=\"width: 100%;\"><b>1. Strategic Alignment</b><br></p><p>The CXO collaborates closely with top management to match the company\'s overarching goals and objectives with customer and employee experience plans. The CXO makes sure that all decisions and efforts are focused on providing great experiences by including CX and EX into the strategic planning process. \r\n</p><p><b>2. Employee Empowerment \r\n</b></p><p>The CXO is essential in building an environment where employees feel empowered and engaged. They collaborate closely with HR and other pertinent departments to create projects and programmes that improve employee growth, well-being, and satisfaction. The CXO can boost employee engagement and productivity by fostering a favourable work environment.</p><p>Manage your workforce, maximize resource utilization, bring organizational agility, engage and onboard the right talent, leverage valuable AI insights to craft a better workspace with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-human-resources/\">Dynamics 365 Human Resources</a>.</p><p><b>3. Customer Insights \r\n</b></p><p>The CXO collects and evaluates customer feedback via <a href=\"https://www.zonkafeedback.com/blog/customer-feedback-tools\" target=\"_blank\">customer feedback tools</a> and insights in his or her capacity as the link between staff members and customers. The CXO can direct the organization in making data-driven decisions that improve the overall customer experience by understanding the demands, preferences, and pain points of the consumers. \r\n</p><p><b>4. Continuous Improvement \r\n</b></p><p>Implementing a culture of continuous improvement throughout the organization is the CXO\'s responsibility. They pinpoint areas that need improvement, put plans into action, and track the effects of these adjustments. The consumer and employee experiences are continually changing and getting better thanks to this iterative process. \r\n</p><p>Ready to boost your ROI? Get <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-marketing/\">Dynamics 365 for Marketing Implementation</a> today!! \r\n</p><h2>Benefits of Chief Experience Officer \r\n</h2><p>Companies can access a number of advantages that boost their long-term success by employing a CXO and merging CX and EX:</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1776926706025377.Benefits of Chief Experience Officer (CXO).jpeg\" style=\"width: 100%;\"><br></p><p> \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Increased Customer Loyalty \r\n</b></li></ul><p>Customers are more inclined to stick with a business if they have a good experience with it. The CXO can boost customer loyalty, lower churn, and spur revenue growth by putting CX at the forefront of their efforts. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Increased Employee Engagement and Retention \r\n</b></li></ul><p>Happy employees are more likely to stick with a company and give their best work. The CXO can foster a productive workplace culture and boost employee retention and productivity by giving EX top priority. \r\n</p><ul><li>&nbsp;<b>Standing-out in Market \r\n</b></li></ul><p>Delivering outstanding client experiences helps businesses stand out from the competition in the market. The CXO may assist organizations in standing out in the market and luring in new clients by merging CX and EX.</p><div><h3>FAQs \r\n</h3><p><b>1. What is the range of chief experience officer salary? \r\n</b></p><p>A Chief Experience Officer salary is approximately $169,6041 per year. In the United States, the basic salary for this position ranges from $177,337 to $230,5782, with an average of $202,608. Cash bonuses, commissions, tips, and profit sharing are all possible forms of additional compensation. \r\n</p><p><b>2. Who is a chief customer experience officer? \r\n</b></p><p>A chief customer experience officer works to improve client experiences. They act as a company\'s customer ambassador, fostering relationships with customers, enhancing customer service, and promoting corporate expansion. \r\n</p><p><b>3. What is a chief employee experience officer? \r\n</b></p><p>A chief employee experience officer is a senior executive who oversees how customers interact with an organization\'s goods and services as a whole.</p><h4><b>Witness a Scalable Transformation With our Team</b></h4><p>Experience real-time synchronization and flexibility with a consistent view across your business.\r\n</p><p><b><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Get in Touch</a></b></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p></div>', 'Chief Experience Officer (CXO) - The C-Suite Edit', 'chief experience officer', 'Chief experience officer helps businesses to do more with less. The most proven yet overlooked solution that can help CXOs achieve their goals and be agile, is by focusing on customer experience (CX) and building a strong team (EX – employee experience).', 'dynamics 365 marketing,customer engagement,cxo,dynamics 365 customer engagement', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1776926760777482.Chief Experience Officer (CXO).jpeg', 'Meha Khera', 'meha.khera@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/chief-experience-officer-c-suite/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Chief Experience Officer (CXO) - The C-Suite Edit\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Chief experience officer helps businesses to do more with less. The most proven yet overlooked solution that can help CXOs achieve their goals and be agile, is by focusing on customer experience (CX) and building a strong team (EX – employee experience).\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1776926760777482.Chief Experience Officer (CXO).jpeg\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Madhushree Agarwal\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Madhushree-Agarwal/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2023-09-13\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2023-09-13\"\r\n}', NULL, '03:55:27pm', '2023-11-18', '6 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-08-05 15:55:27'),
(183, 'How Supply Chain Can Bring Sustainability With Dynamics 365 for Manufacturing', 'sustainability-with-dynamics-365-for-manufacturing', 'Microsoft Dynamics 365', 'microsoft-dynamics-365', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1777367219292996.Sustainability With Dynamics 365 for Manufacturing.jpg', 'Dynamics 365 for Manufacturing module of supply chain is today\'s modern ERP solution to bring sustainability across the ever-changing landscape of the manufacturing industry.', '<p>Dynamics 365 for Manufacturing module of supply chain is today\'s modern ERP solution to bring sustainability across the ever-changing landscape of the manufacturing industry.</p><ul><li><b>If your manufacturing business is small</b> or for that matter a mid-sized organization, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> includes all standard configurations. To prepare production bills of materials (BOMs) and routings to define how end items are produced and prepare machine or work centers to perform the required operations. \r\n</li><li>But, <b>if you are a manufacturing enterprise</b> with complexities to drive, Dynamics 365 for manufacturing module of Supply Chain Management will be the business management solution key for you! \r\n</li></ul><p>The challenge is from digital advancements to consumer demands of net-zero carbon products, manufacturing industries find sustainability a critical constraint in their daily operations. \r\n</p><p>Now, to <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://dynamics.microsoft.com/en-us/industry/manufacturing/\" target=\"_blank\">achieve end-to-end sustainable manufacturing</a>, it is imperative to understand the type of business and the manufacturing process that is involved. Manufacturing process can be a complex activity that involves a range of machinery, tools, and equipment with many levels of automation using computers, robots, and cloud-based technology.</p><p>Thereby, a company decides which production method to choose based on factors such as consumer demand, sales forecasts, the assembly technique, materials involved, and what resources are available. The effective use of <a href=\"https://www.diligent.com/\" target=\"_blank\">governance software</a> can also support decision-making by providing real-time insights and ensuring compliance with operational standards.</p><p>Sounds complex and appears like a dilemma? Don’t worry. \r\n</p><p>Let us explore how <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation</a> can ease these complexities at every level with its innovative adaptability. Before unveiling the secret to drive new opportunities with substantial economic growth, let us delve into the major challenging factors affecting it first. \r\n</p><p>Get in touch with your <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Partner</a> like Dynamics Square for more information regarding the pricing and licensing of D365 Business Central, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-sales/\">Dynamics 365 for sales</a>, and Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations. \r\n</p><h2>Challenges Faced by Manufacturing Industries \r\n</h2><p>The manufacturing industry typically involves process-centric operations. Moreover, there is a continual need for customer engagement to build a positive customer experience for the business to excel.</p><p>Be it any type of manufacturer — from process to <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/modules/get-started-discrete-manufacturing-dyn365-supply-chain-mgmt/\" target=\"_blank\">discrete</a>, batch to repetitive—all can benefit from overhauling their daily operations with Dynamics 365 for manufacturing. Let us run down the <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.austintec.com/8-challenges-manufacturing-industry-facing-2023/\" target=\"_blank\">challenges</a> that you as manufacturing businesses face in doing so, \r\n</p><p><b>1. Employee Recruitment \r\n</b></p><p>The shortage of skilled workers in manufacturing industries is leading to higher turnover rates and increased competition for top talent. This, in turn, is driving up costs for companies and hindering their ability to meet production demands. \r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-human-resources/\">Dynamics 365 Human Resources</a> helps you to manage recruiting requests. It also helps you seamlessly transition job candidates to employees. Moreover, offering competitive benefits packages, flexible work arrangements, and opportunities for professional development can also be managed effortlessly under benefits management, task management, and employee development sections of the HR infrastructure. \r\n</p><p><b>2. Rising Prices \r\n</b></p><p>The rising price of raw resources is a big additional difficulty. Inflation trend in commodity prices in recent years is anticipated to continue. Examples of these commodities include steel, aluminum, and oil.</p><p>Manufacturers are under pressure as a result, and they are battling to keep costs down without sacrificing the quality of their goods. Consumer prices rise because of rising raw material costs, making it harder for producers to sell their products. \r\n</p><p><b>3. Supply Chain Disruptions \r\n</b></p><p>Since the COVID-19 epidemic began, supply chain disruptions have impacted practically all sectors of the global economy. Due to the pandemic\'s aftereffects, natural calamities, and geopolitical unrest, many businesses now face more supply chain unpredictability.  \r\n</p><p>Longer lead times, greater costs, and lower product quality as a result are affecting businesses\' production schedules, customer happiness, and overall profitability. \r\n</p><p><b>4. High Customer Expectations \r\n</b></p><p>Customers are demanding not only more convenient items but also more individualized experiences. This increases the pressure on producers to provide high-quality, customized goods more quickly and inexpensively. \r\n</p><p>Customers are also growing more socially and environmentally sensitive, therefore businesses must implement sustainable practices and place a premium on social responsibility.</p><p>Making the necessary technological investments is necessary to meet these expectations, and failing to do so could hurt manufacturing enterprises\' market share, reputation, and revenues. \r\n</p><p><b>5. Data Security \r\n</b></p><p>In 2023, data security will continue to be a major issue for the manufacturing sector. Manufacturing companies are gathering and keeping enormous amounts of sensitive data due to an increased dependence on technology and digitalization.</p><p>This makes the sector a popular target for cyberattacks because it comprises everything from consumer information to trade secrets.  \r\n</p><p>Financial fines for data breaches and regulatory pressure to secure personal data are other issues that businesses must deal with. Companies must invest in cybersecurity tools like firewalls, encryption, <a href=\"https://nordvpn.com/features/threat-protection/malware-scanner/\" target=\"_blank\">malware scanners</a>, and threat detection systems as well as create and implement data security policies to mitigate these risks. Data security violations can have negative financial, legal, and reputational effects. \r\n</p><p><b>6. Sustainability \r\n</b></p><p>Pressure to implement sustainable practices is another problem affecting the industrial sector. Consumers are seeking items that are created in a more sustainable way because, as we previously indicated, they are looking for ways to be more ecologically friendly.  \r\n</p><p>As a result, manufacturers must enact stricter rules to lower their carbon emissions and waste production. There is an increase in investment in renewable energy and more effective production techniques, both of which raise the price of manufacturing. \r\n</p><p><b>7. Technology \r\n</b></p><p>Automation and other cutting-edge technology are also posing more difficulties and competition for the manufacturing sector. Robotic technology is constantly developing, enabling producers to produce items quickly and effectively.</p><p>While this is excellent news for consumers, it also makes it more challenging for manufacturers to compete in their sector if their rivals can stay up with the most cutting-edge innovations.  \r\n</p><p>As was already said, more sophisticated technology can also lead to additional risks like data breaches and cyberattacks. As manufacturers you will need to keep coming up with strategies for data security while still utilizing this new technology. \r\n</p><h2>How to Minimize Disruptions in Manufacturing with Dynamics 365 Implementation? \r\n</h2><p>Dynamics 365 for manufacturing helps to unify different operations, no matter what the nature of <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/paths/configure-use-process-manufacturing-dyn365-supply-chain-mgmt/\" target=\"_blank\">manufacturing process</a> is. Whether it is a local industrial machinery shop or a 3D printing process, you can achieve complete visibility of the process and engage with your customers, breaking down the complex silos between front and back-end processes. \r\n</p><p>Concisely, it is Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management that is the ultimate solution designed to cater to industries to streamline their manufacturing procedures.  \r\n</p><p>Get in touch with your Dynamics 365 Partner like Dynamics Square for more information regarding the pricing and licensing of Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management (formerly known as <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance-operations/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations</a>) \r\n</p><p>Let us explore the wide range of features and capabilities of the Manufacturing module within Dynamics 365 that enables industries to perform their production operations flawlessly. \r\n</p><p><b>1. Production Planning and Scheduling  \r\n</b></p><p>Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management offers powerful master production scheduling (MPS), material requirements planning (MRP), and capacity planning tools for production planning and scheduling.</p><p>To ensure effective production processes and prompt order fulfillment, the module gives users the ability to create and manage production orders, optimize resource allocation, and monitor work center capacities. \r\n</p><p><b>2. Bill of Materials (BOM) and Routing Management \r\n</b></p><p>The module provides sophisticated BOM and route management features, enabling businesses to specify and maintain intricate product structures, business processes, and work center needs.</p><p>Users can establish routings for each activity, monitor modifications, and create multi-level BOMs to ensure precise cost and production planning. \r\n</p><p><b>3. Shop Floor Control \r\n</b></p><p>Shop floor control functions, such as work order management, work center scheduling, and real-time production monitoring, are offered by Dynamics 365 for manufacturing. Users can manage production exceptions, track production progress, and keep an eye on machine utilization, increasing shop floor visibility and efficiency.  \r\n</p><p><b>4. Lean Manufacturing \r\n</b></p><p>The module supports Kanban, continuous improvement, and value stream mapping, among other lean manufacturing ideas and processes. Lean manufacturing techniques can be used by users to save waste, better production flow, and boost overall manufacturing effectiveness. \r\n</p><p><b>5. Quality Management \r\n</b></p><p>Organizations may ensure product quality, compliance, and safety by using the extensive quality management tools provided by <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\">Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</a>.</p><p>To enable compliance with industry-specific standards and client requirements, users can establish quality tests, inspections, and sample plans, track quality data, and generate quality reports. \r\n</p><p><b>6. Production Costing and Analysis \r\n</b></p><p>Standard cost, real cost, and activity-based costing are just a few of the different costing methodologies that the module offers. To ensure accurate costing and increased profitability, users can manage and evaluate production costs, keep an eye on cost fluctuations, and find ways to cut expenses. \r\n</p><p><b>7. Integration with IoT and AI (Artificial Intelligence) \r\n</b></p><p>Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management uses <a href=\"https://www.hiddenbrains.com/artificial-intelligence-solutions.html\" target=\"_blank\">artificial intelligence (AI) technologies</a> and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/azure-iot-hub/\" target=\"_blank\">Internet of Things (IoT) integration</a> to give real-time insights, forecasts, and suggestions.</p><p>This makes it possible for businesses to keep an eye on the functioning of their equipment, improve maintenance plans, and boost overall operational effectiveness. \r\n</p><p><b>8. Collaboration and Communication \r\n</b></p><p>Engineers, operators, and managers who are part of the production team can collaborate and communicate easily thanks to the module. To keep everyone informed and involved, it interacts with Microsoft Teams, SharePoint, and other collaboration platforms. \r\n</p><p><b>9. Reporting and Analytics \r\n</b></p><p>Dynamics 365 for manufacturing delivers strong reporting and analytics features that give manufacturers immediate access to information about their operations. To track production parameters including productivity, throughput, and quality, users can construct custom reports, dashboards, and key performance indicators (KPIs).</p><p>The analytical capabilities are improved through <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">integration with Power BI</a>, enabling dynamic data visualization and sophisticated reporting.  \r\n</p><p><b>10. Compliance and Risk Management \r\n</b></p><p>The module offers features and capabilities to assist businesses in managing risks, adhering to industry-specific standards, and ensuring the quality of their products. It helps firms maintain regulatory compliance and reduce production disruptions by supporting traceability, quality control, and audit trails.  \r\n</p><p><b>11. Integration and Extensibility \r\n</b></p><p>The Dynamics 365 for Manufacturing module integrates with other Dynamics 365 modules (like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance/\">Dynamics 365 Finance</a>, Sales, and Customer Service), Microsoft products (like Office 365 and Azure), and third-party applications without any issues.</p><p>This gives users a unified experience across multiple business applications and increases the organization\'s overall productivity.</p><p><b>12. Scalability and Performance \r\n</b></p><p>Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management, which is built on the <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-azure/\">Microsoft Azure Cloud platform</a>, gives businesses the scalability and performance they want to manage high volumes of production data and transactions.</p><p>The module offers a flexible and affordable solution for managing manufacturing processes and is simple to scale up or down as business requirements change.  \r\n</p><p><b>13. Mobility and Accessibility \r\n</b></p><p>Users of Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management can access the system from any place and device thanks to its responsive, mobile-friendly user interface. The users can manage production processes, access reports, and work with stakeholders while on the go. The native mobile apps and a web-based interface assures continuity and increases productivity.</p><p><b>14. Environmental and Sustainability Management \r\n</b></p><p>The module assists businesses in tracking their energy use, trash production, and emissions in support of environmental and sustainability programs. Users may analyze how their industrial processes affect the environment and put policies in place to cut emissions, save resources, and limit waste.  \r\n</p><p><b>15. Product Lifecycle Management (PLM) Integration \r\n</b></p><p>PLM solutions can be integrated with Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management, allowing businesses to manage product information, engineering changes, and product development processes on a single platform.</p><p>The market time is shortened, and product quality is increased because of this integration, which guarantees smooth communication between the design, engineering, and production teams.  \r\n</p><h3>To Summarize \r\n</h3><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a> is a comprehensive set of predictive business applications with AI-driven insights. It takes care of CRM (<a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a>) and ERP functionalities of your manufacturing industry seamlessly allowing integration with your existing system along with power BI.</p><p>Now you can proactively respond to changes and advancements by combining your business data, supply chain data, and public data like maps and weather forecasts in a system infused with artificial intelligence and machine learning. This will help you reduce wastage of time and resources. \r\n</p><p>Putting in place a comprehensive system that serves as a \"<b>single source of truth</b>\" can aid in producing more precise schedules, forecasts, and budgets, which in turn power a firm that is more productive. \r\n</p><p>Email us at <a href=\"harsh.nager@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\"><b>harsh.nager@dynamicssquare.com</b></a> or call us at <a href=\"http://+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\"><b>+1 281 899 0865</b></a>, if you are a manufacturing industry on the lookout for Dynamics 365 implementation.</p>', 'How Supply Chain Can Bring Sustainability With Dynamics 365 for Manufacturing', 'dynamics 365 for manufacturing', 'Unlock sustainability in manufacturing with Dynamics 365. Explore how supply chains drive eco-friendly solutions. Join us now!', 'dynamics 365,microsoft dynamics 365,dynamics 365 for manufacturing,dynamics 365 supply chain management,dynamics 365 finance and operations,dynamics 365 implementation,dynamics 365 partner', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1777367219293001.Sustainability With Dynamics 365 for Manufacturing.jpg', 'Arish Siddiqui', 'arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/sustainability-with-dynamics-365-for-manufacturing/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"How Supply Chain Can Bring Sustainability With Dynamics 365 for Manufacturing\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Unlock sustainability in manufacturing with Dynamics 365. Explore how supply chains drive eco-friendly solutions. Join us now!\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1777367233258569.Sustainability With Dynamics 365 for Manufacturing.jpg\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Arish Siddiqui\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Arish-Siddiqui/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2023-09-18\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2023-09-18\"\r\n}', NULL, '04:13:46pm', '2023-09-19', '12 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-12-18 16:13:46'),
(184, 'Insert-Delete-Modify Records in Business Central - 3 Smart Ways', 'insert-delete-modify-records-in-business-central', 'Business central', 'business-central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1778000403744095.Insert-Delete-Modify Records in Business Central.png', 'In Business Central, there may be times when you need to insert or modify a record, but the system does not enable you to do so directly owing to permissions constraints.', '<p>An overview of permission sets via the User Interface (UI) on objects in Dynamics 365 Business Central. \r\n</p><p>In <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Business Central</a>, there may be times when you need to insert or modify a record, but the system does not enable you to do so directly owing to permissions constraints. This can be annoying, but there are workarounds that can help you achieve the result. \r\n</p><p>It is the <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/ui-define-granular-permissions\" target=\"_blank\">permissions property</a> that sets whether an object has additional permission necessary to do operations on one or more tables. The operations can be to read, insert, modify, and delete data. </p><p>Moreover, the property applies to Code unit, Table, Request Page, Page, Xml Port, Report, Query, Permission Set, and Permission Set Extension. \r\n</p><p>If you just have indirect permission to insert data into a specific table, you cannot do so using the standard user interface. To enter data into the table, you must utilize a database object that has been granted additional authority permission. Let us explore the process in detail. \r\n</p><p>Get help to modify data across various departments in <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\">Microsoft Dynamics ERP</a>, with our passionate team of consultants! \r\n</p><h2>How to Insert, Delete, and Modify Records When Permission is not Allowed? \r\n</h2><p>Users\' permissions in Dynamics 365 Business Central are determined by their license. The security permission sets that administrators grant to users further enhance these permissions. The data access kinds include Read, Insert, Modify, and Delete.  \r\n</p><p>A user who has Read permission can access the page that displays data from a table, such as the Item or Customer tables. To edit or delete data, however, the user must have Modify and Delete permissions. \r\n</p><p>Sometimes the license or permission set only allows the user indirect permission to conduct operations on specific data in tables (Table Data). A user with Indirect Read permission cannot open a page that displays data from a table unless the page has been granted the user\'s permission to read data from the table. That is, the user can only execute an action on the data via another object.  \r\n</p><p>In other words, if you only have indirect permission to, say, insert data into a certain table, you cannot do so using the standard user interface. To enter data into the table, you must utilize a database object that has been granted additional permission. \r\n</p><p>Objects do not have the permission attribute declared by default and utilize the same permissions as the user. Users do not have write or edit permissions in some circumstances, such as the numerous Ledger Entries tables. In such a scenario, users should instead run posting routines that make ledger entries on their behalf. \r\n</p><p>With <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation</a>, explore how to grow your business and debug the glitches surrounding <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-gp/\">Microsoft Dynamics GP</a> or Dynamics Nav&nbsp;or Microsoft Dynamics Business Central or any other Microsoft Dynamics ERP for that matter! \r\n</p><h2>The Best Way to do it - Indirect Permission! \r\n</h2><p>You can grant users access to an object, but only via another object. This is called giving \"<b>Indirect</b>\" permission.  \r\n</p><p>When a user has Indirect permission, he or she can only edit the Sales Line table via running the Sales-Post code unit or another object with Sales Line table modification permission.</p><p>Only from supported application areas can the user alter the Sales Line table. Other techniques cannot be used by the user to run the feature mistakenly or maliciously. \r\n</p><p>The table below shows how the Permission property interacts with the permissions provided to an object by a license or a permission set. The table compares the runtime results when and when not the Permission attribute is set.</p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center; \">Permissions Granted by Permission Set<span style=\"color:#161616\"> </span></th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center;\">Permission Property not Set<span style=\"color:#161616\"> </span></th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center;\">Permission Property Set<span style=\"color:#161616\"> </span></th>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">None<span style=\"color:#161616\"> </span></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Runtime error caused by missing permissions.<span style=\"color:#161616\"> </span></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Runtime error caused by missing permissions.<span style=\"color:#161616\"> </span></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Indirect Permission<span style=\"color:#161616\"> </span></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Runtime error caused by missing permissions.<span style=\"color:#161616\"> </span></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Success<span style=\"color:#161616\"> </span></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Direct Permission<span style=\"color:#161616\"> </span></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Success<span style=\"color:#161616\"> </span></td>\r\n    <td><div style=\"text-align: center;\">Success</div><div style=\"text-align: center;\">User has full access to the data.</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>The example below demonstrates how to set the permissions property for the code unit used for customer ledger entries. In the same way, you may define the permissions attribute in other objects.</p><table class=\"table table-bordered\"><tbody><tr><td>codeunit 50113 CreateCustomer\r\n<br>{\r\n<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; Permissions = TableData \"Cust. Ledger Entry\" = rm;\r\n<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; TableNo = Customer;\r\n<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; trigger OnRun();\r\n<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;begin\r\n<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; InsertEntry(Rec);\r\n<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; end;\r\n<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; procedure InsertEntry(var Cust : Record Customer)\r\n<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; var\r\n<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; CustLedgerEntry: Record \"Cust. Ledger Entry\";\r\n<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; begin\r\n<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; CustLedgerEntry.Init();\r\n<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; CustLedgerEntry.\"Entry No.\" := 1;\r\n<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; CustLedgerEntry.\"Customer No.\" := Cust.\"No.\";\r\n<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; CustLedgerEntry.\"Posting Date\" := WorkDate();\r\n<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; CustLedgerEntry.Insert();\r\n<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; end;\r\n<br>}\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</td></tr></tbody></table><p>If you are still fighting hard to find solutions, contact our <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-support-services/\">Dynamics 365 support partner</a> to help you fix the problem instantly. Get, Set, Go! \r\n</p><h2>3 Simple Methods to Modify Records in Business Central \r\n</h2><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/dev-itpro/developer/devenv-insert-modify-modifyall-delete-and-deleteall-methods\" target=\"_blank\">Insert, Modify or Delete</a> records in Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central when permissions are not allowed, following these easy to go methods: \r\n</p><p><b>1. By Making Use of an Extension \r\n</b></p><p>- Create a New Extension \r\n</p><ul><li>Open Visual Studio Code \r\n</li><li>Create a new AL project \r\n</li><li>Define a new table extension \r\n</li><li>Add fields and functions as required \r\n</li><li>Publish the extension \r\n</li></ul><p>- Insert or Modify a Record using the Extension \r\n</p><ul><li>Open Business Central \r\n</li><li>Go to the Extension Management page \r\n</li><li>Install the extension \r\n</li><li>Navigate to the desired record page \r\n</li><li>Use the extension to insert or modify the record \r\n</li></ul><p><b>2. By Making Use of Web Services \r\n</b></p><p>- Create a Web Service \r\n</p><ul><li>Open Business Central \r\n</li><li>Go to the Web Services page \r\n</li><li>Create a new web service \r\n</li><li>Define the required fields and functions \r\n</li><li>Publish the web service \r\n</li></ul><p>- Insert or Modify a Record using the Web Service \r\n</p><ul><li>Use a tool like Postman to send a POST or PUT request to the web service endpoint \r\n</li><li>Include the necessary data in the request body \r\n</li><li>The web service will insert or modify the record accordingly \r\n</li></ul><p><b>3. By Making Use of an Integration Platform \r\n</b></p><p>- Select an Integration Platform \r\n</p><ul><li>Research different integration platforms that are compatible with Microsoft Business Central \r\n</li><li>Consider factors such as ease of use, pricing, and available features \r\n</li><li>Choose the integration platform that best fits your needs \r\n</li></ul><p>- Configure the Integration Platform \r\n</p><ul><li>Set up the integration platform according to the provided instructions \r\n</li><li>Connect it to your Business Central instance \r\n</li><li>Define the necessary mappings and transformations \r\n</li></ul><p>- Insert or Modify a Record using the Integration Platform \r\n</p><ul><li>Use the integration platform\'s interface to insert or modify the record \r\n</li><li>Follow the platform\'s documentation for specific steps \r\n</li></ul><p><b>Did you Know?  \r\n</b></p><p>Microsoft has discontinued its support for Dynamics GP! Make a smooth <a href=\"/dynamics-gp-to-business-central-migration/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics GP to Business Central</a> migration today. \r\n</p><p>There are several methods via indirect permission to achieve the desired outcome when Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central&nbsp;does not allow direct permissions for inserting, deleting, or modifying data.</p><p>Utilizing extensions, web-based services, or connection platforms are some simple ways to effectively handle the data in Microsoft Dynamics Business Central (earlier known as <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-nav/\">Dynamics NAV</a>). With these techniques, you can experiment to see which one best suit your needs. \r\n</p><p>For more queries on which methods help to maintain the database by adding, modifying, and removing records, you can drop us an email at <a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a> or call us directly at <a href=\"http://+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"\">+1 281 899 0865</a>. Get in touch with your trusted <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/microsoft-dynamics-365-partner/\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a>.</p>', 'Insert-Delete-Modify Records in Business Central - 3 Smart Ways', 'business central', 'Efficient data management in Business Central: Learn 3 smart methods to Insert, Delete, and Modify records for optimized operations.', 'business central,dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics business central,dynamics nav,microsoft dynamics gp,microsoft dynamics erp', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1778000403744101.Insert-Delete-Modify Records in Business Central.png', 'Vivek Gururani', 'vivek.gururani@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/insert-delete-modify-records-in-business-central/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Insert-Delete-Modify Records in Business Central - 3 Smart Ways\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Efficient data management in Business Central: Learn 3 smart methods to Insert, Delete, and Modify records for optimized operations.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1778000517526497.Insert-Delete-Modify Records in Business Central.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Vivek Gururani\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Vivek-Gururani/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2023-09-25\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2023-09-25\"\r\n}', NULL, '01:56:18pm', '2023-09-25', '8 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 13:56:18');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(185, 'Top 10 KPIs for Measuring the Success of ERP Implementation', 'top-kpi-for-success-of-erp-implementation', 'ERP', 'erp', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1778823915674228.Top KPIs for Measuring the Success of ERP Implementation.png', 'We all know that a large expenditure goes into Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) implementation in an organization. So as an entrepreneur you would want to evaluate the success of the implementation for good return on investment (ROI).', '<p>We all know that a large expenditure goes into Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) implementation in an organization. So as an entrepreneur you would want to evaluate the success of the implementation for good return on investment (ROI).</p><p>Successful implementation of an ERP system can spur creativity and enhance a business\'s various aspects. For example, just imagine the benefit of all decision-makers being able to collaborate effectively on the cloud ERP with centralized data coming from numerous departments. \r\n</p><p>No matter where you are in your digital transformation, we are here for the guidance, perspective, questions, and resources to help your <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation</a> succeed. \r\n</p><h2>How to Evaluate the Success of ERP Implementation? \r\n</h2><p>It\'s important to consider other factors in addition to deployment speed when evaluating an ERP implementation\'s effectiveness. While a successful implementation is a good start, an ERP system doesn\'t start to provide value until it is used in streamlining company operations. Measuring advancements in the ten KPIs mentioned below helps reveal such organizational workflow improvements over time. \r\n</p><p>Answers to the questions below can also assist business managers in determining the worth of a recent ERP implementation in addition to those KPIs:  \r\n</p><ul><li>Which operational procedures saw a quick improvement? Which was hampered, and how was it resolved? \r\n</li><li>Has the ERP system lived up to all the goals established for it before the installation process started? \r\n</li><li>Do company managers observe an overall decline in errors? decisions that are better? \r\n</li><li>Customer satisfaction and relations have they improved? \r\n</li><li>Have workers made use of the ERP system in their daily activities? \r\n</li><li>Has business growth started to pick up speed? \r\n</li><li>Do corporate processes feel more unified or less dispersed overall? \r\n</li><li>Are corporate executives more content and relaxed post the deployment of ERP? \r\n</li></ul><p>These questions will have some subjective answers, and some may take some time to become evident. However, by combining these with the KPIs that are more immediately measurable, business managers should gain a clear understanding of the value their new ERP system is bringing to the company. \r\n</p><p>To further track the progress and get answers to any of the above questions, contact our <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-support-services/\">Dynamics 365 support partner</a> for instant solutions. \r\n</p><h2>Top 10 KPIs for ERP Implementation \r\n</h2><p>Here’s a select set of key performance indicators (KPIs) that can assist you in proving the viability of the new system. \r\n</p><p>Companies benefit from their ERP systems for a considerable amount of time. Therefore, it\'s critical to monitor both short- and long-term KPIs that will collectively gauge how the business is progressing toward its strategic goals.</p><p>Following the completion of an ERP implementation, monitoring changes in the following KPIs can assist a business in gauging its success and/or determining where it may wish to make further adjustments to its ERP strategy. \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Real Time Data</b></h3><p>Gaining a consistent view of people, performance, and technology throughout a company depends on real-time data. For decision-makers to base their goals and plans on the same information, regardless of where they sit in the organization, a successful ERP deployment should create better, more precise information about business operations and procedures and consolidate that information. \r\n</p><h3><b>2. Accurate Forecasting of Demands</b></h3><p>Predicting demand KPIs demonstrate how accurately a company can forecast future demand for its goods and services. For instance, to prevent stockouts or over-ordering, a chain of grocery stores has to estimate the things that its customers will buy at different times of the year.</p><p>High forecast accuracy is provided by a well-configured ERP solution, which enables businesses to anticipate demand based on a combination of historical data and present-day signs. For example, an impending event, like thanksgiving or a significant storm, or a general economic trend, such as shortfall in the supply chain.   \r\n</p><h3><b>3. System Performance</b></h3><p>This KPI gauges the ERP system\'s reliability and efficiency following its adoption. It considers elements like system availability, response times, and uptime. To ensure efficient operations and user happiness, an ERP system must be reliable and high performing. \r\n</p><h3><b>4. Customer Experience</b></h3><p>Customers, as well as internal and external stakeholders, may be impacted by ERP implementations. By monitoring comments, grievances, and other customer satisfaction indicators, this KPI tracks customer satisfaction levels.</p><p>High customer satisfaction scores show that the ERP system is fulfilling consumer needs, raising service standards, and improving the entire customer experience. \r\n</p><h3><b>5. Project Margins</b></h3><p>Project margins are used to calculate how much a company makes in project-based industries like construction after deducting its costs for supplies, labor, and overhead.</p><p>A company needs to keep track of several data, such as cost estimates and budgets, project expenses, and revenue the project generates, to effectively calculate project margins. To provide businesses with a complete picture of income and costs for each project, the best <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\">Microsoft Dynamics ERP</a> systems combine data on all these variables. \r\n</p><h3><b>6. IT Spending</b></h3><p>Metrics for IT spending assist firms in getting the most value out of their technological investments at the lowest possible cost. The complexity of legacy systems and procedures, which inevitably produce inefficiencies and unneeded expenses, is especially difficult for more established businesses.</p><p>At the corporate or user level, an ERP can monitor costs for hardware, software, and cloud subscriptions. With our <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/erp-implementation-cost-calculator/\" target=\"_blank\">ERP implementation cost calculator</a>, businesses can accurately estimate their implementation expenses and identify areas to optimize costs, helping them improve and consolidate their systems without compromising performance.</p><h3><b>7. Inventory Turnover</b></h3><p>Inventory turnover shows how many items are sold over a certain period. A producer of white-label computer displays, for instance, would aim to sell 5,000 units every week. An ERP system will track its development after a successful implementation, giving visibility into inventory operations and showing how it can move things more swiftly. \r\n</p><p>Additionally, it aids in preventing losses from overstocking and improving demand forecasting based on market behavior. Manufacturers must establish precise inventory performance ratios to enhance production without compromising efficiency in their warehouses, which makes inventory turnover of particular importance to them. \r\n</p><h3><b>8. Schedule Adherence</b></h3><p>Scheduling KPIs, as their name suggests, assist businesses in monitoring production rates in relation to their production schedules to make sure they don\'t lag or skip important deadlines. A milestone for a toy company might be producing and delivering twice as many of its hottest games in time for the Black Friday shopping frenzy.</p><p>The launch of a software vendor\'s most recent product upgrade could follow a rigid production schedule. An ERP system makes scheduling simpler by giving teams insight into potential disruptions and a clear picture of how manufacturing and production processes are progressing in relation to deadlines. \r\n</p><h3><b>9. Employee Experience</b></h3><p>A successful ERP deployment can measure employee engagement and satisfaction even though it is not a precisely quantifiable statistic like ROI or revenue. Higher levels of productivity or employee retention, as well as a rise in sales, are all indicators of satisfaction and engagement, which are all positive signs for a company\'s financial health.</p><p>An ERP, on the other hand, can demonstrate when KPIs are heading in the wrong direction, giving a company the knowledge necessary to identify and resolve any possible problems as soon as they arise. Additionally, doing so can aid in maintaining the investments made in employee morale and training. \r\n</p><h3><b>10. Return on Investment and Sales</b></h3><p>ERP implementations can be expensive, thus calculating the ROI is crucial to determining the project\'s success. This KPI compares the costs associated with adopting and maintaining the ERP system to the financial gains resulting from its deployment, such as higher revenue, cost reductions, and enhanced profitability. A high ROI shows that the ERP implementation has produced the anticipated financial gains.</p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Revenue and sales metrics show how much money a company has made through the sale of its goods and services over a certain time frame, as well as how that changes over larger time frames, such as quarter over quarter and year over year.</p><p>Average profit per item sold, operating margin, and average order value are common metrics in this area. Companies may identify their greatest revenue development possibilities and receive insight into areas where they can improve efficiency to reduce operating costs with the help of a correctly implemented ERP and the appropriate KPIs. When combined, these kinds of data can boost sales and profit margins. \r\n</p><p>ERP implementations need effort, commitment, and support from teams across the numerous departments of the organization. Although the article\'s list of KPIs is not exhaustive, companies can ensure a successful adoption by concentrating on these ten-performance metrics.  \r\n</p><p>While it may be alluring to focus only on ROI and revenue, businesses may achieve demonstrable ERP installation benefits and position themselves for long-term success by improving the customer experience, internal operations, and workplace culture. \r\n</p><p>For more assistance in ERP Implementation, you can drop us an email at <a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a> or call us directly at <a href=\"tel:+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"\">+1 281 899 0865</a>. Get in touch with your trusted <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a>.</p>', 'Top 10 KPIs for Measuring the Success of ERP Implementation', 'erp implementation', 'Learn about the critical KPIs for evaluating the success of an ERP implementation. Read more regarding the top 10 performance metrics.', 'dynamics erp,microsoft dynamics erp,erp implementation,dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics 365 finance and operations,dynamics 365 implementation,microsoft dynamics 365 partner', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1778823915674234.Top KPIs for Measuring the Success of ERP Implementation.png', 'Arish Siddiqui', 'arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/top-kpi-for-success-of-erp-implementation/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Top 10 KPIs for Measuring the Success of ERP Implementation\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Learn about the critical KPIs for evaluating the success of an ERP implementation. Read more regarding the top 10 performance metrics.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1778823958753030.Top KPIs for Measuring the Success of ERP Implementation.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Madhushree Agarwal\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Madhushree-Agarwal/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2023-10-04\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2023-10-04\"\r\n}', NULL, '09:51:28pm', '2023-10-04', '8 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-01-30 21:51:28'),
(187, 'Top 7 Supply Chain Challenges That Business Central Overcomes', 'top-supply-chain-challenges-that-business-central-overcomes', 'Business central', 'business-central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1780907186066740.png', 'With constant changes in the dynamic environment of supply chain logistics, organizations can face unforeseen challenges to both profitability and productivity. Businesses are rapidly adopting agile methodologies to strategize the way they operate.', '<p>With constant changes in the dynamic environment of supply chain logistics, organizations can face unforeseen challenges to both profitability and productivity. Businesses are rapidly adopting agile methodologies to strategize the way they operate.</p><p>However, there is room for everyone to sustain their business by remaining highly competitive, with the right tools and technologies. <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> is a powerful all-in-one platform that helps small and mid-sized businesses to navigate the supply chain issues.</p><p>In this article, we will explore the top seven supply chain challenges that can be overcome by Business Central.</p><blockquote><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Contact our experts for user-friendly overview of faster yet secure ways to interact with data in Business Central.</b></a></blockquote><h2>Top 7 Supply Chain Challenges\r\n</h2><p>Companies are being thrown off balance by fundamental shifts in markets, supply networks, and customer behavior. Major challenges faced by supply chains globally, include the following. Let\'s look how each challenge can be overcome by dynamics 365 business central:</p><h3>1. Data Compliance\r\n</h3><p>Data compliance and its traceability are two crucial aspects of <a href=\"/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</a>. A variety of data are frequently exchanged throughout supply chains, including delivery routes, client information, financial data, and product specifications.</p><p>Moreover, businesses frequently have trouble keeping track of their products along the supply chain, guaranteeing the quality and safety of their products, and adhering to legal regulations. Any supply chain\'s success depends on the preservation of this delicate and sometimes quite important data.</p><h3>2. Demand Forecasting\r\n</h3><p>Companies are being thrown off balance by fundamental shifts in markets, supply networks, and customer behavior. Major challenges faced by supply chains globally, include the following.</p><p>Demand forecasting is essential to supply chain management because it enables businesses to foresee market trends, make informed decisions, and maximize their available resources. For most firms, however, understanding the complexity of demand forecasting may be an overwhelming and time-consuming effort.</p><p>Globalization and geopolitical factors, changing buyer preferences, and an ever-greater dependence on data expose organizations with several difficulties in forecasting demand.</p><p>Moreover, inaccurate demand forecasting can lead to overstocking or stockouts, resulting in lost sales and increased costs.\r\n</p><h3>3. Inventory Holding Cost\r\n</h3><p>One of the biggest expenses a business has in reaching targeted service levels is inventory holding costs. 15–30% of the overall inventory value is considered a reasonable baseline for inventory holding costs. These costs are primarily divided into four categories:</p><ul><li><b>Capital\r\n</b></li></ul><p>Purchase-related expenses, financing charges, and interest rates on loans for purchases are all considered capital costs.</p><ul><li><b>Service\r\n</b></li></ul><p>Investments in software, technology, taxes, insurance, labor costs to provide these services, etc. are all considered service costs.</p><ul><li><b>Storage\r\n</b></li></ul><p>Rent, overhead, opportunity costs for storage, safety inventory levels, and other considerations are included in storage expenses.</p><ul><li><b>Inventory Risk Costs\r\n</b></li></ul><p>Shrinkage, obsolescence, and the possibility of unanticipated events causing harm to inventory into consideration.<img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1780907098256274.inventory-holding-costs-chart.jpeg\" style=\"width: 100%;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: center; \"><b>Source: latentview</b></p><p>An example representation of the inventory holding costs for a retailer<br></p><h3>4. Planning and Replenishment Process \r\n</h3><p>Your replenishment and planning process becomes more complicated with each new location and channel. You must be forecasting demand for each shop and channel independently, as opposed to predicting demand for one store and a small number of SKUs.</p><p><b>There are several factors specific to each channel and location that will affect your replenishment, such as: \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Demographics \r\n</li><li>Consumer Preferences \r\n</li><li>Local Competitors \r\n</li><li>Product Seasonality \r\n</li><li>Distance to a Distribution Centre \r\n</li><li>Shipping Time \r\n</li><li>Shipping Cost \r\n</li></ul><h3>5. End-to-End Visibility \r\n</h3><p>A major difficulty for many firms is supply chain management (SCM), which is intricate, time-consuming, and occasionally frustratingly opaque. Obtaining the best return on investment (ROI) necessitates firms, no matter how big or small, to balance spend activities, logistics, risk management, and supplier relationships.</p><p>Unfortunately, without end-to-end supply chain visibility, one or more of those balls might fall off, which will have <b>expensive repercussions</b>. \r\n</p><h3>6. Costly Supply Chain Operations \r\n</h3><p>Profit margins are being squeezed as expenses rise across the whole supply chain network. There are numerous sources of these costs, and a lack of transparency and accountability for cutting them, lead to an <b>increase in operating costs</b>. The primary contributors of rising expenses are: \r\n</p><ul><li>Growing cost of fuel for products transportation by air, sea, or road \r\n</li><li>The rising cost of raw materials due to rising commodity prices. \r\n</li><li>Increased labor expenses from manufacturers and suppliers \r\n</li><li>Intricate global logistics resulting in increased costs for product management, storage, and transportation \r\n</li></ul><h3>7. Increased Demand for Transportation of Goods \r\n</h3><p>In the years plagued by pandemics, the e-commerce sector has grown at a rate never seen before. In addition, companies now serve a worldwide clientele rather than just the local one.</p><p>The need for the transportation of completed goods and raw materials has grown as a result. With consequent <b>shortage of raw materials</b> and increased demand for transportation of goods, leading to delays at ports. \r\n</p><h2>How Business Central Overcomes Supply Chain Challenges \r\n</h2><p>With its highly adaptable and rich features, Dynamics 365 Business Central is a complete business management solution to streamline all your supply chain challenges.</p><p>It is a user-friendly ERP, that is fast to implement, easy to configure and enables companies to manage finance, sales, shipping, project management, warehousing, inventory and more. \r\n</p><h3>1. Meets Supply Chain Expectations</h3><p>Supply chain management-focused businesses must overcome several obstacles, including managing several warehouses, selling through multiple channels, and using <b>logistics tools to track shipments</b>.</p><p>Customers want services to be more immediate and of higher quality, and businesses must live up to these expectations. With Microsoft Dynamics Business Central and its supply chain management tools, the planning, purchasing, inventory, warehouse, and sales functions can be operated effectively, providing clients with goods or services on time.</p><h3>2. Offers Supplier Collaboration \r\n</h3><p>Effective collaboration with suppliers is essential for a smooth and efficient supply chain. However, many businesses struggle to establish seamless communication channels, share information, and coordinate activities with their suppliers. \r\n</p><p>Business Central offers robust supplier management capabilities, allowing businesses to streamline communication, track supplier performance, and manage procurement processes effectively.</p><p>With integrated communication tools, automated workflows, and real-time supplier visibility, Microsoft Business Central enables businesses to establish strong relationships with their suppliers, improve collaboration, and drive supply chain efficiency. \r\n</p><h3>3. Automates Time-consuming Processes \r\n</h3><p>Manual and time-consuming processes can hinder the agility and responsiveness of a supply chain. Tasks such as order processing, inventory management, and production planning often involve manual data entry, paper-based documentation, and repetitive tasks, which are prone to errors and delays. \r\n</p><p>Business Central automates key supply chain processes, eliminating manual data entry and streamlining operations. By leveraging <b>intelligent workflows</b>, <b>barcode scanning</b>, and <b>integration with IoT devices</b>, Business Central enables businesses to automate repetitive tasks, reduce errors, and improve overall efficiency. \r\n</p><h3>4. Simplifies Multi-location Management \r\n</h3><p>Managing multiple locations in a supply chain can be challenging, as each location may have different stock management procedures, product offerings, and accounting rules. Coordinating activities and maintaining consistency across different locations can be time-consuming and complex. \r\n</p><p>Business Central simplifies multi-location management by providing a <b>centralized platform for inventory management</b>, <b>order processing</b>, and <b>financial reporting</b>. With configurable processes, <b>automated workflows</b>, and real-time data synchronization, D365 Business Central helps businesses streamline operations across multiple locations, ensuring consistency and efficiency. \r\n</p><h3>5. Mitigates Supply Chain Disruptions and Manages Cost \r\n</h3><p>Supply chain disruptions, such as natural disasters, pandemics, or political unrest, can have a significant impact on business operations. These disruptions can disrupt the flow of goods, cause delays, and increase costs. \r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Microsoft Dynamics Business Central</a> helps businesses mitigate supply chain disruptions by providing <b>real-time visibility into inventory levels</b>, <b>production capacities</b>, and <b>transportation routes</b>.</p><p>With this visibility, businesses can proactively identify potential disruptions, develop contingency plans, and make informed decisions to minimize the impact of disruptions on their supply chains. \r\n</p><h3>6. Leverages Data Analytics and Insights \r\n</h3><p>Data analytics and insights play a crucial role in optimizing supply chain performance. However, many businesses struggle to extract meaningful insights from their data due to limited analytics capabilities and disconnected systems. \r\n</p><p>Business Central leverages advanced analytics and reporting capabilities to provide businesses with actionable insights into their supply chains. With <b>pre-built dashboards</b>, <b>customizable reports</b>, and <b>AI-powered analytics</b>, Business Central helps businesses identify trends, spot opportunities for improvement, and drive data-informed decision-making. \r\n</p><p>Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central offers a comprehensive solution to overcome the exhaustive supply chain challenges faced by businesses today.</p><p>With its end-to-end visibility, demand forecasting capabilities, supplier collaboration tools, process automation, multi-location management features, and advanced analytics, Business Central empowers businesses to optimize their supply chain operations, improve efficiency, and drive growth.</p><p>By leveraging the power of Business Central, organizations can navigate the complexities of supply chain management with confidence and stay ahead in today\'s competitive business landscape. \r\n</p><p>Streamline your supply chain and boost profitability with Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central. You can drop us an email at <a href=\"harsh.nager@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"\">harsh.nager@dynamicssquare.com</a> or call us directly at <a href=\"http://+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"\">+1 281 899 0865</a>. Get in touch with your trusted <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" style=\"background-color: white; font-family: sans-serif; font-weight: 400;\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a> today!</p>', 'Top 7 Supply Chain Challenges That Business Central Overcomes', 'supply chain challenges', 'Check out our top 7 list to learn how Business Central overcomes supply chain obstacles. Simplify processes with ease. Examine right away!', 'business central,dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics business central,microsoft business central,supply chain management,dynamics 365 supply chain management', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1780907186068529.png', 'Arish Siddiqui', 'arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/top-supply-chain-challenges-that-business-central-overcomes/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Top 7 Supply Chain Challenges That Business Central Overcomes\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Check out our top 7 list to learn how Business Central overcomes supply chain obstacles. Simplify processes with ease. Examine right away!\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1780901889623789.Supply Chain Challenges That Business Central Overcomes.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Arish Siddiqui\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Arish-Siddiqui/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2023-10-27\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2023-10-27\"\r\n}', NULL, '02:15:28pm', '2023-11-18', '9 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 14:15:28'),
(188, 'A Complete Guide to Migrate from Microsoft Dynamics NAV to Business Central', 'process-to-migrate-dynamics-nav-to-business-central', 'Dynamics Nav', 'dynamics-nav', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1782623598331566.Dynamics NAV to Business Central.jpg', 'Microsoft Dynamics NAV has been a lifesaver for small and medium-sized businesses, providing a simple yet powerful ERP solution.', '<p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-nav/\">Microsoft Dynamics NAV</a> has been a lifesaver for small and medium-sized businesses, providing a simple yet powerful ERP solution. It enabled businesses to create a centralized operations hub across various departments, including manufacturing, supply chain, sales, and finance.</p><p>Collating all the business information into one place allowed enterprises to generate insights and analytics for better productivity and profitability. However, with emerging technologies like cloud computing making inroads into mainstream industries, Nav\'s solution has become obsolete. \r\n</p><p>Organizations are keen to migrate NAV to Business Central to maximize the advantages that the robust ERP solution has to offer. Business Central comes with a lot of modern and advanced capabilities, which is attracting quite a few companies to shift to it.</p><p>Let’s quickly understand the differences between NAV and Business Central to learn if you should opt for a NAV upgrade.\r\n</p><h2>Why Migrate from Dynamics NAV to Business Central?</h2>\r\n<p>Quick Comparison of Dynamics NAV and Microsoft Business Central Features for Migration Decision:</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n</p><p></p><table><thead>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">Aspect</span></th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">Dynamics NAV</span></th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:700;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">Business Central</span></th>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">User Interface</span></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">Clunky UI with a learning curve</span></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">Simpler UI for easy accessibility</span></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">Deployment</span></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">On-prem solution, limited to designated devices</span></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">Cloud deployment for access anywhere, any device</span></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">Scalability</span></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">Limited adaptability to market needs</span></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">Greater scalability to adapt to changing business ops</span></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">Integrations</span></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">Supports only standard integrations</span></td>\r\n    <td class=\"tg-0lax\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">Seamless integrations with AI/ML capabilities</span></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">Infrastructure</span></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">Requires specific operating systems, hardware solutions</span></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;color:#000;background-color:transparent\">Browser-based platform, reducing operational costs</span></td></tr></tbody></table><ul><li>Migration of NAV to Dynamics 365 offers a range of benefits, including:\r\n</li><ul><li>Reduced IT costs\r\n</li><li>Tighter data security\r\n</li><li>Accelerated innovation</li></ul></ul><p><b>Additional Insight:</b></p><p>Both Business Central and NAV are centralized data hubs. However, Dynamics 365 Business Central provides insights across all devices from a single screen.\r\n</p><p>With Microsoft offering a SaaS model for D365 Business Central, it has become appealing for emerging businesses to save IT costs with advanced functionalities. If you have decided to migrate Navision to Business Central and are worried about the complexity of doing so, here’s a list of simple steps.</p><p>Read more: <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-business-central-implementation/\" target=\"_blank\">Business Central Implementation</a></p><p>\r\n</p><h2>Steps to Migrate NAV to Business Central \r\n</h2><p>Follow the easy 9-step process to successfully migrate Dynamics NAV to the Dynamics 365 suite and unlock access to several advanced features.\r\n</p><h3>1. Assess and Plan your Existing NAV Migration</h3><p>As the very first step, you need to understand your existing ERP usage, limitations, and benefits with Dynamics NAV. You can compare these to the capabilities of Microsoft Dynamics Business Central to get a fair idea of the new platform\'s scope. It will help you design a strategy to maximize the upgraded ERP version.\r\n</p><h3>2. Identify the Data to Migrate</h3><p>Get a detailed overview of the existing data in your Dynamics NAV environment like master data, transactional data, and historical records. It will help you prioritize the data that needs to be migrated to Business Central.</p><h3>3. Ensure the Hygiene of your Data\r\n</h3><p>Once you get an outlay of the data available in the existing ERP system, you need to run a hygiene check through it all. This step is necessary to ensure that no duplicates or errors scrawl into the <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> environment. It gives you confidence that the data on the platform is accurate and complete.\r\n</p><h3>4. Have a Full Data Backup during Migration\r\n</h3><p>Even before you begin migration, it is critical that you backup all of your data in your Dynamics NAV database. Securing your business data will soften the damage that may arise from any unexpected disruptions when you migrate NAV to Business Central.\r\n</p><h3>5. Uninstall Unnecessary Extensions or Plugins\r\n</h3><p>Ensure you remove all the unnecessary plugins, as it may complicate your migration process. It is because these plugins may not be compatible with Business Central. You can enhance your experience with Microsoft Dynamics Business Central by eliminating the redundant burden of adding to simple management.\r\n</p><h3>6. Compile NAV Objects\r\n</h3><p>When migrating from <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-nav-to-business-central/\">Dynamics NAV to Business Central</a>, you must compile NAV objects to ensure their integrity. Compiling the objects allows you to identify and fix underlying errors and mistakes that may crop up during migration.\r\n</p><h3>7. Upgrade your NAV Solution\r\n</h3><p>If you are using an older version of NAV, it may not be compatible with migrating data to Business Central. You will have to upgrade to a more recent <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-nav/\">Dynamics NAV</a> version for a smooth migration.\r\n</p><h3>8. Test the Migration\r\n</h3><p>To ensure the success of migration, conduct thorough testing of data and functionality once you migrate Dynamics NAV to Business Central.\r\n</p><h3>9. Conduct Training Sessions for Users\r\n</h3><p>The move from one ERP system to another will always lead to confusion and frustration. Having been used to NAV, your team may find it challenging to adapt to Microsoft Business Central initially. To ease the transition, you must provide proper training sessions on capabilities that are available to them, along with timely support.\r\n</p><p>These 9 simple steps will help you migrate Dynamics Navision to Dynamics 365 without hiccups or bottlenecks. The latest ERP platform will enhance your efficiency once your team gets comfortable with the new features and processes.\r\n</p><h2>Make Migration Seamless with Dynamics Square\r\n</h2><p>The journey to migrate Dynamics NAV to Business Central is simple but can soon turn into a nightmare if not properly executed. You will have to overcome challenges like compiling issues and data duplication, which could become more complicated. Enterprises must ensure that the migration process stays on track despite these roadblocks.\r\n</p><p>The ideal way to approach migration is to collaborate with a leading <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a> like Dynamics Square. With nearly two decades of experience and 150+ Microsoft Certified Professionals, the US-based service provider has catered to the migration requirements of 100s small and medium-sized businesses.</p><p>We also provide personalized training sessions to enable your team to utilize new features and processes for improved efficiency.</p><p>Our team has wide expertise in the <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 suite</a> and experience in implementing tailored strategies based on unique business needs. Let Dynamics Square experts help you through your migration process. <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" style=\"background-color: white; font-family: sans-serif; font-weight: 400;\">Contact us today</a>.</p>', 'Process to Migrate Microsoft Dynamics NAV to Business Central', 'dynamics nav to business central', 'Effortlessly migrate Microsoft Dynamics NAV to Business Central with our step-by-step guide. Unlock advanced features and streamline your operations.', 'dynamics nav,microsoft dynamics nav,business central,dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics 365 business central,dynamics nav to business central migration', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1782623598331573.Dynamics NAV to Business Central.jpg', 'Arish Siddiqui', 'arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/process-to-migrate-dynamics-nav-to-business-central/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Process to Migrate Microsoft Dynamics NAV to Business Central\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Effortlessly migrate Microsoft Dynamics NAV to Business Central with our step-by-step guide. Unlock advanced features and streamline your operations.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1782623555441971.Dynamics NAV to Business Central.jpg\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Harsh Nager\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Harsh-Nager/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2023-11-15\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2023-11-15\"\r\n}', NULL, '06:46:24pm', '2023-11-22', '7 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-11-13 18:46:24');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(190, 'Everything You Need to Know About Microsoft Dynamics NAV', 'everything-know-about-microsoft-dynamics-nav', 'Dynamics Nav', 'dynamics-nav', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1782826494465169.jpg', 'Discover Microsoft Dynamics NAV (Navision) ERP, a flexible business management solution that streamlines operations, financials, and supply chain for SMBs.', '<p>Process efficiency sits at the core of business profitability through proper decision-making and better productivity. Enterprises rely primarily on the data to guide them through the dynamic market demands. It helps them enhance their day-to-day processes through insights and predictions into various operations from manufacturing to distribution.</p><p>The challenge, however, lies in consolidating all the business-critical data in one place for valuable insights. This is precisely where <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-nav/\">Microsoft Dynamics NAV</a> helps. It helps businesses eliminate data silos, operational blockheads and integrates your multiple teams for seamless collaboration.\r\n</p><p>In this article, we will explore everything you need to know to start with Dynamics NAV.</p>\r\n<div class=\"blog-content-container\">\r\n    <div class=\"blog-content active\">\r\n    <h4 class=\"blog-content-title\">&nbsp;Table of Content</h4>\r\n    <div class=\"inner\">\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-is-microsoft-dynamics-nav\">1. What is Microsoft Dynamics NAV? </a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Benefits-of-microsoft-dynamics-nav\">2. Benefits of Microsoft Dynamics NAV</a> \r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-does-dynamics-nav-do\">3. What does Dynamics NAV do?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Evolution-of-microsoft-dynamics-erp\">4. Evolution of Microsoft Dynamics ERP </a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Make-microsoft-dynamics-nav-your-own-with-the-right-implementation\">5. Make Microsoft Dynamics NAV your own with the right Implementation</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n   <button class=\"blog-content-toggle\"> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"><!--! Font Awesome Free 6.4.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license (Commercial License) Copyright 2023 Fonticons, Inc. --><path d=\"M201.4 342.6c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0l160-160c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0L224 274.7 86.6 137.4c-12.5-12.5-32.8-12.5-45.3 0s-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160z\"></path></svg></button>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 id=\"What-is-microsoft-dynamics-nav\">What is Microsoft Dynamics NAV?\r\n</h2><p>MS Dynamics NAV is a robust enterprise resource planning (ERP) platform built to help businesses manage their end-to-end processes from one place. It centralizes all your business operations into one cohesive platform to streamline daily happenings.\r\n</p><p>It provides a unified hub to consolidate your financial data, manufacturing processes, sales, supply chain activities, inventory details, and customer interaction. It gathers all the business-critical data to help you make insights-driven decisions for profitability and operational efficiency.</p><p><b>Check Also</b>: <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.co.uk/blog/why-microsoft-dynamics-nav-used-for/\" target=\"_blank\">Why Microsoft Dynamics NAV used for?</a></p><p>\r\n</p><p>Some of its key benefits are listed below.\r\n</p><h2 id=\"Benefits-of-microsoft-dynamics-nav\">Benefits of Microsoft Dynamics NAV\r\n</h2><p>MS Dynamics NAV empowers you to efficiently manage your operations across departments, including accounts, manufacturing, supply chain, warehouse, and customer service, to improve productivity and enhance data management.\r\n</p><ul><li>It gives you all the capabilities to handle your business accounts, finance reports, budget planning, and cash flow management.\r\n</li><li>With Microsoft NAV, you can optimize inventory management by minimizing carrying costs and ensuring you have enough stock to meet dynamic customer demands.\r\n</li><li><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-support-services/\">Microsoft Navision supports</a> you in creating a strong sales discipline by automating sales management, including lead tracking and managing customer interactions.\r\n</li><li>It allows you to generate insightful reports through an intuitive dashboard so that you can stay on top of your business operations and make data-driven decisions.\r\n</li><li>Dynamics NAV can be customized to suit your business use case so that you can maximize its capabilities. It is also configurable for scalability and other changes as and when required.\r\n</li><li>Dynamics 365 Business Central offers you the flexibility of multiple deployment options in the cloud and on-prem.\r\n</li><li>Through a Microsoft Dynamics 365 partner like Dynamics Square, you have access to reliable vendor support for NAV implementation, updates, and other development needs.\r\n</li></ul><p>Below we discuss some of the core features that make the NAV <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\">ERP system</a> a must-have for companies with a primary goal of streamlining their processes for overall efficiency.\r\n</p><h2 id=\"What-does-dynamics-nav-do\">What does Dynamics NAV do?\r\n</h2><h3>1. Financial Management\r\n</h3><p>With Microsoft Dynamics NAV, enterprises gain better control over business accounts and cash flow which helps them maintain financial hygiene. Further, you can use this information to identify customer behavior and market trends. It allows you to \r\n</p><ul><li>Maintain and analyze your financial data\r\n</li><li>Keep track of your payables and receivables\r\n</li><li>Manage the health of your cash flow\r\n</li><li>Ensure compliance with tax regulations\r\n</li></ul><h3>2. Supply Chain Management\r\n</h3><p>A major chunk of your supply management activities, like managing inventory, reporting stock details, and planning distribution routes, can be automated using Microsoft Navision. All of these activities that become operational overhead can be automated to\r\n</p><ul><li>Improve order fulfilment rate with optimal inventory levels\r\n</li><li>Eliminate bottlenecks in procurement workflow\r\n</li><li>Streamline order management, pricing, and deliveries\r\n</li></ul><h3>3. Manufacturing\r\n</h3><p>In setting uninterrupted manufacturing flow, Dynamics NAV helps you draw up realistic production plans to optimize costs, enforce consistent instructions, and manage resources for enhanced productivity. For manufacturing, the NAV ERP platform allows you to\r\n</p><ul><li>Manage product assembly instructions and BOM (Bill of Materials).\r\n</li><li>Control manufacturing progress through data-driven plans\r\n</li></ul><h3>4. Reporting and Analytics\r\n</h3><p>Dynamics NAV allows you to collect and analyze business data, such as sales numbers, purchase orders, operational costs, and budgets, to identify trends and customer behavior that will help in forecasting growth rates.\r\n</p><ul><li>Customize your reports to unlock insights for a specific use case.\r\n</li><li>Generate granular analysis reports and visualizations through <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">Power BI integration</a>.\r\n</li></ul><h3>5. Project Management</h3><p>You can perform common project management tasks like assigning jobs to resources, setting task schedules, managing budget allocations, and monitoring progress.\r\n</p><ul><li>Configure, assign, and track the progress of jobs from one place\r\n</li><li>Manage HR operations such as employee information management\r\n</li><li>Optimize expenditures and other cost-related operations\r\n</li></ul><h3>6. Workflow Automation</h3><p>MS Navision eliminates delays and mistakes in your daily operations by automating several tasks like approvals and notifications by assigning conditions and associated actions. \r\n</p><ul><li>Increase efficiency by automating repetitive tasks\r\n</li><li>Keep track of progress by configuring reminders\r\n</li></ul><h2 id=\"Evolution-of-microsoft-dynamics-erp\">Evolution of Microsoft Dynamics ERP\r\n</h2><p>Microsoft NAV has a history underscored by multiple upgrades and enhancements to make it a solid ERP platform. It was first launched in 1984 as Navision by a Danish software firm.</p><p>It was built to simplify finance management for small and medium-sized businesses. Microsoft acquired Navision software to create its ERP platform. Navision was rebranded as Microsoft Dynamics NAV in 2004.\r\n</p><p>Over time, Microsoft Navision saw new capabilities like RTC (role-tailored client) for user-specific interface and seamless access through web browsers.\r\n</p><p>Microsoft added Navision software to its Dynamics 365 ecosystem as Business Central and offered a cloud-based ERP solution. With this, businesses could choose from two deployment options for their ERP platform - on-prem or cloud. \r\n</p><p>The constant refinement of Navision software to turn it into a holistic Dynamics 365 Business Central solution has made it a go-to ERP option for many enterprises. \r\n</p><h3>Business Central vs. Navision\r\n</h3><p>Dynamics NAV and Business Central are more or less the same ERP platform. However, Microsoft\'s advancements in Business Central make it a part of the <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 suite</a>. Below are some of the differences between these two ERP systems:\r\n</p><ul><li><b>Deployment Options:</b> Dynamics NAV is traditionally an on-premises solution, which means the software is deployed on the company’s private servers. Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central, however, offers cloud-based deployment to extend SaaS-based experience to customers. \r\n</li><li><b>Licensing Model:</b> For the NAV solution, you need to buy a license upfront in a perpetual model, while <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> offers a subscription-based pricing model.\r\n</li><li><b>Update and Release Cycle:</b> Dynamics NAV represents a typical enterprise solution with fewer and less frequent upgrades or feature updates. The Business Central constantly enhances the platform with improvements and features through a regular update cycle.\r\n</li><li><b>Dynamics 365 Integration:</b> Although a product of Microsoft, Navision is a standalone solution. That’s not the case with Microsoft Dynamics Business Central. It offers seamless integration with the Dynamics 365 ecosystem, enabling CRM like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM</a> and AI-driven functionalities.\r\n</li><li><b>UI Adaptability:</b> While Dynamics NAV has a classic but old-fashioned client interface, Business Central provides a role-specific and customizable UI.\r\n</li><li><b>Platform Target:</b> Dynamics NAV is designed to cater to the operational needs of small and medium-sized businesses. Microsoft Business Central is a relatively modern SaaS-based ERP platform for new-age enterprises.\r\n</li></ul><p>Regardless of how it fairs against Dynamics Business Central, Dynamics NAV remains a popular choice for small and medium-sized companies. It gives enterprises a comprehensive solution to handle their entire operations from a centralized platform. It breaks down departmental silos so that you can efficiently use data to drive your profitability.</p><p><b>See Also</b> - <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.co.uk/dynamics-nav-to-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics NAV To Business Central Upgrade</a></p><p>\r\n</p><h2 id=\"Make-microsoft-dynamics-nav-your-own-with-the-right-implementation\">Make Microsoft Dynamics NAV your own with the right Implementation\r\n</h2><p>More than a value-added ERP platform, MS Dynamics NAV is an essential tool for enterprises today. One of its core advantages is the ability to tailor the solution to suit specific business requirements.</p><p>You can do that through automated workflows and integrations. However, it is easier said than done. For successful implementation of Dynamics Navision, you will need the expertise of <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a>&nbsp;like Dynamics Square.\r\n</p><p>Our expertise in configuring NAV solutions for small and mid-sized businesses spans decades with over 500 customers. With our expertise, you will have a tailor-made Dynamics NAV platform that your team can easily adapt to from day one.\r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Contact us</a> for more information.</p>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"image-viewer\" style=\"display: none;\">\r\n  <span class=\"close\">×</span>\r\n  <img class=\"modal-content\" id=\"full-image\">\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">// <![CDATA[\r\nconst buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n\r\nbuttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n    button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n  );\r\n});\r\n// ]]></script>\r\n<style>\r\n/* The Modal (background) */\r\n#image-viewer {\r\n  display: none;\r\n  position: fixed;\r\n  z-index: 999;\r\n  padding: 70px;\r\n  left: 0;\r\n  top: 0;\r\n  width: 100%;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  overflow: auto;\r\n  background-color: rgb(0,0,0);\r\n  background-color: rgba(45, 62, 80, 0.99);\r\n}\r\n.modal-content {\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n  display: block;\r\n  width: 80%;\r\n  max-width: 100%;\r\n}\r\n.modal-content { \r\n  animation-name: zoom;\r\n  animation-duration: 0.6s;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@keyframes zoom {\r\n  from {transform:scale(0)} \r\n  to {transform:scale(1)}\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close {\r\n  position: absolute;\r\n  top: 15px;\r\n  right: 35px;\r\n  color: #f1f1f1;\r\n  font-size: 40px;\r\n  font-weight: bold;\r\n  transition: 0.3s;\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close:hover,\r\n#image-viewer .close:focus {\r\n  color: #bbb;\r\n  text-decoration: none;\r\n  cursor: pointer;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@media only screen and (max-width: 700px){\r\n  .modal-content {\r\n      width: 100%;\r\n      height:auto;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<script src=\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js\"></script><script>\r\n$(\"img\").on(\'click\',function(){\r\n   $(\"#full-image\").attr(\"src\", $(this).attr(\"src\"));\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').show();\r\n});\r\n\r\n$(\"#image-viewer .close\").click(function(){\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').hide();\r\n});\r\n</script><script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n      button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n    );\r\n  });\r\n  </script>\r\n<script>\r\n $(document).on(\'click\', \'a[href^=\"#\"]\', function (event) {\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    $(\'h2\').css(\'padding-top\',\'75px\');\r\n   $(\'html, body\').animate({\r\n        scrollTop: $($.attr(this, \'href\')).offset().top\r\n    });\r\n});\r\n\r\n</script>', 'What is Microsoft Dynamics NAV?', 'Microsoft dynamics nav', 'Discover Microsoft Dynamics NAV (Navision) ERP, a flexible solution that streamlines operations, financials, and supply chain for SMBs.', 'microsoft dynamics nav,dynamics nav,dynamics nav support,dynamics navision,microsoft dynamics navision', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1782826494466791.jpg', 'Arish Siddiqui', 'arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/everything-know-about-microsoft-dynamics-nav/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Everything You Need to Know About Microsoft Dynamics NAV\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Explore Microsoft Dynamics NAV for streamlined business operations. From finance to workflow automation, discover a centralized solution for efficiency.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1782826469469864.Microsoft Dynamics NAV.jpg\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Arish Siddiqui\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Arish-Siddiqui/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2023-11-17\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2023-11-17\"\r\n}', '[]', '01:45:32pm', '2023-12-06', '10 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-09-08 13:45:32'),
(191, 'What are the Phases of Implementation in Dynamics 365?', 'phases-of-implementation-in-dynamics-365', 'Microsoft Dynamics 365', 'microsoft-dynamics-365', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1782901002641518.Dynamics 365 Implementation Phases.jpg', 'There are 6 phases of implementation in Dynamics 365: Analysis (Discovery and Planning), Design, Development, User Acceptance Testing, Deployment, and Go-live Support. It is an iterative process with back-and-forth movement in between the phases.', '<p>There are 6 phases of implementation in Dynamics 365: Analysis (Discovery and Planning), Design, Development, User Acceptance Testing, Deployment, and Go-live Support. It is an iterative process with back-and-forth movement in between the phases.  \r\n</p><p>Though 70% of enterprise resource planning (ERP) implementation projects stumble, you can maximize your success when designed with precision and clear objectives. There are contributing factors that affect the completion of <a href=\"/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation</a> such as scattered data in the legacy systems, the size of your organization, confusion across departments to consolidate and get real-time reporting, duplicate data, and difficulty in training the users to adapt to a new platform.</p><p>The entire process ranging from simple to complex integrations might take a period of six months to two years to get over. \r\n</p><p>A lot of effort goes into the deployment of a D365 ERP and CRM project, and for a successful implementation, ongoing support is an imperative part of the process. Let us understand the phases of D365 implementation in detail to reduce the failure rate of implementation projects. \r\n</p><blockquote><a href=\"/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Contact your Dynamics 365 implementation partner to detect the reason behind your ERP implementation failure. </b></a></blockquote><h2>How to Implement Microsoft Dynamics 365? \r\n</h2><p>Microsoft Dynamics 365 implementation project plan includes active involvement of program leaders, project managers, solution architects, system administrators, and business stakeholders.</p><p>For a successful Dynamics 365 implementation to take place, deep research, planning, and resources are required. The journey is divided into 6 phases, with expert guidance at each step to culminate.  \r\n</p><h3>1. Analysis</h3><p>Involves evaluation of the capabilities and features of the existing software, to determine the scope of the project. It is the primary phase to understand for the client the issues that the current processes are facing and what are their expectations from <a href=\"/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\">Microsoft Dynamics ERP</a> implementation. Based on their requirement, existing ISV solutions and customizations are reviewed for detailed analysis.</p><p><b>1. Functional Analysis:</b> The functionalities are discussed in detail like how purchase is done, how is bin management being done etc. What are the processes that do not fit their requirement and gaps are ascertained, to determine the level of complexity.</p><p>Nonetheless to overcome the challenges of operational shifts and budget constraints, encountered during fit gap analysis following measures are adopted to overcome them:</p><ul><li><b>Change Management:</b> According to <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://online.hbs.edu/blog/post/change-management-process\" target=\"_blank\">Harvard Business Review</a>, it is vital for organizations to adopt the change management process to overcome challenges posed due to strategic shifts right from beginning of ERP/CRM planning to implementation to resolution/deployment \r\n</li><li><b>Staggered Gap Analysis:</b> The analyzed gaps need to be split into phases to achieve a comprehensive view. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>2. Technical Analysis:</b> the technical architecture like the object designer in NAV, the interfaces and the data migration elements are reviewed in this phase. \r\n</p><p>For successful implementation avoiding scope creep in the project as time progresses, it is necessary to have all the requirements documented and signed off with the client. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Functional Requirement Document:</b> this defines the scope of work, the cost estimate, and the expected period of implementation. \r\n</li><li><b>Gap Fit Document:</b> defines the gaps as business-critical gaps (that are to be prioritized) and nice to have gaps (that can be done in phase II of implementation). \r\n</li><li><b>Technical Integration Document:</b> defines the requirement of any additional integrations like Shopify in <a href=\"/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central</a>. \r\n</li></ul><h3>2. Design</h3><p>In the design phase, a detailed requirement is necessary from the client to design the structure of the new solution. Creating a satisfying and coherent architecture that articulates your vision. </p><p>It includes designing new business processes and customizations that are lacking in the current workflow (Gaps) stated by the users. According to the budget of the project, solutions are structured that will deliver optimum results.</p><p>At this stage a functional design document (FDD) is signed that defines the customizations to be included in the project, along with the configuration and the processes.</p><h3>3. Development</h3><p>In this phase, final configuration and customization of the software is done following the FDD. Finalizing the custom code required to support the solution.</p><p>The functionalities are developed based on the business requirements and integrated testing is done with other existing business applications. 2 or 3 rounds of testing are run to ensure all the developments are tested and rework is not required.</p><p>Along with software development, training materials are also provided to assist users in adjusting to the new system. Training materials include:</p><ul><li>Train the Trainer \r\n</li><li>Workshops \r\n</li><li>Personalized Training \r\n</li><li>User Manuals \r\n</li></ul><p>The development phase also involves planning data migration, which can be complicated because it frequently requires extracting, processing, and loading data from various systems, each of which may utilize different formats and may contain duplicate or inconsistent information.</p><p>During this phase, the project team should decide which data to move, avoiding a blanket migration of all previous data, much of which is likely to be irrelevant. \r\n</p><p><b><a href=\"/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation services</a> at Dynamics Square include comprehensive on-site training. We ensure to attend to your end users’ requirements in totality! \r\n</b></p><h3>4. User Acceptance Testing</h3><p>In this phase, the project team tests the modules and features of the D365 ERP or CRM, makes repairs or adjustments based on the results, and then retests. Alternatively, it may test one ERP/CRM module while another is still being developed. </p><p>Initial testing of the software\'s fundamental functions (in a sand-box environment) is followed by rigorous testing of the system\'s complete capabilities. You are also allowed to test the system for transferred data with pre- and post-deployment tools (provided by your Dynamics 365 implementation partner).</p><p>\r\n</p><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 57, 63); font-size: 1.75rem;\">5. Deployment</span></h3><p>The deployment phase is where the project team\'s efforts come together to ensure a smooth transition to the new Dynamics 365 ERP or <a href=\"/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\">Dynamics CRM</a>&nbsp;solution.  We perform end-user training sessions during this time to address any potential issues or resolve any confusion and difficulties in understanding the new system.</p><p>In addition, all system testing is finished at this phase, and the client provides the sign-off to acknowledge that the system is ready for go-live.   \r\n</p><h3>6. Go-Live and Support</h3><p>Go-live is always done on weekends. The final data migration and knowledge transfer are done. Your implementation partner continues to provide you with all the back-end and front support and resolve any issue that arises or is pending.</p><p>Read more: <a href=\"/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Support</a></p><p> \r\n</p><h2>Which Methodology to Choose for Dynamics 365 Implementation? \r\n</h2><p>Microsoft Dynamics 365 implementation methodology should be discussed before the commencement of the D365 implementation project. Following a particular methodology helps both the implementation partner and the client to avoid scope creep, and pitfalls and plan the project for successful implementation with on-time deployment. \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Agile Methodology \r\n</b></h3><p>Follows the sprint approach of back-and-forth feedback between the client and partner faster release of the ERP/CRM \r\n</p><h3><b>2. Waterfall Methodology \r\n</b></h3><p>Follows the traditional non-iterative pattern for on-premises Dynamics 365 implementation. It is not suitable for on-cloud implementations. \r\n</p><h3><b>3. Hybrid \r\n</b></h3><p>Follows a combination of agile and waterfall methodologies to meet the changing trends in technology today. It allows for early detection of issues and their quick resolution. \r\n</p><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>ERP/CRM implementation is the foundation to reap supreme benefits and boost profitability in your business. It is quintessential for you to know how your business is performing, what are the challenges and what are the goals to be met for the fiscal year.\r\n</p><p>With requirements set clear, the blueprint of the solution can be planned with the help of Microsoft Dynamics 365 implementation partners.</p><p>To further polish your knowledge, run down the <a href=\"/blog/top-kpi-for-success-of-erp-implementation/\" style=\"\">Top 10 KPIs to evaluate the success of ERP implementation</a>.  \r\n</p><p><b>For further queries contact our <a href=\"/our-services/dynamics-365-support-services/\">Dynamics 365 support partner</a> for instant solutions. \r\n</b></p><p>We recommend stakeholders participate in the business validation reviews at regular intervals. \r\n</p><p>For faster and more successful Dynamics 365 Implementation, you can drop us an email at <a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a> or call us directly at <a href=\"http://+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"\">+1 281 899 0865</a> to get in touch with your trusted <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/microsoft-dynamics-365-partner/\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a>.&nbsp;</p>', 'What are the Phases of Implementation in Dynamics 365?', 'dynamics 365 implementation phases', 'Explore Dynamics 365 implementation phases: Plan, Configure, Test, Deploy. Maximize your system efficiency step by step with expert guidance.', 'microsoft dynamics 365,dynamics 365 ,dynamics 365 implementation,microsoft dynamics 365 implementation', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1782901002641524.Dynamics 365 Implementation Phases.jpg', 'Vivek Gururani', 'vivek.gururani@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/phases-of-implementation-in-dynamics-365/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"What are the Phases of Implementation in Dynamics 365?\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Explore Dynamics 365 implementation phases: Plan, Configure, Test, Deploy. Maximize your system efficiency step by step with expert guidance.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1782900973982888.Dynamics 365 Implementation Phases.jpg\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Vivek Gururani\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Vivek-Gururani/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2023-11-18\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2023-11-18\"\r\n}', NULL, '07:29:23pm', '2023-11-18', '8 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-11-14 19:29:23'),
(192, 'ERP for Construction Industry: A Necessity for Modern Business', 'erp-for-construction-industry', 'ERP', 'erp', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1784615210394074.ERP for Construction.png', 'ERP for construction industry is the need of the hour. You need to choose an ERP solution that perfectly fits with your business and provides the necessary tools to withstand customer demand and win the competitive market.', '<p>ERP for construction industry is the need of the hour. You need to choose an <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\">ERP solution</a> that perfectly fits with your business and provides the necessary tools to withstand customer demand and win the competitive market. Before understanding the need for an ERP system in construction businesses, let’s understand why businesses require such a solution.</p>\r\n<img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1784696350859769.Dynamics ERP for Construction Industry.png\"><br>\r\n   <div class=\"blog-content-container\">\r\n    <div class=\"blog-content active\">\r\n    <h4 class=\"blog-content-title\">&nbsp;Table of Content</h4>\r\n    <div class=\"inner\">\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Why-Businesses-Requires-an-ERP-for-Construction-Business\">1. Why Businesses Requires an ERP for Construction Business?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Must-Have-Features-in-Construction-ERP-System\">2. Must Have Features in Construction ERP System </a> \r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Best-ERP-System-for-Construction-Businesses-Check-out-the-Popular-ERP-Solutions\">3. Best ERP System for Construction Businesses: Check out the Popular ERP Solutions </a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Which-Solution-is-Best-for-Unique-Construction-Business\">4. Which Solution is Best for Unique Construction Business?  </a>\r\n      \r\n  </div>\r\n   <button class=\"blog-content-toggle\"> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"><!--! Font Awesome Free 6.4.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license (Commercial License) Copyright 2023 Fonticons, Inc. --><path d=\"M201.4 342.6c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0l160-160c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0L224 274.7 86.6 137.4c-12.5-12.5-32.8-12.5-45.3 0s-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160z\"></path></svg></button>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h2 id=\"Why-Businesses-Requires-an-ERP-for-Construction-Business\" style=\"padding-top: 75px;\">Why Businesses Requires an ERP for Construction Business? \r\n</h2><p>As we can see, the construction industry is becoming more and more complex with the unpredicted demands of the customer and fluctuations in market trends. Such sudden changes have updated the industry with new ways of doing business. Technological advancement and changing global conditions play a vital role in the changing scenario of construction businesses. </p><p>Earlier, each process and activity in the construction industry consisted of manual methods with a lot of errors, inaccuracy, and process inefficiency. We are witnessing the technological advancements that are affecting the business\'s ability to manage people, equipment, and growth. With an advanced ERP for construction, your business can manage entire business scale and achieve new heights.</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1784696322328891.ERP for Construction Industry.png\">In this competitive market, we can witness different ERP solutions, especially those built for the construction business. You can customize such solutions to manage the numerous processes of the organization. These processes include obtaining insights, tracking processes, accepting automation, and increasing business efficiency to achieve goals.<br></p><p>The construction industry is full of complexities, errors, and issues. If you are in this industry, you must be aware of such roadblocks and system redundancies. In your daily business operations, you might be facing difficulties in managing different projects, simplifying operations, optimizing resources, and tracking budgets for each project in real-time.  Also, building strong communication across the team as well as the department is one of the major concerns for the business. Many companies address this by adopting <a href=\"https://remato.com/crew-management/\" target=\"_blank\">construction crew management</a> software alongside their ERP systems, ensuring smoother workforce coordination and better scheduling.</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1784696309098984.Constrution Business.png\">Do you want to get rid of such issues?<br></p><p>Implement a business-centric and advanced ERP solution that can understand your business needs and help you achieve your goals.  Among numerous ERP solutions, you need to choose the one that aligns with your business requirements and offers you the necessary capabilities for business growth. But, before going for a solution, analyzing your existing requirements is the first step you need to consider.</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1784696360823968.Dynamics ERP for Construction Business.png\">Before we check out the 5 performing ERP systems for <span style=\"background-color: white;\">construction businesses</span>, let’s understand the must-have qualities in a construction ERP system.<br></p><h2 id=\"Must-Have-Features-in-Construction-ERP-System\" style=\"padding-top: 75px;\">Must Have Features in Construction ERP System \r\n</h2><p>Before choosing the right ERP solution, you should consider the below factors as must-have features. The essential factors are:</p><h4>Responsive Access for all</h4><p>The ERP system must offer access for all users, including team members, field teams, project owners, engineers, contractors, and vendors. With access, the entire business data can be unified to build a collaborative approach for the organization’s growth.</p><h4>Comes with Cost Management</h4><p>There are numerous processes in the construction business where cost plays a major role. Whether it is purchasing goods or services to optimize the materials, cost management must be an important module of the ERP system.</p><h4>Inbuilt Financial Management Module</h4><p>Good management of finances will empower the business to save costs and achieve higher profit margins with limited resources. Finance management in construction ERP includes budgeting, financial reporting, cash flow management, forecasting requirements, and cost control.</p><h4>Seamless Automation</h4><p>Automation in a construction ERP will eliminate 90% of errors and issues users have to deal with while managing different processes simultaneously. Leveraging the power of automation, a business can automate most of the recurring and manual processes, like workflow automation, document approval, generating invoices, and more, to enhance business productivity.</p><h4>Data Reporting and Analytics</h4><p>Users, project owners, managers, and stakeholders must be informed about each activity happening in the business. Here comes the effective data reporting and analytics capabilities of an ERP system that removes the boundaries between the business and the people to drive transparency.</p><h4>Must be Customizable</h4><p>Each business runs on some sort of process that makes it unique with respect to processing customer requirements and staying ahead in the market. So, the ERP system must adapt to such unique businesses to offer the extra capabilities they require to stay on top. \r\n</p><h2 id=\"Best-ERP-System-for-Construction-Businesses-Check-out-the-Popular-ERP-Solutions\" style=\"padding-top: 75px;\">ERP System for Construction Businesses: Check out the 5 Popular ERP Solutions \r\n</h2><p>Here is the list of the 5 popular ERP solutions that are considered the most practical and effective for all kinds of construction businesses. \r\n</p><h3>1. Microsoft Dynamics 365 \r\n</h3><p>Microsoft Dynamics 365 is a suite of advanced solutions that offers ERP and CRM applications like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a> for all businesses, regardless of size. If you have a small construction business, you can go with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central</a>, as it is highly customizable and easily aligned with unique business needs.</p><p>Also, if you are a diverse organization with business operations around the globe, you can go with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance-operations/\">Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations</a>, also known as Dynamics 365 Finance and Supply Chain Management, as it can seamlessly handle complex construction industry operations. It comes with: \r\n</p><ul><li>Construction Accounting \r\n</li><li>Construction Payroll \r\n</li><li>Mobile App \r\n</li><li>Equipment Management \r\n</li><li>Inspection Management \r\n</li><li>Construction Business Intelligence</li></ul><h3><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1784696335880164.ERP for Construction Business.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 57, 63); font-size: 1.75rem;\">2. Penta</span></h3><p>Penta is a specific construction ERP solution available in the industry with process management capabilities for contractors. With 35 years in the industry, Penta offers diversified tools to manage and streamline a construction business with minimal effort.</p><p>You can easily manage multiple entities with this solution. However, it offers limited integration and customization options for contractors and the business. Even though the interface is a bit complicated and offers fewer tools to profitably manage global business operations, \r\n</p><h3>3. SAGE \r\n</h3><p>SAGE is specifically designed accounting software, but it does come with the necessary tools required to manage a construction business. You can process financial transactions, build project estimates, calculate project margins, manage leads, and simplify operations.</p><p>Being a finance-specific ERP solution, it comes with limited capabilities that might hinder your business growth. However, if you are a construction business that needs an ERP solution specifically to manage finance and accounting, this is the considerable solution for you. \r\n</p><h3>4. Maestro ERP \r\n</h3><p>Maestro ERP has been recently acquired by SailPoint, a leader in offering security to cloud businesses. This solution is basically built to streamline the finance and operations of the construction business, with a few capabilities of other modules as well.</p><p>Also, it comes with full capabilities for project management to help a business streamline different projects altogether. After the acquisition, SailPoint is improving its capabilities and adding more features to make it a modern ERP for construction businesses. \r\n</p><h3>5. Epicor \r\n</h3><p>Epicor is an industry-specific ERP solution for construction businesses. It comes with almost all the business management modules generally required to simply operate and manage a business. Not only in manufacturing, but you can also establish this solution in other industries as well due to its flexible deployment and customization options.</p><p>However, it isn’t specifically built for the construction business as it lacks some of the essential tools like establishing centralized communication, minimizing project uncertainty, tracking manpower, and more.</p><p>  \r\n</p><h2 id=\"Which-Solution-is-Best-for-Unique-Construction-Business\" style=\"padding-top: 75px;\">Which ERP Solution is Right for Unique Construction Business? \r\n</h2><p>Other than these 5 solutions, there are numerous others on the market that claim to be the perfect ERP for construction industry. Let me tell you that it is not advisable to choose a solution until you understand your business requirements and what it needs to grow. \r\n</p><p>Once you have the data on what your business needs to grow in today’s competitive market and what it is going to need in the future, you can proceed to choose a solution. \r\n</p><p>However, analyzing a business is a complicated process, and you might seek expert guidance throughout the process. In such a scenario, Dynamics Square, your reliable Microsoft Dynamics 365 partner, is available to help you understand your core requirements and choose the right solution to accelerate your business growth.</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1784696299661188.Construction Industry.png\">Being a Microsoft Gold Partner or <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a> for 12+ years, we have gained a lot of knowledge and experience in <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation</a> in construction industry. With 150+ technical consultants, we can help you stay on top in this highly competitive market while generating a consistent stream of revenue.<br></p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<script src=\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js\"></script><script>\r\n$(\"img\").on(\'click\',function(){\r\n   $(\"#full-image\").attr(\"src\", $(this).attr(\"src\"));\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').show();\r\n});\r\n\r\n$(\"#image-viewer .close\").click(function(){\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').hide();\r\n});\r\n</script><script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n      button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n    );\r\n  });\r\n  </script>\r\n<script>\r\n $(document).on(\'click\', \'a[href^=\"#\"]\', function (event) {\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    $(\'h2\').css(\'padding-top\',\'75px\');\r\n   $(\'html, body\').animate({\r\n        scrollTop: $($.attr(this, \'href\')).offset().top\r\n    });\r\n});\r\n\r\n</script>', 'ERP for Construction Industry: A Necessity for Modern Business', 'erp for construction', 'Choose the best ERP solution for your construction industry. Choose the one that can manage equipment, manpower, accounting, and different projects with ease.', 'dynamics erp,microsoft dynamics erp,dynamics 365,microsoft dynamics 365,erp for construction business,erp for contsruction industry,erp software for construction industry', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1784615210394080.ERP for Construction.png', 'Samar Malik', 'samar.malik@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/erp-for-construction-industry/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"ERP for Construction Industry: A Necessity for Modern Business\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Choose the best ERP solution for your construction industry. Choose the one that can manage equipment, manpower, accounting, and different projects with ease.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1784618641318275.ERP for Construction.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Arshad A.S.\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Arshad-A.S.\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2023-12-07\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2023-12-07\"\r\n}', '[]', '03:22:30pm', '2023-12-08', '9 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2026-02-19 22:22:30');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(193, 'Emerging Trends in Supply Chain Management in 2026', 'trends-in-supply-chain-management', 'supply chain management', 'supply-chain-management', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1817504317219971.Trends in Supply Chain Management.png', 'Explore the current trends in supply chain management, including automation, AI, sustainability, and advanced analytics to streamline operations and enhance efficiency.', '<p>Do you know more than 50% of supply chain organizations will invest in applications that support artificial intelligence and advanced analytics capabilities?</p><p>Current trends in supply chain management have been a breakthrough for organizations worldwide. Companies are becoming adept in handling complex business demands of various industries whilst leveraging advanced automation through <a href=\"/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\">Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</a> ERP.</p><p>These organizations are pacing ahead by managing quick end-to-end supply chain and logistical requirements by leveraging Dynamics 365 Automation. This is because they are moving forward with time.</p><p>Similarly, every organization should keep pace with new technology and Automation in the Supply Chain Industry. The future of the supply chain realm is dynamic, and organizations should align with it to succeed.</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1788527724551563.Microsoft Data for Supply Chain Management.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">This blog will take you to supply chain trends that will help you stay ahead in this ever evolving, racing modern world. Find out more.<br></p>\r\n<div class=\"blog-content-container\">\r\n    <div class=\"blog-content active\">\r\n    <h4 class=\"blog-content-title\">&nbsp;Table of Content</h4>\r\n    <div class=\"inner\">\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-is-supply-chain-management\">1. What is Supply Chain Management?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Future-trends-in-supply-chain-management\">2. Future Trends in Supply Chain Management</a> \r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#How-Dynamics-Square-can-help-you-to-elevate-your-business\">3. How Dynamics Square can help you to elevate your business</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n   <button class=\"blog-content-toggle\"> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"><!--! Font Awesome Free 6.4.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license (Commercial License) Copyright 2023 Fonticons, Inc. --><path d=\"M201.4 342.6c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0l160-160c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0L224 274.7 86.6 137.4c-12.5-12.5-32.8-12.5-45.3 0s-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160z\"></path></svg></button>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 id=\"What-is-supply-chain-management\">What is Supply Chain Management?</h2>\r\n<p>When we think of Supply Chain Management the first thing that comes across is supplying goods, however, it is much more than that. It is not only the supplying of goods but also the management and flow of goods.</p><p>Supply chain management is handled by AI, software, or other intelligent automated business solutions in the modern world of a digital paradigm shift. These applications manage order creation, <a href=\"https://jooble.org/jobs-work-from-home-order-taker\" target=\"_blank\">order taker jobs</a>, fulfillment, and information tracking among suppliers, manufacturers, retailers, transport managers, and logistics professionals. These features are unlike the usual traditional processes of operating.   \r\n</p><p>One of the most important features includes product lifecycle management, and supply chain planning which incorporates planning and the maintenance of the production process.</p><p>Secondly, it also has logistics control which comprises fleet, transport management, and order management.</p><p>Further, Supply Chain Management can support, monitor, and streamline activities around global trade involving multinational processes.</p><p><b>Make sure your supply chain is all set for the future. <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Contact Our Expert</a></b></p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Future-trends-in-supply-chain-management\">Current Trends in Supply Chain Management</h2><p>The global supply chain landscape is evolving rapidly due to increasing business complexities around the world. Technological advancements play a major role in helping businesses surpass these complexities.</p><p>However, there are so many more game-changing trends that are going to shift the paradigm. Scroll to learn major future trends in Supply Chain Management in 2026 &amp; beyond.</p>\r\n<h3>1. Advanced Automation and AI Trends in Supply Chain Management \r\n</h3><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1788527712137999.Advanced Automation and AI trends in supply chain management.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">Did you know that the recent research done by <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.mckinsey.com/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background-color: white; font-family: sans-serif; font-weight: 400;\">McKinsey</a> says that implementing AI in logistics has led to an increase in the success rate of global companies?<br></p><p>This is because industry leaders are witnessing success rates with artificial intelligence in supply chain management in the contemporary business landscape.  Professionals know that the future of the supply chain is huge.</p><p>Even when we look at the Data from Statista, it shows that Automation and AI have helped global organizations streamline inventory management processes, smart manufacturing strategies, and real-time, logistics and delivery control.</p><p>Let’s read how trends in AI have optimized the way organizations work.</p><ul><li>Demand Forecasting in Warehouse Supply and Management is boosting productivity and decreasing the cost.  \r\n</li><li>Easy prediction of delays in delivery and other vehicle processes. \r\n</li><li>Real Time Visibility whilst loading and tracking parcels. \r\n</li><li>Decreased rate in overall processing.  \r\n</li><li>The organization is efficient in forecasting, optimizing, and improving efficiency.  \r\n</li><li>Now businesses can drive operational benefits with the help of AI &amp; Automation. \r\n</li></ul><h3>2. Cloud-based Technology Supply Chain Trends \r\n</h3><p>According to the stats and research, cloud technology in supply chain management will surpass 40$ Billion by 2027. \r\n</p><p>This is enough to justify the fact that there is a significant shift in traditional ways of managing supply chain trends. This is because, the Cloud-based solutions permit companies to get the hang of actionable insights, making them make better decisions, analyze what is befitting for company growth etc. Let’s scroll to read how cloud-based technology is managing business like never before.</p><ul><li>Garnering Intelligent insights from customers, retailers, wholesalers etc.  \r\n</li><li>Planning logistics management, inventory, and transport Management efficiently  \r\n</li><li>Insights on sourcing and procurement as cloud-based solutions can curate a master, insightful database of all the suppliers.  \r\n</li><li>Save Costs as cloud-based technology doesn’t require any charges, it is subscription-based.  \r\n</li><li>Improve Scalability during high and unmanageable demands.  \r\n</li></ul><h3>3. Digital Supply Chain Management Trends  \r\n</h3><p>As per insights from <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.gartner.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Gartner</a>, bringing digital transformation into the supply chain can increase 20% revenue and can lead to a 50% reduction in costs. \r\n</p><p>The entire world now talks about digital transformation because they know that this is the need of the hour.  The earlier quoting process with a multitude of suppliers was time-consuming, however, now digital is here, we take less turnaround time.</p><p>Even issues like disruption in quality and control can be managed efficiently. Further, access to a team anywhere geographically is bound to keep quality and control situations in check. Managing vendors overseas is getting simpler with digital supply chain trends and there are other game-changing advantages as well. Read below:</p><ul><li>Functioning in real-time rather than outdated historical transactional inputs accelerates innovation and reduces time to market.  \r\n</li><li>Better Decision-making with Integrated IT and informational technology can easily predict risks, which is again imperative for any organization. \r\n</li><li>Increased Productivity as with Digital Supply Chain trends one can observe maximum productivity and efficiency.    \r\n</li><li>Reduced Cost as accurate forecasting can maximize productivity and efficiency. This leads to quicker access and thereby the costs.  \r\n</li><li>With digital amplification one can improve customer satisfaction, by managing and replying to customers on time.  \r\n</li></ul><p>Therefore, after figuring out the ever-growing demand of machine customers who rely on digital solutions, we can sure see that the current trends in supply chain management are here to stay.</p><h3>4. Supply Chain Resiliency</h3><p>Bain and Company reported that companies that have arrangements for supply chain resilience were able to expand their output capacity by up to 25% or more!</p><p>Supply chain resiliency is the organization\'s ability to manage operational disruptions through contingency forecasting. This initiates from material sourcing to logistics till the final delivery of products and services. The features below ensure that the Supply Chain Resiliency trend will always stay.</p><ul><li><b>Lower Risk Factors</b></li></ul><p>Supply Chains can be vulnerable to risks and company losses if not operated well. Resilient supply chain technology can reduce risk by streamlining the potential disruption.<br></p><ul><li><b>More Innovations</b></li></ul><p>Resilience in Supply Chain Management can indeed lead companies to reduce the risks and thereby focus more on innovation and growth.</p><ul><li><b>Powerful and Secure Data</b></li></ul><p>Supply Chain resiliency leads to understanding data and then making decisions that better the productivity and success rate. This intelligent automation gives supply chain professionals the insights they need to respond quickly to unexpected events.</p><p><b>Read More:</b>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/what-is-dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: What Is It?</a></p><p>  \r\n</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"How-Dynamics-Square-can-help-you-to-elevate-your-business\">How Dynamics Square Helps You to Elevate Your Business</h2>\r\n<p>You can embrace the future of the supply chain with Dynamics Square effectually! See how</p><p><b>Leverage AI-informed real-time metrics for your next project WIN \r\n</b></p><p>By ensuring modern automation which incorporates digital solutions, such as dashboards, business intelligence, and Internet of Things (IoT) technology to further simplify processes such as stock management. \r\n</p><p>The D365 Supply Chain Management solution will let you stay ahead of the curve with real-time visibility, unified data, and predictive AI features that help you improve resource planning and expedite product and service delivery. \r\n</p><p>Expect reduced manual tasks, such as invoicing, through automation, which will save time and reduce money. \r\n</p><h3>Stay Agile and Resilient with Emerging Trends in the Supply Chain  \r\n</h3><ul><li><b>Maximize and Streamline Asset Performance</b></li></ul><p>Witness Improved overall equipment effectiveness (OEE) and reduced redundant downtime. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Revolutionize Manufacturing Operations</b></li></ul><p>Dynamics 365 Supply chain management will innovate your operations with advanced technologies. Our Dynamics 365 consultants&nbsp;will help you attain that purpose. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Amplify Growing Digital Commerce needs with Reduced Risks</b></li></ul><p>We ensure that order fulfillment with AI and real-time stock will help you overcome supply chain disruptions.  \r\n</p><p>Being a <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a> for 12+ years, we have garnered a lot of knowledge and experience in <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">implementing Dynamics 365</a> Supply Chain solutions. We know how to future-proof your business with trending and advanced technology.</p><p>With 150+ technical consultants, we will let you create a niche in this highly competitive market. You can drop us an email at <b><a href=\"arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a></b> or call us directly at <a href=\"http://+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\"><b>+1 281 899 0865</b></a>.</p>\r\n\r\n<div id=\"image-viewer\" style=\"display: none; top: 0px !important;\">\r\n  <span class=\"close\">×</span>\r\n  <img class=\"modal-content\" id=\"full-image\">\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">// <![CDATA[\r\nconst buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n\r\nbuttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n    button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n  );\r\n});\r\n// ]]></script>\r\n<style>\r\n/* The Modal (background) */\r\n#image-viewer {\r\n  display: none;\r\n  position: fixed;\r\n  z-index: 999;\r\n  padding: 70px;\r\n  left: 0;\r\n  top: 0;\r\n  width: 100%;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  overflow: auto;\r\n  background-color: rgb(0,0,0);\r\n  background-color: rgba(45, 62, 80, 0.99);\r\n}\r\n.modal-content {\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n  display: block;\r\n  width: 80%;\r\n  max-width: 100%;\r\n}\r\n.modal-content { \r\n  animation-name: zoom;\r\n  animation-duration: 0.6s;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@keyframes zoom {\r\n  from {transform:scale(0)} \r\n  to {transform:scale(1)}\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close {\r\n  position: absolute;\r\n  top: 15px;\r\n  right: 35px;\r\n  color: #f1f1f1;\r\n  font-size: 40px;\r\n  font-weight: bold;\r\n  transition: 0.3s;\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close:hover,\r\n#image-viewer .close:focus {\r\n  color: #bbb;\r\n  text-decoration: none;\r\n  cursor: pointer;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@media only screen and (max-width: 700px){\r\n  .modal-content {\r\n      width: 100%;\r\n      height:auto;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<script src=\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js\"></script><script>\r\n$(\"img\").on(\'click\',function(){\r\n   $(\"#full-image\").attr(\"src\", $(this).attr(\"src\"));\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').show();\r\n});\r\n\r\n$(\"#image-viewer .close\").click(function(){\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').hide();\r\n});\r\n</script><script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n      button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n    );\r\n  });\r\n  </script>\r\n<script>\r\n $(document).on(\'click\', \'a[href^=\"#\"]\', function (event) {\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    $(\'h2\').css(\'padding-top\',\'75px\');\r\n   $(\'html, body\').animate({\r\n        scrollTop: $($.attr(this, \'href\')).offset().top\r\n    });\r\n});\r\n\r\n</script>', '4 Current Trends in Supply Chain Management in 2026', 'trends in supply chain management', 'Discover the current supply chain trends like automation, AI, sustainability, and analytics to boost efficiency and streamline operations.', 'supply chain management,dynamics 365 supply chain,supply chain trends,dynamics 365 supply chain trends', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1817504317219975.Trends in Supply Chain Management.png', 'Arish Siddiqui', 'arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/trends-in-supply-chain-management/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Emerging Trends in Supply Chain Management in 2026\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1788434594279941.trends in supply-chain-management.jpg\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Arish Siddiqui\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Arish-Siddiqui/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-01-18\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-01-18\"\r\n}', '[]', '01:56:33pm', '2024-01-19', '10 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2026-01-02 20:56:33'),
(194, '11 Latest CRM Trends To Watch in 2026 and Beyond', '11-latest-crm-trends-to-watch-in-2026-and-beyond', 'CRM', 'crm', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1789689577203032.CRM Trends.png', 'Stay ahead with the latest CRM trends. Discover insights on AI integration, customer engagement strategies, and automation to enhance your business growth.', '<p>The Customer Relationship Management System has been raised above from a simple contact management tool. It has been repurposed into a pivotal tool that is ushering us towards a future-forward world, where CRM trends are changing the game like never before.  \r\n</p><p>This equipped software system has been repurposed to capture unique yet complex demands in the marketplace. Presently, brands like Microsoft, Salesforce, Oracle, and SAP are creating a stir because of the transformation they are bringing with new and latest CRM trends in 2026.  \r\n</p><p><b>Further, it is certainly not a surprise that the CRM industry’s market value is going to grow at a significant growth rate (CAGR) of 13.9% from 2024 to 2030, as stated in Grand View Research</b>.   \r\n</p><p>As 90% of companies with more than 20 employees already have at least one CRM system.  However, the question is, how do companies will make the most of the software system in 2026? \r\n</p><p>Rest, we all know the progression in the market, and advanced tech integration has transformed the world. Now, let’s see how these attributes have not skipped creating a powerful impact on CRM software trends.</p><h2>11 Latest CRM Trends in 2026</h2><p>  \r\n</p><p>Let’s read about the promising customer relationship management trends in 2026. And how they are revolutionizing the way we will work and progress.  \r\n</p><h3>1. Intervention of Artificial Intelligence  \r\n</h3><p>As per a recent <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forrester.com/bold\" target=\"_blank\">Forrester</a> analyst, “With AI, new CRM systems can analyze vast amounts of data to deliver predictive analytics on business outcomes. It enables employees to “interrogate the data differently.” \r\n</p><p>The ability of AI to automate repeatable processes and operational workflows has created wonders in every industry and CRM is no less.  AI has taken the world by storm as it has taken traditional business process automation (BPA) to another façade. \r\n</p><p>Through AI sales professionals can dive into the world of data analytics and whilst garnering information through AI, they can reap more profitable relationships with their customers.  \r\n</p><p><b>Also Read:</b> <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/best-crm-platform-for-businesses/\">CRM Platform for Businesses</a></p><h3>2. Integrating Sustainable Strategies into CRM Market Trends \r\n</h3><p>This is the era where customers’ expectations are to the next level, organizations prefer to take a step beyond to create a powerful impact that aligns with the present momentum.   \r\n</p><p>Therefore, companies are now adopting Sustainable CRM practices that show the organization’s promise to take the responsibility of adhering to environmental and social practices. They focus on building customer relationships with sustainable values and visions.  \r\n</p><p>Brands know that this will even strengthen their goodwill among the target audience. These practices include reducing energy consumption, minimizing paper waste and usage, strategies waste management strategies etc. Some companies prefer recycling initiatives and sustainable supplier selection in their modern CRM process.  \r\n</p><p><b><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Contact our Expert</a> To know more about this CRM Trend</b>. \r\n</p><h3>3. Continuing with Cloud-Based Modern CRM Solutions \r\n</h3><p>Continuing with the cloud is one of the most crucial CRM industry trends. It will be topping the chart again as now clients are satisfied with accessibility and scalability.  \r\n</p><p>The main advantage of cloud-based CRM solutions is that one can delve into CRM data from any location in the world.  \r\n</p><p>Further, another reason is that Cloud-based CRM solutions often include disaster recovery systems.  \r\n</p><p>Data is constantly backed up, reducing the reasons for data loss due to unexpected events. Not only this, but also Cloud-based CRM solutions come with other advantages.  \r\n</p><p><b>To learn how to take this trend to another level with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a> \r\n</b></p><h3>4. Building Cybersecurity Measure  \r\n</h3><p>In the year 2026, CRM companies will heavily allocate significant resources towards cybersecurity protocols. \r\n</p><p>This will focus on ensuring security, aiming to protect sensitive customer data. They will refrain from cyber threats by integrating Blockchain technology which is known for its security parameters.  \r\n</p><p>This feature will be incorporated into CRM systems to protect sensitive customer information. \r\n</p><p>&nbsp;As businesses are transforming due to digitization, getting cybersecurity measures within CRM systems is pivotal for maintaining sensitive customer details.  \r\n</p><p>Therefore, this CRM Industry trend is here to stay even after many years we know.  \r\n</p><h3>5. Augmented Reality (AR) Support  \r\n</h3><p>We are already seeing how real estate and jewellery companies offer advanced &amp; virtual tours through <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.techtarget.com/searchcustomerexperience/tip/Businesses-use-AR-VR-in-CRM-to-boost-customer-experience\" target=\"_blank\">CRM-integrated AR applications</a>. We are also seeing with this feature; it is becoming easy for customers to make an informed decision.  \r\n</p><p>Therefore, looking at the advantages of technology, AR will be integrated into CRM capabilities. The businesses will give immersive experiences to the customer and thereby improve efficient outputs.  \r\n</p><p><b>Read More: </b><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/crm-software-for-real-estate/\">CRM Software for Real Estate</a></p><h3>6. Integration of Voice Assistants \r\n</h3><p>The brouhaha around voice assistant is not false, as we can see Siri and Alexa have added so much to our daily tasks.  If we look to future-proof the CRM systems, then adding these voice assistants is the solution.  \r\n</p><p>These assistants are building powerful interactions like never before. Imagine how simple it will be to access customer data or schedule calls, follow-ups etc. with a simple voice command.  \r\n</p><p>This trend will enhance productivity and will save time. This feature will be intelligent to protect data from potential risk. Isn’t it worthy and enticing, a task away from mundane?  \r\n</p><h3>7. Harnessing IoT-Driven Insights  \r\n</h3><p>Data is the king nowadays and harnessing IoT data will help companies to gain valuable insights from real customer behavior patterns.  \r\n</p><p>By using real-time, rich data from IoT devices, one can create secure and efficient customer experiences.  \r\n</p><p>This is the reason IoT-driven data insights should be woven with CRM strategies. This integration will ensure timely and relevant communication with the customers.  \r\n</p><h3>8. Advanced Reporting and Analytics \r\n</h3><p>Insightful reporting analytics will be at the forefront of CRM systems in 2026. Organizations will be generating in-depth reports and gain real-time insights, and predictive analysis from their CRM data.  \r\n</p><p>Because understanding the customer’s behavior pattern is important, organizations can use strategies to progress based on customers\' historical actions through advanced analytics. \r\n</p><p>This helps the sales team to offer personalized experiences. Thereby helping the organizations to evolve. \r\n</p><h3>9. New Age Data Visualization   \r\n</h3><p>People are transcending the way they work and being productive and this feature is a cherry on the top. Features like depictive graphs, charts, and other visual diagrams amplify CRM analytics. \r\n</p><p>Therefore, this is a future-compliant CRM industry trend and will stay in 2026 &amp; beyond.  \r\n</p><h3>10. Accessible Mobile CRM  \r\n</h3><p>In the era of smartphones, people are now comfortable performing their daily assigned tasks with their smart devices. With this transition, the CRM industry is primarily focusing on mobile-friendly interfaces and applications to let the operators manage customer data from anywhere, quickly or at their own pace.  \r\n</p><p>The CRM market trends forecasted for 2026 and beyond have a huge potential in the coming years. Be it Small Business or Medium Business, real estate or any other sector, everyone will benefit from these game-changing trends.</p><h3>11. Integrating Whatsapp Business to CRM</h3><p>Integrating CRM systems with this popular messaging platform has risen as a trend. It assists businesses to communicate and nurture customers in real-time, providing instant support and personal interaction.  As a better result, this integration allows business to boost customer engagement and streamline communication with a seamless and efficient communication channel.\r\n</p><p><a href=\"http://www.kommo.com\" target=\"_blank\">Kommo</a>, one of the business solution providers, has designed messenger-based CRM systems that focus on whatsapp business integration. It facilitates businesses with an abundance of features such as unified inbox, chatbot builder, templates, and AI-driven message composing to build strong relationships with customers. Businesses can connect with the customers while automating the sales process effectively.</p><p>  \r\n</p><p>Adapting to these CRM trends will not only help you to create a niche but also will garner a customer satisfaction ratio &amp; growth rate and thus better CX. \r\n</p><p>So, what are you waiting for? Here is the time to stay ahead of the curve by getting in touch with your <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/microsoft-dynamics-365-partner/\">Dynamics 365 consultants</a> who have more than 12 years of experience.   \r\n</p><p>Being a trusted <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\">Microsoft Dynamics partner</a>, Dynamics Square has established itself as a name to be reckoned with in this industry.  Time to get in touch with us for a business-centric, CRM for your business.</p><p>Explore <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/crm-implementation-services/\" target=\"_blank\">CRM implementation services</a> designed to scale and grow businesses</p>', '11 Latest CRM Trends To Watch in 2026 and Beyond', 'crm trends', 'Explore the latest CRM trends, including AI integration and customer engagement strategies, to enhance your business growth and stay competitive.', 'microsoft dynamics crm,dynamics crm,crm trends,crm software trends,Latest CRM Trends', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1789689577203036.CRM Trends.png', 'Vivek Gururani', 'vivek.gururani@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/crm-trends/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"10 Significant CRM Trends to Watch for in 2026 and Beyond\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Stay ahead in business with insights on 10 CRM trends for 2026 & beyond. Discover the latest strategies shaping customer relationships.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1789689543000839.CRM Trends.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Vivek Gururani\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Vivek-Gururani/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-02-01\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-02-01\"\r\n}', '[]', '02:00:13pm', '2024-02-01', '8 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2026-01-02 21:00:13'),
(195, 'How to Choose an ERP Consultant for Your Business?', 'choose-erp-consultant-for-business', 'ERP', 'erp', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1817503590255767.ERP Consultant (3).png', 'Do you know that a study by Gartner has confirmed that about 55-75% of the ERP implementation falls short of meeting their objectives? There can be several reasons behind this, however, most prominent one is choosing an inexperienced ERP consultant.', '<p>Do you know that a study by <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.gartner.com/en/documents/1329324\" target=\"_blank\">Gartner</a> has confirmed that about 55-75% of the ERP implementation falls short of meeting its objectives? </p><p>There can be several reasons behind this; however, the most prominent one is choosing an inexperienced ERP consultant.</p><p>Acknowledging the need for an ERP system is just half the job done. To make sure the <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\">Dynamics ERP</a> is in line with your business requirements and is successfully implemented, you need the guidance and support of an ERP consultant like Dynamics Square.\r\n</p><p>This post addresses the most frequently asked questions about an ERP consultant:</p> \r\n<div class=\"blog-content-container\">\r\n    <div class=\"blog-content active\">\r\n    <h4 class=\"blog-content-title\">&nbsp;Table of Content</h4>\r\n    <div class=\"inner\">\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-is-an-erp-consultant\">1. What is an ERP Consultant?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-does-an-erp-consultant-do\">2. What does an ERP Consultant Do?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-is erp-consulting\">3. What is ERP Consulting?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#How-to-choose-an-erp-implementation-consultant\">4. How to Choose an ERP Implementation Consultant?</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n   <button class=\"blog-content-toggle\"> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"><!--! Font Awesome Free 6.4.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license (Commercial License) Copyright 2023 Fonticons, Inc. --><path d=\"M201.4 342.6c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0l160-160c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0L224 274.7 86.6 137.4c-12.5-12.5-32.8-12.5-45.3 0s-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160z\"></path></svg></button>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<h2 id=\"What-is-an-erp-consultant\">What is an ERP Consultant?</h2>\r\n<p>The term ‘<b>ERP Consultant</b>’ can be used for both professionals and companies. An ERP software consultant helps businesses choose and implement the right ERP based on their specific business requirements and objectives.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"What-does-an-erp-consultant-do\">What does an ERP Consultant Do?</h2>\r\n<p>An ERP consultant offers ERP consulting services that primarily include ERP implementation and maintenance support. Professionals, working with an ERP consultant company, audit business operations and gather in-depth information on different processes to configure the Microsoft Dynamics ERP so that it is in line with the requirements of the business.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"What is ERP Consulting?\">What is ERP Consulting?</h2>\r\n<p>Seeking the help of professionals in determining and implementing the right ERP is known as ERP consulting. For instance, Dynamics Square, a <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a> company, offers ERP consulting services.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"How-to-choose-an-erp-implementation-consultant\">How to Choose an ERP Implementation Consultant?</h2>\r\n<p>The market is full of ERP consultants offering ERP consulting services. However, the decision must be taken only after careful consideration. The final decision would be critical because it would have a direct impact on your business. You can always look for the following traits while shortlisting potential ERP consultants: \r\n</p><h4>1. Industry Experience &amp; Specialization \r\n</h4><p>The ERP consulting firm must have a strong background in implementing ERP systems, especially in the industry your business belongs to. <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Get in touch with the experts</a>&nbsp;at the firm to understand their expertise and ability to customize and deploy an ERP as per your business needs. \r\n</p><p>A credible ERP consultant will have a deep understanding of your business and its various key processes. They are more likely to keep up with the latest trends and provide solutions that are closely aligned with your business needs. \r\n</p><h3>2. Proven Track Record \r\n</h3><p>When interacting with a potential ERP consultant, do not go by their words alone. Make sure to ask for concrete evidence that may include references and case studies from previous projects, similar in scope to yours. It will provide you with valuable insights into their expertise in successful <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">ERP implementation</a>. \r\n</p><h3>3. Clear Communication \r\n</h3><p>To be able to communicate clearly, the ERP consultant must have the required technical expertise. Make sure to check if the ERP consultants is an authorized partner and has the required certification and resources to ensure successful ERP implementation. \r\n</p><p>Being a Microsoft Solutions Partner, Dynamics Square banks on a team of qualified professionals who have the expertise to comprehend, evaluate, and communicate the needs of the business clearly.</p><p>A good ERP consultant like Dynamics Square puts clients’ interests above all and goes the extra mile to work in tandem with your team to help you achieve the desired outcomes. \r\n</p><h3>4. Pricing and Value Proposition \r\n</h3><p>Price is a decisive factor when it comes to partnering with an ERP consultants. Our tool, the <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/erp-implementation-cost-calculator/\" target=\"_blank\">ERP implementation cost calculator</a>, can help estimate potential costs, allowing you to compare quotes more effectively. However, the focus should always be to ensure you get the best value for your investment.</p><p>While the price should not be the only deciding factor, it is always wise to thoroughly compare quotes from different ERP consultants and go with the one that has a proven track record and offers quality service at a competitive price. \r\n</p><h3>5. Availability for Ongoing Support \r\n</h3><p>Constant support during the ERP implementation process and even beyond is critical for businesses. Make sure to get all terms and conditions in writing before signing a contract with an ERP consultant. ERP implementation is a lengthy process and may take up to 6-12 months to complete. \r\n</p><p>During this phase, the consultant must be available at every step of the process, right from the selection of functionalities to the final deployment. It is their responsibility to ensure all business needs have been taken care of.</p><p>Other than managing technical requirements, they must have strategies to help the business undergo this transformation by means of proper training and change management.</p>\r\n<p>Want to learn more about ERP implementation? </p><p>Get in touch with your <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation</a> partner for a detailed discussion. We are here to help you.</p>\r\n\r\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">// <![CDATA[\r\nconst buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n\r\nbuttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n    button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n  );\r\n});\r\n// ]]></script>\r\n<style>\r\n/* The Modal (background) */\r\n#image-viewer {\r\n  display: none;\r\n  position: fixed;\r\n  z-index: 999;\r\n  padding: 70px;\r\n  left: 0;\r\n  top: 0;\r\n  width: 100%;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  overflow: auto;\r\n  background-color: rgb(0,0,0);\r\n  background-color: rgba(45, 62, 80, 0.99);\r\n}\r\n.modal-content {\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n  display: block;\r\n  width: 80%;\r\n  max-width: 100%;\r\n}\r\n.modal-content { \r\n  animation-name: zoom;\r\n  animation-duration: 0.6s;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@keyframes zoom {\r\n  from {transform:scale(0)} \r\n  to {transform:scale(1)}\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close {\r\n  position: absolute;\r\n  top: 15px;\r\n  right: 35px;\r\n  color: #f1f1f1;\r\n  font-size: 40px;\r\n  font-weight: bold;\r\n  transition: 0.3s;\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close:hover,\r\n#image-viewer .close:focus {\r\n  color: #bbb;\r\n  text-decoration: none;\r\n  cursor: pointer;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@media only screen and (max-width: 700px){\r\n  .modal-content {\r\n      width: 100%;\r\n      height:auto;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<script src=\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js\"></script><script>\r\n$(\"img\").on(\'click\',function(){\r\n   $(\"#full-image\").attr(\"src\", $(this).attr(\"src\"));\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').show();\r\n});\r\n\r\n$(\"#image-viewer .close\").click(function(){\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').hide();\r\n});\r\n</script><script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n      button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n    );\r\n  });\r\n  </script>\r\n<script>\r\n $(document).on(\'click\', \'a[href^=\"#\"]\', function (event) {\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    $(\'h2\').css(\'padding-top\',\'75px\');\r\n   $(\'html, body\').animate({\r\n        scrollTop: $($.attr(this, \'href\')).offset().top\r\n    });\r\n});\r\n\r\n</script>', 'How to Choose an ERP Consultant for Your Business?', 'ERP Consultant', 'Choosing the right ERP consultant is essential. With knowledgeable advice on making informed decisions, find the critical elements for your business\'s success.', 'erp consultant,erp consultants,erp implementation,erp implementation consultant,microsoft dynamics erp,erp consulting services', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1817503590255774.ERP Consultant (3).png', 'Arish Siddiqui', 'arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/choose-erp-consultant-for-business/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"How to Choose an ERP Consultant for Your Business?\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Choosing the right ERP consultant is essential. With knowledgeable advice on making informed decisions, find the critical elements for your business\'s success.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1795328484377387.ERP Consultant.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Arish Siddiqui\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Arish-Siddiqui/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-04-03\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-04-03\"\r\n}', NULL, '03:43:34pm', '2024-05-29', '6 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-06-16 15:43:34');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(196, 'Microsoft Cloud for Financial Services: A Perfect Choice to Simplify Finances', 'microsoft-cloud-for-financial-services', 'Microsoft Cloud', 'microsoft-cloud', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1797133608990792.png', 'Microsoft Cloud for Financial Services is a set of different cloud-based solutions that offer an omnichannel experience for simplifying diverse and complex financial transactions.', '<p>Microsoft Cloud for Financial Services is a set of different cloud-based solutions that offer an omnichannel experience for simplifying diverse and complex financial transactions. Such solutions accelerate a business towards growth, scalability, and a good customer experience, along with managing complex operations.</p><p>Before understanding the core concept, let’s understand why managing finances is necessary. Managing finances with 100% accuracy has become an essential part of an organization.</p><p>Businesses are investing a lot of resources and infrastructure to streamline complete financial operations, eliminating any chances of errors through any means.</p><p>You cannot cope with the increasing complexity of financial functioning using legacy solutions or outdated technologies. You will need to integrate or implement an advanced solution that understands your business needs and aligns with the changing requirements. \r\n</p><p>If you are looking for a centralized solution that comes with high-tech capabilities to manage modern financial needs, Microsoft Cloud for Financial Services is the answer.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blog-content-container\">\r\n    <div class=\"blog-content active\">\r\n    <h4 class=\"blog-content-title\">&nbsp;Table of Content</h4>\r\n    <div class=\"inner\">\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-is-microsoft-cloud-for-financial-services\">1. What is Microsoft Cloud for Financial Services?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Microsoft-cloud-financial-solutions-and-their-core-applications\">2. Microsoft Cloud Financial Solutions and their Core Applications</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#How-to-get-more-with-microsoft-cloud-for-financial-services\">3. How to get more with Microsoft Cloud for Financial Services?</a>\r\n\r\n  </div>\r\n   <button class=\"blog-content-toggle\"> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"><!--! Font Awesome Free 6.4.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license (Commercial License) Copyright 2023 Fonticons, Inc. --><path d=\"M201.4 342.6c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0l160-160c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0L224 274.7 86.6 137.4c-12.5-12.5-32.8-12.5-45.3 0s-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160z\"></path></svg></button>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h2 id=\"What-is-microsoft-cloud-for-financial-services\">What is Microsoft Cloud for Financial Services?</h2>\r\n<p>Microsoft Cloud for Financial Services enables businesses to avail of embedded AI and cloud technologies to get unified services, cater to a high level of customer satisfaction, empower employees with sufficient collaboration opportunities, and deal with financial infringement. \r\n</p><p>The applications available in the <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-cloud\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft cloud</a> empower you to automate core financial processes, avail real-time insights to make data-driven decisions, capture customer interaction to personalize services, and drive business towards profitability. \r\n</p><p>Such strong capabilities of cloud solutions enable a business to align with changing business requirements and simplify business complexity to boost growth. \r\n</p><p>In general, the solutions of Microsoft Cloud include the applications from <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a>, Power Platform, and other Microsoft 365 business solutions that we use daily.</p><p>Microsoft 365 Financial Services provides a unified approach to resolving financial complexities and promotes team strengthening. It even helps the business build and deploy workflows to establish a consistent flow of data across different solutions. </p><p>Additionally, <a href=\"https://intellias.com/geospatial-data-for-insurance-industry/\" target=\"_blank\">GIS in insurance</a> can be integrated into such cloud platforms, enhancing risk management and providing valuable location-based insights to better serve clients and mitigate potential losses.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Microsoft-cloud-financial-solutions-and-their-core-applications\">Microsoft Cloud Financial Solutions and their Core Applications</h2>\r\n<p>We have different solutions in Microsoft Dynamics 365 Financial Services, which comes with different applications for businesses. Some of the solutions, along with their core advantages, are discussed below: \r\n</p><h3>1. Dynamics 365 Customer Insights \r\n</h3><p>It is one of the <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM</a> solutions that enables businesses to fetch hidden information out of customer data to personalize further interaction. Some of the practical applications of Dynamics 365 Customer Insights in the Microsoft cloud for financial services are: \r\n</p><ul><li>Wealth Management: The Microsoft cloud lets you analyze the accounts and portfolios of customers, track their risk tolerance, and manage different financial goals to process personalized investments. \r\n</li><li>Retail Banking: Understand customer habits of purchase and predict future needs to recommend relevant products. \r\n</li><li>Streamlining Insurance: Offer bespoke insurance options based on different requirements or parameters. Also, financial data enables you to understand the risk profiles of customers through different milestones of their lifecycle.</li></ul><h3>2. Microsoft Power Apps \r\n</h3><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-apps/\">Power Apps</a> is a powerful business solution that empowers users to build custom, personalized applications without writing a line of code. Also, it helps you automate tasks and simplify the complex processes of financial institutions. Integrating <a href=\"https://nachonacho.com/business-loans-and-debt-financing-for-smbs-and-startups\" target=\"_blank\">startup business loans</a> into your financial services strategy can significantly enhance the efficiency and customer satisfaction of your loan origination, underwriting, and claim processing workflows.</p><ul><li>Loan Origination: Simplify the process of loan applications, from applying to dispatching the amount to the borrower’s account through custom applications. It will make the process simple, fast, and reliable while focusing on the customer experience, similar to how services like <a href=\"https://www.dotdotloans.co.uk/short-term-loans/\" target=\"_blank\">short term loans</a> make <a href=\"https://www.achieve.com/learn/personal-loans/short-term-loan\" target=\"_blank\">short-term borrowing</a> accessible and straightforward\r\n</li><li>Underwriting: Approve loan applications when a customer profile meets the standard loan requirements. Also, you can automate the risk assessment process while improving efficiency.</li><li>Claim Processing: Build simple and interactive mobile applications to process the loan and claim application without any hassle. It will enable you to track each application with improved convenience.</li></ul><h3>3. Microsoft 365 \r\n</h3><p>Access the Microsoft Cloud capabilities to utilize popular and effective productive tools from Microsoft, like Outlook, Word, Excel, and more. \r\n</p><ul><li>Secure Team Collaboration: Establish secure and consistent communication channels to share data with the team in real-time. It lets different departments collaborate on a single project, accelerating overall business efficiency. \r\n</li><li>Simplify External Communication: Communicate with the clients while ensuring data safety through secure communication channels, like email, team meetings, and financial discussion. \r\n</li><li>Regulatory Compliance: Get access to the advanced capabilities of Microsoft 365 Financial Services, like data loss prevention and audit trails, to regulate financial communication and transactions.</li></ul><h3>4. Microsoft Power Platform \r\n</h3><p>It is a complete platform that offers five applications to build custom apps without code, automate tasks, visualize data, build workflows, and make compelling landing pages. \r\n</p><ul><li>Automate Workflows: Eliminate manual tasks with automation. You can automate report generation, account reconciliation, payroll management, the onboarding process, and building a self-help platform for employees. \r\n</li><li>Data Analytics Dashboards: Create reports and dashboards to analyze and visualize data to make data-driven decisions. Fetch the hidden information and find useful insights from a centralized dashboard. \r\n</li><li>Fraud Detection &amp; Monitoring: Build tailored reports in <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">Microsoft Power BI</a> to find any kind of data inaccuracy, issues in transaction data, and fraudulent actions.</li></ul><h3>5. Dynamics 365 Fraud Protection \r\n</h3><p>Leverage the limitless capabilities of Microsoft Cloud embedded with AI technologies to find any kind of fraud and malicious activity in real-time and eliminate them before they do any harm to the financial data or to the system.  \r\n</p><ul><li>Real-time Transaction Monitoring: Track and analyze financial transactions in real-time to identify any kind of suspicious action, activity, or pattern. \r\n</li><li>Adaptive Machine Learning: The adaptive learning of the Microsoft cloud for financial activities lets you access historical or master data to protect the customer from all threats. \r\n</li><li>Prevent Suspicious Activities: Access the capabilities of AI to find legal or fraudulent transactions happening in your business to cater your services to genuine customers only.</li></ul><h3>6. Compliance Program for Microsoft Cloud \r\n</h3><p>The Compliance Program for Microsoft Cloud empowers you to adhere to global, changing compliance\'s to deal with financial complexities. \r\n</p><ul><li>Data Residency and Encryption: Microsoft will make sure to store your precious data and encrypt it whenever you process a financial transaction while following compliance regulations, like GDPR. \r\n</li><li>Audit Logging and Reporting: You can track user activity, maintain comprehensive audit logs, and regulate the data to meet compliance. \r\n</li><li>Regulatory Updates: The Microsoft Cloud for Financial Services will let you stay updated and relevant as per changing financial regulations. Also, it will let you follow <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/\">Microsoft’s guidance</a> within the Microsoft Cloud Environment. \r\n</li></ul>\r\n<h2 id=\"How-to-get-more-with-microsoft-cloud-for-financial-services\">How to get more with Microsoft Cloud for Financial Services?</h2>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.miquido.com/blog/generative-ai-in-banking-and-finance/\" target=\"_blank\">Generative AI</a> is evolving and helping businesses to accelerate performance, simplify financial operations, empower employees, manage risk, digitalize the business, and maximize revenue, eliminating redundancies from the system. Implementing an industry-focused Microsoft cloud solution will resolve all business issues while pushing operations to scale. \r\n</p><p>Choosing the perfect financial solution for a unique business might seem like a hectic task for you. Because, you know your business well, but do not know the practical capabilities of a solution that can supercharge operations. \r\n</p><p>In such a scenario, feel free to contact Dynamics Square, your reliable <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/microsoft-dynamics-365-partner/\">Microsoft global financial support partner</a>. With 12+ years of experience and 135+ technical consultants, we are ready to take your business to the next level - in terms of growth and revenue.</p><p>Whenever there is a need, feel free to write us an email <b>arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</b> or you can call us at <b>+1 281 899 0865</b> for instant support.</p>\r\n\r\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">// <![CDATA[\r\nconst buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n\r\nbuttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n    button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n  );\r\n});\r\n// ]]></script>\r\n<style>\r\n/* The Modal (background) */\r\n#image-viewer {\r\n  display: none;\r\n  position: fixed;\r\n  z-index: 999;\r\n  padding: 70px;\r\n  left: 0;\r\n  top: 0;\r\n  width: 100%;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  overflow: auto;\r\n  background-color: rgb(0,0,0);\r\n  background-color: rgba(45, 62, 80, 0.99);\r\n}\r\n.modal-content {\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n  display: block;\r\n  width: 80%;\r\n  max-width: 100%;\r\n}\r\n.modal-content { \r\n  animation-name: zoom;\r\n  animation-duration: 0.6s;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@keyframes zoom {\r\n  from {transform:scale(0)} \r\n  to {transform:scale(1)}\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close {\r\n  position: absolute;\r\n  top: 15px;\r\n  right: 35px;\r\n  color: #f1f1f1;\r\n  font-size: 40px;\r\n  font-weight: bold;\r\n  transition: 0.3s;\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close:hover,\r\n#image-viewer .close:focus {\r\n  color: #bbb;\r\n  text-decoration: none;\r\n  cursor: pointer;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@media only screen and (max-width: 700px){\r\n  .modal-content {\r\n      width: 100%;\r\n      height:auto;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<script src=\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js\"></script><script>\r\n$(\"img\").on(\'click\',function(){\r\n   $(\"#full-image\").attr(\"src\", $(this).attr(\"src\"));\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').show();\r\n});\r\n\r\n$(\"#image-viewer .close\").click(function(){\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').hide();\r\n});\r\n</script><script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n      button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n    );\r\n  });\r\n  </script>\r\n<script>\r\n $(document).on(\'click\', \'a[href^=\"#\"]\', function (event) {\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    $(\'h2\').css(\'padding-top\',\'75px\');\r\n   $(\'html, body\').animate({\r\n        scrollTop: $($.attr(this, \'href\')).offset().top\r\n    });\r\n});\r\n\r\n</script>', 'Microsoft Cloud for Financial Services: A Perfect Choice to Simplify Finances', 'microsoft cloud for financial services', 'Unlock a personalized banking experience & fight fraud with cutting-edge tech! ️ Discover the power of Microsoft Cloud for Financial Services.', 'cloud for financial services microsoft,microsoft cloud for financial services,cloud for financial services,microsoft financial services,microsoft 365 financial services,microsoft cloud financial services', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1797133608993185.png', 'Samar Malik', 'samar.malik@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/microsoft-cloud-for-financial-services/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Microsoft Cloud for Financial Services: A Perfect Choice to Simplify Finances\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Unlock a personalized banking experience & fight fraud with cutting-edge tech! ️ Discover the power of Microsoft Cloud for Financial Services.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1797134172340562.Microsoft Cloud for Financial Services.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Samar Malik\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Samar-Malik/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-04-23\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-04-23\"\r\n}', '[]', '03:45:39pm', '2024-06-10', '9 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2026-01-23 22:45:39'),
(197, 'Everything Need to Know About Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM', 'overview-of-microsoft-dynamics-365-crm', 'Dynamics 365 CRM', 'dynamics-365-crm', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1797214706106219.jpg', 'Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM is an advanced solution that enables organizations to manage their customer relationships and improve their sales and marketing strategies. This blog post sheds light on different aspects of Microsoft Dynamics CRM.', '<p>Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM is an advanced solution that enables organizations to manage their customer relationships and improve their sales and marketing strategies.</p><p>A report by <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://market.us/\" target=\"_blank\">Market.us</a> reveals that the world market size for CRM software is speculated to hit USD 248.2 billion mark by 2033 from USD 75.1 Billion in 2023. It is expected to expand at an impressive rate of 12.7% from 2024 to 2033.</p><p>So, what is it about this software solution that businesses want to invest in it? Let’s find out in this blog post that particularly sheds light on different aspects of Microsoft Dynamics CRM. Keep reading to learn more about them.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blog-content-container\">\r\n    <div class=\"blog-content active\">\r\n    <h4 class=\"blog-content-title\">&nbsp;Table of Content</h4>\r\n    <div class=\"inner\">\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-is-microsoft-dynamics-crm\">1. What is Microsoft Dynamics CRM?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-is-the-purpose-of-using-microsoft-dynamics-365-crm\">2. What is the Purpose of Using Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Benefits-of-microsoft-dynamics-365-crm\">3. Benefits of Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM</a>\r\n\r\n  </div>\r\n   <button class=\"blog-content-toggle\"> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"><!--! Font Awesome Free 6.4.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license (Commercial License) Copyright 2023 Fonticons, Inc. --><path d=\"M201.4 342.6c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0l160-160c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0L224 274.7 86.6 137.4c-12.5-12.5-32.8-12.5-45.3 0s-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160z\"></path></svg></button>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h2 id=\"What-is-microsoft-dynamics-crm\">What is Microsoft Dynamics CRM?</h2>\r\n<p>Dynamics 365 CRM (now known as <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-customer-engagement/\">Dynamics 365 Customer Engagement</a>) is a package of software applications designed to help businesses keep records of their existing and potential customers.  \r\n</p><p>Keeping customer information in an integrated way helps users to access data anytime and from anywhere. They can conveniently interact with existing customers and prospects, generate leads, and provide better resolution to their concerns.  \r\n</p><p>Being a cloud-based solution, it offers immediate visibility across multiple channels of a business operation. Besides, it enables businesses to timely respond to customers’ demands and understand their behavior. \r\n</p><p>This advanced software takes care of several critical business aspects, including marketing, sales, lead generation, field service, technical support, and customer service.  \r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM</a> can help minimize costs and drive growth by managing and automating operations that elevate customer satisfaction.  \r\n</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"What-is-the-purpose-of-using-microsoft-dynamics-365-crm\">What is the Purpose of Using Dynamics 365 CRM?</h2>\r\n<p>Earlier, companies would rely on emails, spreadsheets, and mostly paper-based CRM tools to track customer data. This conventional approach often lacked consistency, automation, and coordination across the teams while sharing updated information.  \r\n</p><p>Microsoft Dynamics CRM fills this void by bringing all aspects of business to the same page and ruling out silos.  \r\n</p><p>The customer data in the CRM includes a wealth of information related to customers, including their contact numbers, email addresses, locations, purchase details, chat histories, feedback, etc. This collection of data helps companies analyze their customers in a better way and make decisions accordingly.  \r\n</p><p>Customer data provides businesses with significant insights regarding their purchase patterns, preferences, and requirements. Also, they can easily gauge which approach brings the most or least profit to their companies.  \r\n</p><p>Businesses can seamlessly integrate Dynamics CRM with different business tools, like online chat and file-sharing apps. Besides, it comes powered with AI capabilities that optimize and accelerate workflow and help organizations make more informed decisions.  \r\n</p><h3>How does Microsoft Dynamics CRM help Businesses Grow Faster? \r\n</h3><p>Dynamics 365 CRM is responsible for increasing customer engagement with businesses.  \r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-sales/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales</a> consolidates all sales and customer data, providing an in-depth view of customer’s online activity, nurturing customer satisfaction, enhancing brand loyalty, and converting them into leads. This helps them reach out to more customers while saving time and resources. \r\n</p><p>Also, this CRM solution comes with powerful analytical capabilities that provide critical business insights and help manage the overall customer support chains. \r\n</p><h3>Why Implement a Microsoft Dynamics CRM Solution? \r\n</h3><p>Dynamics 365 CRM facilitates customer engagement, centralizes sales data, and simplifies the sales and marketing process. \r\n</p><p>This cloud-based CRM is a highly flexible and customizable software solution, offering tools to organize all customer information in one place. Users can leverage this centralized information to improve communication, enhance customer relationships, and ultimately boost sales.  \r\n</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Benefits-of-microsoft-dynamics-365-crm\">Benefits of Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM</h2>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a> can streamline your business efficiently while minimizing the travel time for field agents, improving overall efficiency, and delivering customers a better experience. It has several benefits: \r\n</p><h3>1. Seamless Integration with Other Software Solutions from Microsoft Ecosystem \r\n</h3><p>Dynamics CRM easily integrates with the Office 365 suite to work in tandem with different productivity tools. As a result, users can move data from Dynamics 365 CRM to Microsoft Excel for organizing and assessing it. Besides, it can be integrated with the Teams app to collaborate through voice and video calls and even <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">Power BI</a> for data analytics. \r\n</p><p>Seamless integration facilitates fast data sharing as it is quite easy to switch between multiple apps. For instance, users can tap into <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-marketing/\">Dynamics 365 Customer Insights</a> functionality to assess customer data and gauge their buying behavior and preferences.  \r\n</p><h3>2. Improved Customer Service Experience \r\n</h3><p>Earn customers for life by optimizing the productivity of your agents with the help of the <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-customer-service/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Customer Service</a> application.  \r\n</p><p>This empowers your agents to address customer queries/requests from any channel and even manage more than one session at a time using multiple apps while being relevant. This helps improve their efficiency and enhance customer service experience. \r\n</p><h3>3. 24/7 Accessibility \r\n</h3><p>Using cloud technology, Dynamics 365 CRM offers seamless remote access in any part of the world. For instance, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-field-service/\">Dynamics 365 Field Service</a> applications enable businesses to offer onsite services at customer locations. \r\n</p><p>With information access at their fingertips, professionals can easily update their work status on the go anytime, anywhere. \r\n</p><h3>4. Better Decision Making  \r\n</h3><p>Dynamics CRM is powered by advanced analytics and AI capabilities to enable predictive assessment. It can examine market trends, identify buying patterns, and monitor customer behavior. \r\n</p><p>The data-driven predictions and visibility across the business help business leaders make quick and careful decisions which can lead to minimizing costs and increasing revenues.    \r\n</p><h3>5. Automated Workflows \r\n</h3><p>Repetitive and mundane business tasks are often tedious and time-consuming. They are susceptible to human errors. Dynamics CRM equips advanced automation tools like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-automate/\">Microsoft Power Automate</a> and built-in workflow to save time and resources on redundancies and manual entries.  \r\n</p><p>In addition, users can build customized apps in a few steps. Automation helps make the entire process paperless and boosts productivity while eliminating mundane tasks.   \r\n</p><h3>6. Robust Data Security \r\n</h3><p>Microsoft Dynamics CRM is a cloud-based solution that comprises different security features such as a disaster recovery tool to back up the entire database.  \r\n</p><p>Dynamics CRM adheres to industry norms and regulations in terms of data security. It is under regulatory control of <a href=\"https://nordlayer.com/security-compliance/iso-27001/\" target=\"_blank\">ISO 27001</a> which keeps a close watch on data safety using strict data security measures. \r\n</p><p>To learn more about or <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">implement Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM</a>, get in touch with us today!</p><p>Explore <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/crm-implementation-services/\" target=\"_blank\">CRM implementation services</a> designed to scale and grow businesses</p>\r\n\r\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">// <![CDATA[\r\nconst buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n\r\nbuttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n    button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n  );\r\n});\r\n// ]]></script>\r\n<style>\r\n/* The Modal (background) */\r\n#image-viewer {\r\n  display: none;\r\n  position: fixed;\r\n  z-index: 999;\r\n  padding: 70px;\r\n  left: 0;\r\n  top: 0;\r\n  width: 100%;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  overflow: auto;\r\n  background-color: rgb(0,0,0);\r\n  background-color: rgba(45, 62, 80, 0.99);\r\n}\r\n.modal-content {\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n  display: block;\r\n  width: 80%;\r\n  max-width: 100%;\r\n}\r\n.modal-content { \r\n  animation-name: zoom;\r\n  animation-duration: 0.6s;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@keyframes zoom {\r\n  from {transform:scale(0)} \r\n  to {transform:scale(1)}\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close {\r\n  position: absolute;\r\n  top: 15px;\r\n  right: 35px;\r\n  color: #f1f1f1;\r\n  font-size: 40px;\r\n  font-weight: bold;\r\n  transition: 0.3s;\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close:hover,\r\n#image-viewer .close:focus {\r\n  color: #bbb;\r\n  text-decoration: none;\r\n  cursor: pointer;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@media only screen and (max-width: 700px){\r\n  .modal-content {\r\n      width: 100%;\r\n      height:auto;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<script src=\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js\"></script><script>\r\n$(\"img\").on(\'click\',function(){\r\n   $(\"#full-image\").attr(\"src\", $(this).attr(\"src\"));\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').show();\r\n});\r\n\r\n$(\"#image-viewer .close\").click(function(){\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').hide();\r\n});\r\n</script><script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n      button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n    );\r\n  });\r\n  </script>\r\n<script>\r\n $(document).on(\'click\', \'a[href^=\"#\"]\', function (event) {\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    $(\'h2\').css(\'padding-top\',\'75px\');\r\n   $(\'html, body\').animate({\r\n        scrollTop: $($.attr(this, \'href\')).offset().top\r\n    });\r\n});\r\n\r\n</script>', 'Everything Need to Know About Dynamics 365 CRM', 'dynamics 365 crm', 'Unleash the power of Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM! Learn how this cloud-based CRM can boost sales, personalize customer service and streamline your business.', 'microsoft dynamics 365 crm,dynamics 365 crm,microsoft dynamics crm,dynamics crm,dynamics 365 customer engagement,d365 customer engagement', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1797214706108860.jpg', 'Mukesh Jha', 'mukesh.jha@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/overview-of-microsoft-dynamics-365-crm/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Everything Need to Know About Dynamics 365 CRM\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Unleash the power of Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM! Learn how this cloud-based CRM can boost sales, personalize customer service and streamline your business.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1797215627635862.Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM.jpg\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Mukesh Jha\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Mukesh-Jha/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/backend/assets/images/dynamics_square_tm_logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-04-24\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-04-24\"\r\n}', NULL, '01:54:12pm', '2024-05-07', '8 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-04-18 13:54:12'),
(198, 'How Power Apps with Business Central Integration Works?', 'power-apps-with-business-central', 'Integration', 'integration', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1797764774799880.Power Apps with Business Central.png', 'Power Apps with Business Central has become the chemical X to survive in the world of cutting-edge technologies and dealing with business particularities.', '<p>Power Apps with Business Central has become the chemical X to survive in the world of cutting-edge technologies and dealing with business particularities. This combination is in demand among business owners due to the powerful capabilities of <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Dynamics Business Central</a> and the low-code ability of Power apps to build personalized applications with minimal effort.</p><p>Before getting into the process and benefits of Power Apps integration with Business Central, let’s understand the need for this active cooperation. \r\n</p><p>The core growth factor is the uniqueness of the way a business manages its internal and external operations while continuously approaching the growth path. It’s a fact, and we (business owners and decision-makers) accept this through customer responses and market scenarios. \r\n</p><p>Streamlining and managing the uniqueness of the business requires resources, infrastructure, and high-tech business solutions. In modern businesses, we see several operations that must be handled accurately.</p><p>Like getting real-time sales insights, maintaining inventory levels across different warehouses, automating invoicing, and building cross-sell and upsell opportunities. \r\n</p><p>You can easily tackle such challenges by leveraging a perfectly aligned <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\" target=\"_blank\">ERP solution</a>, like Microsoft Business Central. It is an all-in-one cloud-based business solution with powerful functionalities to manage and streamline business operations regardless of industry type and size.</p><p>Being a cost-effective and reliable solution, Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central offers seamless customization and native integration capabilities to match the originality of the business. \r\n</p><p>You can easily integrate Power Apps (one of the solutions of the <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-platform/\">Microsoft Power Platform</a>) to build customized applications to meet the specific requirements of a business. To understand the practical usage of this powerful blend (Business Central with Power Apps), check out the case study below:</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blog-content-container\">\r\n    <div class=\"blog-content active\">\r\n    <h4 class=\"blog-content-title\">&nbsp;Table of Content</h4>\r\n    <div class=\"inner\">\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Case-study-streamlining-inventory-management-system-of-a-business\">1. Case Study: Streamlining Inventory Management System of a Business</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#How-power-apps-can-enhance-your-business-central-experience\">2. How Power Apps Can Enhance Your Business Central Experience?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Power-apps-with-business-central-integration\">3. Power Apps with Business Central Integration: Let’s Get Started</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n   <button class=\"blog-content-toggle\"> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"><!--! Font Awesome Free 6.4.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license (Commercial License) Copyright 2023 Fonticons, Inc. --><path d=\"M201.4 342.6c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0l160-160c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0L224 274.7 86.6 137.4c-12.5-12.5-32.8-12.5-45.3 0s-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160z\"></path></svg></button>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h2 id=\"Case-study-streamlining-inventory-management-system-of-a-business\">Case Study: Streamlining Inventory Management System of a Business</h2>\r\n<p><b>Challenge:</b> The company doesn’t have any ERP system and totally relies on manual ways of managing different inventory operations. Such operations include, purchase order creation, low stock alert, maintaining stock levels, real-time data, modifying stocks, locating inventory, and more. Such processes require a lot of time and come with numerous errors due to manual methods. \r\n</p><p><b>Solution:</b> To resolve such issues, the company has opted for <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-business-central-implementation/\">Business Central implementation</a> along with Microsoft Power Apps integration. With this implementation, they can perform the following operations seamlessly: \r\n</p><p><b>1. Real-time Scanning \r\n</b></p><p>Power Apps enables the business to build custom applications to scan barcodes using mobile devices during stock monitoring. When you update the data using the mobile app, it will automatically be updated in the Business Central database, offering a bi-directional connection. \r\n</p><p><b>2. Stock Alerts \r\n</b></p><p>You can enable the custom build application to monitor stock levels and notify the user in case of stockouts or overstocking. It will help you maintain an optimum level of stocks. \r\n</p><p><b>3. Purchase Order Creation \r\n</b></p><p>Using the capabilities of Power Apps, you can create sale and purchase orders based on inventory levels. Based on your inputs, the app will automatically fetch relevant data from Business Central, like product information and pricing. \r\n</p><p>The integration of Power Apps with Business Central empowers the organization to become more productive, efficient, and accurate. \r\n</p><p>There are numerous applications of Power Apps, and the previous case study is one such example. You can access <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-apps/\">Microsoft Power Apps</a> to build low-code applications to streamline unique business operations. \r\n</p><ul><li>Build personalized applications for sales professionals so that they can track leads, opportunities, and prospects while focusing on the conversion rate. \r\n</li><li>Build apps for field and service agents to track customer issues, resources, and issue resolution status. \r\n</li><li>Develop a workflow for expense reports, leave applications, and purchase requests.  \r\n</li></ul>\r\n<h2 id=\"How-power-apps-can-enhance-your-business-central-experience\">How Power Apps Can Enhance Your Business Central Experience?</h2>\r\n<p>Microsoft Power Apps enables a business to simplify a complex operation or workflow with a custom-built app that totally justifies the system requirements. In most cases, Business Central offers standard capabilities, but what if business requires advanced tools to simplify a process? In such a scenario, the integration of Business Central with Power Apps comes into play. \r\n</p><p><b>1. Enhanced Efficiency \r\n</b></p><p>Eliminate system redundancies and embrace automation to increase overall efficiency while maintaining a growth path. With Power Apps, you can automate the repetitive and manual tasks that consume a lot of resources and remove any chances of human errors. \r\n</p><p><b>2. Automation \r\n</b></p><p>Simplify business operations and influence employees to utilize cloud-based automation capabilities. Also, you can use Microsoft Power Apps to fetch important information and set up pre-defined triggers to reduce manual data entry and accelerate the entire process. \r\n</p><p><b>3. Improved User Efficiency \r\n</b></p><p>Build an application and tailor its user interface to match the custom requirements of specific roles. It lets you consume the important information you need to focus on your tasks. Also, you can connect with Microsoft Dynamics Business Central data anytime and anywhere using cloud deployment. \r\n</p><p><b>4. Good Data Visibility \r\n</b></p><p>Power Apps lets you build custom dashboards to access real-time data using D365 Business Central. With a centralized data repository, you can access accurate insights to make data-driven decisions. Also, MS Power Apps lets you connect different data sources to collect data and perform in-depth analysis. \r\n</p><p><b>5. Easy Scalability \r\n</b></p><p>The best part of the <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 </a>ecosystem is its strong scalability capabilities. The performance of Microsoft Business Central and Power Apps can be scaled as your business grows. Also, you can build department-oriented applications to address unique business challenges and requirements. \r\n</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Power-apps-with-business-central-integration\">Power Apps with Business Central Integration: Let’s Get Started</h2>\r\n<p>The process of connecting Power Apps with Business Central is simple and can be easily accessed with the right procedure. However, in cases of complexity or any unknown issue, you can contact Dynamics Square at <b><a href=\"tel:+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a></b> to get instant help.</p><p> \r\n</p><ul><li>Open the Microsoft Power Apps and log in with your credentials. (licensed version) \r\n</li><li>Open the Power Apps, find the Business Central option on the homepage under Connections. \r\n</li><li>Choose the connection type: Business Central Cloud or on-premises tenant. \r\n</li><li>Now, enter your Business Central credentials, select the work environment, and specify the company you want to connect with. \r\n</li><li>Once we can establish a connection between Power Apps and Business Central, you will see the list of tables (BC’s data) on the Power Apps homepage. \r\n</li><li>These tables contain the data you will need to build the app in Power App. \r\n</li><li>Leverage the easy navigation module and drag-and-drop features to build the application. \r\n</li><li>Based on collected data through Business Central, you can create forms, charts, and galleries within the app. \r\n</li><li>Also, you can access the formulas and logic to utilize the data and build your application.</li></ul><p>No one is aware of any unexpected error or issue. If you encounter any issues while connecting Power Apps with Business Central or building a desired application, feel free to contact Dynamics Square at <b><a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a></b>. The team of <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation</a> experts is readily available to resolve any kind of complexity in no time.</p>\r\n\r\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">// <![CDATA[\r\nconst buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n\r\nbuttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n    button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n  );\r\n});\r\n// ]]></script>\r\n<style>\r\n/* The Modal (background) */\r\n#image-viewer {\r\n  display: none;\r\n  position: fixed;\r\n  z-index: 999;\r\n  padding: 70px;\r\n  left: 0;\r\n  top: 0;\r\n  width: 100%;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  overflow: auto;\r\n  background-color: rgb(0,0,0);\r\n  background-color: rgba(45, 62, 80, 0.99);\r\n}\r\n.modal-content {\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n  display: block;\r\n  width: 80%;\r\n  max-width: 100%;\r\n}\r\n.modal-content { \r\n  animation-name: zoom;\r\n  animation-duration: 0.6s;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@keyframes zoom {\r\n  from {transform:scale(0)} \r\n  to {transform:scale(1)}\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close {\r\n  position: absolute;\r\n  top: 15px;\r\n  right: 35px;\r\n  color: #f1f1f1;\r\n  font-size: 40px;\r\n  font-weight: bold;\r\n  transition: 0.3s;\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close:hover,\r\n#image-viewer .close:focus {\r\n  color: #bbb;\r\n  text-decoration: none;\r\n  cursor: pointer;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@media only screen and (max-width: 700px){\r\n  .modal-content {\r\n      width: 100%;\r\n      height:auto;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<script src=\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js\"></script><script>\r\n$(\"img\").on(\'click\',function(){\r\n   $(\"#full-image\").attr(\"src\", $(this).attr(\"src\"));\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').show();\r\n});\r\n\r\n$(\"#image-viewer .close\").click(function(){\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').hide();\r\n});\r\n</script><script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n      button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n    );\r\n  });\r\n  </script>\r\n<script>\r\n $(document).on(\'click\', \'a[href^=\"#\"]\', function (event) {\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    $(\'h2\').css(\'padding-top\',\'75px\');\r\n   $(\'html, body\').animate({\r\n        scrollTop: $($.attr(this, \'href\')).offset().top\r\n    });\r\n});\r\n\r\n</script>', 'How Power Apps with Business Central Integration Works?', 'power apps with business central', 'Simplify business processes! Craft custom apps in Power Apps that connect directly to your Dynamics 365 Business Central data. Streamline workflows and boost efficiency. Learn more about Power Apps with Business Central integration.', 'microsoft power apps,power apps,business central,dynamics 365 business central,power apps with business central,power apps integration with business central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1797764774799884.Power Apps with Business Central.png', 'Vivek Gururani', 'vivek.gururani@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/power-apps-with-business-central/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"How Power Apps with Business Central Integration Works?\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Simplify business processes! Craft custom apps in Power Apps that connect directly to your Dynamics 365 Business Central data. Streamline workflows and boost efficiency. Learn more about Power Apps with Business Central integration.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1797764735440147.Power Apps with Business Central.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Vivek Gururani\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Vivek-Gururani/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-04-30\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-04-30\"\r\n}', NULL, '04:58:02pm', '2024-05-03', '8 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-11-13 16:58:02');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(199, 'Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare: Enhance Patient Care', 'microsoft-cloud-for-healthcare', 'Microsoft Cloud', 'microsoft-cloud', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1801832261743244.Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare.png', 'Improve patient care with Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare. Streamline operations, enhance collaboration, and drive better health outcomes.', '<p></p><p>Imagine a bustling emergency room where doctors and nurses are racing against time to save lives. A patient arrives in a critical condition, and every second counts. The medical team needs immediate access to the patient\'s history, current medications, and previous treatments to make informed decisions. However, the information is scattered across different systems, causing delays and increasing the risk of errors. \r\n</p><p>This scenario highlights the urgent need for Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare. By integrating patient data into a unified, secure platform, healthcare providers can access real-time information, streamline workflows, and enhance patient care. Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare offers advanced analytics, AI-driven insights, and seamless collaboration tools, ensuring that healthcare professionals have the resources they need to deliver timely and effective care. \r\n</p><p>Before we embark on our journey to explore the detailed aspects of Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare, let’s take a look at these startling stats regarding the rise of cloud computing in the healthcare sector. The healthcare domain is moving towards cloud computing due to its expansion and demand for a centralized data system.  \r\n</p><p>The global healthcare cloud computing market is expected to grow at a CAGR of 17.9%, from $41.12 billion in 2024 to $320.9 billion in 2034. (<a href=\"https://www.factmr.com/report/healthcare-cloud-computing-market\" target=\"_blank\">Source</a>)</p><h2>What is Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare?\r\n</h2><p>The best way to define Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare is to think of a hospital where technology delivers life-saving insights to doctors, alerts nurses before emergencies happen, and lets patients heal at home without feeling alone. </p><p>That’s exactly what this comprehensive solution does. It is a digital lifeline that transforms scattered medical data into meaningful actions. And it’s not just about even technology; it’s about giving healthcare professionals superhuman awareness and patients the comfort of knowing they’re always connected to care.</p><h2>How can Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare transform the health sector? \r\n</h2><p>Let’s take a real-life example to understand how Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare can revolutionize the entire health domain. Let’s suppose, there is a City Health Hospital, which used Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare to significantly enhance patient care and operational efficiency.  \r\n</p><p>By leveraging Azure Healthcare Data Services, the hospital centralized patient records, allowing healthcare professionals to access real-time, secure information from any location. This improved decision-making and reduced errors. \r\n</p><p>The hospital also implemented Microsoft Teams for Healthcare, facilitating seamless communication among doctors, nurses, and administrative staff. This enhanced collaboration led to quicker responses and more coordinated care.  \r\n</p><p>Additionally, telemedicine capabilities allowed virtual consultations, expanding access to care and reducing waiting times, especially for remote or immobile patients. \r\n</p><p>To ensure data security and compliance with regulations like <a href=\"https://sprinto.com/blog/hipaa-compliance/\" target=\"_blank\">HIPAA compliance</a>, the hospital utilized Azure Security Center, which provided robust protection for patient information. Azure AI helped identify high-risk patients, enabling early interventions and personalized treatment plans, ultimately improving patient outcomes. \r\n</p><p>Administrative tasks like appointment scheduling and billing were streamlined using Microsoft Power Platform, freeing up staff to focus more on patient care. Finally, Azure Synapse Analytics enabled the hospital to forecast resource needs and optimize staff allocation, improving overall efficiency. \r\n</p><p>In the end, the hospital was able to provide better care, improve operational efficiency, and ensure data security and compliance, all while leveraging the power of Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare. \r\n</p><blockquote><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Want to take your healthcare services to the next level utilizing the benefits of Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare. Schedule a free call now!&nbsp;</b></a></blockquote><h2>Microsoft Cloud Service for Healthcare Providers \r\n</h2><p>Microsoft Cloud Service for Healthcare Providers offers numerous capabilities, among which some are discussed below. \r\n</p><h4>1. Clinical Documentation \r\n</h4><p>Utilize clinical intelligence to establish communication with the patients and track their activities. Also, you can integrate the clinical speech recognition add-ons for ease of communication. Even so, you can utilize Nuance Dragon Medical Advisor, a computer-operated physician documentation program, to receive reliable and relatable real-time support.</p><h4>2. Enhance Team Productivity \r\n</h4><p>Establish communication with the patient to transfer the right information to the right authority while maintaining a streamlined communication channel. Also, it lets you optimize team performance and find gaps in the treatment process. \r\n</p><h4>3. Strong Diagnostic Capabilities \r\n</h4><p>Collect and centralize the diagnostics of a patient to let the care team focus on critical measures. You can even upload or store the diagnostic reports so that anyone can access the data from anywhere and anytime, promoting a good patient experience. \r\n</p><h4>4. Patient Health Data Management \r\n</h4><p>Analyze the existing patient data to find new growth opportunities leveraging the functionalities of AI, actionable intelligence, and machine learning. With accurate clinical analytics, you can streamline financial operations, risk assessment processes, and data modeling capabilities. \r\n</p><h4>5. Establishing Connection with Patient \r\n</h4><p>Connect with patients anytime and anywhere with a responsive mobile application. It enables you to take care of your patients virtually and offers personalized experiences across the wellbeing journey. Also, you can integrate AI-enabled chatbots to schedule appointments and submit documents digitally. \r\n</p><h2>What does Microsoft Cloud have for Patients? \r\n</h2><p>Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare connects patients with professionals to deliver an exceptional level of care. It optimizes the core processes, reduces overall costs, and ensures optimum quality with adequate coordination effectiveness. \r\n</p><p>Some of the core Microsoft Cloud for healthcare features are specifically built for patients. \r\n</p><h4>1. Offer Great Patient Experience \r\n</h4><p>Utilize cognitive AI capabilities to build a platform where a patient can talk to the expert whenever they want. Also, you can avail yourself of a 360-degree view of the activities and interactions that a healthcare executive is performing. \r\n</p><h4>2. Digitalize Patient Operations \r\n</h4><p>Collect and track all healthcare operations using digital means through a secure connection. This data will help you prevent disease and forecast critical illnesses. Based on data, you can build tailored patient care plans while offering a good executive experience. \r\n</p><h4>3. Enhance Workforce Experience \r\n</h4><p>Streamline processes through automation to set up a unified system for data exchange. It will promote you to boost productivity, enhance performance, and maximize patient experience. With real-time process transparency, you can take care of resources and executive management. \r\n</p><p><b>Also Read: </b><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/best-practices-for-healthcare-hiring/\" target=\"_blank\">Best Practices for Healthcare Hiring</a> \r\n</p><h4>4. Protection of Sensitive Data \r\n</h4><p>Microsoft offers a totally secure platform where you can share and collect data without worrying about threats or data leaks. During the transfer, Microsoft encrypts the data to make it almost impossible to crack and read. \r\n</p><h4>5. Compliance Friendly \r\n</h4><p>International businesses have to follow different compliance and tax norms to perform smooth business across global boundaries. It leverages the latest technologies to automate the process of accepting different compliances while monitoring the complete process.</p><h2>Microsoft Cloud for HealthCare Pricing Structure</h2><p>The pricing structure for Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare is designed to be flexible and scalable, depending on the specific needs of your organization. Here’s a simple breakdown.&nbsp;</p><ul><li><b>Base Licensing</b>: You need to have licenses for the core Microsoft products like Microsoft 365, Dynamics 365, Power Platform, and Azure. These are the foundational services that support the healthcare-specific features.&nbsp;</li><li><b>Healthcare Add-On</b>: This is an additional cost on top of the base licenses. The add-on provides healthcare-oriented templates, workflows, and applications. The cost for this add-on is $95 USD per user per month.&nbsp;</li><li><b>Azure Services</b>: Some services like Azure FHIR (Fast Healthcare Interoperability Resources) and Health Bot are billed separately depending on the usage. It implies that you will pay for these services based on how much you use them.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><p>Let’s take a look at the table below summarizes the price:&nbsp;</p><table class=\"table table-bordered\"><tbody><tr><td><b>Component</b></td><td><b>Cost</b>&nbsp;</td></tr><tr><td>Microsoft 365</td><td>Varies based on plan</td></tr><tr><td>Dynamics 365</td><td>Varies based on plan</td></tr><tr><td>Power Platform</td><td>Varies based on plan</td></tr><tr><td>Azure</td><td>Based on consumption</td></tr><tr><td>Healthcare Add-On</td><td>$95 USD per user, per month<br>\r\n</td></tr><tr><td>Azure API for FHIR<br>\r\n</td><td>Based on consumption<br>\r\n</td></tr><tr><td>Health Bot<br>\r\n</td><td>First 3,000 messages free, then based on usage<br>\r\n</td></tr></tbody></table><p>This structure allows organizations to pay for what they need and scale as they grow. </p><p></p><h3>Types of Licensing: Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare </h3><p><b>1. Prerequisite Licensing</b>: A prerequisite is something that is required before you can use or access another service or feature.&nbsp;</p><p><b>For example</b>: To use Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare, you must have certain foundational services like Microsoft 365, Power Platform, Dynamics 365, and Azure. These are essential and must be in place first.&nbsp;</p><p><b>2. Recommended Licensing</b>: Recommended means suggested or advised for optimal performance or experience, but not strictly necessary.&nbsp;</p><p><b>For example</b>: While you must have Microsoft 365, Power Platform, Dynamics 365, and Azure to use Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare, it is recommended to have specific plans like Microsoft 365 E3/E5 or Office 365 E3/E5 for better functionality and integration.&nbsp;</p><p>Along with this monthly subscription fee, you need to pay for the subscription to Microsoft Azure based on your data servers.&nbsp;</p><p>What will you get with a single license?&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Reliable healthcare connectors&nbsp;</li><li>Healthcare customizations and configurations&nbsp;</li><li>Attractive healthcare templates and effective workflows&nbsp;</li><li>Data model and API configurations</li></ul><p>Also, you need to get some prerequisite licenses for different Microsoft products to avail of certain capabilities of Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare.&nbsp;</p><h3>Pricing Datasheet: Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare&nbsp;</h3>\r\n<div class=\"table-responsive\">\r\n<table class=\"table-sakshii\" style=\"text-wrap-mode: nowrap;\"><tbody><tr><th rowspan=\"2\">Healthcare Scenario</th><th rowspan=\"2\">Capability</th><th colspan=\"1\">Microsoft 365</th><th colspan=\"3\">Power Platform</th><th colspan=\"5\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</th><th colspan=\"3\">Microsoft Azure</th></tr><tr><th>Microsoft Teams</th><th>Power Apps</th><th>Power Automate</th><th>Power BI</th><th>Marketing</th><th>Customer Insights</th><th>Customer Service Enterprise</th><th>Digital Messaging add-on</th><th>Field Service</th><th>API for FHIR</th><th>Health Bot</th><th>AI, ML, IoT Hub, IoT Edge</th></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"3\">Enhance Patient Engagement</td><td>Personalized Care</td><td></td><td class=\"blue-dot\">●</td><td></td><td class=\"blue-dot\">●</td><td></td><td class=\"diamond\">◆</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td class=\"blue-dot\">●</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Patient Insights</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td class=\"blue-dot\">●</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td class=\"blue-dot\">●</td><td></td><td></td><td class=\"blue-dot\">●</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Virtual Health</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td class=\"blue-dot\">●</td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"3\">Empower Health Team Collaboration</td><td>Care Team Collaboration</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td class=\"blue-dot\">●</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Care Coordination</td><td class=\"diamond\">◆</td><td class=\"blue-dot\">●</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td class=\"diamond\">◆</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Continuous Patient Monitoring</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td class=\"diamond\">◆</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td class=\"blue-dot\">●</td><td></td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"3\">Improve Clinical &amp; Operational Insights</td><td>Data Interoperability</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td class=\"blue-dot\">●</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Operational Analytics</td><td></td><td class=\"blue-dot\">●</td><td></td><td class=\"blue-dot\">●</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td class=\"blue-dot\">●</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Clinical Analytics</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td class=\"blue-dot\">●</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td class=\"blue-dot\">●</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n<p>As you can see in the above table, to avail yourself of Microsoft Healthcare, you need to purchase licenses of Microsoft 365, Power Platform, Microsoft Dynamics 365, and Microsoft Azure.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blog-faq-style\">\r\n                    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\r\n                    <h3>1. What is Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare?</h3>\r\n                    <p>Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare is a comprehensive suite of solutions designed to improve patient care, enhance health team collaboration, and optimize clinical and operational insights. It integrates capabilities from Microsoft Azure, Dynamics 365, Microsoft 365, and Power Platform to provide secure and connected patient experiences.</p>\r\n                  \r\n                    <h3>2. How does Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare enhance patient engagement? </h3> <p>Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare enhances patient engagement by providing personalized care, virtual health options, and patient insights. It empowers patients with tools for engagement and provides healthcare providers with insights to tailor interactions. Features include virtual visits, patient outreach, and a unified patient view.</p>\r\n<h3>3. Is Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare compliant with healthcare regulations?</h3>\r\n                    <p>Yes, Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare is compliant with various healthcare regulations, including HIPAA, HITRUST, and GDPR. It employs a robust security framework that encompasses industry best practices and standards, ensuring the protection and compliance of health data. </p> <h3>4. Can Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare integrate with existing Electronic Health Record (EHR) systems? </h3> <p>Yes, Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare can integrate with existing EHR systems. For example, it supports integration with systems like Epic on Azure, allowing healthcare organizations to leverage their existing EHR data while benefiting from cloud capabilities. </p>\r\n<h3>5. What are the key components of Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare?</h3> <p>The key components of Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare include: </p> <ul>\r\n                        <li>Patient Engagement: Tools for personalized care and virtual health.</li>\r\n<li>Health Team Collaboration: Solutions for seamless communication and coordination.</li>\r\n<li>Clinical and Operational Insights: Data analytics and insights to improve decision-making.</li>\r\n<li>Security and Compliance: Robust frameworks to ensure data protection and regulatory compliance.</li>\r\n                    </ul>\r\n<h3>6. How can my organization get started with Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare?</h3>\r\n                    <p>To get started with Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare, you can explore the <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/industry/healthcare/\" target=\"_blank\">official documentation and training resources</a> provided by Microsoft. These resources offer guidance on deploying and configuring the solutions, as well as practical exercises to help you set up healthcare applications using Dynamics 365, Power Platform, Microsoft 365, and Azure. </p> </div>  \r\n\r\n\r\n<h2>Explore the future of healthcare with Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare – Get started today!</h2><p>The power of Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare is undeniable in transforming the way health organizations operate, deliver, care, and improve patient outcomes. With its advanced capabilities in data management, security, and seamless collaboration, it’s time for your healthcare organization to elevate its services to new heights.  \r\n</p><p>At Dynamics Square, our expert consultants are here to guide you through every step of the implementation process. Whether you are looking to streamline your operations, enhance patient care, or boost your organization’s digital transformation, our team is equipped with the knowledge and experience to help you make the most out of Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare.  \r\n</p><p>Don’t wait, take the first step towards revolutionizing your healthcare services today. Contact Dynamics Square for a consultation, and let’s embark on this journey together. With our support you can grab the full potential of Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare and stay ahead of your competitors.  \r\n</p><p>If you need any help, don\'t hesitate to reach out to us. You can give us a call at <a href=\"tel:+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a> or send us an email at <a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a>.&nbsp;</p><style>\r\n        .table-sakshii {\r\n            width: 100%;\r\n            border-collapse: collapse;\r\n            text-align: center;\r\n            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\r\n        }\r\n        th, td {\r\n            border: 1px solid #ccc;\r\n            padding: 8px;\r\n        }\r\n        th {\r\n            background-color: #e6f2ff;\r\n        }\r\n        .blue-dot {\r\n            color: blue;\r\n            font-size: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n        .diamond {\r\n            color: black;\r\n            font-size: 20px;\r\n        }\r\n    </style><p></p>', 'Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare: Enhance Patient Care', 'Microsoft cloud for healthcare', 'Improve patient care with Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare. Streamline operations, enhance collaboration, and drive better health outcomes.', NULL, 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1801832261743248.Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare.png', 'Arish Siddiqui', 'arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\r\n  \"mainEntity\": [{\r\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n    \"name\": \"What is Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare?\",\r\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\r\n      \"text\": \"Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare is a comprehensive suite of solutions designed to improve patient care, enhance health team collaboration, and optimize clinical and operational insights. It integrates capabilities from Microsoft Azure, Dynamics 365, Microsoft 365, and Power Platform to provide secure and connected patient experiences.\"\r\n    }\r\n  },{\r\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n    \"name\": \"How does Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare enhance patient engagement?\",\r\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\r\n      \"text\": \"Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare enhances patient engagement by providing personalized care, virtual health options, and patient insights. It empowers patients with tools for engagement and provides healthcare providers with insights to tailor interactions. Features include virtual visits, patient outreach, and a unified patient view.\"\r\n    }\r\n  },{\r\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Is Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare compliant with healthcare regulations?\",\r\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\r\n      \"text\": \"Yes, Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare is compliant with various healthcare regulations, including HIPAA, HITRUST, and GDPR. It employs a robust security framework that encompasses industry best practices and standards, ensuring the protection and compliance of health data.\"\r\n    }\r\n  },{\r\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Can Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare integrate with existing Electronic Health Record (EHR) systems?\",\r\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\r\n      \"text\": \"Yes, Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare can integrate with existing EHR systems. For example, it supports integration with systems like Epic on Azure, allowing healthcare organizations to leverage their existing EHR data while benefiting from cloud capabilities.\"\r\n    }\r\n  },{\r\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n    \"name\": \"What are the key components of Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare?\",\r\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\r\n      \"text\": \"The key components of Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare include:\r\n\r\nPatient Engagement: Tools for personalized care and virtual health.\r\nHealth Team Collaboration: Solutions for seamless communication and coordination.\r\nClinical and Operational Insights: Data analytics and insights to improve decision-making.\r\nSecurity and Compliance: Robust frameworks to ensure data protection and regulatory compliance.\"\r\n    }\r\n  },{\r\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n    \"name\": \"How can my organization get started with Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare?\",\r\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\r\n      \"text\": \"To get started with Microsoft Cloud for Healthcare, you can explore the official documentation and training resources provided by Microsoft. These resources offer guidance on deploying and configuring the solutions, as well as practical exercises to help you set up healthcare applications using Dynamics 365, Power Platform, Microsoft 365, and Azure.\"\r\n    }\r\n  }]\r\n}', '[]', '04:50:57pm', '2024-05-29', '14 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2026-01-23 23:50:57'),
(200, 'All You Need to Know About Microsoft Cloud for Retail', 'microsoft-cloud-for-retail-industry', 'Microsoft Cloud', 'microsoft-cloud', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1798395316788030.png', 'Supply chain interruption and the world labor crisis gave a tough reality check to the retail industry during the pandemic era.', '<p>Supply chain interruption and the world labor crisis gave a tough reality check to the retail industry during the pandemic era. However, the rise of data-driven cloud-based solutions has reshaped the retail industry by eliminating market uncertainties. One such solution is Microsoft Cloud for Retail. It drives digital potential, streamlines the supply chain, provides a competitive edge over other retailers, and yields better business outcomes. </p><p>Retail cloud aims to equip retailers with the required capabilities to meet their genuine business challenges. This suite of solutions can enable retailers to know their customers and put a flexible supply chain in place.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blog-content-container\">\r\n    <div class=\"blog-content active\">\r\n    <h4 class=\"blog-content-title\">&nbsp;Table of Content</h4>\r\n    <div class=\"inner\">\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-is-microsoft-cloud-for-retail\">1. What is Microsoft Cloud for Retail?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-are-the-benefits-of-using-microsoft-cloud-for-retail\">2. What are the Benefits of using Microsoft Cloud for Retail?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#How-does-dynamics-square-help-you-with-microsoft-cloud-for-retail\">3. How Does Dynamics Square Help You with Microsoft Cloud for Retail?</a>\r\n\r\n  </div>\r\n   <button class=\"blog-content-toggle\"> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"><!--! Font Awesome Free 6.4.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license (Commercial License) Copyright 2023 Fonticons, Inc. --><path d=\"M201.4 342.6c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0l160-160c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0L224 274.7 86.6 137.4c-12.5-12.5-32.8-12.5-45.3 0s-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160z\"></path></svg></button>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h2 id=\"What-is-microsoft-cloud-for-retail\">What is Microsoft Cloud for Retail? \r\n</h2><p>Microsoft Cloud for Retail Services is a set of unified solutions that comprises capabilities from <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a>, Microsoft 365, Microsoft Azure, and Microsoft Fabric to cater to the industry-specific needs of retailers. It is tailored to drive growth to the retail businesses by bringing customers and related data on the same page.  \r\n</p><p>Also, Microsoft Retail Cloud is powered with AI capabilities to increase productivity across different aspects of the retail industry. This solution can help you manage your supply chain and store operations.</p><p>In addition, Microsoft Cloud for Retail enables you to create and assess your data and offer personalized shopping experiences to customers, resulting in enhanced customer satisfaction and retention.  \r\n</p><p>Microsoft Retail integrates data from various sources through middleware, apps, or <a href=\"https://www.dckap.com/blog/ipaas-solutions-platforms/\" target=\"_blank\">iPaaS platforms</a>, eliminates complexity, and increases data-driven efficiency. This advanced solution delivers an end-to-end experience with detailed insight into customers’ online activity and buying behavior.  \r\n</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"What-are-the-benefits-of-using-microsoft-cloud-for-retail\">What are the Benefits of using Microsoft Cloud for Retail?</h2>\r\n<p>Microsoft for Retail is a purpose-built cloud that helps retailers accelerate their growth by providing a holistic view of their customers’ data. It centralizes separate data sources and lets users leverage the value of data. It includes the following benefits:</p>\r\n<h3>Deliver a Customized Shopping Experience</h3>\r\n<p>It can redefine the overall shopping experience through in-depth data assessments. The new store technology can help increase customer engagement. Cloud for Retail enables retailers to boost conversion using customized recommendations.</p>\r\n\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: left;\">Capability</th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: left;\">Description</th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: left;\">Solutions Included</th>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Intelligent Stores</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Maximize sales by optimizing in-store customer and product signals</td>\r\n    <td><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Application template for smart store analytics (Smart Store Analytics)</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Dynamics 365 Connected Spaces</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Unified Commerce</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Increase engagement and drive conversations across channels</td>\r\n    <td><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Dynamics 365 Commerce</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Azure Cognitive Search</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Real-time personalization</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Enable personalized recommendations and search results to improve customer engagement and product discovery</td>\r\n    <td><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Copilot template for personalized shopping</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Microsoft Intelligent Recommendations</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Azure Cognitive Search</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Dynamics 365 Marketing</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Digital Advertising Solutions</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Enhance your advertising to drive growth and acquire new customers</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Microsoft Advertising</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Seamless Customer Service</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Utilize intelligent and automated customer service tools to improve the customer experience</td>\r\n    <td><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Dynamics 365 Commerce</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Omnichannel for Customer Service</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Power Virtual Agents</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\"><b>Source: Microsoft</b></p>\r\n<h3>Build a Real-time, Sustainable Supply Chain</h3>\r\n<p>Microsoft Cloud for Retail is equipped with AI to deliver real-time visibility across supply chain management. Retailers can build a sustainable retail supply chain by centralizing data and streamlining performance.</p>\r\n\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: left;\">Capability</th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: left;\">Description</th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: left;\">Solutions Included</th>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Demand planning and optimization</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Predict demand using AI to optimize inventory</td>\r\n    <td><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Microsoft 365 Teams for Frontline Workers</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Supply chain visibility</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Use demand and supply signals for future opportunities.<br></td>\r\n    <td><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Insights</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Dynamics 365 Intelligent Order Management</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Microsoft 365 Teams for Frontline Workers</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Flexible fulfillment</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Optimize order management, giving customers a choice across delivery channels</td>\r\n    <td><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Dynamics 365 Commerce</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Dynamics 365 Intelligent Order Management</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Microsoft 365 Teams for Frontline Workers</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\"><b>Source: Microsoft</b></p>\r\n<h3>Empower Your Frontier Staff Members</h3>\r\n<p>With Microsoft Cloud for Retail, you can empower your first-line workers and elevate your customer retention rate. By tapping on the Teams feature, you can build up collaboration and ease the burden on your store associates by automating managerial tasks.</p>\r\n\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: left;\">Capability</th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: left;\">Description</th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: left;\">Solutions Included</th>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Real-time store communication and collaboration</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Use modern tools for connecting your team</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Microsoft 365 Teams for Frontline Workers</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Retail workforce management</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Automate managerial tasks such as store scheduling</td>\r\n    <td><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Application template for store operations (Store Operations Assist)</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Copilot template for store operations</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Microsoft 365 Teams for Frontline Workers</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Process automation and career development</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Expand what your stores and people can do through automation</td>\r\n    <td><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Microsoft Viva Learning</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Microsoft Viva Insights</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Microsoft Viva Connections</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:center;\"><b>Source: Microsoft</b></p>\r\n<h3>Maximize the Value of Your Data</h3>\r\n<p>The retail sector has no shortage of customer data, but some companies have not yet fully utilized the correlation between their data and engagement platforms.  \r\n</p><p>Unifying the customer profile with ecosystems throughout the whole shopping journey has several advantages to offer. By using AI to recognize patterns and analyze income, Dynamics 365 with Azure Synapse can safeguard your business from fraud and provide omnichannel insights through sophisticated analytics.  \r\n</p><p>And lastly, there\'s an added advantage of striking a balance between investment and marketing media by leveraging knowledgeable data solutions like Microsoft PromoteIQ to maximize return on client lifetime value.</p>\r\n\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: left;\">Capability</th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: left;\">Description</th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: left;\">Solutions</th>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Unified customer profile</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Gain insights across the complete view of a shopper\'s journey</td>\r\n    <td><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Dynamics 365 Customer Insights</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Retail channel churn model</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Shopper and operations analytics<br></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Omnichannel insights with advanced analytics</td>\r\n    <td><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Application template for smart store analytics (Smart Store Analytics)</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Dynamics 365 Customer Insights</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Azure Synapse Analytics</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Microsoft Clarity</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Retail media<br></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Unlock ad revenue using your shopper data.<br></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Microsoft PromoteIQ</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: left;\">Retail data solutions</td>\r\n    <td><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Unify retail data from disparate systems, create new shopping experiences, and reimagine retail with next-generation AI<br></div></td>\r\n    <td><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Sitecore OrderCloud Connector (Preview)</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Frequently bought together (Preview)</div><div style=\"text-align: left;\">Retail industry data model (Preview)</div></td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><b>Source: Microsoft</b></p>\r\n<h3>Prevents Data Loss and Fraud</h3><p>Microsoft Cloud for Retail is an AI-powered solution that empowers users to detect data anomalies, ward off cyber frauds, payment fraud, fake accounts, etc. This <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/industries/ecommerce/\">Microsoft Cloud</a> retail solution helps retailers combat losses and minimize revenue impact.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"How-does-dynamics-square-help-you-with-microsoft-cloud-for-retail\">How Does Dynamics Square Help You with Microsoft Cloud for Retail?</h2>\r\n<p>Microsoft Cloud for Retail can enhance the shopping experience and increase sales by streamlining in-store customer and product signals with tools like Dynamics 365. \r\n</p><p>Besides, it enables you to get real-time insights across your store’s space. Real-time trend and pattern analysis allow you to produce customized, actionable insights for every store, increase customer engagement, and maximize staffing by utilizing pre-built AI-powered abilities.</p><p>Microsoft Cloud for Retail is an industry-specific solution for growing retailers. It helps retailers become more streamlined, sustainable, and profitable.</p><p>To learn more about Microsoft Cloud for Retail and how you can easily integrate other solutions of Microsoft Dynamics 365 with it, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">contact us</a> today!</p><p>With rich industry experience, Dynamics Square has managed several successful <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation</a>. In case any assistance is required, feel free to call us directly at <b>+1 281 899 0865</b> or simply write us an email at <b>arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</b>. We are a trusted and renowned <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft&nbsp;Dynamics 365 partner</a>.</p>\r\n\r\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">// <![CDATA[\r\nconst buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n\r\nbuttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n    button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n  );\r\n});\r\n// ]]></script>\r\n<style>\r\n/* The Modal (background) */\r\n#image-viewer {\r\n  display: none;\r\n  position: fixed;\r\n  z-index: 999;\r\n  padding: 70px;\r\n  left: 0;\r\n  top: 0;\r\n  width: 100%;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  overflow: auto;\r\n  background-color: rgb(0,0,0);\r\n  background-color: rgba(45, 62, 80, 0.99);\r\n}\r\n.modal-content {\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n  display: block;\r\n  width: 80%;\r\n  max-width: 100%;\r\n}\r\n.modal-content { \r\n  animation-name: zoom;\r\n  animation-duration: 0.6s;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@keyframes zoom {\r\n  from {transform:scale(0)} \r\n  to {transform:scale(1)}\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close {\r\n  position: absolute;\r\n  top: 15px;\r\n  right: 35px;\r\n  color: #f1f1f1;\r\n  font-size: 40px;\r\n  font-weight: bold;\r\n  transition: 0.3s;\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close:hover,\r\n#image-viewer .close:focus {\r\n  color: #bbb;\r\n  text-decoration: none;\r\n  cursor: pointer;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@media only screen and (max-width: 700px){\r\n  .modal-content {\r\n      width: 100%;\r\n      height:auto;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<script src=\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js\"></script><script>\r\n$(\"img\").on(\'click\',function(){\r\n   $(\"#full-image\").attr(\"src\", $(this).attr(\"src\"));\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').show();\r\n});\r\n\r\n$(\"#image-viewer .close\").click(function(){\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').hide();\r\n});\r\n</script><script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n      button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n    );\r\n  });\r\n  </script>\r\n<script>\r\n $(document).on(\'click\', \'a[href^=\"#\"]\', function (event) {\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    $(\'h2\').css(\'padding-top\',\'75px\');\r\n   $(\'html, body\').animate({\r\n        scrollTop: $($.attr(this, \'href\')).offset().top\r\n    });\r\n});\r\n\r\n</script>', 'All You Need to Know About Microsoft Cloud for Retail', 'microsoft cloud for retail', 'Deliver seamless shopping experiences with Microsoft Cloud for Retail. Connect data, personalize journeys, & optimize stores with AI & cloud solutions.', 'microsoft cloud for retail services,cloud for retail,microsoft retail,retail cloud,dynamics 365 partner', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1798395316789746.png', 'Mukesh Jha', 'mukesh.jha@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/microsoft-cloud-for-retail-industry/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"All You Need to Know About Microsoft Cloud for Retail\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Deliver seamless shopping experiences with Microsoft Cloud for Retail. Connect data, personalize journeys, &amp; optimize stores with AI &amp; cloud solutions.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1798394985919808.Microsoft Cloud for Retail.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Mukesh Jha\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Mukesh%20Jha/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-05-07\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-05-07\"\r\n}', NULL, '06:31:52pm', '2024-05-07', '10 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-02-13 18:31:52');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(201, 'Shopify Integration with Dynamics 365 Business Central: A Simple Guide with Quick Steps', 'shopify-integration-with-business-central', 'Integration', 'integration', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1799119328481306.Shopify Integration with Business Central.png', 'Seamlessly Shopify integration with Dynamics 365 Business Central to enhance inventory management, streamline order processing, and boost sales efficiency.', '<p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> has associated with Shopify to enable businesses to connect their Shopify Stores on it. The Shopify integration with Dynamics 365 Business Central empowers businesses to:</p><ul><li>Setup and manage multiple Shopify stores \r\n</li><li>Sync customer data and inventory levels across platforms for consistency \r\n</li><li>Keep track of fulfillment and order status \r\n</li><li>Keep product information consistent and accurate \r\n</li><li>Manage processes like returns and orders more efficiently \r\n</li><li>Respond to customer inquiries faster by having all data readily available \r\n</li></ul><p>The partnering of Dynamics 365 Business Central with Shopify helps users eliminate manual processing and enhance efficiency for key processes while maintaining data consistency. \r\n</p><p>This blog post sheds light on the methods for Shopify integration with Business Central while highlighting their benefits. \r\n</p><h2>Shopify Connector Integration Options \r\n</h2><p>When it comes to integrating Shopify connector with Business Central, there are two main methods: \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Pre-built Connector</b>: It is comparatively a simpler option suitable for most businesses with standard integration needs. It offers a user-friendly setup process and streamlines data synchronization between platforms. \r\n</li><li><b>Custom Development</b>: This option caters to businesses with unique integration requirements that go beyond the capabilities of the pre-built connector. This process involves custom coding to customize the integration to the specific needs of the business. \r\n</li></ul><blockquote><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Want to ensure smooth Shopify integration with Dynamics 365 Business Central? Schedule a free call now! </b></a></blockquote><h3>Shopify Connect (Option 1): Using the Pre-built Connector \r\n</h3><p>It is the simplest way to connect Shopify with Business Central. However, it is important to note that the specific steps for locating and installing extensions in Business Central are most likely to vary depending on your version. \r\n</p><h4>1. Define Your Integration Goals \r\n</h4><p>When you choose to connect Shopify with Microsoft Dynamics Business Central using a pre-built connector, you need to be specific in terms the of data you want to synchronize. For instance, customer data, product information, orders, inventory, and so on. \r\n</p><h4>2. Install the Pre-built Connector \r\n</h4><ul><li>Visit the Shopify App Store and search for the Dynamics Business Central integration app. \r\n</li><li>Install the app and provide your Business Central and Shopify credentials to authenticate. \r\n</li><li>Choose and configure the data you want to synchronize between the platforms. \r\n</li></ul><h4>3. Test and Monitor the Integration \r\n</h4><ul><li>Run a thorough test to ensure data is syncing accurately between Shopify and Business Central. \r\n</li><li>Monitor the integration performance on an ongoing basis. \r\n</li></ul><h5>Benefits of Using the Pre-built Connector \r\n</h5><ul><li><b>Ease of Installation</b>: The pre-built connector method is simplified to integrate Shopify and Business Central. It typically involves a straightforward installation process through the app store with minimal configuration. It is ideal for businesses that don’t have any extensive technical expertise. \r\n</li><li><b>No Development Fees</b>: The pre-built connector method is cost-effective compared to custom development. Since there are no development fees involved, the ongoing maintenance requirement is almost minimal. \r\n</li><li><b>Less Risk of Errors</b>: As the pre-built connector is a pre-developed and tested solution, it has less risk of errors or unexpected outcomes compared to the custom development method. \r\n</li><li><b>Faster Implementation</b>: Setting up the pre-built connector is generally much faster than developing a custom integration. This allows businesses to reap the benefit of integration sooner. \r\n</li><li><b>Automatic Updates</b>: One of the key benefits of using the pre-built connector is that it receives automatic updates. This ensures the system remains compatible with the latest versions of Shopify and Business Central. \r\n</li></ul><h3>Shopify Connect (Option 2): Using Custom Development \r\n</h3><p>Custom development is ideal for businesses with unique integration needs that go beyond the capabilities of the pre-built connector. It involves creating custom code to connect the APIs of Dynamics Business Central and Shopify. \r\n</p><h4>1. Prepare Shopify Store and Credentials \r\n</h4><ul><li>Generate API credentials in your Shopify admin dashboard. \r\n</li><li>Create a new private app in Shopify to obtain API keys and password. \r\n</li></ul><h4>2. Configure Microsoft Dynamics Business Central \r\n</h4><ul><li>Sign in to your Microsoft Dynamics Business Central account. \r\n</li><li>Depending on your version, you may need assistance from a Dynamics 365 partner to configure the required APIs.) \r\n</li></ul><h4>3. Develop the Integration \r\n</h4><p>A developer will create code to integrate Business Central and Shopify for data exchange. \r\n</p><p>This process is likely to involve the following tasks: \r\n</p><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>Authentication</b>: It involves setting up API keys or OAuth tokens for secure access to Business Central and APIs. \r\n</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>Data Mapping</b>: In this process, the developer, based on their analysis, will define how data elements (customer information, products, etc.) will be mapped between the two systems. \r\n</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>Data Exchange</b>: It is a crucial step that involves the task of retrieving data from one system and pushing it to the other. \r\n</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>Error Handling</b>: The developer implements several mechanisms to handle potential errors during data synchronization. \r\n</li></ul><h4>4. Testing and Documentation \r\n</h4><ul><li>After the integration, it is time to thoroughly test it with various scenarios and probabilities (product updates, inventory changes, new orders, and more) to ensure integrity. \r\n</li><li>There must be documentation of the entire <a href=\"/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 implementation</a> process. It is important to document code, error handling procedures, and data mapping, for future reference and maintenance purposes. \r\n</li></ul><h4>5. Security and Monitoring \r\n</h4><ul><li>After the Shopify connector for Business Central is established, monitoring for any errors is paramount. \r\n</li><li>Ensure your custom code adheres to security best practices to protect sensitive data. \r\n</li><li>Check and monitor the integration for errors and implement alerting mechanisms. \r\n</li><li>Establish a maintenance routine to ensure your systems get the latest Business Central and Shopify updates. It is crucial for your organization’s growth. \r\n</li></ul><h5>Benefits of Custom Development \r\n</h5><ul><li><b>Tailored Integration</b>: Custom code can address specific business requirements that the pre-built connector cannot meet. \r\n</li><li><b>Greater Control</b>: Businesses have more control over the integration in terms of system behavior and functionality. \r\n</li></ul><p>When you integrate Shopify Connector for Business Central, it brings significant improvement in your e-commerce operations. \r\n</p><p>Whether you wish to carry forward this integration with the pre-built connector or custom development, our extensive and seamless support services for Shopify Connector can bring a great transformation in your e-commerce business, unlocking endless possibilities for it.</p><p><i>For businesses using Shopify Plus, custom development allows greater flexibility in workflows, checkout customization, and API scalability enabling a <a href=\"https://elogic.co/services/shopify-plus-development-services/\" target=\"_blank\">Shopify Plus development</a> approach.</i></p>        \r\n<h2>Partner with Dynamics Square for seamless Shopify Integration with Business Central</h2><p>We are Dynamics Square, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">a Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a>, that can help you transform your business. With over a decade of experience in deploying Microsoft solutions, we can help you seamlessly connect your Shopify Store and Business Central. \r\n</p><p>To learn more about it, feel free to contact our expert consultant. You can write us an email at <a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a> or simply connect at <a href=\"tel:+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a>.</p>\r\n<div class=\"blog-faq-style\">\r\n                    <h2>FAQ\'s about Shopify Integration with Business Central</h2>\r\n                    <h3>1. What is the Shopify integration with Dynamics 365 Business Central?</h3>\r\n                    <p>The Shopify integration with Dynamics 365 Business Central allows businesses to connect their Shopify stores with Business Central. This integration helps manage multiple Shopify stores, sync customer data and inventory levels, track fulfillment and order status, maintain consistent product information, and respond to customer inquiries faster.</p>\r\n                    <h3>2. What are the benefits of Shopify integration with Business Central?</h3>\r\n                    <p>The benefits include:</p>\r\n                    <ul>\r\n                        <li>Streamlined operations by automating data synchronization.</li> \r\n<li>Improved inventory management and order tracking.</li> \r\n<li>Consistent and accurate product information across platforms.</li> \r\n<li>Enhanced customer service with quick access to data.</li>\r\n<li>Reduced manual processing and increased efficiency.</li>\r\n                    </ul>\r\n                    <h3>3. What are the methods available for Shopify integration with Business Central?</h3>\r\n                    <p>There are two main methods:</p>\r\n                    <ul>\r\n<li>Pre-built Connector: A simpler option suitable for most businesses with standard integration needs. It offers a user-friendly setup process and streamlines data synchronization.</li>\r\n<li>Custom Development: Ideal for businesses with unique integration requirements. This involves custom coding to meet specific business needs.</li>\r\n                    </ul>\r\n                    <h3>4. How do I install the pre-built connector for Shopify and Business Central?</h3>\r\n                    <p>To install the pre-built connector:</p>\r\n                    <ul>\r\n                        <li>Visit the Shopify App Store and search for the Dynamics Business Central integration app.</li> <li>Install the app and provide your Business Central and Shopify credentials to authenticate.</li> <li>Choose and configure the data you want to synchronize between the platforms.</li> <li>Test and monitor the integration to ensure data is syncing accurately.</li>\r\n                    </ul>\r\n                    <h3>5. What are the steps involved in custom development for Shopify integration with Business Central?</h3>\r\n                    <p>The steps include:</p>\r\n                    <ul>\r\n<li>Prepare your Shopify store and generate API credentials.</li>\r\n<li>Configure Microsoft Dynamics Business Central, possibly with assistance from a Dynamics 365 partner.</li>\r\n<li>Develop the integration by creating custom code to connect the APIs of Business Central and Shopify.</li>\r\n<li>Test the integration thoroughly and document the process.</li>\r\n<li>Monitor the integration for errors and ensure security best practices are followed.</li>\r\n                    </ul>\r\n                    <h3>6. What are the advantages of using the pre-built connector over custom development?</h3>\r\n                    <p>The advantages of using the pre-built connector include:</p>\r\n                    <ul>\r\n<li>Ease of installation with a straightforward setup process.</li>\r\n<li>No development fees, making it cost-effective.</li>\r\n<li>Less risk of errors as it is a pre-developed and tested solution.</li>\r\n<li>Faster implementation, allowing businesses to benefit from the integration sooner.</li>\r\n<li>Automatic updates to ensure compatibility with the latest versions of Shopify and Business Central</li>\r\n                    </ul>\r\n                    <h3>7. Can I manage multiple Shopify stores with Business Central integration?</h3>\r\n                    <p>Yes, the integration allows you to set up and manage multiple Shopify stores within Dynamics 365 Business Central, ensuring consistent data synchronization and efficient management of all your stores.</p>\r\n                </div>', 'Shopify Integration with Dynamics 365 Business Central', 'Shopify Integration with Dynamics 365 Business Central', 'Shopify integration with Dynamics 365 Business Central to streamline order processing, enhance inventory management, and boost sales efficiency.', 'Integrating Shopify with Business Central,connect business central to shopify,shopify connector,shopify integration with dynamics 365 business central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1799119328481310.Shopify Integration with Business Central.png', 'Arish Siddiqui', 'arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\r\n  \"mainEntity\": [{\r\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n    \"name\": \"What is the Shopify integration with Dynamics 365 Business Central?\",\r\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\r\n      \"text\": \"The Shopify integration with Dynamics 365 Business Central allows businesses to connect their Shopify stores with Business Central. This integration helps manage multiple Shopify stores, sync customer data and inventory levels, track fulfillment and order status, maintain consistent product information, and respond to customer inquiries faster.\"\r\n    }\r\n  },{\r\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n    \"name\": \"What are the benefits of integrating Shopify with Business Central?\",\r\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\r\n      \"text\": \"The benefits include:\r\n\r\nStreamlined operations by automating data synchronization.\r\nImproved inventory management and order tracking.\r\nConsistent and accurate product information across platforms.\r\nEnhanced customer service with quick access to data.\r\nReduced manual processing and increased efficiency.\"\r\n    }\r\n  },{\r\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n    \"name\": \"What are the methods available for integrating Shopify with Business Central?\",\r\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\r\n      \"text\": \"There are two main methods:\r\n\r\nPre-built Connector: A simpler option suitable for most businesses with standard integration needs. It offers a user-friendly setup process and streamlines data synchronization.\r\nCustom Development: Ideal for businesses with unique integration requirements. This involves custom coding to meet specific business needs.\"\r\n    }\r\n  },{\r\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n    \"name\": \"How do I install the pre-built connector for Shopify and Business Central?\",\r\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\r\n      \"text\": \"To install the pre-built connector:\r\n\r\nVisit the Shopify App Store and search for the Dynamics Business Central integration app.\r\nInstall the app and provide your Business Central and Shopify credentials to authenticate.\r\nChoose and configure the data you want to synchronize between the platforms.\r\nTest and monitor the integration to ensure data is syncing accurately.\"\r\n    }\r\n  },{\r\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n    \"name\": \"What are the steps involved in custom development for Shopify integration with Business Central?\",\r\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\r\n      \"text\": \"The steps include:\r\n\r\nPrepare your Shopify store and generate API credentials.\r\nConfigure Microsoft Dynamics Business Central, possibly with assistance from a Dynamics 365 partner.\r\nDevelop the integration by creating custom code to connect the APIs of Business Central and Shopify.\r\nTest the integration thoroughly and document the process.\r\nMonitor the integration for errors and ensure security best practices are followed.\"\r\n    }\r\n  },{\r\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n    \"name\": \"What are the advantages of using the pre-built connector over custom development?\",\r\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\r\n      \"text\": \"The advantages of using the pre-built connector include:\r\n\r\nEase of installation with a straightforward setup process.\r\nNo development fees, making it cost-effective.\r\nLess risk of errors as it is a pre-developed and tested solution.\r\nFaster implementation, allowing businesses to benefit from the integration sooner.\r\nAutomatic updates to ensure compatibility with the latest versions of Shopify and Business Central\"\r\n    }\r\n  },{\r\n    \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Can I manage multiple Shopify stores with Business Central integration?\",\r\n    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"Answer\",\r\n      \"text\": \"Yes, the integration allows you to set up and manage multiple Shopify stores within Dynamics 365 Business Central, ensuring consistent data synchronization and efficient management of all your stores.\"\r\n    }\r\n  }]\r\n}', '[]', '02:16:33pm', '2024-05-29', '9 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-06-19 14:16:33'),
(202, 'A Detailed Guide to Microsoft Power Automate Pricing Plans', 'power-automate-pricing-plans', 'Microsoft Power Automate', 'microsoft-power-automate', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1799208185664841.Microsoft-Power-Automate.avif', 'Want to crack Power Automate pricing? If your answer is a nod, then you are in the right place. Here, in this post, you will get insights into MS Power Automate pricing and more. Keep reading to learn about them.', '<p>Want to crack Power Automate pricing? If your answer is a nod, then you are in the right place.  \r\n</p><p>Here, in this post, you will get insights into MS Power Automate pricing and more. Keep reading to learn about them. \r\n</p><p>Let’s begin with an introduction to Power Automate.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blog-content-container\">\r\n    <div class=\"blog-content active\">\r\n    <h4 class=\"blog-content-title\">&nbsp;Table of Content</h4>\r\n    <div class=\"inner\">\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-is-microsoft-power-automate\">1. What is Microsoft Power Automate?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Microsoft-power-automate-pricing-plans\">2. Microsoft Power Automate Pricing Plans</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Power-automate-add-ons\">3. Power Automate Add-ons</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Are-power-automate-pricing-plans-worth-considering\">4. Are Power Automate Pricing Plans Worth Considering?</a>\r\n\r\n  </div>\r\n   <button class=\"blog-content-toggle\"> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"><!--! Font Awesome Free 6.4.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license (Commercial License) Copyright 2023 Fonticons, Inc. --><path d=\"M201.4 342.6c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0l160-160c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0L224 274.7 86.6 137.4c-12.5-12.5-32.8-12.5-45.3 0s-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160z\"></path></svg></button>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h2 id=\"What-is-microsoft-power-automate\">What is Microsoft Power Automate?</h2>\r\n<p>We are living in a world where things have gone digital. Businesses are making all possible efforts to stay on top of their game. For that, they are adopting advanced digital solutions like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-automate/\">Microsoft Power Automate</a>. \r\n</p><p>Microsoft Power Automate is a cloud-based workflow automation platform that empowers organizations to streamline repetitive tasks and complex processes. It allows businesses to connect their favorite apps and services, automate data transfer, and improve overall efficiency.</p><p>Microsoft 365 Power Automate shines with its ability to connect to virtually any app thanks to hundreds of built-in connectors and support for third-party APIs. This lets you automate tasks across your entire business ecosystem,  including <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\" style=\"\">D365 Business Central</a> and other  Microsoft 365 apps. By creating intelligent workflows, you can streamline processes and dramatically boost productivity.</p><p>Power Automate goes beyond basic automation. It offers features like process mining to help you identify opportunities for improvement, Copilot for creating workflows with natural language, and robotic process automation (RPA) for automating repetitive tasks on your desktop. These features are available in various pricing plans to fit your specific needs.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Microsoft-power-automate-pricing-plans\">Microsoft Power Automate Pricing Plans</h2>\r\n<p>For businesses, it is crucial to learn about pricing details before signing up for any software solution. Microsoft Power Automate pricing plans are broadly categorized into two categories:  \r\n</p><ol><li>Power Automate Premium  \r\n</li><li>Power Automate Process \r\n</li></ol><p>Besides, you can even sign up for a trial to explore its capabilities and features. \r\n</p><p>The prices mentioned below are indicative and thus should not be considered exact as they are dependent on various factors such as organization, region, currency, country, and so on. Plus, there are Microsoft 365 Power Automate add-on licensing options available as well that can impact the final pricing. \r\n</p><p>Now, let’s explore Power Automate pricing plans, one by one: \r\n</p><h3>1. Power Automate Premium  \r\n</h3><p>Power Automate premium pricing is available at USD 15 per user/month. It lets users handle both new and legacy apps by letting them create and run unlimited cloud flows with digital process automating (DPA), plus work on legacy apps with desktop flows through robotic process automation (RPA) in attended mode.  \r\n</p><p>Microsoft Power Automate desktop pricing includes full Process Mining on desktops and a limited amount of Process Mining data space (50 MB that can be shared up to 100GB per tenant).</p><p>Also, Power Automate Premium gives access to AI tools to help with tasks like form processing, object detection, making predictions, classification, and recognition of text and lets a user run an attended RPA bot on a computer. \r\n</p><p>Remember, to run an RPA bot in an unattended mode, you need to add an extra Power Automate Hosted Process license. \r\n</p><h3>2. Power Automate Process  \r\n</h3><p>Power Automate premium pricing is available at USD 150 per bot/month. It lets you use an autonomous or self-running bot for tasks that don\'t need a person, or for a critical task that everyone in the company can use without each person needing their own license. \r\n</p><p>This license also allows you to use AI Builder for things like form processing, object detection, making predictions, sorting texts, and spotting details. \r\n</p><p><b>When setting up autonomous or self-running bots, keep the following points in mind: \r\n</b></p><ul><li>If you want the same task to run at the same time in different places, you need an additional unattended bot for each one. \r\n</li><li>These bots can work on your own computer, a remote desktop, or in a virtual environment or cloud setup. However, this license doesn\'t cover the cost of those setups. The Microsoft 365 Power Automate Hosted Process license does include a virtual machine by Microsoft for this. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>When setting up business processes, keep the following points in mind: \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Each top-level main task flow needs its own license. But, if one task triggers another, you don\'t need extra licenses for those follow-up tasks. \r\n</li><li>You can set tasks to start every minute, no matter the license type. There\'s no limit to how often tasks can run, as long as the connector tool you\'re using allows it. \r\n</li></ul>\r\n<h2 id=\"Power-automate-add-ons\">Power Automate Add-ons</h2>\r\n<p>There are three main Power Automate Add-ons: \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Hosted RPA:</b> It is priced at USD 215 per bot/month and is available as an add-on for Power Automate Premium. \r\n</li><li><b>AI Builder:</b> This add-on of AI Builder Power Automate is available at the pricing of USD 500 per unit/month. It is available for existing Power Automate, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-apps/\">Power Apps</a>, or paid subscription plans for Dynamics 365. \r\n</li><li><b>Process Mining:</b> It is priced at USD 5000 per tenant/month and is available for Power Automate Premium. \r\n</li></ul><p>For what all these add-ons cover, take a glance at the following table:</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1799206315214563.Microsoft-Power-Automate-Pricing-Subscription-Plans.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align: center; \"><b>Source: Microsoft</b></p><h3>Impact of Connectors Integration on Power Automate Pricing Plans \r\n</h3><p>Speaking of Microsoft Power Automate premium connectors pricing, users can use them under both plans. However, the only difference would be the database capacity and file capacity of Microsoft Dataverse for these plans.</p><p>In the case of Power Automate Premium, you will have 250 MB database capacity and 2 GB file capacity, whereas the Power Automate Process plan will offer 50 MB database capacity and 200 MB file capacity. \r\n</p><p>Pre-built connectors that come with Microsoft 365 Power Automate are hugely powerful. Users can integrate these connectors with multiple Microsoft and third-party software programs. Hence, you can use connectors to perform specific operations in one application and still follow a certain trigger in other applications.</p><p><b>Also Read:</b> <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/power-apps-with-business-central/\">Power Apps with Business Central</a></p><p> \r\n</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Are-power-automate-pricing-plans-worth-considering\">Are Power Automate Pricing Plans Worth Considering?</h2>\r\n<p>Every business requires automation today to thrive and remain competitive. Whenever an organization decides to invest in such automation tools, it thinks about ROI. But it can only be discovered if organizations look closely into it. Talking to certified <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/microsoft-dynamics-365-partner/\">Microsoft Power Automate consultants</a> can clear all your doubts and help you make a major decision for the benefit of your business in the long run.  \r\n</p><p>By utilizing Power Automate, several organizations are getting great ROI. After going through the pricing plans and features mentioned above, you can choose the ideal plans that can cater to your specific organizational automation needs. \r\n</p><p>If you want to leverage Microsoft Power Automate to make your daily operations more efficient, just let us know. We, Dynamics Square, are a <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\">Microsoft Solutions Partner</a> that helps organizations automate manual processes to save time and let them focus on what is more important for their business.</p>\r\n\r\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">// <![CDATA[\r\nconst buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n\r\nbuttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n    button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n  );\r\n});\r\n// ]]></script>\r\n<style>\r\n/* The Modal (background) */\r\n#image-viewer {\r\n  display: none;\r\n  position: fixed;\r\n  z-index: 999;\r\n  padding: 70px;\r\n  left: 0;\r\n  top: 0;\r\n  width: 100%;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  overflow: auto;\r\n  background-color: rgb(0,0,0);\r\n  background-color: rgba(45, 62, 80, 0.99);\r\n}\r\n.modal-content {\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n  display: block;\r\n  width: 80%;\r\n  max-width: 100%;\r\n}\r\n.modal-content { \r\n  animation-name: zoom;\r\n  animation-duration: 0.6s;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@keyframes zoom {\r\n  from {transform:scale(0)} \r\n  to {transform:scale(1)}\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close {\r\n  position: absolute;\r\n  top: 15px;\r\n  right: 35px;\r\n  color: #f1f1f1;\r\n  font-size: 40px;\r\n  font-weight: bold;\r\n  transition: 0.3s;\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close:hover,\r\n#image-viewer .close:focus {\r\n  color: #bbb;\r\n  text-decoration: none;\r\n  cursor: pointer;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@media only screen and (max-width: 700px){\r\n  .modal-content {\r\n      width: 100%;\r\n      height:auto;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<script src=\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js\"></script><script>\r\n$(\"img\").on(\'click\',function(){\r\n   $(\"#full-image\").attr(\"src\", $(this).attr(\"src\"));\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').show();\r\n});\r\n\r\n$(\"#image-viewer .close\").click(function(){\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').hide();\r\n});\r\n</script><script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n      button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n    );\r\n  });\r\n  </script>\r\n<script>\r\n $(document).on(\'click\', \'a[href^=\"#\"]\', function (event) {\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    $(\'h2\').css(\'padding-top\',\'75px\');\r\n   $(\'html, body\').animate({\r\n        scrollTop: $($.attr(this, \'href\')).offset().top\r\n    });\r\n});\r\n\r\n</script>', 'A Detailed Guide to Microsoft Power Automate Pricing Plans', 'power automate pricing', 'Confused by Microsoft Power Automate pricing? Our guide breaks down all the plans to help you find the perfect fit for your budget and automation needs.', 'power automate pricing,microsoft power automate pricing,power automate premium pricing,microsoft power automate,microsoft power platform', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1799208185664845.Microsoft-Power-Automate.avif', 'Samar Malik', 'samar.malik@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/power-automate-pricing-plans/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"A Detailed Guide to Microsoft Power Automate Pricing Plans\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Confused by Microsoft Power Automate pricing? Our guide breaks down all the plans to help you find the perfect fit for your budget and automation needs.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1799208280833391.Microsoft-Power-Automate.jpg\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Samar Malik\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Samar-Malik/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-05-16\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-05-16\"\r\n}', NULL, '05:32:25pm', '16-05-2024', '8 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-05-16 17:32:25'),
(203, 'Transforming Sales Process with Copilot in Dynamics 365 Sales', 'copilot-in-dynamics-365-sales', 'Dynamics 365 Sales', 'dynamics-365-sales', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1799583829941665.Copilot in Dynamics 365 Sales.png', 'Microsoft Copilot in Dynamics 365 Sales (formerly known as Bing Chat) is an AI assistant designed to help sales teams bolster productivity and efficiency.', '<p></p><p>Microsoft Copilot in Dynamics 365 Sales (formerly known as Bing Chat) is an AI assistant designed to help sales teams bolster productivity and efficiency.  \r\n</p><p>In other words, the Copilot chatbot is responsibly built into Dynamics 365 by Microsoft, empowering employees to deliver better customer experiences and drive efficiency across the organization. It offers a wide range of capabilities, including: \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Record Summarization:</b> Quickly summarizes opportunity and lead records. \r\n</li><li><b>Recent Changes:</b> Keeps track of recent changes made to records. \r\n</li><li><b>Information Assistance:</b> Fetches product-related documents and answers from SharePoint. \r\n</li><li><b>Meeting Preparation:</b> Helps prepare for meetings by summarizing relevant information. \r\n</li><li><b>Email Assistance:</b> Generates personalized emails based on recent emails and related information. \r\n</li><li><b>News Updates:</b> Provides the latest news about accounts. \r\n</li></ul><p>You can interact with Copilot through a chat interface in natural language or use predefined prompts. It’s also integrated with Outlook, Teams, and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM</a> solutions allowing you to work with customer data within these applications.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blog-content-container\">\r\n    <div class=\"blog-content active\">\r\n    <h4 class=\"blog-content-title\">&nbsp;Table of Content</h4>\r\n    <div class=\"inner\">\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Dynamics-365-sales-copilot-capabilities\">1. Dynamics 365 Sales Copilot Capabilities</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Microsoft-sales-copilot-pricing-and-availability\">2. Microsoft Sales Copilot Pricing and Availability</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#How-to-install-copilot-in-dynamics-365-sales\">3. How to Install Copilot in Dynamics 365 Sales?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Leverage-the-power-of-copilot-with-dynamics-square\">4. Leverage the Power of Copilot with Dynamics Square</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n   <button class=\"blog-content-toggle\"> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"><!--! Font Awesome Free 6.4.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license (Commercial License) Copyright 2023 Fonticons, Inc. --><path d=\"M201.4 342.6c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0l160-160c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0L224 274.7 86.6 137.4c-12.5-12.5-32.8-12.5-45.3 0s-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160z\"></path></svg></button>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h2 id=\"Dynamics-365-sales-copilot-capabilities\">Dynamics 365 Sales Copilot Capabilities</h2>\r\n<p>By bringing AI and sales insights from their CRM platform into Microsoft 365 productivity tools like Outlook, Teams, and Word, sales professionals can work more efficiently and improve customer experiences. \r\n</p><p>Microsoft Copilot for Dynamics 365 Sales offers the following capabilities: \r\n</p><ul><li>Generates Content or Product Description \r\n</li><li>Sparks Creativity \r\n</li><li>Recaps Meetings \r\n</li><li>Helps Accomplish Tasks \r\n</li></ul><p>Copilot for Sales goes beyond email assistance, customized sales content creation, and next-step recommendations. Apart from furnishing AI-generated insights, it can join Teams meetings for you and prepare an overview of it. Copilot for Sales for Outlook can access contacts, calendar events, and draft your emails as well.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Microsoft-sales-copilot-pricing-and-availability\">Microsoft Sales Copilot Pricing and Availability</h2>\r\n<p>Microsoft Dynamics Copilot cost for Sales is USD 50 per user/month with annual commitment. Besides <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-sales/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales</a>, it works smoothly with Salesforce Sales Cloud as well, and owing to its flexibility, it can be easily configured to work with other sales solutions. \r\n</p><p>Let\'s go into the specifics to learn more about its pricing. So, when it comes to purchasing Microsoft Sales Copilot, it is important to understand the eligibility criteria first. \r\n</p><p>For enterprise customers, it is a must to obtain a license either for Microsoft 365 E3 or E5 or Office 365 E3 or E5. Speaking of business customers, it is mandatory to secure a license for Microsoft 365 Business Standard or Business Premium or any one version of these suites, excluding Microsoft Teams.  \r\n</p><h3>What Can Microsoft Sales Copilot Do? \r\n</h3><p>Microsoft Sales Copilot is an AI assistant designed to transform the way sellers work within <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a>. Here’s what it can do: \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Maximize Sales Productivity:</b> Integrating with Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales and Salesforce Sales Cloud, it helps sellers manage their workflows more efficiently. \r\n</li><li><b>Personalize Customer Interactions:</b> It provides personalized recommendations and insights, helping to tailor interactions with customers. \r\n</li><li><b>Stay in the Flow of Work:</b> The AI assistant works within the productivity tools sellers use daily, like Outlook, Teams, and Word, ensuring they can stay focused on their tasks. \r\n</li><li><b>Simplify Tasks:</b>&nbsp;Acting as an <a href=\"https://www.centripe.ai/what-is-a-chatbot\" target=\"_blank\">AI-powered chatbot</a>, Copilot prepares sales meeting briefs, summarizes key points from email threads, and streamlines various sales-related activities. \r\n</li><li><b>Streamline Workflow with AI Support:</b> It analyzes sales calls, extracts insights, and does meeting recordings, making follow-ups and planning more effective. \r\n</li></ul><p>Additionally, Microsoft Sales Copilot can be customized according to business needs and integrates seamlessly with various sales solutions.  \r\n</p><p>It’s available in multiple languages and may require additional licenses depending on your existing subscriptions as explained above. \r\n</p><h3>The Impact of Microsoft Copilot for Dynamics 365 Sales \r\n</h3><p>The impact of Microsoft Copilot for D365 Sales has been significant in transforming the way sales are conducted. It’s an AI assistant that integrates with Microsoft 365 and Dynamics 365 CRM solutions to streamline sales productivity, personalize customer interactions, and simplify tasks through AI support. Here are some key points about its impact: \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Time-Saving:</b> Microsoft Copilot for Sales is designed to make processes more efficient and save time for sales professionals. It does so by summarizing key points from multiple email threads and assisting in crafting responses to clients. \r\n</li><li><b>Work-Life Balance:</b> By reducing the manual workload, it contributes to a better work-life balance for sales professionals. \r\n</li><li><b>Revenue Increase:</b> Microsoft Copilot for Sales can bolster revenue while ensuring a simplified workflow.  \r\n</li><li><b>Productivity Boost:</b>&nbsp;By adding AI-powered insights to seller actions and decisions, it increases efficiency and boosts customer engagement.</li><li><b>Integration:</b> Sales Copilot works seamlessly with Outlook and Teams, reducing redundant work and allowing teams to work more effectively. \r\n</li></ul><p>Overall, Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales Copilot seems to be a game-changer for sales teams, offering a variety of features that enhance performance and results.</p><p><b>Also Read: </b><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/microsoft-introduces-dynamics-365-copilot/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Copilot</a></p>\r\n<h2 id=\"How-to-install-copilot-in-dynamics-365-sales\">How to Install Copilot in Dynamics 365 Sales?</h2>\r\n<p>To install Copilot in Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales, you can follow these steps: \r\n</p><p><b>1. Verify Prerequisites</b></p><ul><li>Ensure you have a Dynamics 365 Sales Premium or Dynamics 365 Sales Enterprise license. \r\n</li><li>Confirm that you are a System Administrator</li></ul><p><b>\r\n\r\n</b></p><table>\r\n<thead>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center; \">Requirement Type</th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center;\">You must have</th>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">License</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Dynamics 365 Sales Premium or Dynamics 365 Sales Enterprise</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Security Roles</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">System Administrator</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p></p><p><b>2. Turn on Copilot Features</b></p><p></p><ul><li>In the Sales Hub app, go to the Change area in the lower-left corner of the page and select App Settings. \r\n</li><li>Under General Settings, select Copilot. \r\n</li><li>On the Set-up Copilot in Dynamics 365 Sales page, you can turn on Copilot features or try the newest preview features. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>3. Provide Consent for Data Movement (if required)</b></p><p>If your region does not have an Azure Open AI Service endpoint, you must provide consent for data movement across regions in the <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-platform/\">Power Platform</a> admin center. \r\n</p><p><b>4. Configure Copilot</b></p><p>You can configure fields for generating summaries and recent changes lists as per your business needs. Please note that effective April 1, 2024, Copilot in Dynamics 365 Sales is turned on by default for certain regions and organizations.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Leverage-the-power-of-copilot-with-dynamics-square\">Leverage the Power of Copilot with Dynamics Square</h2>\r\n<p>Being a powerful AI bot, Copilot is transforming the landscape of businesses. For a detailed guide and additional steps, you can reach out to us. We are Dynamics Square, a trusted and renowned <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation </a>partner.  \r\n</p><p>Schedule a free call with our expert consultant today. Call us at <b>+1 281 899 0865</b> or simply write us an email at <b>arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</b>.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">// <![CDATA[\r\nconst buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n\r\nbuttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n    button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n  );\r\n});\r\n// ]]></script>\r\n<style>\r\n/* The Modal (background) */\r\n#image-viewer {\r\n  display: none;\r\n  position: fixed;\r\n  z-index: 999;\r\n  padding: 70px;\r\n  left: 0;\r\n  top: 0;\r\n  width: 100%;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  overflow: auto;\r\n  background-color: rgb(0,0,0);\r\n  background-color: rgba(45, 62, 80, 0.99);\r\n}\r\n.modal-content {\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n  display: block;\r\n  width: 80%;\r\n  max-width: 100%;\r\n}\r\n.modal-content { \r\n  animation-name: zoom;\r\n  animation-duration: 0.6s;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@keyframes zoom {\r\n  from {transform:scale(0)} \r\n  to {transform:scale(1)}\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close {\r\n  position: absolute;\r\n  top: 15px;\r\n  right: 35px;\r\n  color: #f1f1f1;\r\n  font-size: 40px;\r\n  font-weight: bold;\r\n  transition: 0.3s;\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close:hover,\r\n#image-viewer .close:focus {\r\n  color: #bbb;\r\n  text-decoration: none;\r\n  cursor: pointer;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@media only screen and (max-width: 700px){\r\n  .modal-content {\r\n      width: 100%;\r\n      height:auto;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<script src=\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js\"></script><script>\r\n$(\"img\").on(\'click\',function(){\r\n   $(\"#full-image\").attr(\"src\", $(this).attr(\"src\"));\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').show();\r\n});\r\n\r\n$(\"#image-viewer .close\").click(function(){\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').hide();\r\n});\r\n</script><script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n      button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n    );\r\n  });\r\n  </script>\r\n<script>\r\n $(document).on(\'click\', \'a[href^=\"#\"]\', function (event) {\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    $(\'h2\').css(\'padding-top\',\'75px\');\r\n   $(\'html, body\').animate({\r\n        scrollTop: $($.attr(this, \'href\')).offset().top\r\n    });\r\n});\r\n\r\n</script>', 'Copilot in Dynamics 365 Sales | Transforming Sales Process', 'copilot in dynamics 365 sales', 'Transform your sales process with Copilot in Dynamics 365 Sales. For greater outcomes, increase productivity, simplify processes, and give your sales team more authority.', 'dynamics 365 sales copilot,dynamics copilot,microsoft sales copilot,copilot for sales,microsoft dynamics 365 copilot,microsoft copilot for sales,dynamics 365 sales', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1799583829941669.Copilot in Dynamics 365 Sales.png', 'Vivek Gururani', 'vivek.gururani@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/copilot-in-dynamics-365-sales/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Copilot in Dynamics 365 Sales | Transforming Sales Process\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Transform your sales process with Copilot in Dynamics 365 Sales. For greater outcomes, increase productivity, simplify processes, and give your sales team more authority.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1799583840050446.Copilot in Dynamics 365 Sales.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Vivek Gururani\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Vivek-Gururani/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-05-20\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-05-20\"\r\n}', '[]', '02:13:02pm', '2024-05-21', '8 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-11-07 21:13:02');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(204, 'Migrating from Xero to Dynamics 365 Business Central', 'xero-to-dynamics-365-business-central-migration', 'Business central', 'business-central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1799857833892940.Xero to Dynamics 365 Business Central Migration.png', 'Are you using Xero? It is a great tool for small business but has limited capabilities, which can bottleneck your business as it grows.', '<p>Are you using Xero? It is a great tool for small business but has limited capabilities, which can bottleneck your business as it grows. Merely, it allows 2,000 invoices and bills per month and lacks functionalities, such as project management, complex reporting, inventory management, and more. \r\n</p><p>If your business demands additional features apart from finance and is using separate tools for business operation, it’s time to migrate from Xero to Dynamics 365 Business Central. But why Business Central?  Well, it is an all-in-one solution and named the <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.forbes.com/advisor/business/software/best-erp-systems/\" target=\"_blank\">best ERP system of 2024 by Forbes Advisor</a>. \r\n</p><p>Migrating from Xero to Business Central offers various benefits with its wide range of functionality, which includes both ERP and CRM like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a>. This robust software solution also supports your organization to scale and integrate with another system when required, with easy user adoption, accurate reporting, and analytics. \r\n</p><p>In this blog, we will plunge into the detailed intricacies of migration from Xero to Business Central.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blog-content-container\">\r\n    <div class=\"blog-content active\">\r\n    <h4 class=\"blog-content-title\">&nbsp;Table of Content</h4>\r\n    <div class=\"inner\">\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-is-business-central\">1. What is Business Central?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-is-xero-accounting\">2. What is Xero Accounting?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Comparison-between-xero-and-business-central\">3. Comparison Between Xero and Business Central</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Limitations-of-xero-accounting-software\">4. Limitations of Xero Accounting Software</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Key-reasons-to-upgrade-from-xero-to-business-central\">5. Key Reasons to Upgrade from Xero to Business Central</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Steps-to-migrate-from-xero-to-business-central\">6. Steps to Migrate from Xero to Business Central</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n   <button class=\"blog-content-toggle\"> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"><!--! Font Awesome Free 6.4.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license (Commercial License) Copyright 2023 Fonticons, Inc. --><path d=\"M201.4 342.6c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0l160-160c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0L224 274.7 86.6 137.4c-12.5-12.5-32.8-12.5-45.3 0s-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160z\"></path></svg></button>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h2 id=\"What-is-business-central\">What is Business Central?</h2>\r\n<p>Business Central, also known as D365 BC, is an all-in-one solution that helps businesses with every requirement, including finance, sales, inventory, production management, and warehouse management. Since this is a cloud-based application, you can use it in real time and can leverage its AI capabilities to get data-driven actionable insight. \r\n</p><p>Microsoft Dynamics Business Central can be your partner in growth, and you can streamline your various operations using this tool only.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"What-is-xero-accounting\">What is Xero Accounting?</h2>\r\n<p>Xero accounting is a cloud-based accounting software, which is the ideal solution for businesses, especially SMBs. It fosters connections between businesses and their trusted advisors, such as banks, payment services, accounts, and third-party apps.</p><p>This provides instant access to your company\'s financial access, keeping your business finances effortless.  By leveraging this direct visibility, you can create invoices and integrate them with third-party apps.</p><p>However, it is paramount to remember Xero accounting is not an ERP solution. It might not help you with complete resource planning, but you can go for third-party integration to fulfill your requirements.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Comparison-between-xero-and-business-central\">Comparison Between Xero and Business Central</h2>\r\n\r\n<table><thead>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center; \"> </th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center;\">Xero </th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center;\">Business Central</th>\r\n  </tr></thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center; \">Functionality</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Primary focus on financial management</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Financial management, supply chain, inventory, warehouse, and more</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">AI</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">No</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Yes</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Office 365 Integration</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Limited integration</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Seamless integration with all solutions</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Automation</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">No</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Yes</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Transactions</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">4000 pm</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Unlimited</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Customization</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Limited Option</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Highly Customizable</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Cloud/On-Premises</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Cloud only</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Both</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Multi-Currency Support</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Yes</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Yes</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</tbody></table>\r\n\r\n<h3>Pricing Comparison</h3>\r\n\r\n<table><thead>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center; \">Xero</th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center;\">Business Central</th>\r\n  </tr></thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Early - $15 per month</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Essential- $70 per user/month</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Growing - $42 per month</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Premium- $100 per user/month</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Established - $78 per month</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Team Members- $8 per user/ month</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<h2 id=\"Limitations-of-xero-accounting-software\">Limitations of Xero Accounting Software</h2>\r\n<p>Xero Accounting has a few limitations. You can only handle 2000 invoices per month. This includes 1000 sales invoices and 1000 purchase bills.  Additionally, it also suggests that each invoice or bill can contain 5-10 lines if you want to avoid performance issues.</p>\r\n<p>Xero also allows businesses to handle up to 2000 bank transactions per month. It depends on the frequency and variability of transactions. Moreover, you can only track 4000 inventory items in your organization. \r\n</p><p>Once you apply manual payment, it can’t be rolled back until payment is removed. You can’t delete invoices. This limitation can impose a serious threat on you as your business grows. \r\n</p><p>That’s why businesses should upgrade from Xero to D365 Business Central. You can leverage Microsoft Dynamics Business Central functionalities as your business. It is flexible and can fulfill your business requirements. By using Microsoft Business Central, you can also streamline other operations of your business apart from finance.</p><h2 id=\"Key-reasons-to-upgrade-from-xero-to-business-central\">Key Reasons to Upgrade from Xero to Business Central</h2>\r\n<p>If you are constantly looking for an alternative to Xero, you should <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-nav-to-business-central/\">upgrade to Dynamics Business Central</a>. It can cover all your basics from sales and finance to inventory management. \r\n</p><p>But what set Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central apart? Its features. Here is how it can help your organization: \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Comprehensive Integration \r\n</b></h3><p>D365 Business Central can seamlessly integrate with Microsoft products and third-party applications to fulfill your business requirements. This integration can enhance productivity, which Xero can’t match. \r\n</p><p>By using Business Central (BC), you can create detailed reports and analytics in real time without any need for extra software. However, if you are still using Xero, you might require additional software to achieve similar reporting capabilities. \r\n</p><h3><b>2. Advanced Customization \r\n</b></h3><p>Business Central seamlessly integrates with Power Platform, like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-automate/\">Power Automate</a>, Power BI, Power Apps. This integration allows businesses to customize and extend <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\">Microsoft Dynamics ERP</a> functionality, which is feasible with Xero.  \r\n</p><h3><b>3. Scalability \r\n</b></h3><p>Dynamics 365 Business Central is designed to support your business\'s growing demand. As technology evolves and your business demand changes, like handling complexities in operation, Microsoft releases regular updates to cater to all the needs. \r\n</p><h3><b>4. Flexibility \r\n</b></h3><p>Your business might require support in other modules, like supply chain and manufacturing. D365 Business Central offers customization options so you can ensure streamlined operation. This prevents you from paying for unnecessary features. \r\n</p><h3><b>5. Improves Sales and Customer Service \r\n</b></h3><p>Migrating from Xero to Microsoft Dynamics Business Central enables robust CRM and ERP capabilities, allowing to improve sales and customer service. By using this software, you can automate your sales process, manage your sales pipeline, and track your leads. This enables a holistic view of your customers’ data, ensuring efficient customer service. \r\n</p><h3><b>6. Centralize Data \r\n</b></h3><p>When you choose D365 BC for your organization, it centralizes the data of your organization. It acts as the single source of truth, ensuring data is stored in secure environments. This helps everyone in your organization to access the data in real-time and update it.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Steps-to-migrate-from-xero-to-business-central\">Steps to Migrate from Xero to Business Central</h2>\r\n<ul><li>Identify Your Business Needs. This will help you understand which functionality of Business Central is crucial for your business operation. By doing this, you can eliminate unnecessary complications and can ensure effortless migration. \r\n</li><li>Collaborate with Dynamics 365 Implementation Partner. They can help you implement BC hassle-free, as they have decades of experience and expertise.</li><li>Once you have collaborated with a <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Business Central partner</a>, you can rest assured of data migration. However, it is a crucial step, where you need to extract the data from Xero and transform it into Microsoft Business Central.</li><li>Set up modules, customize reports, and more once data is successfully migrated. Moreover, be assured that  your Microsoft Solutions partner, like Dynamics Square, will work closely with you to customize your specific requirements and ensure hassle-free upgrades.</li><li>If you want to reap the maximum benefit, you should provide adequate training to your employees.  \r\n</li></ul><p>Furthermore, you can also choose Xero integration for Business Central to further leverage more functionality, ensuring streamlined business operations. Integration ensures hassle-free data flow between these two solutions. This allows you to prevent manual data entry.</p><p>Read more: <a href=\"/dynamics-gp-to-business-central-migration/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics GP to Business Central Migration</a></p><p> \r\n</p><h3>Get Dynamics Square Support Now! \r\n</h3><p>Migrating from Xero to Business Central can streamline your business operation. It facilitates exceptional functionalities and modules. Businesses should collaborate with a&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/microsoft-dynamics-365-partner/\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a> to experience seamless migration. \r\n</p><p>Collaborating with a renowned <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation</a> partner can help your business stay relevant in the constantly evolving landscape. Dynamics Square is a renowned Microsoft solution partner that provides onsite support, ensuring your project success. \r\n</p><p>Additionally, we offer 24/7 support service to resolve any queries. Dynamics Square also offer training so your employees can reap the maximum benefits. \r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Get in touch with our consultant</a> for successful implementation!</p>\r\n\r\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">// <![CDATA[\r\nconst buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n\r\nbuttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n    button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n  );\r\n});\r\n// ]]></script>\r\n<style>\r\n/* The Modal (background) */\r\n#image-viewer {\r\n  display: none;\r\n  position: fixed;\r\n  z-index: 999;\r\n  padding: 70px;\r\n  left: 0;\r\n  top: 0;\r\n  width: 100%;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  overflow: auto;\r\n  background-color: rgb(0,0,0);\r\n  background-color: rgba(45, 62, 80, 0.99);\r\n}\r\n.modal-content {\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n  display: block;\r\n  width: 80%;\r\n  max-width: 100%;\r\n}\r\n.modal-content { \r\n  animation-name: zoom;\r\n  animation-duration: 0.6s;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@keyframes zoom {\r\n  from {transform:scale(0)} \r\n  to {transform:scale(1)}\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close {\r\n  position: absolute;\r\n  top: 15px;\r\n  right: 35px;\r\n  color: #f1f1f1;\r\n  font-size: 40px;\r\n  font-weight: bold;\r\n  transition: 0.3s;\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close:hover,\r\n#image-viewer .close:focus {\r\n  color: #bbb;\r\n  text-decoration: none;\r\n  cursor: pointer;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@media only screen and (max-width: 700px){\r\n  .modal-content {\r\n      width: 100%;\r\n      height:auto;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<script src=\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js\"></script><script>\r\n$(\"img\").on(\'click\',function(){\r\n   $(\"#full-image\").attr(\"src\", $(this).attr(\"src\"));\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').show();\r\n});\r\n\r\n$(\"#image-viewer .close\").click(function(){\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').hide();\r\n});\r\n</script><script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n      button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n    );\r\n  });\r\n  </script>\r\n<script>\r\n $(document).on(\'click\', \'a[href^=\"#\"]\', function (event) {\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    $(\'h2\').css(\'padding-top\',\'75px\');\r\n   $(\'html, body\').animate({\r\n        scrollTop: $($.attr(this, \'href\')).offset().top\r\n    });\r\n});\r\n\r\n</script>', 'Migrating from Xero to Dynamics 365 Business Central', 'xero to dynamics 365 business central', 'Outgrowing Xero? Dynamics 365 Business Central offers powerful features for scaling businesses. Learn more about migration & streamlining operations.', 'migrating from Xero to Business Central,Xero accounting,upgrade from Xero to Business Central,Xero integration for Business Central,dynamics 365 business central,dynamics 365 implementation', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1799857833892945.Xero to Dynamics 365 Business Central Migration.png', 'Mukesh Jha', 'mukesh.jha@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/xero-to-dynamics-365-business-central-migration/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Migrating from Xero to Dynamics 365 Business Central\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Outgrowing Xero? Dynamics 365 Business Central offers powerful features for scaling businesses. Learn more about migration & streamlining operations.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1799859371562396.Xero to Dynamics 365 Business Central Migration.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Mukesh Jha\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Mukesh-Jha/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-05-23\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-05-23\"\r\n}', NULL, '04:25:29pm', '2024-05-23', '10 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 16:25:29'),
(205, 'The Ultimate Dynamics 365 CRM Implementation Handbook', 'dynamics-365-crm-implementation', 'Dynamics 365 CRM', 'dynamics-365-crm', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1800324578311566.Dynamics 365 CRM Implementation.png', 'There are two types of decision-makers—proactive and reactive. What type of decision-makers are you? A successful business owner doesn’t react to challenges, rather they choose a proactive approach, fueled by data-visibility and resources.', '<p>There are two types of decision-makers—proactive and reactive. What type of decision-makers are you? A successful business owner doesn’t react to challenges, rather they choose a proactive approach, fueled by data-visibility and resources. Hence, Dynamics 365 CRM implementation comes in.  \r\n</p><p>Microsoft Dynamics CRM, now known as <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-customer-engagement/\">Dynamics 365 Customer Engagement</a>, equips businesses with AI-driven insights and a set of tools, enabling them to take proactive actions against obstacles. You can identify problems before they arise and prepare a robust strategy to overcome them.</p>\r\n<p>Dynamics 365 CRM also allows businesses to track the customer journey and improve interaction. Due to its advantages, CRM (Customer Relationship Management) adoption is at an all-time high, and its market is expected to surpass <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.globenewswire.com/en/news-release/2023/06/01/2680071/0/en/Customer-Relationship-Management-Market-Size-to-Surpass-USD-157-53-Billion-by-2030-exhibiting-a-CAGR-of-12-0.html\" target=\"_blank\">USD 157.53 billion</a> by 2030.</p><p>However, if you are a business owner and want to leverage CRM, this guide will help you to choose the right D365 CRM solution(s) and crucial steps for Dynamics 365 CRM implementation. Let\'s start with the reasons to implement Dynamics CRM.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blog-content-container\">\r\n<div class=\"blog-content active\">\r\n<h4 class=\"blog-content-title\">&nbsp;Table of Content</h4>\r\n<div class=\"inner\">\r\n                <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Why-should-you-implement-dynamics-crm\">1. Why Should You Implement Dynamics CRM?</a>\r\n                <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Explore-microsoft-dynamics-365-crm-solutions\">2. Explore Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM Solutions</a>\r\n                <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Steps-for-successful-dynamics-crm-implementation\">3. Steps for Successful Dynamics CRM Implementation</a>\r\n                <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Factors-that-can-affect-the-length-and-cost-of-implementation\">4. Factors That Can Affect the Length and Cost of Implementation</a>\r\n</div>\r\n<button class=\"blog-content-toggle\"> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"><!--! Font Awesome Free 6.4.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license (Commercial License) Copyright 2023 Fonticons, Inc. --><path d=\"M201.4 342.6c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0l160-160c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0L224 274.7 86.6 137.4c-12.5-12.5-32.8-12.5-45.3 0s-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160z\"></path></svg></button>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h2 id=\"Why-should-you-implement-dynamics-crm\">Why Should You Implement Dynamics CRM?</h2>\r\n<p>Customer satisfaction is the ultimate goal of every business. You can achieve this by implementing a CRM, allowing you to handle and assess important customer data. Here are some of the benefits of Dynamics CRM implementation: \r\n</p><h3>Increase Customer Retention \r\n</h3><p>Customer churn is the biggest issue that any business faces, leading to losses in revenue. To prevent customer churn, business has two options—acquisition and retention. However, acquiring a new customer is about five times costlier than retaining customers.  \r\n</p><p>Retaining your existing customers is the best way to ensure long-term success in your organization. Additionally, if the retention rate increases by 5%, the profit rate can <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://hbswk.hbs.edu/archive/the-economics-of-e-loyalty\" target=\"_blank\">go up from 25% to 95%</a>. \r\n</p><p>That’s where Dynamics 365 CRM can help you precisely. It ensures seamless communication between you and your customer by offering detailed information, such as preferences, requirements, and future needs. You can customize your offering by utilizing this data, ensuring enhanced customer retention. \r\n</p><h3>Make Data-driven Decision \r\n</h3><p>Data is a great resource; however, you can’t understand what it says without CRM. <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a> analyzes the vast set of data and provides actionable business insights. \r\n</p><p><b>These insights offer details, like: \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Performance of your marketing campaign in the specific demographic area \r\n</li><li>Fulfillment of customer expectations \r\n</li></ul><p>Microsoft Dynamics CRM implementation helps your team to perform better by eliminating guesswork. These will help your team to make better decisions and allocate the resources more effectively to increase ROI. \r\n</p><h3>Centralize Customer Data \r\n</h3><p>Dynamics CRM centralizes all the data at a single point so all your team can access the data according to their requirements. This ensures teams in your organization are on the same page and can access data at their fingertips. \r\n</p><h3>Automate the Repetitive Tasks</h3><p>Microsoft Dynamics CRM allows you to eliminate boring manual tasks. From sending personalized emails to managing billing through integrated <a href=\"https://www.invoicera.com/blog/invoicing/19-best-invoicing-software-for-prompt-payment/\" target=\"_blank\">invoicing software</a>, you don’t need to do everything manually. CRM allows you to send mail to everyone with a single effort. Moreover, CRM also qualifies leads for you in minimum time before your leads forget about your offering.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Explore-microsoft-dynamics-365-crm-solutions\">Explore Microsoft Dynamics 365 CRM Solutions</h2>\r\n<p>Microsoft offers a wide range of CRM solutions to businesses to fulfill their business requirements. Here is a list of some Dynamics 365 CRM solutions:</p><h3>Dynamics 365 Sales</h3><p>Microsoft\'s Dynamics 365 Sales has been a leader in Sales Force automation for 13 consecutive years. It helps the sales team to fulfill customers’ expectations.</p><p>By implementing Dynamics 365 for Sales, you can track and manage the sales pipeline, contacts, accounts, leads, and more. Additionally, its AI-powered solution can allow us to track competitors.</p><p><i><b>Here are a few more CRM solutions provided by Microsoft:</b></i></p><ul><li>Dynamics 365 Project Operations</li><li>Dynamics 365 Relationship Sales</li><li>Dynamics 365 Customer Service Professional</li></ul><h3>Dynamics 365 Customer Service \r\n</h3><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-customer-service/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Customer Service</a> is a CRM solution that helps businesses increase the productivity of the customer-facing agent, personalize customer experience, and optimize business operations. \r\n</p><p>It has an inbuilt <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/microsoft-introduces-dynamics-365-copilot/\">Microsoft Copilot</a>, which increases the customer experience with generative AI. This CRM solution also provides an omnichannel solution to exceed customer expectations. \r\n</p><p><i><b>It offers: \r\n</b></i></p><ul><li>Customer service center \r\n</li><li>AI-suggested cases \r\n</li><li>Voice channels \r\n</li><li>Integration with Dynamics 365  \r\n</li><li>Virtual Agent for Customer  \r\n</li><li>And more</li></ul><h3>Dynamics 365 Field Service \r\n</h3><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-field-service/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 field service</a> is another CRM solution that empowers companies to provide seamless onsite services to their clients. It utilizes AI, IoT, and mixed reality to help mobile workers at customer locations. \r\n</p><p>For instance, mobile workers will get visibility about the appointments in real-time using this CRM solution.  \r\n</p><p><i><b>It offers various features, such as: \r\n</b></i></p><ul><li>Automated communication \r\n</li><li>Post-engagement surveys \r\n</li><li>Periodic data sync \r\n</li><li>Self-service scheduling \r\n</li><li>Remote access \r\n</li><li>Offline capabilities \r\n</li></ul><h3>Dynamics 365 Marketing \r\n</h3><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-marketing/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Marketing</a>, now known as Dynamics 365 Customer Insights, provides tools to help companies. This builds customer journeys, improves communication, and more. \r\n</p><p>Using this solution, you can know customer information in detail. These details allow you to engage with them more effectively, improving customer satisfaction. This will boost your productivity.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Steps-for-successful-dynamics-crm-implementation\">Steps for Successful Dynamics CRM Implementation</h2>\r\n<p>Successful implementation requires a robust strategy. So, follow these steps for successful implementation: \r\n</p><h3>Assess Your Organization Goals and Needs \r\n</h3><p>Organizations leverage Dynamics 365 CRM to improve their customer engagement and make their business more effective and efficient. However, to get the best out of CRM, organizations should identify their unique customer requirements to make their business more efficient. \r\n</p><p>By doing this, you can use CRM in the best possible way to support your business. For instance, your sales team can track the data to find crucial information, like customer behavior. \r\n</p><h3>Establish CRM Budget \r\n</h3><p>To support your needs and budget, you need to establish a budget for CRM solutions. You can choose the features of Dynamics CRM based on your budget. For instance, an out-of-the-box system is beneficial for small and medium-size businesses while large organizations require highly customized CRM solutions. \r\n</p><p>Extra features might cost you more money. Additionally, you might pay for CRM implementation. Microsoft Dynamics CRM implementation partners customize the solution for you based on your requirements and provide the necessary support and training for successful implementation. \r\n</p><h3>Choose a Suitable CRM Solution \r\n</h3><p>Microsoft Dynamics 365 offers various CRM solutions, such as <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-sales/\">Dynamics 365 Sales</a>, Dynamics 365 Project Operations, etc. You can choose a suitable solution based on the required features. You can also consult with a <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 partner</a>, like Dynamic Square, regarding implementing the right CRM solutions. \r\n</p><h3>Create Dynamics CRM Implementation Strategy \r\n</h3><p>Purchasing the CRM system won’t solve your problems. You should create a robust implementation strategy to reap the maximum benefits. While creating these strategies, you should define the roles and responsibilities of your team members. \r\n</p><p>Additionally, CRM strategy should also include integration plans, implementation processes, data migration, testing techniques, and more. If required, also include training and support plans.  \r\n</p><h3>Provide Final Training for CRM \r\n</h3><p>CRM can be a very beneficial tool for your business across departments, such as marketing, sales, and customer service departments. However, Dynamics CRM might be overwhelming for your teams while leveraging its various capabilities.  \r\n</p><p>That’s why you should conduct training for users. This will help in improving usability, acceptability, user adoption, and confidence. \r\n</p><h3>Offer Ongoing Support to Your Business \r\n</h3><p>Once implementation is completed successfully, the organization should also provide ongoing maintenance. You can have an in-house team who can support you with minor issues. Moreover, you should go for a Microsoft solution partner if you want support apart from traditional help.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Factors-that-can-affect-the-length-and-cost-of-implementation\">Factors That Can Affect the Length and Cost of Implementation</h2>\r\n<p>The cost of implementation and its duration can vary depending on several factors. For instance, implementing out-of-the-box sales modules will take less time than an in-depth customized module. \r\n</p><p>Time and cost will vary directly on the uniqueness of your CRM implementation. Here are some of the factors that can influence the length and cost of the project: \r\n</p><ul><li>Customization \r\n</li><li>Infrastructure \r\n</li><li>Licensing \r\n</li><li>Data Migration \r\n</li><li>Training \r\n</li><li>Ongoing support and maintenance \r\n</li><li>Integration with third party \r\n</li></ul><p>Moreover, the Microsoft Dynamics CRM implementation time can vary depending on your organization’s size and your business needs. A small business usually takes less time compared to mid- and large-sized businesses. \r\n</p><h3>Experience Hassle-Free Implementation with Dynamic Square \r\n</h3><p>Dynamics 365 CRM implementation might be overwhelming; however, it is essential to improve your business process in marketing, sales, and other modules.  That’s why you should collaborate with a <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics CRM implementation partner</a>. \r\n</p><p>Dynamic Square is a recognized Microsoft Gold Partner and helps you simplify the complexity of implementing Dynamics 365 CRM. At Dynamic Square, we have a team of experienced professionals who will understand your needs and evaluate your system to identify a suitable solution. \r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Book a free consultation with us</a> to start your implementation journey. Call us at <b>+1 281 899 0865</b> or write us an email at <b>arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</b>.</p><p>Also know about <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/crm-implementation-services/\" target=\"_blank\">CRM implementation services</a>.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">// <![CDATA[\r\nconst buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n\r\nbuttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n    button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n  );\r\n});\r\n// ]]></script>\r\n<style>\r\n/* The Modal (background) */\r\n#image-viewer {\r\n  display: none;\r\n  position: fixed;\r\n  z-index: 999;\r\n  padding: 70px;\r\n  left: 0;\r\n  top: 0;\r\n  width: 100%;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  overflow: auto;\r\n  background-color: rgb(0,0,0);\r\n  background-color: rgba(45, 62, 80, 0.99);\r\n}\r\n.modal-content {\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n  display: block;\r\n  width: 80%;\r\n  max-width: 100%;\r\n}\r\n.modal-content { \r\n  animation-name: zoom;\r\n  animation-duration: 0.6s;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@keyframes zoom {\r\n  from {transform:scale(0)} \r\n  to {transform:scale(1)}\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close {\r\n  position: absolute;\r\n  top: 15px;\r\n  right: 35px;\r\n  color: #f1f1f1;\r\n  font-size: 40px;\r\n  font-weight: bold;\r\n  transition: 0.3s;\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close:hover,\r\n#image-viewer .close:focus {\r\n  color: #bbb;\r\n  text-decoration: none;\r\n  cursor: pointer;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@media only screen and (max-width: 700px){\r\n  .modal-content {\r\n      width: 100%;\r\n      height:auto;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<script src=\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js\"></script><script>\r\n$(\"img\").on(\'click\',function(){\r\n   $(\"#full-image\").attr(\"src\", $(this).attr(\"src\"));\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').show();\r\n});\r\n\r\n$(\"#image-viewer .close\").click(function(){\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').hide();\r\n});\r\n</script><script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n      button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n    );\r\n  });\r\n  </script>\r\n<script>\r\n $(document).on(\'click\', \'a[href^=\"#\"]\', function (event) {\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    $(\'h2\').css(\'padding-top\',\'75px\');\r\n   $(\'html, body\').animate({\r\n        scrollTop: $($.attr(this, \'href\')).offset().top\r\n    });\r\n});\r\n\r\n</script>', 'The Ultimate Dynamics 365 CRM Implementation Handbook', 'dynamics 365 crm implementation', 'With the help of our extensive guide, discover the potential of Dynamics 365 CRM! Unleash professional tactics for seamless implementation.', 'Dynamics 365 CRM implementation,Dynamics CRM implementation,Microsoft Dynamics CRM implementation,Microsoft Dynamics CRM implementation partners,Dynamics 365 for sales,Dynamics 365 customer engagement', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1800324578311573.Dynamics 365 CRM Implementation.png', 'Arish Siddiqui', 'arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/dynamics-365-crm-implementation/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"The Ultimate Dynamics 365 CRM Implementation Handbook\",\r\n  \"description\": \"With the help of our extensive guide, discover the potential of Dynamics 365 CRM! Unleash professional tactics for seamless implementation.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1800324724725383.Dynamics 365 CRM Implementation.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Arish Siddiqui\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Arish-Siddiqui/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-05-28\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-05-28\"\r\n}', '[]', '03:11:49pm', '2024-05-29', '11 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2026-01-27 22:11:49');
