(206, 'Warehouse Management in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management', 'warehouse-management-in-dynamics-365-supply-chain-management', 'Dynamics 365 Sales', 'dynamics-365-sales', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1817503927678781.Warehouse Management in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management.png', 'Warehouse management in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management is a comprehensive module that facilitates the management of warehouse operations for businesses engaged in manufacturing, distribution, and retail.', '<p>Warehouse management in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management is a comprehensive module that facilitates the management of warehouse operations for businesses engaged in manufacturing, distribution, and retail.  \r\n</p><p>This module is designed to support the warehouse facility at an optimal level, anywhere and anytime, and is fully connected with other business processes, including transportation, manufacturing, quality control, purchase, transfer, sales, and returns. \r\n</p><p>Let’s learn about it in detail.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blog-content-container\">\r\n    <div class=\"blog-content active\">\r\n    <h4 class=\"blog-content-title\">&nbsp;Table of Content</h4>\r\n    <div class=\"inner\">\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Getting-started-with-warehouse-management-in-dynamics-365-supply-chain-management\">1. Getting Started with Warehouse Management in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-is-a-warehouse-management-System\">2. What is a Warehouse Management System?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-are-the-benefits-of-a-warehouse-management-system\">3. What are the Benefits of a Warehouse Management System?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Warehouse-management-in-dynamics-365-finance-and-operations\">4. Warehouse Management in Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Importance-of-warehouse-management-in-supply-chain-management\">5. Importance of Warehouse Management in Supply Chain Management</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#How-to-access-dynamics-365-warehouse-management\">6. How to access Dynamics 365 Warehouse Management</a>\r\n\r\n  </div>\r\n   <button class=\"blog-content-toggle\"> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"><!--! Font Awesome Free 6.4.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license (Commercial License) Copyright 2023 Fonticons, Inc. --><path d=\"M201.4 342.6c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0l160-160c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0L224 274.7 86.6 137.4c-12.5-12.5-32.8-12.5-45.3 0s-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160z\"></path></svg></button>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h2 id=\"Getting-started-with-warehouse-management-in-dynamics-365-supply-chain-management\">Getting Started with Warehouse Management in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</h2>\r\n<p>To get started with warehouse management in <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\">Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</a>, you need to set up general warehouse parameters that support your company’s business processes.</p><p>This involves configuring components for inbound and outbound warehouse process workflows, such as wave templates, work templates, work pools, and location directives. \r\n</p><p>The warehouse management module offers a wide range of features, including: \r\n</p><ul><li>Integrated support for source documents like sales orders, returns, transfer orders, production orders, and kanban. \r\n</li><li>Flexible support for material workflow, both inbound and outbound, depending on queries. \r\n</li><li>Full integration with manufacturing and transportation modules. \r\n</li><li>Control over location volumetric and stocking constraints. \r\n</li><li>Inventory properties controlled by inventory status. \r\n</li><li>Full batch and serial item support. \r\n</li><li>Multiple picking strategies and advanced counting capabilities. \r\n</li><li>Manual and automatic movement of inventory. \r\n</li><li>Fully integrated quality control (QMS). \r\n</li><li>Support for automatic containerization, manual packing, and outgoing wave processing. \r\n</li></ul><p>Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management offers a highly efficient warehouse inventory management system. Both the terms, warehouse and inventory, are quite identical but there are some differences between them.  \r\n</p><p>Before delving into warehouse management in <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\">Microsoft Dynamics ERP</a>, let’s explore the differences between the warehouse management system and the inventory management system. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Warehouse Management System:</b> It is about handling stock storage, picking, packing, and shipping in a warehouse. Besides, it helps you track stock location within a particular warehouse. It even handles comprehensive stock movement in the warehouse. \r\n</li><li><b>Inventory Management System:</b> It helps you track the total number of items in your stock for a particular storage location. Also, it can facilitate forecasting, ordering, receiving, and allocating stock.</li></ul>\r\n<h2 id=\"What-is-a-warehouse-management-System\">What is a Warehouse Management System?</h2>\r\n<p>A Warehouse Management System (WMS) or warehouse management software is an important software application that helps you optimize your warehouse operations in the retail, distribution, and manufacturing industries. \r\n</p><p>It can help you carry out goods tracking, bin management, quality control, transportation, item ledger entries, stock locating, cycle counting, wave planning, order allocation, and put-away activities.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"What-are-the-benefits-of-a-warehouse-management-system\">What are the Benefits of a Warehouse Management System?</h2>\r\n<p>A warehouse management solution can automate operations and boost productivity. It includes a whole host of features to streamline your entire supply chain management. It has the following benefits: \r\n</p><h3>1. Streamlined Business Processes \r\n</h3><p>Warehouse management solution comprises essential functionalities such as warehouse shipments, bins, inventory picks, and movement worksheets to simplify everyday warehousing processes. It can efficiently enhance your inventory accuracy and deliver real-time insights into your supply chain.  \r\n</p><h3>2. Automated Supply Chain Management \r\n</h3><p><a href=\"/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Dynamics 365</a> integrates a highly advanced supply chain management module to automate the inventory system. It lets you handle sales and purchase orders. Also, you can efficiently track your inventory levels in real-time.  \r\n</p><p>WMS facilitates your inventory by creating packing receipts, picking lists, and shipping labels for organized order fulfillment. \r\n</p><h3>3. Organized Warehouse \r\n</h3><p>A warehouse management system can help you get an organized warehouse as it includes bin management which can categorize smaller locations into smaller sections to streamline pick and put-away operations.  \r\n</p><h3>4. Improved Customer Satisfaction and Seamless Fulfilment \r\n</h3><p>A warehouse management system accelerates the supply chain workflow with efficient order fulfillment.  \r\n</p><p>It strengthens order accuracy through barcode scanning, which further leads to improved customer satisfaction and customer retention rates. WMS can optimize supply chain performance by carrying out the following things: \r\n</p><ul><li>Automated order management and product picking lists. \r\n</li><li>Proper coordination between shipping carriers for smooth order fulfillment. \r\n</li><li>Improved order accuracy via barcode scanning.  \r\n</li></ul><h3>5. Supplier Collaboration \r\n</h3><p>A warehouse Management System gives a boost to supplier collaboration as inefficient co-ordination can cause delayed delivery and disturbed supply chain management which can further impact your customer satisfaction.  \r\n</p><p>Effective supplier coordination can help forge better relationships with suppliers, ensure time-bound delivery, and reduce lead times.  \r\n</p><h3>6. Labor Management  \r\n</h3><p>Labor management is a crucial feature of WMS as it can eliminate errors and discrepancies through performance monitoring and proper training. Also, it can lead to enhanced productivity and keep checks on increased labor costs. \r\n</p><p>Moreover, proper labor management includes training and performance monitoring. It can minimize errors and reduce operational costs. \r\n</p><h3>7. Space Utilization \r\n</h3><p>Inaptly utilizing warehouse space may lead to a mess, potential damage to inventory items, and difficulty while tracking items.  \r\n</p><p>Warehouse management implementation can boost efficiency, minimize storage costs, and enhance the overall warehouse organization.    \r\n</p><p>Warehouse Management System in Supply Chain Management includes the following advantages:</p><ul><li>Advanced warehouse arrangement with proper space optimization features.  \r\n</li><li>Well-organized bin management to optimize storage locations. \r\n</li><li>Efficient bin management to streamline storage locations.  \r\n</li><li>Smart suggestions for adequate product placement. \r\n</li></ul><p>Apart from the above benefits, these two things are notable for businesses that physically take goods in and out of the warehouse: \r\n</p><ul><li>They can easily track inventory levels and item locations in the warehouse.  \r\n</li><li>They can timely and efficiently receive, pick, and ship out items. \r\n</li></ul><p>To cater to the above requirements the warehouse module in Business Central brings the following functionalities to inventory management:</p><ul><li>Bins \r\n</li><li>Warehouse shipments \r\n</li><li>Inventory picks \r\n</li></ul>\r\n<h2 id=\"Warehouse-management-in-dynamics-365-finance-and-operations\">Warehouse Management in Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations</h2>\r\n<p>We have discussed warehouse management in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management. However, it is interesting to note that <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance-operations/\">Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations</a> includes an advanced warehouse management system that can streamline the entire supply chain process.  \r\n</p><p>With the warehouse management module in Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations, businesses can automate processes, boost production efficiency, and bring agility to their manufacturing.  \r\n</p><p>The warehouse management module within Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance &amp; Operations includes the following: \r\n</p><ul><li>Placement and storage \r\n</li><li>Inventory dimensions \r\n</li><li>Serial and batch number control \r\n</li><li>Random location storage \r\n</li><li>RFID (Radio-frequency identification) and barcoding \r\n</li><li>Work template \r\n</li><li>Replenishment \r\n</li><li>Warehouse performance \r\n</li></ul><p>Leveraging the inventory dimension feature of the warehouse management module in Dynamics 365 for Finance &amp; Operations, users can create unlimited batch numbers or serial numbers for the automatic numbering of their products.  \r\n</p><p>One can track the exact location of the inventory using the details, like warehouse location, pallet ID, serial number, warehouse batch number, and RFID (Radio-frequency identification) tags.  \r\n</p><p>Moreover, the inventory dimension number can be associated with shipments and deliveries to get a clear visibility of the items in the warehouse. The inventory dimension can help users track serial and batch numbers as well.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Importance-of-warehouse-management-in-supply-chain-management\">Importance of Warehouse Management in Supply Chain Management</h2>\r\n<p>In order to satisfy your constantly changing needs and achieve your targeted warehouse efficiency objective, you can design your warehouse layout using more flexible methods thanks to the warehouse management process (WMS) in supply chain management.  \r\n</p><ul><li>It provides you with enough elbow room to accommodate high-priority and low-priority storage regions for ideal placement of the inventory items.  \r\n</li><li>You can categorize your warehouse into different zones to meet your storage requirements according to quickly changing circumstances like temperatures or turnover rates of the goods.  \r\n</li><li>To meet different storage requirements, such as different item turnover rates or temperature requirements, you can create zones within your warehouse. \r\n</li><li>You can effortlessly use any level to specify different warehouse locations, including site, aisle, rack, shelf, warehouse, and bin position. \r\n</li><li>You can efficiently manage item storage and placements, leveraging unique query-defined rules. \r\n</li></ul><p>To access WMS in the <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\">D365 Supply Chain Management</a> solution, you need to create a warehouse first and then enable it. Once this is done, choose the option of ‘warehouse management process’ available on the Warehouses page.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"How-to-access-dynamics-365-warehouse-management\">How to access Dynamics 365 Warehouse Management</h2>\r\n<p>Remember, the specific steps may vary depending on your organization’s setup and the version of Dynamics 365 you are using. It’s always a good idea to refer to the official Microsoft documentation or consult with a D365 specialist for guidance tailored to your situation. \r\n</p><p>To access Dynamics 365 Warehouse Management, follow these steps: \r\n</p><p><b>1. General Warehouse Parameters Setup</b></p><ul><li>Go to Warehouse management &gt; Setup &gt; Warehouse management parameters. \r\n</li><li>Configure the general warehouse parameters to support your company’s business processes. This setup includes defining components for inbound and outbound warehouse workflows, such as wave templates, work templates, work pools, and location directives. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>2. Track Configuration Processes</b></p><ul><li>Use the Warehouse implementation tasks workspace to track your configuration processes. This workspace helps you identify important implementation tasks and monitor your progress. \r\n</li><li>Create an implementation project in the workspace to organize your tasks. \r\n</li><li>Import the default configuration task list provided by Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management to get started. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>3. Mobile Access</b></p><p>To access Warehouse Management on mobile devices:  \r\n</p><ul><li>Download and install the Warehouse Management mobile app on each device. \r\n</li><li>Configure the app to connect to your Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management environment. \r\n</li><li>You can use <a href=\"https://www.free-qr-code-generator.com/\" target=\"_blank\">free QR code</a> generators like <a href=\"https://www.uniqode.com/qr-code-generator\" target=\"_blank\">Uniqode</a> to create QR codes for financial reports, payments, and customer service portals.</li></ul><p>Remember to configure components like wave templates, work templates, and location directives to optimize your warehouse processes. With Warehouse Management, you’ll have integrated support for various source documents, flexible material workflows, and control over inventory properties.</p><h3>Unlock the Full Potential of D365 Supply Chain Management with Dynamics Square \r\n</h3><p>Dynamics 365 Supply Chain is creating waves in the retail, distribution, and manufacturing industries. For a comprehensive guide and additional steps, you can reach out to us.  \r\n</p><p>We are Dynamics Square, a reliable and renowned <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/microsoft-dynamics-365-partner/\">Microsoft Dynamics partner</a> with more than 11+ years of experience. <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Schedule a free call with our expert </a>today. Call us at <b><a href=\"tel:+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a></b> or simply write us an email at <b><a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a></b>.</p>\r\n\r\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">// <![CDATA[\r\nconst buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n\r\nbuttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n    button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n  );\r\n});\r\n// ]]></script>\r\n<style>\r\n/* The Modal (background) */\r\n#image-viewer {\r\n  display: none;\r\n  position: fixed;\r\n  z-index: 999;\r\n  padding: 70px;\r\n  left: 0;\r\n  top: 0;\r\n  width: 100%;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  overflow: auto;\r\n  background-color: rgb(0,0,0);\r\n  background-color: rgba(45, 62, 80, 0.99);\r\n}\r\n.modal-content {\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n  display: block;\r\n  width: 80%;\r\n  max-width: 100%;\r\n}\r\n.modal-content { \r\n  animation-name: zoom;\r\n  animation-duration: 0.6s;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@keyframes zoom {\r\n  from {transform:scale(0)} \r\n  to {transform:scale(1)}\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close {\r\n  position: absolute;\r\n  top: 15px;\r\n  right: 35px;\r\n  color: #f1f1f1;\r\n  font-size: 40px;\r\n  font-weight: bold;\r\n  transition: 0.3s;\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close:hover,\r\n#image-viewer .close:focus {\r\n  color: #bbb;\r\n  text-decoration: none;\r\n  cursor: pointer;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@media only screen and (max-width: 700px){\r\n  .modal-content {\r\n      width: 100%;\r\n      height:auto;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<script src=\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js\"></script><script>\r\n$(\"img\").on(\'click\',function(){\r\n   $(\"#full-image\").attr(\"src\", $(this).attr(\"src\"));\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').show();\r\n});\r\n\r\n$(\"#image-viewer .close\").click(function(){\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').hide();\r\n});\r\n</script><script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n      button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n    );\r\n  });\r\n  </script>\r\n<script>\r\n $(document).on(\'click\', \'a[href^=\"#\"]\', function (event) {\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    $(\'h2\').css(\'padding-top\',\'75px\');\r\n   $(\'html, body\').animate({\r\n        scrollTop: $($.attr(this, \'href\')).offset().top\r\n    });\r\n});\r\n\r\n</script>', 'Warehouse Management in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management', 'warehouse management in dynamics 365 supply chain management', 'Optimize inventory, streamline operations & enhance productivity with Warehouse Management in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management. Explore now!', 'warehouse management system,warehouse management software,warehouse inventory management ,inventory warehouse management software', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1817503927678785.Warehouse Management in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management.png', 'Samar Malik', 'samar.malik@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/warehouse-management-in-dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Warehouse Management in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Optimize inventory, streamline operations & enhance productivity with Warehouse Management in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management. Explore now!\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1800397374631225.Warehouse Management in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Samar Malik\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Samar-Malik/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-05-29\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-05-29\"\r\n}', '[]', '06:47:09pm', '2024-05-29', '11 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-12-11 01:47:09'),
(207, 'Copilot for Power BI: Take Productivity to the Next Level', 'copilot-for-power-bi', 'Power BI', 'power-bi', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1800480116343645.Copilot for Power BI.png', 'Microsoft Copilot for Power BI is an effective tool that uses generative AI capabilities to help users with report creation, DAX measure formulation, and improving Q&A sessions.', '<p>Microsoft Copilot for Power BI is an effective tool that uses generative AI capabilities to help users with report creation, DAX measure formulation, and improving Q&amp;A sessions. Its goal is to make data analysis into an easy-to-use, AI-driven procedure. \r\n</p><p>Now, let’s start with comprehending Power BI.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blog-content-container\">\r\n    <div class=\"blog-content active\">\r\n    <h4 class=\"blog-content-title\">&nbsp;Table of Content</h4>\r\n    <div class=\"inner\">\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-is-microsoft-power-bi\">1. What is Microsoft Power BI?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#The-parts-of-power-bi\">2. The Parts of Power BI</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#How-to-use-copilot-in-power-bi\">3. How to Use Copilot in Power BI?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Benefits-of-using-copilot-for-power-bi\">4. Benefits of using Copilot for Power BI</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#How-to-turn-on-copilot-in-power-bi\">5. How to Turn on Copilot in Power BI</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Start-copilot-in-power-bi-desktop-for-the-first-time\">6. Start Copilot in Power BI Desktop for the First Time</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n   <button class=\"blog-content-toggle\"> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"><!--! Font Awesome Free 6.4.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license (Commercial License) Copyright 2023 Fonticons, Inc. --><path d=\"M201.4 342.6c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0l160-160c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0L224 274.7 86.6 137.4c-12.5-12.5-32.8-12.5-45.3 0s-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160z\"></path></svg></button>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h2 id=\"What-is-microsoft-power-bi\">What is Microsoft Power BI?</h2>\r\n<p>Power BI is a collection of software programs, apps, and connectors that cooperate to transform your data from silos or inconsistencies into coherent information that is visually appealing and offers comprehensive and understandable insights.<br></p><p>Whether the data comes from a complicated cloud-based warehouse or your spreadsheet, with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">Microsoft Power BI</a>, you can quickly view and examine your data from every perspective, gain a thorough understanding of the information, and use that knowledge to guide your decision-making.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-platform/\">Microsoft Power Platform</a>, a low-code platform that allows the development of customized business solutions, comprises five product areas: Power Pages, Power Apps, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-automate/\">Power Automate</a>, Power Virtual Agents, and Power BI.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"The-parts-of-power-bi\">The Parts of Power BI</h2>\r\n<p>Power BI is a suite of different software and applications that work in cohesion to enable faster data analysis, starting with these three basics: \r\n</p><ul><li>A Windows desktop application called Power BI Desktop. \r\n</li><li>The Power BI service is an online software as a service (SaaS) provider. \r\n</li><li>Power BI Mobile apps for Windows, iOS, and Android devices. \r\n</li></ul><p>While leveraging the capabilities, Copilot in Microsoft Power BI or Copilot Power BI manages all your data handling tasks, including combined data visualization, quick and customized reporting, advanced calculations and financial modeling, and robust data summaries.</p><p>Besides, it is also responsible for interactive data exploration, complex data manipulation, and creating precise financial forecasts. \r\n</p><p>Here’s a brief overview of how you can use Copilot in Power BI:</p><ol><li><b>Report Creation:</b> Reports can be automatically customized by selecting a subject or asking Copilot to concentrate on a particular area.</li><li><b>Data Analysis:</b> Copilot can analyze data, create charts and graphs, and provide actionable insights almost instantly.</li><li><b>Enhanced Q&amp;A:</b> The feature improves the Q&amp;A experience by understanding natural language queries and delivering relevant content.</li></ol><p>To start using Copilot in Power BI, your administrator needs to enable it in Microsoft Fabric. You’ll also need access to a workspace assigned to a paid Fabric capacity (F64 or higher) or Power BI Premium capacity (P1 or higher) with Copilot enabled.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"How-to-use-copilot-in-power-bi\">How to Use Copilot in Power BI?</h2>\r\n<p>Copilot in Power BI is a powerful feature that leverages generative AI to assist users in creating reports, analyzing data, preparing narrative summaries, and generating insights. Here’s how you can use Copilot in Microsoft Power BI: \r\n</p><p><b>1. Enable Copilot</b></p><ul><li>In Power BI Desktop, navigate to the File menu, then select Options and Settings, and finally choose Preview Features. \r\n</li><li>Enable the Quick Measure Suggestions option. \r\n</li><li>Close and reopen Power BI Desktop to apply the changes. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>2. Access Copilot</b></p><ul><li>In Power BI Desktop, go to the View tab. \r\n</li><li>Click on the AI Visualizations dropdown menu. \r\n</li><li>Select Copilot to activate the assistant. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>3. Ask Questions and Describe Data</b></p><ul><li>Open Power BI and type a question about your data into the Copilot tab on the screen. \r\n</li><li>You can describe the topic you want to explore, ask questions, or provide instructions. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>4. Generate Reports and Insights</b></p><ul><li>Copilot will analyze your data and automatically create visuals, narratives, and summaries based on your input. \r\n</li></ul>\r\n<h2 id=\"Benefits-of-using-copilot-for-power-bi\">Benefits of using Copilot for Power BI \r\n</h2><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/microsoft-introduces-dynamics-365-copilot/\">Microsoft Copilot</a> is a powerful generative AI that adds more capabilities to Power BI and transforms it into a smart business analytics solution. It can lead businesses to enhanced data visualization, deep insights, vast data exploration, greater productivity, and growth.  \r\n</p><p>Here are some of the benefits of using Copilot for Power BI: \r\n</p><p><b>1. Simplified DAX Formula Creation \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Non-professional developers can create DAX (Data Analysis Expressions) formulas without requiring extensive coding expertise. \r\n</li><li>The Copilot assists in writing complex DAX expressions, making it easier to perform calculations and create custom measures. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>2. Efficient Data Model Changes \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Copilot’s suggestions streamline the process of modifying the data model within Power BI. \r\n</li><li>Users can quickly adjust relationships, hierarchies, and data transformations based on Copilot’s recommendations. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>3. Streamlined Visual Reporting \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Adding visuals (charts, graphs, tables) to reports becomes more straightforward and intuitive. \r\n</li><li>Copilot provides context-aware suggestions for visualizations, helping users create compelling and informative reports. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>4. Faster Report Creation \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Copilot accelerates report creation by offering relevant insights and automating repetitive tasks. \r\n</li><li>Users can generate reports in seconds, reducing the time spent on manual design and data exploration. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>5. Intuitive Data Exploration \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Users can ask questions about their data in conversational language. \r\n</li><li>Copilot assists in exploring data by providing relevant visualizations, filtering options, and insights. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>6. Faster Decision Making \r\n</b></p><p>Copilot for Power BI can help access data insights in real-time which can further contribute to informed and faster decision-making.  \r\n</p><p><b>7. Futuristic Approach \r\n</b></p><p>Copilot for Power BI ensures you a futuristic business approach. It gives you a competitive edge over other businesses that have not embraced AI. \r\n</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"How-to-turn-on-copilot-in-power-bi\">How to Turn on Copilot in Power BI</h2>\r\n<p>Turning on Copilot in Power BI involves a few steps. Here’s a general guide to help you get started: \r\n</p><p><b>1. Enable Copilot in your Tenant Settings</b></p><ul><li>Open the Fabric Admin portal and navigate to the Tenant settings. \r\n</li><li>Locate the Copilot settings by using the Search function. \r\n</li><li>Toggle the switch on to Enable Copilot in Fabric. \r\n</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1800475747510949.Microsoft.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align: center; \"><b>Source: Microsoft</b></p><p><b>2. Enable Sharing Data Across Geographic Boundaries (if necessary)</b></p><ul><li>This step is only required if Azure OpenAI isn’t available in your geographic region. \r\n</li><li>In the Fabric Admin portal, find the setting that allows data to be processed outside your capacity’s geographic region and toggle it on. \r\n</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1800475757855520.Microsoft 2.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align: center; \"><b>Source: Microsoft</b></p><p><b>3. Use Copilot for Power BI in the Service</b></p><ul><li>Ensure that reports are in a workspace with the right capacity (Premium Power BI or paid Fabric capacity). \r\n</li><li>Check your license type in the Workspace settings and apply either Premium or Fabric capacity. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>4. Use Copilot in Power BI Desktop</b></p><ul><li>Select Copilot from the ribbon when you open a Power BI report. \r\n</li><li>The Copilot pane will prompt you to select a workspace. Only workspaces that support Copilot will appear. \r\n</li></ul><p>Remember, you must have Fabric admin privileges to enable Copilot settings.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Start-copilot-in-power-bi-desktop-for-the-first-time\">Start Copilot in Power BI Desktop for the First Time</h2>\r\n<p>Using Copilot in Power BI Desktop for the first time may ask you to choose a Copilot-compatible workspace while selecting the Copilot button in the ribbon. \r\n</p><p>The workspace you select and the one where you want to publish your report do not need to be the same.</p><p><b>Also Read:</b> <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/how-to-generate-interactive-reports-in-power-bi/\">Interactive Reports in Power BI</a></p><p>  \r\n</p><p>To start Copilot in Power BI Desktop for the first time, you’ll need to follow these steps: \r\n</p><ol><li>Open <b>Power BI Desktop</b>. \r\n</li><li>In the ribbon, select ‘<b>Get Data</b>’, then choose the type of data source you want to connect to. \r\n</li><li>After selecting a data source, click ‘<b>Connect</b>’ to load your data into Power BI Desktop. \r\n</li><li>Once your data is loaded, click on the <b>Copilot icon</b> in the ribbon to open the Copilot pane in the report view. \r\n</li><li>The first time you click the <b>Copilot ribbon button</b>, you’ll be prompted to pick a <b>Copilot-compatible workspace</b>. Select any workspace assigned to the required capacity (Note: This doesn’t need to be where you’ll publish your report). \r\n</li><li>If you don’t have access to any workspaces that are in the correct capacity to use Copilot, you’ll see a message indicating this issue in the Copilot settings. \r\n</li><li>After selecting a workspace, you’ll see a <b>welcome card</b> in the Copilot pane. Click ‘<b>Get started</b>’ to begin interacting with Copilot. \r\n</li></ol><p>You don’t need to repeat the steps once you successfully implemented them. \r\n</p><p><b>Change the Selected Workspace \r\n</b></p><p>However, if you want you can change the assigned workspace to a different Copilot-compatible workspace. You can follow the below steps to change the associated workspace: \r\n</p><p><b>Select File &gt; Options and settings &gt; Options &gt; Copilot (preview) setting under Global</b>. \r\n</p><p>Here you can find the name of the selected workspace along with an option to choose a new workspace.  \r\n</p><p>Remember, to use Copilot, you must have admin, member, or contributor access to at least one workspace that is assigned to a paid Fabric capacity (F64 or higher) or Power BI Premium capacity (P1 or higher) with Copilot enabled. \r\n</p>\r\n<h3>How Can Dynamics Square Help You with Power BI Implementation?</h3>\r\n<p>So far in this article, we have gone into detail regarding Copilot for Power BI. However, if you want to know more about it, you can reach out to Dynamics Square.  \r\n</p><p>Dynamics Square is a renowned <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\">Microsoft Dynamics partner</a> in the market. With rich industry experience and relevant resources, Dynamics Square is an ideal option for your <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/power-bi-implementation/\">Power BI implementation</a>. We have a team of experts who will work diligently for the successful implementation of Power BI. \r\n</p><p>They can efficiently assess your business needs and suggest the optimal solution that can best align with your organizational goals. In case any assistance is required, feel free to call us directly at <b><a href=\"tel:+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a></b> or simply write an email at <b><a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a></b>.</p>\r\n\r\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">// <![CDATA[\r\nconst buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n\r\nbuttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n    button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n  );\r\n});\r\n// ]]></script>\r\n<style>\r\n/* The Modal (background) */\r\n#image-viewer {\r\n  display: none;\r\n  position: fixed;\r\n  z-index: 999;\r\n  padding: 70px;\r\n  left: 0;\r\n  top: 0;\r\n  width: 100%;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  overflow: auto;\r\n  background-color: rgb(0,0,0);\r\n  background-color: rgba(45, 62, 80, 0.99);\r\n}\r\n.modal-content {\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n  display: block;\r\n  width: 80%;\r\n  max-width: 100%;\r\n}\r\n.modal-content { \r\n  animation-name: zoom;\r\n  animation-duration: 0.6s;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@keyframes zoom {\r\n  from {transform:scale(0)} \r\n  to {transform:scale(1)}\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close {\r\n  position: absolute;\r\n  top: 15px;\r\n  right: 35px;\r\n  color: #f1f1f1;\r\n  font-size: 40px;\r\n  font-weight: bold;\r\n  transition: 0.3s;\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close:hover,\r\n#image-viewer .close:focus {\r\n  color: #bbb;\r\n  text-decoration: none;\r\n  cursor: pointer;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@media only screen and (max-width: 700px){\r\n  .modal-content {\r\n      width: 100%;\r\n      height:auto;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<script src=\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js\"></script><script>\r\n$(\"img\").on(\'click\',function(){\r\n   $(\"#full-image\").attr(\"src\", $(this).attr(\"src\"));\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').show();\r\n});\r\n\r\n$(\"#image-viewer .close\").click(function(){\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').hide();\r\n});\r\n</script><script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n      button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n    );\r\n  });\r\n  </script>\r\n<script>\r\n $(document).on(\'click\', \'a[href^=\"#\"]\', function (event) {\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    $(\'h2\').css(\'padding-top\',\'75px\');\r\n   $(\'html, body\').animate({\r\n        scrollTop: $($.attr(this, \'href\')).offset().top\r\n    });\r\n});\r\n\r\n</script>', 'Copilot for Power BI: Take Productivity to the Next Level', 'copilot for power bi', 'Boost your productivity with Copilot for Power BI. Learn how this tool helps you create tailored reports effortlessly and enhances your data analysis capabilities.', 'microsoft copilot for power bi,copilot in power bi,microsoft power bi copilot,microsft power bi ,microsoft power platform', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1800480116343649.Copilot for Power BI.png', 'Vivek Gururani', 'vivek.gururani@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/copilot-for-power-bi/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Copilot for Power BI: Take Productivity to the Next Level\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Boost your productivity with Copilot for Power BI. Learn how this tool helps you create tailored reports effortlessly and enhances your data analysis capabilities.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1800480090171588.Copilot for Power BI.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Vivek Gururani\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Vivek-Gururani/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-05-30\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-05-30\"\r\n}', NULL, '07:03:00pm', '2024-05-30', '11 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-08-23 19:03:00');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(208, 'The Role of Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing in Empowering Businesses', 'role-of-microsoft-cloud-for-manufacturing', 'Microsoft Cloud', 'microsoft-cloud', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1800855463877095.Role Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing.png', 'Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing is designed to streamline operations, optimize different processes, eliminate redundancies, reduce downtime, and boost overall productivity.', '<p>Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing is designed to streamline operations, optimize different processes, eliminate redundancies, reduce downtime, and boost overall productivity.</p><p>It consists of different Dynamics 365 solutions, that include Business Central, Finance, and Supply Chain Management. Such cloud-based solutions allow you to improve process quality, enhance agility, empower workforce, and reduce costs. \r\n</p><p>But why does the manufacturing business require this solution? Let’s delve into this. \r\n</p><p>The Covid-19 pandemic impacted almost every industry, and manufacturing was no exception. Due to unprecedented market and supply chain disruptions, the industry witnessed various challenges, including forecasting demand, staying resilient, supply chain management, operational visibility, employee safety, and remote work.  \r\n</p><p>To counter these challenges, the industry realized the need to incorporate a digital strategy to grow a sustainable future and reap the maximum benefits from their technology investments. Post-pandemic, <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/industry/blog/manufacturing-and-mobility/2021/06/24/5-manufacturing-trends-driving-the-need-for-an-industry-cloud/\" target=\"_blank\">62%</a> of manufacturers invested in digitizing their factories and increasing factory &amp; field asset safety.  \r\n</p><p>Manufacturers need a unified ecosystem to digitize their factories. Here, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/industries/microsoft-cloud-for-manufacturing/\">Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing</a> comes into the picture. It helps create a resilient supply chain by introducing innovation in manufacturing, making factories intelligent, and more. It does so by bringing data, processes, people, and technology together.  \r\n</p><p>In this blog, we will delve deeper into how Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing empowers manufacturers.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blog-content-container\">\r\n    <div class=\"blog-content active\">\r\n    <h4 class=\"blog-content-title\">&nbsp;Table of Content</h4>\r\n    <div class=\"inner\">\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Introducing-microsoft-cloud-for-manufacturing\">1. Introducing Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Why-is-microsoft-cloud-for-manufacturing-software-necessary\">2. Why is Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing Software Necessary?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#How-does-this-solution-empower-businesses\">3. How does this Solution Empower Businesses?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-are-key-benefits-for-manufacturers\">4. What are Key Benefits for Manufacturers?</a>\r\n      <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#The-bottom-line\">5. The Bottom Line!</a>\r\n  </div>\r\n   <button class=\"blog-content-toggle\"> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"><!--! Font Awesome Free 6.4.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license (Commercial License) Copyright 2023 Fonticons, Inc. --><path d=\"M201.4 342.6c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0l160-160c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0L224 274.7 86.6 137.4c-12.5-12.5-32.8-12.5-45.3 0s-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160z\"></path></svg></button>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h2 id=\"Introducing-microsoft-cloud-for-manufacturing\">Introducing Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing</h2>\r\n<p>As manufacturing entities are digitizing their factories, an industry-specific solution, that is intelligent, user-friendly, integrated, secure, and scalable, becomes necessary for them.  \r\n</p><p>Microsoft, the second-largest provider of cloud infrastructure services, introduced Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing. It consists of multiple tools that accelerates digital transformation in manufacturing by bringing design and engineering with AI and cloud computing.</p><p>It facilitates industry-specific solutions into a single platform, Microsoft partner ecosystem, to create a resilient supply chain, intelligent factories, and seamless customer experience.  \r\n</p><p>These features allow businesses to create a safe and secure environment in the factory, enabling frontline and asset worker productivity. You don’t need a different system for your operation, as Microsoft Cloud orchestrates all the complex solutions in Microsoft manufacturing software.   \r\n</p><p>Additionally, Microsoft manufacturing solutions also eliminate data silos by connecting IT, OT, and ET, offering transparent and efficient data insights. With its broader range of features, businesses can begin with a particular area, where digitization is paramount.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Why-is-microsoft-cloud-for-manufacturing-software-necessary\">Why is Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing Software Necessary?</h2>\r\n<p>Let’s understand the importance of the cloud manufacturing solution available in the Dynamics 365 suite by an example. For instance, the dashboard of these systems shows production is lower than the normal production rate.</p><p>It will show work order is going down, but unable to tell what exactly. The operator decides to increase the machine speed, resulting in quality degradation and waste being produced.   \r\n</p><p>Additionally, the operator might be unaware of the possibility of a postponed delivery date, as its information resides in a separate <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 ERP</a> system. Due to limited visibility and data silos, manufacturers rely on a reactive approach.  \r\n</p><p>To prevent these problems, every machine should be connected and provide insight to the operator in real-time, also known as digital feedback. Due to the transition to Industry 4.0, manufacturing companies also need a system that can analyze tons of data and help them with their manufacturing process.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"How-does-this-solution-empower-businesses\">How does this Solution Empower Businesses?</h2>\r\n<p>Manufacturing Cloud Software can help businesses in several ways to digitize their operation. Here is a list of changes your business is likely to experience after leveraging this suite:  \r\n</p><h3>Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: Building More Intelligent Factories  \r\n</h3><p>The suite of tools extracts data from IT and OT and offers real-time visibility, equipment efficiency, and sustainability by using AI, cloud connectivity, data analytics, and IIoT.</p><p>This data can be useful in fostering collaboration between manufacturers, design, and engineering teams. It can improve manufacturing processes, as these insights facilitate real-world feedback, ensuring continuous improvements.  \r\n</p><p>Additionally, <a href=\"/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\">Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</a>, Azure AI Services, Azure Machine Learning, and Azure IIoT, part of the suite, automate the complex quality inspection process.</p><p>It also offers predictive maintenance solutions and tracks materials within the factory. These solutions work together to detect defects, detect root cause analysis, and ensure final products meet predefined standards.  \r\n</p><p>Furthermore, manufacturers can reduce errors, improve product quality, and streamline their manufacturing process. Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing offers predictive maintenance in your factories and ensures top-notch product quality.  \r\n</p><h3>D365 Guides and D365 Remote Assist: Transforming Your Workforce  \r\n</h3><p>The scope of manufacturing under the Microsoft Dynamics 365 suite also provides communication and collaboration tools, such as Dynamics 365 Guides and Dynamics 365 Remote Assist, to onboard and easily connect with frontline workers. It also helps to upskill workers faster to get the necessary knowledge and expertise.  \r\n</p><p>Upskilling reduces downtime and helps workers with the right resources to get their job done. Workers can seamlessly engage in a company-inclusive culture with tools, like Microsoft Tools and <a href=\"/products/microsoft-power-platform/\">Power Platform</a>. In addition to this, it has in-built security and compliance across machines and devices, improving security.  \r\n</p><h3>Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: A Resilient Supply Chain  \r\n</h3><p>Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing leverages D365 Supply Chain Management, formerly part of <a href=\"/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance-operations/\">Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations</a>, to create a sustainable and resilient supply chain. It comes with in-built AI capabilities, which analyze supplier data, your organization\'s operation &amp; production data, and market signals.   \r\n</p><p>This provides real-time visibility and predicts supply chain disruption, allowing proactive action to avoid disruption. Additionally, tools like <a href=\"/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">Microsoft Power BI</a> and Supply Chain Management improve customer service and automate warehouses. Companies can leverage the system to track and reduce carbon emissions. In industries like <a href=\"https://www.rapidops.com/industries/manufacturing/building-materials\" target=\"_blank\">Digital transformation in building materials industry</a>, this capability ensures a resilient supply chain, helping businesses meet environmental and market demands effectively.\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><h3><span style=\"font-size: 1.75rem;\">Dynamics 365 Sales: Modernizing Customer Experience</span></h3><p>By leveraging tools, such as <a href=\"/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-sales/\">Dynamics 365 Sales</a>, Customer Service, Field Service, and Customer Insights, Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing modernizes the customer experience. It aids your organization’s sellers, service agents, and marketers to understand customer requirements with detailed insights.  \r\n</p><p>Your sales team can use a cloud-based <a href=\"/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a> to get a 360-degree view of customers, attract new customers, close new deals with more speed, and qualify high-value prospects. These solutions allow you for omnichannel customer engagement, issue resolutions, product monitoring, data estate management, and remote support.  \r\n</p><h3>Unlock Innovation and Add New Products \r\n</h3><p>Azure Industrial IoT, Azure Compute, Azure AI Services, and Azure Machine Learning are key Microsoft technologies, that unlock innovation by Digital Twins and Simulation. These tools accelerate production for new products without sacrificing the quality of products.   \r\n</p><p>Additionally, you can design, simulate, and validate the processes and production of products. Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing can reduce time-to-market, optimize the development process, and improve production quality.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"What-are-key-benefits-for-manufacturers\">What are Key Benefits for Manufacturers?</h2>\r\n<p>Manufacturing business faces various challenges in their daily operation. So, leveraging this Microsoft suite, businesses can avail of these benefits:  \r\n</p><h3>Asset Productivity  \r\n</h3><p>Unexpected downtime can be a big challenge for manufacturing companies, leading to significant loss of revenue. Cloud-based manufacturing in Dynamics 365 helps companies secure their assets and company by enabling predictive maintenance. This improves asset productivity, resulting in enhanced production, cost reduction, and profitability enhancement.  \r\n</p><h3>Learning &amp; Knowledge Management  \r\n</h3><p>Manufacturing companies can leverage Cloud ERP for Manufacturing to help their workforce operate at their best. These solutions allow manufacturers to seamlessly collaborate with their workforce and quickly educate. This can ensure safe and reliable production and automated manufacturing.  \r\n</p><h3>Global Supply Chain Visibility  \r\n</h3><p>Since Supply Chain is complex and interconnected; however, sudden disruption can expose your organization to vulnerabilities. Additionally, this business can also face challenges in changing its plan to fulfill customer requirements. Cloud-based manufacturing solution in <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365</a> unifies real-time data and mitigates risk by offering real-time visibility.  \r\n</p><h3>Reliable Always-On Customer Service  \r\n</h3><p><a href=\"/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> and Sales helps businesses to actively serve customers. It can detect, predict, and resolve even before a problem arises.  \r\n</p><h3>Industry-leading Partner Integrations  \r\n</h3><p>Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing incorporates various Microsoft Solutions from the ecosystem, like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance/\">Dynamics 365 for Finance</a> to create a resilient supply chain and improve customer experience.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"The-bottom-line\">The Bottom Line!</h2>\r\n<p>Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing can be instrumental in digitizing to improve productivity, gain agility, sustainability, and speed time-to-market. However, Cloud for Manufacturing is a suite of Microsoft products, which help you fulfill your requirements.  \r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation</a> can be overwhelming for your business, as you need to identify your business requirements and choose the tools. That\'s where <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft&nbsp;Dynamics 365 partner</a>, like Dynamics Square, helps to implement and upgrade these suites of tools.  \r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Get in touch with us</a> to digitize your manufacturing business. Call us at <b>+1 281 899 0865</b> or write us an email at <b>arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</b>.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">// <![CDATA[\r\nconst buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n\r\nbuttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n    button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n  );\r\n});\r\n// ]]></script>\r\n<style>\r\n/* The Modal (background) */\r\n#image-viewer {\r\n  display: none;\r\n  position: fixed;\r\n  z-index: 999;\r\n  padding: 70px;\r\n  left: 0;\r\n  top: 0;\r\n  width: 100%;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  overflow: auto;\r\n  background-color: rgb(0,0,0);\r\n  background-color: rgba(45, 62, 80, 0.99);\r\n}\r\n.modal-content {\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n  display: block;\r\n  width: 80%;\r\n  max-width: 100%;\r\n}\r\n.modal-content { \r\n  animation-name: zoom;\r\n  animation-duration: 0.6s;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@keyframes zoom {\r\n  from {transform:scale(0)} \r\n  to {transform:scale(1)}\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close {\r\n  position: absolute;\r\n  top: 15px;\r\n  right: 35px;\r\n  color: #f1f1f1;\r\n  font-size: 40px;\r\n  font-weight: bold;\r\n  transition: 0.3s;\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close:hover,\r\n#image-viewer .close:focus {\r\n  color: #bbb;\r\n  text-decoration: none;\r\n  cursor: pointer;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@media only screen and (max-width: 700px){\r\n  .modal-content {\r\n      width: 100%;\r\n      height:auto;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<script src=\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js\"></script><script>\r\n$(\"img\").on(\'click\',function(){\r\n   $(\"#full-image\").attr(\"src\", $(this).attr(\"src\"));\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').show();\r\n});\r\n\r\n$(\"#image-viewer .close\").click(function(){\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').hide();\r\n});\r\n</script><script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n      button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n    );\r\n  });\r\n  </script>\r\n<script>\r\n $(document).on(\'click\', \'a[href^=\"#\"]\', function (event) {\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    $(\'h2\').css(\'padding-top\',\'75px\');\r\n   $(\'html, body\').animate({\r\n        scrollTop: $($.attr(this, \'href\')).offset().top\r\n    });\r\n});\r\n\r\n</script>', 'Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing: Empower Businesses', 'microsoft cloud for manufacturing', 'Learn how Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing helps manufacturers remain competitive in the digital age by enhancing productivity, innovation, and scalability.', 'microsoft cloud for manufacturing,microsoft cloud,microsoft manufacturing,dynamics 365 for manufacturing,cloud erp for manufacturing,dynamics erp,dynamics 365 crm,microsoft dynamics 365', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1800855463877099.Role Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing.png', 'Mukesh Jha', 'mukesh.jha@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/role-of-microsoft-cloud-for-manufacturing/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing: Empower Businesses\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Learn how Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing helps manufacturers remain competitive in the digital age by enhancing productivity, innovation, and scalability.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1800855339839186.Role Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Mukesh Jha\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Mukesh-Jha/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Mukesh-Jha/\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-06-03\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-06-03\"\r\n}', NULL, '12:05:29pm', '2024-06-03', '10 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-11-20 12:05:29'),
(209, 'Power Automate with Business Central: Amp Up Your Business with Automated Solutions', 'power-automate-with-business-central', 'Integration', 'integration', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1801111253027372.Power Automate with Business Central.png', 'Every business wants to run their organizations to the fullest potential. So, they streamline business operations by using solutions, like Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central.', '<p>Every business wants to run their organizations to the fullest potential. So, they streamline business operations by using solutions, like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> (BC). However, prioritizing important things without automating them will lead businesses nowhere. Hence, Business goes for Power Automate with Business Central.</p>\r\n<p>The duo work in tandem and automate the repetitive tasks, allowing better utilization of resources. Using Power Automate with Business Central can be a game-changer for your business, as it enhances productivity and unlocks new possibilities. Additionally, you can get the best out of BC and maximize your ROI with the help of this duo.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blog-content-container\">\r\n<div class=\"blog-content active\">\r\n<h4 class=\"blog-content-title\">&nbsp;Table of Content</h4>\r\n<div class=\"inner\">\r\n                <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Power-automate-and-business-central-a-perfect-match\">1. Power Automate and Business Central: A Perfect Match</a>\r\n                <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#What-is-a-business-central-connector\">2. What is a Business Central Connector?</a>\r\n                <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Unleash-automation-capabilities-of-power-automate-in-business-central\">3. Unleash Automation Capabilities of Power Automate in Business Central</a>\r\n                <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Benefits-of-integrating-power-automate-with-business-central\">4. Benefits of Integrating Power Automate with Business Central</a>\r\n                <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#Getting-started-with-power-automate-and-business-central-integration\">5. Getting Started with Power Automate and Business Central Integration</a>\r\n</div>\r\n<button class=\"blog-content-toggle\"> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"><!--! Font Awesome Free 6.4.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license (Commercial License) Copyright 2023 Fonticons, Inc. --><path d=\"M201.4 342.6c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0l160-160c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0L224 274.7 86.6 137.4c-12.5-12.5-32.8-12.5-45.3 0s-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160z\"></path></svg></button>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h2 id=\"Power-automate-and-business-central-a-perfect-match\">Power Automate and Business Central: A Perfect Match</h2>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-automate/\">Microsoft 365 Power Automate</a>, previously Microsoft Flow, is a cloud-based service, that helps businesses to automate their workflows without extensive knowledge of coding. This helps to automate repetitive tasks, such as accounts payable, invoices processing, syncing customer information, and approval processes.  \r\n</p><p>Dynamics 365 Business Central is a cloud-based <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\">Dynamics ERP</a> solution that helps businesses streamline their various needs, such as tracking expenses, data-driven decisions, workflow, warehouse management, assembly management, and more.  \r\n</p><p>Power Automate integration enables automated workflow to remove manual efforts and eliminate human errors. Integration can trigger alerts and notifications within Business Central.</p><p>For instance, a sales representative will notify you when a high-priority lead is assigned. This integration allows businesses to adapt and modify workflows as their business evolves.  \r\n</p><p>According to a study by <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.marketsandmarkets.com/Market-Reports/business-process-automation-market-197532385.html\" target=\"_blank\">Markets and Markets</a>, the global Business Process Automation Market is estimated to reach USD 19.6 billion by the end of 2026 from USD 9.8 billion in 2020 at a CAGR of 12.2%. \r\n</p><p>Moreover, businesses often use multiple applications to streamline their various business operations. Power Automate in Business Central enables seamless integration with various third-party apps. </p><p>Power Automate is also responsible for facilitating seamless data synchronization between Dynamics Business Central and other systems. You can seamlessly update inventory levels, update customer records, or share financial data.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"What-is-a-business-central-connector\">What is a Business Central Connector?</h2>\r\n<p>Business Central should seamlessly talk with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-platform/\">Microsoft Power Platform</a> products to unlock the automation possibilities and streamline workflows. Microsoft Business Central connector facilitates communication between Business Central data and Microsoft 365 Power Automate automation capabilities.  \r\n</p><p>Connector allows businesses to leverage Power Automate low-code capabilities to interact with Business Central data entities. Users can create a flow to retrieve, update, and manipulate data within Microsoft Dynamics Business Central.</p><p>Users can create workflows using Business Central Connector. Additionally, this connector can also initiate action through other connectors, such as sending email or starting a chat.</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1801111082576579.Power Automate with BC Connector.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\">Business Central connector doesn\'t allow Power Automate to connect with Business Central (on-premises). For this, you need to install an on-premises data gateway. You will have two options: on-premises data gateway and on-premises data gateway (personal mode). Both are for different scenarios.<br></p><p>Now, you need to create a custom connector in Power Automate to connect with Business Central (on-premises). Choose to create a flow to establish a connection.  \r\n</p><h3>Key Features of Power Automate  \r\n</h3><p>Microsoft Power Automate is a low-code platform, which allows you to automate various tasks. Its features play a pivotal role in smoothing your business. Let’s see its features:  \r\n</p><ul><li>It has pre-built flows &amp; templates  \r\n</li><li>Allows end-to-end business process flows  \r\n</li><li>Comes with robust analytics and monitoring capabilities  \r\n</li><li>Offers data transformation capabilities  \r\n</li><li>Has an extensive library of connectors &amp; integrations  \r\n</li><li>Enables approval management workflows  \r\n</li></ul>\r\n<h2 id=\"Unleash-automation-capabilities-of-power-automate-in-business-central\">Unleash Automation Capabilities of Power Automate in Business Central</h2>\r\n<p>Think of a world where you can automate approvals and data can flow seamlessly between applications and access information at your fingertips. You can achieve this using Power Automate in Business Central. Here are a few ways you can leverage automation capabilities:  \r\n</p><h3>Automated Approval Workflows  \r\n</h3><p>You can streamline approval procedures, such as employee leave requests, purchase orders, and invoices. A user can set a trigger point for your workflows. For instance, you can set reorder alerts if your inventory reaches a specific level.  \r\n</p><p>Microsoft Business Central connectors retrieve relevant data, such as vendor and order details, from BC and ensure access to Power Automate. Power Automate checks pre-defined criteria and routes the request to appropriate approves via notification.</p><p>Connectors also update the data based on approve status and send notifications to relevant parties. This ensures faster approvals, enhanced control, improved visibility, and reduced error.  \r\n</p><h3>Automated Data Synchronization  \r\n</h3><p>Power Automate facilitates seamless integration with third-party tools. It enables data synchronization between these two systems, whether one-directional or bi-directional. This ensures improved data consistency, enhanced data visibility, and increased accuracy.  \r\n</p><h3>Automated Notifications and Alerts  \r\n</h3><p>Every business wants its teams to be on the same page, in terms of things like inventory levels and access to deadlines. Power Automate automatically generates notifications to the designated personnel to solve their problems proactively, improve decision-making, reduce risks, and improve operational efficiency.</p><p><b>Also Read: </b><a href=\"https://erpsoftwareblog.com/2024/04/power-automate-with-business-central/\">Power Automate with Business Central</a></p><p>  \r\n</p><h3>Automated Report Generation  \r\n</h3><p>Power Automate enables valuable insights to users without human intervention. You can set a schedule for report generation, such as weekly and monthly. To generate reports, connectors gather data and Power Automate automatically generates reports in the desired format. This can help you improve data accessibility, time management, and data-driven decision-making.  \r\n</p><h3>Custom Integrations  \r\n</h3><p>Power Automate allows you to go beyond its pre-built features and allow you to create custom workflows. Power Automate facilitates a drag-and-drop interface that simplifies custom integration. This can enhance collaboration, unmatched flexibility, and increase productivity</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Benefits-of-integrating-power-automate-with-business-central\">Benefits of Integrating Power Automate with Business Central</h2>\r\n<p>Connecting Power Automate and Business Central offers various benefits to businesses. One such benefit is reducing manual efforts and allowing integration with third-party applications. Let\'s see more benefits in detail:  \r\n</p><h3>Smooth Data Synchronization  \r\n</h3><p>Businesses should have access to up-to-date data, which is essential to make informed decisions. <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-automate/\">Microsoft Power Automate</a> helps to synchronize data between D365 BC and other systems and applications.</p><p>For instance, if you make data changes in Business Central, such as inventory levels, customer records, or financial data, it will synchronize in real-time, ensuring improved decision-making.  \r\n</p><h3>Streamline Workflow  \r\n</h3><p>You can create a workflow using Power Automate according to your business needs. You can cater to your business needs, such as order processing, invoice processing, inventory tracking, automated data entry, and more. In simple words, Power Automate flows with Business Central to help your employees focus on value-added activities.  \r\n</p><h3>Triggers Notifications  \r\n</h3><p>Connecting Power Automate with D365 Business Central trigger alerts for specific triggers within Business Central in real-time. For instance, your inventory level reached one point, or you need to manage payable or receivable. Your team can leverage these alerts and respond to them to get the best results from these actions.  \r\n</p><h3>Simplify Approval Procedures  \r\n</h3><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> workflows follow a multiple-step approval process, which can slow down the decision-making process. Power Automate automates the approval process with the help of pre-defined rules and ensures that approvals adhere to organization policies.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"Getting-started-with-power-automate-and-business-central-integration\">Getting Started with Power Automate and Business Central Integration</h2>\r\n<p>A Business Central user has access to Power Automate and they don’t need to pay for this. This means you have access to Power Automate features, which you can find in the more option bar. However, users must agree to privacy notices before accessing these features.  \r\n</p><p>Select the “<b>Automate</b>” option and then click on “<b>Get Started with Power Automate</b>” to agree on the terms. Agreeing with these terms takes you to the next steps with various options in the “<b>Automation</b>” option:  \r\n</p><ul><li>Create approval flow  \r\n</li><li>Create automated flow  \r\n</li><li>Create action based on a flow  \r\n</li><li>Manage Flows   \r\n</li></ul><p></p><p>After this, set up flows and run them from Business Central. You can also view and edit existing flows in Power Automate according to your business requirements. Also, you can manage existing flows in Dynamics 365 Business Central and create new ones.</p><p>Read more: <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-business-central-implementation/\" target=\"_blank\">Business Central Implementation</a></p><h3>The Role of a Dynamics 365 Partner  \r\n</h3><p>Power Automate is crucial for automating various business operations. Businesses using D365 Business Central should go for Power Automate integration with Business. However, the integration process might become challenging for you.   \r\n</p><p>You should choose <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\">Microsoft Dynamics partner</a> for seamless integration. We are a renowned name in <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation</a> with over 150 technical consultants.  \r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">Get in touch with Dynamics Square</a> and automate your business operations!</p>\r\n\r\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">// <![CDATA[\r\nconst buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n\r\nbuttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n    button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n  );\r\n});\r\n// ]]></script>\r\n<style>\r\n/* The Modal (background) */\r\n#image-viewer {\r\n  display: none;\r\n  position: fixed;\r\n  z-index: 999;\r\n  padding: 70px;\r\n  left: 0;\r\n  top: 0;\r\n  width: 100%;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  overflow: auto;\r\n  background-color: rgb(0,0,0);\r\n  background-color: rgba(45, 62, 80, 0.99);\r\n}\r\n.modal-content {\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n  display: block;\r\n  width: 80%;\r\n  max-width: 100%;\r\n}\r\n.modal-content { \r\n  animation-name: zoom;\r\n  animation-duration: 0.6s;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@keyframes zoom {\r\n  from {transform:scale(0)} \r\n  to {transform:scale(1)}\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close {\r\n  position: absolute;\r\n  top: 15px;\r\n  right: 35px;\r\n  color: #f1f1f1;\r\n  font-size: 40px;\r\n  font-weight: bold;\r\n  transition: 0.3s;\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close:hover,\r\n#image-viewer .close:focus {\r\n  color: #bbb;\r\n  text-decoration: none;\r\n  cursor: pointer;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@media only screen and (max-width: 700px){\r\n  .modal-content {\r\n      width: 100%;\r\n      height:auto;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<script src=\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js\"></script><script>\r\n$(\"img\").on(\'click\',function(){\r\n   $(\"#full-image\").attr(\"src\", $(this).attr(\"src\"));\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').show();\r\n});\r\n\r\n$(\"#image-viewer .close\").click(function(){\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').hide();\r\n});\r\n</script><script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n      button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n    );\r\n  });\r\n  </script>\r\n<script>\r\n $(document).on(\'click\', \'a[href^=\"#\"]\', function (event) {\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    $(\'h2\').css(\'padding-top\',\'75px\');\r\n   $(\'html, body\').animate({\r\n        scrollTop: $($.attr(this, \'href\')).offset().top\r\n    });\r\n});\r\n\r\n</script>', 'Power Automate with Business Central: Amp Up Your Business with Automated Solutions', 'power automate with business central', 'Find out how integrating Power Automate with Business Central can improve productivity, optimize workflows, and completely change your business with automated solutions.', 'power automate with business central,power automate integration,power automate in business central,business central connector,power automate flows with business central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1801111253027377.Power Automate with Business Central.png', 'Awanish Kumar', 'awanish.kumar@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/power-automate-with-business-central/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Power Automate with Business Central: Amp Up Your Business with Automated Solutions\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Find out how integrating Power Automate with Business Central can improve productivity, optimize workflows, and completely change your business with automated solutions.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1801111070802390.Power Automate with Business Central.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Awanish Kumar\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Awanish-Kumar/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-06-06\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-06-06\"\r\n}', NULL, '06:56:44pm', '2024-06-06', '10 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-11-13 18:56:44'),
(210, 'Signs It’s Time to Change Your Dynamics NAV Support Partner', 'dynamics-nav-support-partner', 'Dynamics Nav', 'dynamics-nav', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1801573595115839.png', 'If you are facing any issues with your existing Microsoft Dynamics NAV support partner but can’t decide what to do, then this article is for you.', '<p>If you are facing any issues with your existing Microsoft Dynamics NAV support partner but can’t decide what to do, then this article is for you. You might be dealing with certain circumstances which are the following: \r\n</p><ul><li>Your NAV service provider is not responding to your request, and you are tired of calling them and writing emails. \r\n</li><li>The service provider has stopped all the updates and support for NAV software solutions, and they are pushing you to upgrade for a hefty sum of money. \r\n</li><li>You are facing delays from your provider and frequent mistakes on their side have cost your business dearly. \r\n</li><li>You are struggling with unfair billing or lack of transparency in the cost structure. \r\n</li></ul><p>In case you are grappling with the above-mentioned issues, then scroll through the article to get a perfect solution to your problems. So, stop worrying about it and say goodbye to all your Dynamics NAV service-related woes. \r\n</p><p>It seems quite easy to suggest the client move to a different business solution like Business Central, which sounds quite fair. However, the transition to <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> may take a lot of time, effort, and money. And being an on-premises service holder, you might not be ready for it right now.  \r\n</p><p>In such a scenario, switching to a new service provider with an impeccable track record is an ideal solution for your problems.</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"blog-content-container\">\r\n<div class=\"blog-content active\">\r\n<h4 class=\"blog-content-title\">&nbsp;Table of Content</h4>\r\n<div class=\"inner\">\r\n                <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#How-to-choose-the-right-dynamics-nav-service-provider\">1. How to Choose the Right Dynamics NAV Service Provider?</a>\r\n                <a data-index=\"rb-heading-index-0\" class=\"blog-content-text\" href=\"#How-can-dynamics-square-be-an-ideal-microsoft-nav-service-provider\">2. How Can Dynamics Square be an Ideal Microsoft NAV Service Provider?</a>\r\n</div>\r\n<button class=\"blog-content-toggle\"> <svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 448 512\"><!--! Font Awesome Free 6.4.2 by @fontawesome - https://fontawesome.com License - https://fontawesome.com/license (Commercial License) Copyright 2023 Fonticons, Inc. --><path d=\"M201.4 342.6c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0l160-160c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0L224 274.7 86.6 137.4c-12.5-12.5-32.8-12.5-45.3 0s-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160z\"></path></svg></button>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h2 id=\"How-to-choose-the-right-dynamics-nav-service-provider\">How to Choose the Right Dynamics NAV Service Provider?</h2>\r\n<p>Choosing the right service provider for <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-nav/\">Microsoft Dynamics NAV</a> is crucial to ensure a successful implementation and ongoing support. Here are some key factors to consider when selecting a partner: \r\n</p><h3>Partner Competency \r\n</h3><p>Microsoft partners are categorized into Gold and Silver as per the Solutions Partner designations program. Look for a partner whose competencies align with your requirements. Their solution should be a priority for their business. \r\n</p><h3>Industry Experience \r\n</h3><p>Evaluate a partner’s expertise in your specific industry. A partner with experience in your industry will facilitate effective and rapid implementation. Ask for client testimonials and references from businesses similar to yours. \r\n</p><h3>Track Record for Project Implementations \r\n</h3><p>Consider the number of successful projects deployed by the service provider. A strong track record indicates competency and reliability.</p><p><b>Also Read:</b> <a href=\"https://erpsoftwareblog.com/2024/06/nav-support-options/\">NAV Support Options</a></p><p> \r\n</p><h3>Dedicated Customer Support  \r\n</h3><p>Responsive and reliable customer service is crucial. If your current partner isn’t meeting your expectations, finding a new partner who prioritizes excellent service can make a significant difference in your experience. \r\n</p><p>Additionally, when evaluating consultants within a partner organization, consider the following: \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Years of Experience:</b> How many years have they worked with Dynamics NAV? \r\n</li><li><b>Certifications:</b> What certifications do they hold? \r\n</li><li><b>Project Types:</b> What types of projects have they worked on in the past? \r\n</li><li><b>Industry Experience:</b> Do they have experience in your specific industry? \r\n</li></ul><p>If you decide to make the switch, here are some steps to take: \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Plan Ahead:</b> Develop a detailed transition plan, including timelines and responsibilities. \r\n</li><li><b>Communicate with Stakeholders:</b> Inform employees, customers, and vendors about the change. \r\n</li><li><b>Manage Data Migration:</b> Securely and efficiently migrate your data to the new system. \r\n</li><li><b>Integrate Systems:</b> Ensure seamless integration with existing processes. \r\n</li></ul><p>Remember that having the right Dynamics 365 partner can make all the difference in ensuring that your system runs smoothly and efficiently. With the right support, you’ll experience a smooth <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation</a> process, thorough training, and excellent ongoing assistance.</p>\r\n<h2 id=\"How-can-dynamics-square-be-an-ideal-microsoft-nav-service-provider\">How Can Dynamics Square be an Ideal Microsoft NAV Service Provider?</h2>\r\n<p>Dynamics Square stands tall in the market as a prominent NAV service provider. With its extensive 12 years of service experience, it has a team of experts who can provide you with all the <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-support-services/\">Dynamics 365 support</a> services while ensuring a smooth and successful transition.  \r\n</p><p>As a reliable and responsible <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics partner</a>, Dynamics Square has a team of experts having access to modern technology to offer you a competitive edge while keeping up with the latest updates.  \r\n</p><p>We ensure you bolster your productivity and enhance your performance while facilitating Dynamics NAV optimization.  \r\n</p><p>Being a business-friendly organization, we value money and ensure to offer you services at a much more affordable price than our competitors.  \r\n</p><p>Also, our immaculate track record and unmatched customer support are enough to consider Dynamics Square as the best possible option for your new <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/microsoft-dynamics-365-partner/\">Microsoft NAV partner</a>. In fact, there is absolutely nothing stopping you from making the right choice! \r\n</p><p>Dynamics Square totally understands your frustrations and relates to your issues as we value growth-oriented business. For a complete integration of Dynamics NAV with your incumbent systems and processes, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\">contact us today</a>.  \r\n</p><p>Feel free to call us directly on <a href=\"tel:+12818990865\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a> or simply write an email at <a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a>.</p>\r\n\r\n\r\n<script type=\"text/javascript\">// <![CDATA[\r\nconst buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n\r\nbuttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n  button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n    button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n  );\r\n});\r\n// ]]></script>\r\n<style>\r\n/* The Modal (background) */\r\n#image-viewer {\r\n  display: none;\r\n  position: fixed;\r\n  z-index: 999;\r\n  padding: 70px;\r\n  left: 0;\r\n  top: 0;\r\n  width: 100%;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  overflow: auto;\r\n  background-color: rgb(0,0,0);\r\n  background-color: rgba(45, 62, 80, 0.99);\r\n}\r\n.modal-content {\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n  display: block;\r\n  width: 80%;\r\n  max-width: 100%;\r\n}\r\n.modal-content { \r\n  animation-name: zoom;\r\n  animation-duration: 0.6s;\r\n  height: 100%;\r\n  margin: auto;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@keyframes zoom {\r\n  from {transform:scale(0)} \r\n  to {transform:scale(1)}\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close {\r\n  position: absolute;\r\n  top: 15px;\r\n  right: 35px;\r\n  color: #f1f1f1;\r\n  font-size: 40px;\r\n  font-weight: bold;\r\n  transition: 0.3s;\r\n}\r\n#image-viewer .close:hover,\r\n#image-viewer .close:focus {\r\n  color: #bbb;\r\n  text-decoration: none;\r\n  cursor: pointer;\r\n}\r\n\r\n@media only screen and (max-width: 700px){\r\n  .modal-content {\r\n      width: 100%;\r\n      height:auto;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n</style>\r\n<script src=\"https://ajax.googleapis.com/ajax/libs/jquery/3.7.1/jquery.min.js\"></script><script>\r\n$(\"img\").on(\'click\',function(){\r\n   $(\"#full-image\").attr(\"src\", $(this).attr(\"src\"));\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').show();\r\n});\r\n\r\n$(\"#image-viewer .close\").click(function(){\r\n  $(\'#image-viewer\').hide();\r\n});\r\n</script><script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n  const buttons = document.querySelectorAll(\".blog-content-toggle\");\r\n  buttons.forEach((button) => {\r\n    button.addEventListener(\"click\", () =>\r\n      button.parentElement.classList.toggle(\"active\")\r\n    );\r\n  });\r\n  </script>\r\n<script>\r\n $(document).on(\'click\', \'a[href^=\"#\"]\', function (event) {\r\n    event.preventDefault();\r\n    $(\'h2\').css(\'padding-top\',\'75px\');\r\n   $(\'html, body\').animate({\r\n        scrollTop: $($.attr(this, \'href\')).offset().top\r\n    });\r\n});\r\n\r\n</script>', 'Signs It’s Time to Change Your Dynamics NAV Support Partner', 'dynamics nav support', 'Explore pivotal indicators signaling the necessity to switch your Dynamics NAV support partner for heightened service, efficiency, and business growth.', 'dynamics nav support,microsoft support for nav ,dynamics navision support,microsoft dynamics nav,dynamics 365 business central,dynamics 365 implementation,business central implementation,nav to bc upgrade', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1801573595118270.png', 'Arish Siddiqui', 'arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/dynamics-nav-support-partner/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Signs It’s Time to Change Your Dynamics NAV Support Partner\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Explore pivotal indicators signaling the necessity to switch your Dynamics NAV support partner for heightened service, efficiency, and business growth.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1801576181200328.Dynamics NAV Support.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Arish Siddiqui\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Arish-Siddiqui/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-06-11\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-06-11\"\r\n}', NULL, '04:53:56pm', '2024-06-11', '6 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-08-21 16:53:56');
