(211, 'Dynamics GP Support: Lifecycle Policies, Options and BC Comparison', 'dynamics-gp-support', 'Dynamics GP', 'dynamics-gp', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1801744837851606.png', 'Are you a Dynamics GP (Great Plains) user? Looking for Microsoft Dynamics GP support? If so, you are in the right place.', '<p>Are you a Dynamics GP (Great Plains) user? Looking for Microsoft Dynamics GP support? If so, you are in the right place. Before we delve into the details of <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-gp/\" style=\"background-color: white; font-family: sans-serif; font-weight: 400;\">Dynamics GP</a> support requirements, it\'s essential to comprehend that <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics-gp/terms/lifecycle\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft governs Dynamics GP versions</a> through two distinct lifecycle policies - Fixed Lifecycle and Modern Lifecycle.<br></p><p>Fixed Lifecycle governs all Dynamics GP versions before 2019, while Modern Lifecycle governs the 2019 version. \r\n</p><p>Please refer to the illustration below for details regarding mainstream support and extended support.</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1801742672284674.Dynamics GP Versions.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align: center; \"><b>Source: Microsoft</b></p>\r\n<p><b>Here’s the table for more clarity:</b></p>\r\n\r\n<table><thead>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center; \">Product</th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center;\">Support Policy</th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center;\">End Date for Mainstream Support</th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center;\">End Date for Extended Support</th>\r\n  </tr></thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">GP 2013 &amp; GP 2013 R2</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Fixed</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">April 4, 2018</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">April 11, 2023</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">GP 2015 &amp; GP 2015 R2</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Fixed</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">April 14, 2020</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">April 8, 2025</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">GP 2016 &amp; GP 2016 R2</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Fixed</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">July 13, 2021</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">July 14, 2026</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">GP 2018 &amp; GP 2018 R2</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Fixed</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">January 10, 2023</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">January 11, 2028</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">GP 2019</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Modern</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Not Specified</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center; \">Not Specified</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>For products that fall under the Modern Lifecycle policy, Microsoft will give at least a year\'s notice before terminating support if no replacement product or service is provided - except free services and preview versions. \r\n</p><p>Now, let’s get into the details to understand what options are available for Dynamics GP users.</p>\r\n<h2>What Choices do Dynamics GP Users Have?</h2>\r\n<p>It ultimately boils down to your business requirements. As a Dynamics GP user, you can choose to upgrade to the newer version of GP or transition to an advanced ERP solution like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central</a>, which we shall discuss in the next section. \r\n</p><p>Whatever you choose, you have the unwavering support of ours - we are Dynamic Square, a trusted <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\">Microsoft Dynamics partner</a>. \r\n</p><p>To help you understand the difference between Dynamics GP and Business Central, here we present a thorough comparison of both ERPs.</p>\r\n<h2>Dynamics GP vs Business Central Comparison</h2>\r\n<p>When comparing Microsoft Dynamics GP (Great Plains) with Business Central, there are several factors to consider. Here’s a high-level comparison based on the latest information: \r\n</p><h3>Hosting and Licensing \r\n</h3><p><b>1. Dynamics GP \r\n</b></p><ul><li>It is traditionally an on-premises solution, but it can also be hosted on the cloud by a third party. \r\n</li><li>Perpetual licensing starts from $5,000 USD for 3 users. Subscription licensing starts from $65 USD/user/month. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>2. Dynamics 365 Business Central \r\n</b></p><ul><li>It is a cloud-native <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\">Dynamics ERP</a> solution, offering a modern interface and integration with other Microsoft Cloud services. \r\n</li><li>Licensing for Business Central starts at $70 USD/user/month. \r\n</li></ul><h3>Functionality \r\n</h3><ul><li>Both offer robust ERP capabilities, but Dynamics Business Central is more modern and integrated with the Microsoft ecosystem. \r\n</li><li>Business Central provides out-of-the-box features like multi-dimensional accounting and analysis using account Dimensions. \r\n</li></ul><h3>Integration and Extensions \r\n</h3><ul><li>Dynamics GP may require additional tools or services for certain integrations. \r\n</li><li>Microsoft Business Central allows for easier integration with other applications and services, especially within the Microsoft stack. \r\n</li></ul><h3>Future Development \r\n</h3><ul><li>Microsoft is focusing more on the development of Dynamics 365 Business Central, which means more future enhancements and updates for this platform. \r\n</li></ul><h3>Deployment Flexibility \r\n</h3><ul><li>Microsoft Dynamics GP offers deployment flexibility, including on-premises and hybrid options. \r\n</li><li>Business Central is primarily cloud-based, which can lead to easier deployment and lower upfront costs. \r\n</li></ul><h3>Upgrades/Updates \r\n</h3><ul><li><b>Dynamics GP:</b> Free service pack updates for GP 2019 October release and later. Earlier GP versions required manual upgrades. \r\n</li><li><b>Business Central:</b> Free and automated updates. \r\n</li></ul><h3>Add-on Options \r\n</h3><ul><li><b>Dynamics GP:</b> Has a large pool of add-ons. \r\n</li><li><b>Business Central:</b> Offers a rapidly growing pool of apps. \r\n</li></ul><h3>Power BI Integration \r\n</h3><ul><li><b>Dynamics GP:</b> Includes complexity. \r\n</li><li><b>Business Central:</b> Allows easy integration. \r\n</li></ul><h3>Budgeting \r\n</h3><ul><li><b>Dynamics GP:</b> Set up and import Excel-based budgets, with advanced capabilities through Independent Software Vendors (ISVs). \r\n</li><li><b>Business Central:</b> Allows creating multiple budgets for financials, revisions, analysis, and dimensional reporting. \r\n</li></ul><h3>Payroll \r\n</h3><ul><li>Both support US and Canadian payroll, but Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central provides payroll functionality through apps. \r\n</li></ul><h3>Sales/CRM Integration \r\n</h3><ul><li><b>Dynamics GP:</b> Complex using coding. \r\n</li><li><b>Business Central:</b> Seamless using add-ons. \r\n</li></ul><h3>Financial Reporting \r\n</h3><ul><li><b>Dynamics GP:</b> Uses Management Reporter and Jet Reports, leveraging account schedules and analysis views. \r\n</li><li><b>Business Central:</b> Also supports Jet Reports and offers a dimensional chart of accounts. \r\n</li></ul><h3>AI Capability \r\n</h3><ul><li><b>Dynamics GP:</b> No built-in AI. \r\n</li><li><b>Business Central:</b> Includes built-in generative AI called Copilot. \r\n</li></ul><p>In summary, while both solutions offer similar functionality, Business Central’s cloud-native design, automated updates, and AI capabilities make it a compelling choice for businesses transitioning to the cloud.</p>\r\n<p>However, it’s important to consider your organization’s specific needs, budget, and growth plans when deciding between these two ERP solutions. \r\n</p><p>Let’s summarize the above comparison through this quick table:</p>\r\n\r\n<table><thead>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center; \">Product/Feature</th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center;\">Dynamics GP</th>\r\n    <th style=\"text-align: center;\">Dynamics 365 Business Central</th>\r\n  </tr></thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Hosting</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">On-premises or IaaS (not included).</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Cloud (included). There is also an on-premises option.</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Upgrades/Updates</td>\r\n    <td><div style=\"text-align: center;\">GP 2019 October release and later — free service pack updates.</div><div style=\"text-align: center;\">Earlier GP versions — manual upgrades.</div></td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Free and automated updates.</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Power BI Integration</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Yes</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Yes</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Budgeting</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Setup and import Excel-based budgets. Advanced capabilities through ISVs.</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Create multiple budgets for financials, revisions, analysis, and dimensional reporting.</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Payroll (US &amp; Canada)</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Yes  </td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Yes (Using AppSource)</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Dynamics 365 Sales/<a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 CRM</a> Integration</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Yes (requires significant effort)</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Yes (little effort)</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Financial Reporting</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Management Reporter and Jet Reports.</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Leverages account schedules and analysis views. Can also use Jet Reports.</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Purchase Orders</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Purchase Orders Requisitions, PO creation, separate inventory receipt, and 3-way PO invoice matching.</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">PO creation, separate inventory receipt, and 3-way PO invoice matching. Does not have requisitions.</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">AI Capability</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">No</td>\r\n    <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Built-in generative AI with Copilot.</td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</tbody></table>\r\n\r\n<p>Dynamics GP and Business Central are similar in several aspects, particularly in their core functionalities that cater to business management needs. Here are some of the key similarities: \r\n</p><ul><li><b>SmartLists and List Pages:</b> Both platforms offer features that allow users to add, remove, or move columns around to customize views. In Microsoft Dynamics GP, this is known as SmartLists, while in Business Central, it’s referred to as List Pages. \r\n</li><li><b>Sales Order Processing:</b> Dynamics GP uses Sales Order Processing for entering and printing quotes, orders, invoices, back orders, and returns. Dynamics 365 Business Central has Sales Documents that serve a similar purpose, enabling the progression from a quote to an order and then to an invoice. \r\n</li><li><b>Purchase Order Processing:</b> Both systems allow for the entry and posting of receipts, matching shipments to invoices, and applying landed costs to items. Dynamics GP can accrue based on a shipment regardless of the item type, whereas Dynamics Business Central offers the option to accrue or not to accrue a shipment receipt. \r\n</li><li><b>Fixed Assets:</b> The Fixed Asset module in Dynamics GP allows for data import from the Purchasing module and attachment to fixed assets. Microsoft Dynamics Business Central also supports multiple depreciation books and various depreciation methods, including custom methods. \r\n</li><li><b>Financial Reports:</b> Both Dynamics GP and D365 Business Central come with built-in financial reporting tools. Dynamics GP has a Management Reporter, which uses rows, columns, and trees, while Business Central has a tool called Financial Reports. \r\n</li><li><b>Fiscal Period Control:</b> In Dynamics GP, Fiscal Period Control can be used to close sales and purchasing for a certain month while keeping the General Ledger open. Business Central offers custom accounting periods and Deferral Postings. \r\n</li></ul><p>Additionally, both platforms support functionalities like budgeting, reporting, general ledger account structure segmentation, fixed asset management, e-banking, manufacturing/assembly, inter-company processing, inventory tracking, project accounts/jobs, multiple currencies, and the ability to manage multiple companies. \r\n</p><p>These similarities make both Microsoft Dynamics GP and Business Central robust solutions for businesses looking to streamline their operations and financial management.</p><p>However, it’s important to note that there may be differences in licensing, hosting, extensions, and updates/upgrades between the two.</p>\r\n<h2>Is It Important to Migrate from Dynamics GP to Business Central?</h2>\r\n<p>Again, it depends on your business requirements. Moving to a more advanced system has its own benefits like competitive advantage due to higher operational efficiency, but if you don’t feel there is a need to migrate, you can stay with Dynamics GP.</p>\r\n<p></p><blockquote style=\"text-align: justify;\"><b><i><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\">Get in touch with us to learn more about the benefits of GP to BC migration. Book a Free Consultation Now!</a></i></b></blockquote><p></p>\r\n<p>However, comparatively, Microsoft Dynamics Business Central is a futuristic and comprehensive cloud-based ERP solution that offers a wide range of benefits, including its lower costs, enhanced security &amp; privacy, seamless integration, customization, out-of-the-box dashboard, and more. \r\n</p><p>Besides, Business Central gets an edge due to its AI capabilities which significantly enhance overall productivity. So, if you are looking to improve your productivity, scalability, and optimize the entire operation while embracing digital transformation, then Dynamics 365 Business Central is the ideal solution for you.  \r\n</p><p>The decision is yours whether you want to upgrade to a newer GP version or fully migrate to Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central. \r\n</p><p>To clear your doubts, you can test some Business Central modules for a certain period before taking a leap into a full-fledged migration.</p><p>Read more: <a href=\"/dynamics-gp-to-business-central-migration/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics GP to Business Central Migration</a></p>\r\n<h2>Why Choose Dynamics Square for GP Support or Migration to D365 Business Central?</h2>\r\n<p>At Dynamics Square, we have a pool of experts who specialize in both ERP solutions—Dynamics GP and Business Central. Being in the market for more than a decade now, Dynamics Square is a reputable <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation partner</a>&nbsp;that can successfully conduct both Dynamics GP upgrades and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-gp-to-business-central-migration/\">migration to Business Central</a>.  \r\n</p><p>Feel free to contact us for any assistance related to Dynamics GP or <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-business-central-implementation/\">Business Central Implementation</a>. Call us at <a href=\"tel: +12818990865\" target=\"_blank\"><b>+1 281 899 0865</b></a> or simply write us an email at <b><a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a></b>.</p><h3><b>Also Read:</b></h3><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/10-reasons-to-choose-dynamics-365/\" target=\"_blank\">10 Reasons to Migrate Your Legacy ERP To Dynamics 365</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/xero-to-dynamics-365-business-central-migration/\" target=\"_blank\">Migrating from Xero to Business Central</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/process-to-migrate-dynamics-nav-to-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\">Migrate from Dynamics NAV to Business Central</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/steps-to-migrate-gp-to-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\">Easy Steps to Migrate from Dynamics GP to Business Central</a></p>', 'Dynamics GP Support: Lifecycle Policies, Options and BC Comparison', 'dynamics gp support', 'Learn about Dynamics GP support lifecycle policies, options, and how it compares to Business Central for optimal business performance.', 'dynamics gp support,gp support,great plains support,microsoft support for great plains ,ms dynamics gp support,microsoft dynamics gp,dynamics 365 business central,gp to bc migration,dynamics 365 implementation', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1801744837854839.png', 'Vivek Gururani', 'vivek.gururani@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/dynamics-gp-support/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Dynamics GP Support: Lifecycle Policies, Options and BC Comparison\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Learn about Dynamics GP support lifecycle policies, options, and how it compares to Business Central for optimal business performance.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1801755379096319.Dynamics GP Support.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Vivek Gururani\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Vivek-Gururani/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-06-13\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-06-13\"\r\n}', NULL, '01:49:59pm', '2024-06-13', '12 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 13:49:59'),
(212, 'How to Perform Bank Account Reconciliation in Business Central?', 'bank-account-reconciliation-in-business-central', 'Business central', 'business-central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1803556689670376.Bank Account Reconciliation in Business Central.png', 'Bank reconciliation is a critical but tedious and time-consuming process of comparing a company’s cash balance on its balance sheet with the corresponding amount on its bank statement.', '<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Bank reconciliation is a critical but tedious and time-consuming process of comparing a company’s cash balance on its balance sheet with the corresponding amount on its bank statement. \r\n</p><p>In simple terms, it compares the transactions recorded in a company’s accounting records with those on the bank statement. \r\n</p><p>The goal is to ensure that the company’s records match the bank’s records and identify any discrepancies that may exist. Maintaining the accuracy of financial statements and resolving the missing payments can be quite a challenging and time-consuming process.</p><p>This is where <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> comes into play. The module of bank reconciliation in Dynamics 365 Business Central simplifies this process. \r\n</p><p>Dynamics 365 Business Central is a prominent ERP software that facilitates bank reconciliation with its wide range of features, user-friendly interface, and efficient tools. It efficiently eliminates bookkeeping discrepancies and streamlines the financial management of your company.  \r\n</p><p>In this blog post, we will illustrate how you can set up bank account reconciliation in Business Central and how you can use it to gain maximum benefits. \r\n</p><h2>Why Choose Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central for Bank Reconciliation? \r\n</h2><p>Microsoft Dynamics Business Central offers robust features for bank reconciliation, making it an excellent choice for businesses. Here are some reasons why you might consider using it: \r\n</p><h3>Efficiency and Accuracy \r\n</h3><p>Business Central streamlines the reconciliation process by comparing and matching entries in your bank accounts with transactions from your bank. This ensures accuracy and reduces manual effort. \r\n</p><h3>User-friendly Interface \r\n</h3><p>The platform provides a user-friendly interface for reconciling bank accounts. You can easily navigate to the relevant sections and input the necessary information. \r\n</p><h3>Comprehensive Reconciliation Options \r\n</h3><p>Business Central allows the automatic matching of transactions with bank entries. You can use the “<b>Match Automatically</b>” action to reconcile transactions efficiently. \r\n</p><h3>AI-Powered Reconciliation Assist \r\n</h3><p>As part of the bank reconciliation assist feature, an AI-powered “<b>Reconcile with Copilot</b>” action is available. This assists in matching transactions intelligently. \r\n</p><h3>Manual Matching \r\n</h3><p>If needed, you can manually select lines in both panes (bank statement lines and bank account ledger entries) to link them and then use the “Match Manually” action. \r\n</p><h3>Financial Visibility \r\n</h3><p>Reconciliation ensures that your books align with the statements received from your bank. By posting reconciled balances to your bank accounts in Business Central, you provide accurate financial data for finance managers. \r\n</p><h3>Error Detection \r\n</h3><p>Bank reconciliation helps identify missing payments and bookkeeping errors. It’s a practical way to maintain financial integrity. \r\n</p><h2>How to Perform Bank Reconciliation in Dynamics 365 Business Central? \r\n</h2><p>When it comes to reconciliation, the process of matching is crucial. It entails matching and verifying transactions from your bank statements with bank entries in Business Central. There are three ways to do it: \r\n</p><p><b>1.</b> Match Automatically action \r\n</p><p><b>2.</b> Reconcile with Copilot action \r\n</p><p><b>3.</b> Selecting lines manually in both panes using the Match Manually action</p>\r\n<p></p><blockquote style=\"text-align: justify;\"><b><i><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\">Get in touch with Dynamics Square, your Dynamics 365 implementation partner, for bank reconciliation-related or any assistance. Book a free consultation now!</a></i></b></blockquote><p></p>\r\n<p>Here, we have mentioned the steps for bank reconciliation using Copilot:</p>\r\n<p><b>1. Go to Bank Account Reconciliations \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Select the <b>Bank Account Reconciliations icon</b> or enter “Bank Account Reconciliations” in the search bar. \r\n</li><li>Choose the related link to open the reconciliation window. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>2. Open the Reconcile with Copilot Action \r\n</b></p><ul><li>In the reconciliation window, select the <b>Reconcile with Copilot</b> action. This will open the Reconcile with Copilot window. \r\n</li></ul><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1802480294164027.Reconcile with Copilot Action.png\" style=\"width: 100%;\"><br></p><p><b>Note:&nbsp;Pre-Requisite:</b> Navigate to the \'<b>Copilot &amp; AI capabilities</b>\' page on Business Central and enable the functionality according to the below screenshot. \r\n</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1802480493164005.Copliot and AI Capabilities.webp\" style=\"width: 100%;\"><br></p><p><b>3. Select the Bank Account \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Set the Perform reconciliation for this bank account field to the specific bank account that you want to reconcile. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>4. Import Bank Statement (if needed) \r\n</b></p><ul><li>If the selected bank account isn’t linked to an online bank account, you’ll need to import the bank statement file manually. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>5. Review Suggestions and Matches \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Copilot will automatically provide suggestions for unmatched transactions. \r\n</li><li>Review the suggestions and matches carefully. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>6. Accept, Reject, or Modify Suggestions \r\n</b></p><p>Based on Copilot’s recommendations, you can:  \r\n</p><ul><li>Accept a suggestion if it’s accurate. \r\n</li><li>Reject a suggestion if it’s incorrect. \r\n</li><li>Modify a suggestion if adjustments are needed. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>7. Post the Reconciliation \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Once you’ve reviewed and adjusted the suggestions, post the reconciliation to finalize the process. \r\n</li></ul><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>To see the bank reconciliation process in action, check out this video:</b></p><p style=\"text-align: center; \"><iframe frameborder=\"0\" src=\"//www.youtube.com/embed/jhfwx1K0I7Y\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" class=\"note-video-clip\"></iframe><b><br></b></p><p>Remember to verify the accuracy of the reconciled transactions before posting. Copilot aims to streamline the reconciliation process by providing intelligent suggestions, but human oversight is essential. \r\n</p><h2>How to Get the Print of Bank Reconciliation Details via Business Central? \r\n</h2><p>In case you don’t experience any discrepancy, you may find the need to take a print of your bank reconciliation via Business Central. Interestingly, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Business Central</a> includes print options that can be further easily customized as per your requirements and preferences.   \r\n</p><p>You can follow the below steps to get the print of bank account reconciliation reports: \r\n</p><ul><li>Select the appropriate bank account by navigating to the core interface of Business Central.  \r\n</li><li>Choose “<b>Bank account reconciliation</b>” by clicking on the magnifying glass icon. A result window will pop up to show a link. \r\n</li><li>Then get to the “<b>Test report</b>” option. \r\n</li></ul><p>You will find a menu that will let you print your report as per the different options available there. \r\n</p><p>Then, click on <b>Print</b> to find a comprehensive statement of your bank operations. These operations may include the following options: \r\n</p><ul><li>Printing Details \r\n</li><li>Printing of Checks \r\n</li><li>Printing of pending checks \r\n</li><li>Printing of deposits \r\n</li><li>Printing of current deposits \r\n</li><li>Print settings \r\n</li></ul><h2>How Can Dynamics Square Help You with Bank Account Reconciliation with Business Central? \r\n</h2><p>We, at Dynamics Square, totally understand that bank account reconciliation is a complex process, but you don’t need to worry about it at all. We have the required expertise to make your bank account reconciliation a smooth and successful journey.  \r\n</p><p>Dynamics Square is a well-received <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics partner</a> with a team of more than 150 experts for extensive support and guidance tailored to your specific requirements.  \r\n</p><p>In summary, bank account reconciliation in Business Central is a crucial process that ensures financial accuracy and helps identify discrepancies. By matching bank transactions with ledger entries, businesses can maintain reliable financial records and make informed decisions. \r\n</p><p>Remember, reconciling your bank accounts isn’t just about balancing numbers—it’s about maintaining financial integrity. With Business Central’s features, you can streamline this process and gain confidence in your financial data.</p><p>Dynamics Square is a renowned <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation</a> partner with over a decade of experience in successfully deploying Microsoft solutions. In case any assistance is required, feel free to call us directly at <b><a href=\"tel: +12818990865\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a></b> or simply write an email at <b><a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a></b>.</p>', 'How to Perform Bank Account Reconciliation in Business Central?', 'bank reconciliation', 'Learn how to perform bank account reconciliation in Business Central. Simplify your financial management with step-by-step guidance for accurate reconciliations.', 'reconciliation business,business central bank reconciliation,bank account reconciliation,reconciliation in business,dynamics 365 business central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1803556689670383.Bank Account Reconciliation in Business Central.png', 'Mukesh Jha', 'mukesh.jha@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/bank-account-reconciliation-in-business-central/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"How to Perform Bank Account Reconciliation in Business Central?\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Learn how to perform bank account reconciliation in Business Central. Simplify your financial management with step-by-step guidance for accurate reconciliations.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1803556634349513.Bank Account Reconciliation in Business Central.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Mukesh Jha\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Mukesh-Jha/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-06-21\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-06-21\"\r\n}', NULL, '04:23:42pm', '2024-06-21', '7 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 16:23:42'),
(213, 'Harness the Power of Manufacturing in Business Central', 'manufacturing-in-business-central', 'Business central', 'business-central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1803557404549351.Manufacturing in Business Central.png', 'The COVID-19 pandemic severely crippled the manufacturing industry by disrupting the supply chain dynamics.', '<p>The COVID-19 pandemic severely crippled the manufacturing industry by disrupting the supply chain dynamics. After the pandemic was over, the manufacturing domain felt the need for a powerful ERP solution that could manage the ever-evolving demands of the market. \r\n</p><p>The module of <a href=\"/products/dynamics-365-business-central/manufacturing-management/\" target=\"_blank\">Manufacturing Management in Business Central</a> is tailor-made for SMBs to handle all aspects of the manufacturing process. \r\n</p><p>Today, most businesses are moving to Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central for its cloud benefits and ultimate data security capabilities. Investing in Business Central is tantamount to big ROI as it helps businesses optimize costs and boost overall efficiency. A 2023 <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics-365/products/business-central\" target=\"_blank\">Forrester</a> study revealed some impressive facts about the impact of Business Central. Let’s take a glance at them: \r\n</p><ul><li>Companies with Business Central over 3 years achieved 172% ROI \r\n</li><li>They saw up to 18% productivity boost for finance and operations employees \r\n</li></ul><p>These figures clearly state that Business Central is an impactful ERP that can effectively streamline your entire operations without compromising productivity. \r\n</p><h2>Dynamics 365 Business Central: In a Nutshell \r\n</h2><p><a href=\"/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> is a cloud-based ERP system designed for small and medium-sized businesses. It helps streamline operations, improve financial performance, and boost sales and service. With features like financial management, sales, service, and manufacturing among others, it provides an end-to-end solution for business needs. \r\n</p><h2>What does the Microsoft Business Central Manufacturing Module Include? \r\n</h2><p>Dynamics 365 Business Central offers a comprehensive suite of tools for managing manufacturing operations. This suite of tools can help with process manufacturing. Here are some key features included in the Manufacturing module: \r\n</p><h3>1. Production Orders \r\n</h3><p>Manage the conversion of raw materials into manufactured products using production orders. Raw materials include purchased items and subassemblies. \r\n</p><h3>2. Production Bill of Materials (BOM) \r\n</h3><p>Create a list of all components required to produce a parent item. The BOM includes descriptions, quantities, and units of measure for each component. \r\n</p><h3>3. Routings  \r\n</h3><p>Specify the sequence of steps or operations needed to produce a product. Routings help define how to produce an item. \r\n</p><h3>4. Production Orders  \r\n</h3><p>Use production orders to manage the conversion of raw materials into manufactured products. These orders track consumption and output. \r\n</p><h3>5. Inventory Forecasting \r\n</h3><p>Get insights into inventory levels and forecast upcoming product demand. \r\n</p><h3>6. Supply Planning \r\n</h3><p>Optimize supply chain management for efficient production. \r\n</p><h3>7. Version Management \r\n</h3><p>Track changes and efficiently manage different versions of BOMs and routings. \r\n</p><h3>8. Financial Management \r\n</h3><p>Integrate accounting and finance for overall business management. \r\n</p><h3>9. Machine Management  \r\n</h3><p>It allows you to manage machines and their utilization within the manufacturing process. \r\n</p><h3>10. Production Scheduling  \r\n</h3><p>It helps you schedule production orders efficiently, ensuring optimal resource allocation. \r\n</p><h3>11. Supply Planning \r\n</h3><p>It enables effective planning and management of raw material availability for production. \r\n</p><h3>12. Capacity Planning \r\n</h3><p>It helps balance production capacity with demand, ensuring efficient resource utilization. \r\n</p><h3>13.	Order Management</h3><p>It streamlines order processing and fulfillment for manufactured products. \r\n</p><p>In summary, Dynamics 365 Business Central streamlines manufacturing processes, from planning and scheduling to inventory management and financial tracking. If you’re involved in manufacturing, these tools can help you efficiently manage your business.</p><p><b>Also Read: <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/features-dynamics-365-business-central/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central Features</a></b></p><p> \r\n</p><h2>How Can Business Central Be Beneficial for Mid-sized Businesses? \r\n</h2><p>Dynamics 365 Business Central offers several benefits for mid-sized manufacturing businesses. Let’s explore some of the key advantages: \r\n</p><h3>1. Low Cost of Ownership \r\n</h3><p>Business Central helps control costs by offering a subscription-based model with no large upfront payment. You avoid infrastructure investments, upgrade costs, and maintenance expenses. \r\n</p><h3>2. Single Source of Truth \r\n</h3><p>It creates a unified data repository across departments, ensuring everyone uses the same real-time information for decision-making and financial reporting. \r\n</p><h3>3. Streamlined Financial Management  \r\n</h3><p>It helps you manage finances efficiently, from accounting to budgeting and cash flow analysis. \r\n</p><h3>4. Improved Sales and Customer Service \r\n</h3><p>Business Central helps enhance sales processes, track leads, and provide better customer service. \r\n</p><h3>5. Optimized Supply Chain Management \r\n</h3><p>One of the most critical aspects of a manufacturing business is its supply chain. <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</a> helps manage inventory, procurement, and production, ensuring a streamlined process.</p><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 57, 63); font-size: 1.75rem;\">6. Seamless Integration</span></h3><p>With Business Central, you can easily integrate other Microsoft solutions as your business scales. \r\n</p><h3>7. Advanced Customization and Scalability \r\n</h3><p>Adapt Business Central to your unique needs and expand as your business grows. \r\n</p><h3>8. Security and Compliance Assurance \r\n</h3><p>Business Central offers you peace of mind with its built-in security features and compliance standards. \r\n</p><h3>9. Resource Optimization \r\n</h3><p>The Manufacturing module in Business Central enables efficient allocation of resources (equipment, labor, materials) based on demand forecasts, capacity constraints, and production priorities. This leads to higher efficiency and profitability. \r\n</p><h3>10. Product Quality Improvement \r\n</h3><p>By leveraging Business Central, you can enhance product quality through better visibility and control over manufacturing processes. \r\n</p><h3>11. Decreased Production Time \r\n</h3><p>Real-time insights and streamlined processes help reduce production lead times, improving overall efficiency. \r\n</p><h3>12. Efficient Warehouse Management \r\n</h3><p>Business Central facilitates effective warehouse management, ensuring smooth inventory handling and order fulfillment. \r\n</p><p>So, Dynamics 365 Business Central offers a comprehensive solution that can transform mid-sized businesses by streamlining operations and improving overall efficiency.  \r\n</p><p>Also, it empowers mid-size manufacturing businesses to boost productivity, reduce costs, and make data-driven decisions for sustainable growth. \r\n</p><h2>How Can Dynamics Square Help You Grow Your Manufacturing Business? \r\n</h2><p>Dynamics Square can help you leverage the full potential of Business Central which is designed to manage SMBs. Being a <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\">Microsoft Dynamics Gold partner</a>, Dynamics Square is well-positioned to meet the demands of its clients.  \r\n</p><p>With more than 11 years of experience and a team of seasoned experts, Dynamics Square has a painstaking approach to <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-business-central-implementation/\">Business Central implementation</a>, and it holds an immaculate track record for successfully integrating Business Central for business from various industries.  \r\n</p><p>Our experts have collaborated with a wide range of manufacturing setups in the past and are aware of the requirements of manufacturing businesses. So, what’s stopping you from squeezing out the full capability of Business Central to propel the growth of your business.  \r\n</p><p>In case any assistance is required, feel free to call us directly at <a href=\"tel:+12818990865\" target=\"_blank\"><b>+1 281 899 0865</b></a> or simply write an email at <b><a href=\"mailto: arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a></b>.</p>', 'Harness the Power of Manufacturing in Business Central', 'manufacturing in business central', 'Enhance your manufacturing process in Business Central. Improve efficiency, streamline workflows, and manage production effectively.', 'manufacturing in business central,process manufacturing in dynamics 365 business central,microsoft dynamics 365 manufacturing,dynamics 365 manufacturing,microsoft dynamics business central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1803557404549356.Manufacturing in Business Central.png', 'Awanish Kumar', 'awanish.kumar@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/manufacturing-in-business-central/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Harness the Power of Manufacturing in Business Central\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Enhance your manufacturing process in Business Central. Improve efficiency, streamline workflows, and manage production effectively.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1803557337748590.Manufacturing in Business Central.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Awanish Kumar\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Awanish-Kumar/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-06-25\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-06-25\"\r\n}', NULL, '04:02:24pm', '2024-06-24', '6 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 16:02:24');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(214, 'Everything You Need to Know About Dynamics 365 Customer Insights', 'overview-of-dynamics-365-customer-insights', 'Dynamics 365 Customer Insights', 'dynamics-365-customer-insights', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1803024724292198.jpg', 'Suppose your organization has a huge repository of customer data but all this data is scattered, and you are not able to organize or integrate them to understand your customers’ requirements and preferences in a better way.', '<p>Suppose your organization has a huge repository of customer data but all this data is scattered, and you are not able to organize or integrate them to understand your customers’ requirements and preferences in a better way. And thus, you are not able to cash in on this huge database to attain overall customer satisfaction.  \r\n</p><p>But here comes into play Dynamics 365 Customer Insights to help your organization deliver exceptional customer experiences. So, cutting to the chase, let’s get into the details of Dynamics 365 Customer Insights. \r\n</p><p>But before we get into the details of Dynamics 365 Customer Insights, let’s have a look at the following data: \r\n</p><p>Current customers spend 67% more on average than those who are new to a business. [Business.com] \r\n</p><p>Brands that have mastered customer engagement were 41% more likely to report their conversion rates as “much higher” compared to the previous year. [<a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.twilio.com/en-us/state-of-customer-engagement\" target=\"_blank\">Twilio</a>] \r\n</p><p>81% of surveyed customers state customer experience as a competitive differentiator. [SuperOffice] \r\n</p><h2>What is Dynamics 365 Customer Insights? \r\n</h2><p>A part of the <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 CRM</a> suite, Dynamics 365 Customer Insights is a powerful customer data platform (CDP) and analytics tool provided by Microsoft. It enables businesses to unify data from various sources and derive valuable insights. Here’s what you need to know: \r\n</p><h3>1. Unifying Data \r\n</h3><p>Customer Insights allows you to bring together data from different systems, including operational data, IoT data, and customer interactions. \r\n</p><h3>2. Holistic Customer View \r\n</h3><p>By combining data, you gain a comprehensive view of your customers. This unified view helps you understand their behavior, preferences, and needs. \r\n</p><h3>3. Personalized Experiences \r\n</h3><p>With these insights, you can create personalized customer experiences across sales, marketing, and service teams. \r\n</p><h3>4. Real-Time Insights \r\n</h3><p>The platform provides unmatched time-to-insight, allowing you to make informed decisions based on up-to-date data. \r\n</p><h3>5. Predictive Insights \r\n</h3><p>By connecting data from various transactional, behavioral, and observational sources, you can create a 360-degree customer view. These insights help drive customer-centric experiences and processes. \r\n</p><h3>6. Boosted Productivity \r\n</h3><p>Dynamics 365 Customer Insights streamlines processes, allowing you to engage with customers more effectively and improve overall productivity. \r\n</p><p>Whether you’re looking to enhance customer journeys or boost business productivity, Dynamics 365 Customer Insights is a valuable resource for customer-facing teams.  \r\n</p><p>Remember, it’s a versatile solution that empowers businesses to deliver connected customer experiences across marketing, sales, and service teams. \r\n</p><h2>How many Components does Dynamics 365 Customer Insights Include? \r\n</h2><p>Dynamics 365 Customer Insights consists of two main components: \r\n</p><p><b>1. Customer Insights Data \r\n</b></p><p>This component unites customer data from various sources, creating a unified view of customers. It allows you to build segments, analyze data, and gain insights into customer behavior. \r\n</p><p><b>2. Customer Insights Journeys \r\n</b></p><p>Previously known as <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-marketing/\">Dynamics 365 Marketing</a>, this component can create and manage customer journeys in real-time. It enables personalized, responsive, and connected experiences across sales, marketing, and service teams.</p><h2>What are the Key Features of Customer Insights Data? \r\n</h2><p>Dynamics 365 Customer Insights is a powerful toolkit designed to optimize the customer journey. Here are some key features: \r\n</p><h3>1. 360-Degree Customer View \r\n</h3><p>Gain a comprehensive understanding of your customers by unifying transactional, behavioral, and observational data. This holistic view helps drive customer-centric experiences and processes. \r\n</p><h3>2. Real-Time Data Integration \r\n</h3><p>Unify customer data with operational and IoT data in real-time. This integration provides unmatched time-to-insight, allowing you to make informed decisions. \r\n</p><h3>3. Enrichment with Partner Data \r\n</h3><p>Enhance customer profiles by enriching them with data from Microsoft and partner sources. \r\n</p><h3>4. Journey Orchestration \r\n</h3><p>Create personalized customer journeys across all touchpoints using Dynamics 365 Customer Insights – Journeys. Strengthen relationships and earn loyalty by delivering engaging experiences. \r\n</p><h3>5. Natural Language Exploration \r\n</h3><p>Leverage Copilot in Customer Insights to explore, analyze, and understand customer data using natural language. Discover new insights and simplify content creation. \r\n</p><p>Remember, Dynamics 365 Customer Insights empowers your organization to deliver exceptional customer experiences, whether in sales, marketing, or service teams.</p>\r\n<p></p><blockquote style=\"text-align: justify;\"><b><i><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\">Reach out to your Dynamics 365 experts to unlock the full potential of Dynamics 365 Customer Insights and foster better customer engagement.</a></i></b></blockquote><p></p>\r\n<h2>How to Use Copilot in Dynamics 365 Customer Insights?</h2>\r\n<p>Copilot is an AI-powered assistant that simplifies marketing campaign creation and management within Dynamics 365 Customer Insights. Here is how it can help you:</p><h3>1. Target the Right Customers Using Query Assist \r\n</h3><ul><li>Describe your criteria in your natural language, and Copilot will create segments for your journeys. For instance, you can type “<b>customers who bought shoes in the last month</b>,” and Copilot will translate it into a segment query for you. You can then refine segments by adding or removing conditions. \r\n</li><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/customer-insights/journeys/copilot-overview\" target=\"_blank\">Learn more about targeting customers using query assist</a>. \r\n</li></ul><h3>2. Create Journeys Using AI Assistance \r\n</h3><ul><li>Write your journey goals and objectives in natural language, and Copilot will generate real-time journey suggestions. For example, you can type “<b>create a journey that sends a welcome email to all customers that are part of the loyalty member segment</b>,” and Copilot will provide a journey recommendation. \r\n</li><li>Learn more about creating journeys with Copilot. \r\n</li></ul><p>Remember, Copilot streamlines your tasks, making them more accessible and intuitive.  \r\n</p><h2>How to Get Started with Dynamics 365 Customer Insights? \r\n</h2><p>To get started with Dynamics 365 Customer Insights, follow these steps: \r\n</p><p><b>1. Create an Environment \r\n</b></p><ul><li>If you already have a Dynamics 365 environment, visit the installation instructions. \r\n</li><li>If not, create an environment in the Power Platform Admin Center. As a global tenant admin, you can follow the steps in the Create an environment guide. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>2. Import Data \r\n</b></p><ul><li>For quick insights, upload your data from a single CSV file. This feature is available for customers in the United States. Go to the <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/customer-insights/data/get-started\" target=\"_blank\">single data source setup</a>. \r\n</li><li>To work with data from multiple sources, select “<b>Not now</b>” on the Getting Started screen. Then, choose between Azure Data Lake Storage, Azure Synapse Analytics, Microsoft Dataverse, or Power Query connectors. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>3. Unify Data and Set Up Relationships \r\n</b></p><p>Run the data unification process to combine unified profiles. Specify relationships between ingested tables and use enrichment features. Learn more about unifying data. \r\n</p><p><b>4. Enhance Unified Profiles \r\n</b></p><ul><li>With unified profiles, enrich your data further. Use out-of-the-box models to predict churn likelihood or expected revenues. \r\n</li><li>Explore the expanding library of enrichment providers. Find details in the enhance profiles section. \r\n</li></ul><p>Remember, Customer Insights – Data helps you build a deeper understanding of your customers by connecting data from various sources and creating a 360-degree customer view. \r\n</p><h2>How Can Dynamics Square Help You Unlock the Full Capability of Dynamics 365 Customer Insights? \r\n</h2><p>With over 12 years of experience, Dynamics Square is a reliable <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation partner</a> in the USA.  \r\n</p><p>We have a team of highly experienced consultants who are aware of every know-how of the customer-centric approach in today’s data-driven scenarios.  \r\n</p><p>In case any assistance is required, feel free to call us directly at <b><a href=\"tel: +12818990865\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a></b> or simply write an email to <b><a href=\"mailto: arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a></b>.</p>', 'Everything You Need to Know About Dynamics 365 Customer Insights', 'dynamics 365 customer insights', 'Explore Dynamics 365 Customer Insights, a powerful tool that helps businesses harness data to understand customer behavior and drive personalized experiences.', 'dynamics 365 customer insights connectors,dynamics 365 customer insights data,dynamics 365 customer insights features,microsoft customer insights,d365 customer insights', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1803024724293952.jpg', 'Arish Siddiqui', 'arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/overview-of-dynamics-365-customer-insights/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Everything You Need to Know About Dynamics 365 Customer Insights\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Explore Dynamics 365 Customer Insights, a powerful tool that helps businesses harness data to understand customer behavior and drive personalized experiences.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1803025369645862.Dynamics 365 Customer Insights.jpg\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Arish Siddiqui\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Arish-Siddiqui/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-06-27\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-06-27\"\r\n}', NULL, '04:52:46pm', '2024-06-27', '7 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-08-21 16:52:46'),
(215, 'Dynamics 365 Business Central 2024 Release Wave 1: What’s New?', 'dynamics-365-business-central-2024-wave-1', 'Business central', 'business-central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1803753949866019.jfif', 'The 2024 release wave 1 for Dynamics 365 Business Central brings many exciting updates and enhancements that empower businesses and help them further simplify their operations.', '<p>The 2024 release wave 1 for <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> brings many exciting updates and enhancements that empower businesses and help them further simplify their operations.</p><p>From improved project and service management to seamless integration with Power Platform applications, this release aims to enhance productivity, boost automation, and provide an integrated experience for users. \r\n</p><p>In this blog, we’ll get to know the key features and changes introduced in Business Central for the 2024 release wave 1. Let’s explore the latest innovations in Business Central and how they can help in your business processes. \r\n</p><h2>Microsoft Copilot Studio \r\n</h2><p>Microsoft Copilot Studio is a visual software development tool that uses low-code techniques to create and manage copilots. A Copilot is an AI-driven conversational interface that relies on large language models (LLMs) and supplementary information sources. \r\n</p><p>In the 2024 release wave 1, Microsoft Copilot Studio introduces several enhancements: \r\n</p><p><b>1. Native Capabilities for Extending Microsoft Copilots \r\n</b></p><p>Copilot Studio enables creators to build, evaluate, and deploy custom copilots through a comprehensive authoring canvas. You can create generative AI-enabled conversations, manage responses, and automate workflows within Microsoft 365’s governance controls. \r\n</p><p><b>2. IVR Support in Conjunction with Dynamics Customer Service  \r\n</b></p><p>Improved integration with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-customer-service/\">Dynamics 365 Customer Service</a> for interactive voice response (IVR) requirements. \r\n</p><p><b>3. General Availability for Generative Actions \r\n</b></p><p>You can expect more powerful generative actions to increase your copilots’ capabilities. \r\n</p><p><b>4.	Geo-Expansions to UAE and Germany \r\n</b></p><p>Now Copilot Studio will be available in more regions, and that includes the United Arab Emirates (UAE) and Germany. \r\n</p><p><b>5.	Software Lifecycle Management Capabilities \r\n</b></p><p>You can manage your copilot topics with ease using topic-level import/export and role-based access control (RBAC). \r\n</p><p>For additional information, you can explore the <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-platform/release-plan/2024wave1/microsoft-copilot-studio/\" target=\"_blank\">official documentation</a>. \r\n</p><h2>AI Builder \r\n</h2><p>AI Builder is a feature within <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-platform/\">Microsoft Power Platform</a> that allows you to create and use customized AI models for your business needs. Whether you choose prebuilt models or create your own, AI Builder enables you to simplify processes, get insights, and optimize your workflows. \r\n</p><p>As per the release of wave 1 in 2024, AI Builder focuses on three key areas: \r\n</p><h3>1.	Prompt Builder for GPT Prompts \r\n</h3><p>AI Builder introduces a new interface called Prompt Builder. It allows you to develop, evaluate, and deploy generative AI prompts for large language models (LLMs). These prompts can be used for various situations, including content generation, content classification, insight generation, and information extraction. \r\n</p><h3>2.	Intelligent Document Processing \r\n</h3><p>AI Builder expands its capabilities with intelligent document processing. New features and models assist in streamlining tasks like invoice processing, sentiment analysis, text translation, and optical character recognition (OCR).</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(50, 57, 63); font-size: 1.75rem;\">3.	AI Governance Improvements</span><br></p><p>The 2024 release wave 1 includes improvements in AI governance and administration. This covers areas like capacity management, usage monitoring, application lifecycle management (ALM), access control, and sharing and deploying AI models and prompts.</p>\r\n<p></p><blockquote style=\"text-align: justify;\"><b><i><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/schedule-a-demo/\" target=\"_blank\">Reach out to Dynamics Square to maximize the benefits of Dynamics 365 Business Central. Schedule a free consultation today!</a></i></b></blockquote><p></p>\r\n<h2>Power Automate</h2>\r\n<p>Power Automate is a low-code tool that allows the creation of automated workflows between applications and services. It supports file synchronization, notifications, and data gathering, among other tasks, which can be initiated by specific events or manually. In Dynamics 365,<a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-automate/\"> Power Automate</a> provides a way to automate tasks and custom logic. \r\n</p><p>In the 2024 release wave 1, Microsoft Power Automate is introducing several exciting features including: \r\n</p><p><b>1. Copilot for Power Automate:</b> This brings advanced AI capabilities across cloud flows, desktop flows, and process mining. Users can now use natural language to get optimization opportunities, build automation, and troubleshoot issues more efficiently. \r\n</p><p><b>2. Cloud Flows Enhancements</b></p><ul><li>Create Power Automate flows directly in Excel. \r\n</li><li>Use workflows on calendar events in Teams and Outlook. \r\n</li><li>Monitor performance for cloud and desktop flow activities. \r\n</li><li>View two action properties panes simultaneously. \r\n</li><li>Utilize undo and redo while building cloud flows. \r\n</li><li>Simplified OData editor for actions like Get items and Get files. \r\n</li><li>Manage unpublished solution-aware cloud flows using admin APIs. \r\n</li><li>Connect to other environments from the Microsoft Dataverse connector. \r\n</li><li>Cancel all flow runs for a version of a flow. \r\n</li><li>Receive intelligent license recommendations for admins. \r\n</li><li>Create AI flows in Power Automate. \r\n</li><li>Use Copilot with the French language. \r\n</li><li>Generate descriptions for cloud flows using AI. \r\n</li><li>Use flows with connections from users in Copilot Studio. \r\n</li><li>Push cloud flow execution data into Application Insights.</li></ul><p><b>3. Process Mining Improvements</b></p><ul><li>Get insights through AI. \r\n</li><li>Use out-of-the-box templates for rapid deployment. \r\n</li><li>Integrate with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\">Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</a> and more. \r\n</li></ul><p>Remember that these features are planned to be released from April 2024 through September 2024, so stay tuned for updates!  \r\n</p><h2>Microsoft Dataverse \r\n</h2><p>Microsoft Dataverse, in short, is a cloud-based, low-code data platform that serves as a robust solution for managing and storing business data. It provides a secure, scalable solution that serves as a key data storage facility for companies.  \r\n</p><p>Let’s check out the key takeaways from the Dynamics 365 Business Central 2024 release wave 1: \r\n</p><p><b>1. Overview</b></p><ul><li>Business Central is a business management application designed for small and mid-sized organizations. It streamlines processes related to finances, supply chain, manufacturing, shipping, projects, and services. \r\n</li><li>The release focuses on simplicity, making it easy to implement and configure. \r\n</li><li>Copilot capabilities have been enhanced, allowing users to optimize business processes and complete tasks faster. \r\n</li><li>Microsoft Power Platform integration enables easier workflow setup and more automation scenarios. \r\n</li><li>Global Availability: Business Central is now accessible in over 155 countries and regions. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>2. Specific Enhancements</b></p><ul><li><b>Application:</b> Improved project and service management capabilities. \r\n</li><li><b>Finance:</b> Enhanced consolidation experience. \r\n</li><li><b>Development:</b> Continued investment in productivity tools for developers (GitHub, Visual Studio Code, and AppSource marketplace). \r\n</li><li><b>Governance and Administration:</b> Self-service features for granular access management and audit operations. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>3. Power Platform Integration</b></p><ul><li>The release incorporates features from various Power Platform applications, including <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\">Power BI</a>, Power Apps, Power Pages, Power Automate, Microsoft Copilot Studio, and AI Builder. \r\n</li><li>Microsoft Dataverse and Power Platform functionalities enhance governance and administration. \r\n</li></ul><p>In summary, the 2024 release wave 1 brings improvements across several domains such as finance, development, and governance that empower businesses to be more efficient and adaptable.  \r\n</p><p>With these improvements, businesses can optimize their operations, automate functions, and achieve greater productivity. For more details, you can refer to the <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/release-plan/2024wave1/smb/dynamics365-business-central/planned-features\" target=\"_blank\">official Microsoft Learn article</a>.</p>\r\n<h2>How can Dynamics Square help you leverage the latest features of Business Central?</h2>\r\n<p>Dynamics Square is a renowned <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services\">Dynamics 365 implementation partner</a> with extensive experience of more than a decade. With the pool of expert consultants, we have successfully rendered our services to various organizations across the United States.  \r\n</p><p>Our goal is to maximize the growth of our clients by ensuring a seamless <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-business-central-implementation/\">Business Central implementation</a> process. Should you need any assistance, feel free to call us directly on <a href=\"tel:+12818990865\" target=\"_blank\"><b>+1 281 899 0865</b></a> or simply write an email at <a href=\"mailto: arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\"><b>arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</b></a>.</p><p>Read more: <a href=\"/dynamics-gp-to-business-central-migration/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics GP to Business Central Migration</a></p>', 'Dynamics 365 Business Central 2024 Release Wave 1: What’s New?', 'dynamics 365 business central', 'Unveil the latest upgrades in Dynamics 365 Business Central 2024 Release Wave 1, designed to streamline financial management and operations.', 'dynamics 365 business central ,microsoft dynamics 365 business central ,microsoft dynamics business central,d365 business central,business central implementation', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1803753949867586.jfif', 'Vivek Gururani', 'vivek.gururani@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/dynamics-365-business-central-2024-wave-1/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Dynamics 365 Business Central 2024 Release Wave 1: What’s New?\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Unveil the latest upgrades in Dynamics 365 Business Central 2024 Release Wave 1, designed to streamline financial management and operations.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1804022705453715.dynamics 365 business central.jfif\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Vivek Gururani\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Vivek-Gururani/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-07-08\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-07-08\"\r\n}', NULL, '01:52:22pm', '2024-07-05', '7 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 13:52:22'),
(216, 'Dynamics 365 Telecommunication Accelerator: A Powerful Solution for the Telecom Industry', 'dynamics-365-telecommunication-accelerator', 'Microsoft Dynamics 365', 'microsoft-dynamics-365', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1804115019631428.jpg', 'The Dynamics 365 Telecommunications Accelerator is an extension of Microsoft’s Power Platform and Dynamics 365 that caters particularly to the telecommunications industry.', '<p>The Dynamics 365 Telecommunications Accelerator is an extension of <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\">Microsoft\'s Dynamics 365</a> and Power Platform that caters particularly to the telecommunications industry.  \r\n</p><p>It provides a Common Data Model extension that allows network operators and their partners to develop solutions for effectively managing subscribers, services, and network operations.</p><p>The accelerator allows telecom providers to strategize, monitor, and document regular maintenance operations within their networks which leads to improving network efficiency. \r\n</p><p>According to a report by <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.grandviewresearch.com/press-release/global-digital-transformation-market\" target=\"_blank\">Grand View Research</a>, the global digital transformation market is expected to reach USD 4,617.78 billion by 2030, with a projected CAGR of 27.6% from 2024 to 2030. \r\n</p><p>This implies that every business will be affected by this influence, and that includes the telecommunications industry.  \r\n</p><h2>Telecommunications Data Model Entities \r\n</h2><p>The Dynamics 365 Telecommunications Accelerator extends the Common Data Model to offer an expedited process for developing solutions in the telecommunications industry. Let’s explore the primary entities that this accelerator includes: \r\n</p><p><b>1. Geographic Address:</b> A postal address formatted according to the conventions of a particular worldwide region, such as North America, the United Kingdom, or Australia. The data contains geographical coordinates and locality details that determine the governing legislative authority. \r\n</p><p><b>2. Geographic Location:</b> It provides a description of a specific location by utilizing coordinates, points, lines, or spaces. Attributes include geometry type, accuracy, spatial references, encoded points, metadata, grid numbers, and center. \r\n</p><p><b>3. Geographic Place:</b> It represents either a geographical address or geographical location using geospatial coordinates. It serves as a parent entity for Local Place. \r\n</p><p><b>4. Geographic Point:</b> It contains geospatial coordinates (Latitude, Longitude) forming a point within a Geographic Location. \r\n</p><p><b>5. Geographic Sub Address:</b> This entity provides additional details for Geographic Address, such as private street names, building names, levels, and subunit numbers. \r\n</p><p><b>6. External System:</b> It represents a third-party system, app, or data source from which data is imported or integrated \r\n</p><p>These entities help manage subscribers, services, and network operations solutions. If you’re working in the telecom industry, this accelerator can be a valuable starting point! \r\n</p><p>To obtain additional information, please refer to the official documentation on the Dynamics 365 Telecommunications Accelerator. \r\n</p><h2>Telco Sales Solutions \r\n</h2><p>The Telco Sales solution in Dynamics 365 is developed to cater to the telecommunications industry\'s requirements. It extends the standard <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-sales/\">Dynamics 365 Sales</a> application by incorporating unique features specifically designed for telecom operations. Here are some key aspects of the Telco Sales solution: \r\n</p><p><b>1.	Lead Management \r\n</b></p><p>The solution improves and optimizes lead management with the help of automation. It features built-in service availability checks, resource and network mapping, and address lookups. \r\n</p><p><b>2.	Customized Features \r\n</b></p><ul><li><b>Service Address Tracking:</b> It allows tracking of service addresses. \r\n</li><li><b>Street Address Normalization:</b> It ensures consistent and accurate street address formats. \r\n</li><li><b>Lead Qualification:</b> It streamlines lead qualification processes that are specific to telecom operators. \r\n</li><li><b>Integration with Dynamics 365 Sales:</b> The Telco Sales solution integrates with the out-of-the-box Microsoft Dynamics 365 Sales application which enhances it with telco-specific entities. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>3.	Sample Apps \r\n</b></p><p>The solution includes two model-driven sample apps: \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Place Management:</b> It is a standalone app for address and network management. \r\n</li><li><b>Telco Sales:</b> It is an integrated app that expands Dynamics 365 for Sales with telco entities. \r\n</li></ul><p>In summary, the Telco Sales solution allows telecom operators to efficiently manage leads, track service addresses, and enhance their sales processes with the help of Dynamics 365.</p>\r\n<p></p><blockquote style=\"text-align: justify;\"><b><i><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\">Reach out to Dynamics Square for a comprehensive understanding of Dynamics 365 Telecommunications Accelerator and maximize your growth with a data-driven approach. Our team of experts will analyze your business requirements and help you make an informed decision.</a></i></b></blockquote><p></p>\r\n<h2>Plant Maintenance Solution</h2>\r\n<p>The Plant Maintenance solution in the Dynamics 365 Telecommunications Accelerator lets plant operators easily plan repeated maintenance activities. This optimization of operations helps operators respond to audit and liability questions by tracking maintenance activities. \r\n</p><p>The accelerator expands the Common Data Model by introducing entities related to telecommunications, like Geographic Address, Geographic Location, and Geographic Place. These additions are crucial for handling tasks related to physical locations, service territories, network assets, and addresses of customers. \r\n</p><p>In Dynamics 365 Telecommunications, the Plant Maintenance module includes several key features: \r\n</p><p><b>1.	Maintenance Types \r\n</b></p><p>You can define different maintenance types, such as warranty, contractual, and compliance. These types can be aligned with specific maintenance plans. \r\n</p><p><b>2.	Network Resources \r\n</b></p><p>Operators can define various types of network resources, including optical network units, antennas, and switches. This helps track where these resources are deployed, which accounts they serve, and their manufacturers. \r\n</p><p><b>3.	Maintenance Scheduling \r\n</b></p><p>The newest version of the telecommunications accelerator lets plant operators quickly plan recurring maintenance tasks. \r\n</p><p><b>4.	Repeatable Tasks \r\n</b></p><p>The most recent version lets operators quickly plan repeating maintenance activities. Along with simplifying processes, this facilitates audit and liability tracking. \r\n</p><p><b>5.	Extended Data Model \r\n</b></p><p>The accelerator consists of an extended data model with entities and attributes specific to telcos. Operators can tie services and products and deploy network resources to geocoded locations, such as buildings or campuses. \r\n</p><p>Remember, Dynamics 365 Telecommunications guarantees network dependability and manages maintenance tasks to avoid downtime. \r\n</p><h2>How can Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations be Helpful for the Telecommunications Industry? \r\n</h2><p>Although <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance-operations/\">Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations</a> (D365 F&amp;O) isn\'t directly integrated into the Telecommunication Accelerator, it can be a great <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics partner</a> tool for telecom companies using the accelerator. Here\'s why: \r\n</p><ul><li>D365 F&amp;O provides a comprehensive Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) solution, which can manage various back-office functions like inventory, financials, and project management. Telecom businesses can leverage this to manage their network infrastructure resources, track inventory of equipment (routers, cables, etc.), and streamline financial processes related to network operations.</li></ul><ul><li>Integration potential: Although not directly built-in, there\'s potential for custom integration between D365 Finance &amp; Operations and the Telecommunication Accelerator. This could allow data exchange between the two platforms, for example, feeding network resource data from the accelerator into F&amp;O for better inventory management. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>Here\'s an example: \r\n</b></p><p>Imagine a situation where a technician uses the Telecommunication Accelerator app to schedule maintenance on a cell tower. This action could trigger an automatic update in D365 F&amp;O, reserving the necessary spare parts required for the repair.</p><p>This integration would improve operational efficiency and ensure technicians have the right resources on hand. \r\n</p><p>Overall, Dynamics 365 F&amp;O offers a broader enterprise resource planning solution that can complement the Telecommunication Accelerator\'s focus on subscriber management, service management, and network operations.</p><p>By potentially integrating the two, telecom businesses can gain a more holistic view of their operations and achieve greater efficiency. \r\n</p><h2>How can Dynamics 365 Telecommunication Accelerator Impact Telecommunications Field Service? \r\n</h2><p>The Dynamics 365 Telecommunications Accelerator is designed to enhance telecommunication field service by facilitating better management of services, products, and network resources. Here’s how it impacts the industry: \r\n</p><p><b>1.	Place Management \r\n</b></p><p>The accelerator introduces a new Place entity, combining geographic address, location, and site information. This allows operators to relate services and resources to specific physical locations (e.g., buildings, campuses) within their service areas. \r\n</p><p><b>2.	Telco Sales \r\n</b></p><p>By integrating with the <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-platform/\">Power Platform</a>, the accelerator helps telcos streamline sales processes, improving visibility and workforce management. \r\n</p><p><b>3.	Customization and Innovation \r\n</b></p><p>Telco-specific use cases can be customized and automated, driving innovation for network operators, internet service providers, and mobile carriers. \r\n</p><p>To get started, you can install the <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/industry/accelerators/telecommunications-configure\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Telecommunications Accelerator from GitHub</a> and follow the steps to enable Azure Maps, embedded canvas apps, and Power BI reports.</p><p>Ready to elevate your telecommunications field service? Explore the seamless integration of <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a> with the Telecommunication Accelerator for enhanced service management and customer engagement.</p><p> \r\n</p><h3>How can you Make an Impact and Transform Your Business with Dynamics Square? \r\n</h3><p>Dynamics Square is a trustworthy name as a <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/microsoft-dynamics-365-partner/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 implementation partner</a> in the USA. It has been in the industry for more than a decade with many smooth and successful implementations. \r\n</p><p>Dynamics Square can assess your business goals and help you determine your requirements with a team of experts. Our consultants can ensure the smooth implementation and configuration of Dynamics 365 Telecommunications Accelerator.  \r\n</p><p>Dynamics Square also provides the required training and assistance to boost the adoption rate. Please do not hesitate to contact us at <b><a href=\"tel: +12818990865\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a></b> or via email at <b><a href=\"mailto: arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a></b> if you require any assistance.</p>', 'Dynamics 365 Telecommunication Accelerator: A Powerful Solution for the Telecom Industry', 'dynamics 365 telecommunication accelerator', 'Enhance your telecom business with Dynamics 365 Telecommunication Accelerator, a robust solution for improved customer service and operational efficiency.', 'dynamics 365 for telecommunication,microsoft dynamics 365 ,d365 for telecommunication accelerator,dynamics erp', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1804115019634331.jpg', 'Mukesh Jha', 'mukesh.jha@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/dynamics-365-telecommunication-accelerator/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Dynamics 365 Telecommunication Accelerator: A Powerful Solution for the Telecom Industry\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Enhance your telecom business with Dynamics 365 Telecommunication Accelerator, a robust solution for improved customer service and operational efficiency.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1804115271606504.dynamics 365 telecommunications accelerator.jpg\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Mukesh Jha\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Mukesh-Jha/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-07-09\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-07-09\"\r\n}', NULL, '04:42:51pm', '2024-07-09', '8 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-08-21 16:42:51');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(218, 'Business Central for Retail Industry: Build a Resilient Business', 'business-central-for-retail-industry', 'Business central', 'business-central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1804659513350020.jpg', 'Businesses, small or medium, get a big push ahead if they choose the right software for their operations. One such application is Microsoft Dynamics Business Central which works well for many businesses because of its cloud-based accessibility.', '<p>Businesses, small or medium, get a big push ahead if they choose the right software for their operations. One such application is <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> which works well for many businesses because of its cloud-based accessibility. \r\n</p><p>When we talk about Business Central in the context of the retail industry, the application comes with functionalities for customer service, operations, and finance among others, all through an easy-to-use interface.</p><p>Besides, it can be customized to accommodate the unique needs of a growing business. Also, it can help transform the way a business operates and even prepare it for the future. \r\n</p><p>According to a <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.technavio.com/report/digital-transformation-market-in-retail-industry-analysis\" target=\"_blank\">Technavio</a> report, the market size for digital transformation in retail is expected to grow by USD 253.84 billion, with a CAGR of 17.15%, from 2023 to 2028. \r\n</p><p>Keep reading to explore the capabilities of Business Central for the retail industry. \r\n</p><h2><b>Business Central: A Vital Business Solution for the Retail Industry \r\n</b></h2><p>Dynamics 365 Business Central is a must for retailers as it helps make things run smoothly, improve customers\' experiences, and offer strong security measures to protect your sensitive data. To understand how it is a vital solution for the retail industry, let’s check out the following pointers: \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Consolidated Data Management \r\n</b></h3><p>Retailers deal with data from multiple sources, like sales, inventory, and customer interactions. Business Central unifies and centralizes this data to offer one source of truth for all teams so they can use the data to optimize operations and make smart decisions. \r\n</p><h3><b>2. Enhanced Customer Experience \r\n</b></h3><p>Business Central lets retailers customize customer interactions with the <a href=\"https://datascientest.com/en/the-evolution-of-data-insights-data-science-vs-business-intelligence-in-the-big-data-era\" target=\"_blank\">help of data insights</a>. When you have quick access to customers’ preferences and purchasing history, you can use the data to tailor marketing efforts and improve overall customer gratification. \r\n</p><h3><b>3. Streamlined Operations \r\n</b></h3><p>Business Central streamlines retail operations, such as inventory management and financial reporting, by automating key activities. Especially for retailers coordinating across multiple locations or working alongside <a href=\"https://willwork.com/retail-installation/\" target=\"_blank\">retail installation companies</a> that require accurate data flow for store setups, rollouts, and ongoing operational alignment.</p><h3><b>4. Scalability \r\n</b></h3><p>As your retail business gets bigger, Business Central grows too. Its modular design lets you add or drop features as needed which not only offers great flexibility and control but also the ability to adapt to changing demands. \r\n</p><h3><b>5. Robust Security \r\n</b></h3><p>Business Central comes with top-notch safety features to keep the system protected against data breaches and safeguard confidential information. \r\n</p><h2><b>What is the Process for Implementing Business Central in Your Retail Business? \r\n</b></h2><p>To implement Dynamics 365 Business Central&nbsp;into your retail business, there are certain steps that need to be followed. You’ll first have to choose a <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\">Microsoft Dynamics Partner</a> with a proven track record of successful implementation, especially in your business domain. Once that is done, follow the below-mentioned steps: \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Evaluate Your Needs \r\n</b></h3><p>Start by assessing your existing systems. Pinpoint the areas of difficulty or dissatisfaction that are posing operational challenges. It is important to ensure the Business Central implementation improves your processes and brings benefits and innovation to your business. \r\n</p><h3><b>2. Establish Clear Objectives \r\n</b></h3><p>Set up precise goals for the outcomes you intend to achieve with Business Central. This is important for guiding the implementation process. For instance, you need to be clear if it involves enhancing the accuracy of inventory, improving customer service, or gaining better financial visibility. \r\n</p><h3><b>3. Plan and Prepare \r\n</b></h3><p>When you prepare well in advance, it increases the probability of successful <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-business-central-implementation/\">Business Central implementation</a>. Make sure your partner establishes specific timeframes, assigns resources, and develops a detailed plan for carrying out the project. \r\n</p><h3><b>4. Data Migration \r\n</b></h3><p>This process is crucial and needs to be performed with the utmost caution so that data doesn’t lose its integrity or consistency. \r\n</p><h3><b>5. Configure and Customize \r\n</b></h3><p>Get Business Central customized as per your unique retail requirements. Personalize processes, reports, and dashboards. \r\n</p><h3><b>6. Test Thoroughly \r\n</b></h3><p>You need to get the system thoroughly checked to detect any potential problems or gaps. Get them addressed before going live. \r\n</p><h3><b>7. Go Live and Support \r\n</b></h3><p>Make the system live and receive ongoing support from your partner.</p>\r\n<p></p><blockquote style=\"text-align: justify;\"><b><i><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\">Reach out to Dynamics Square to successfully implement Business Central for your retail business. Avail yourself of the maximum benefits of Business Central with Dynamics Square.</a></i></b></blockquote><p></p>\r\n<h2><b>How Does Business Central Resolve the Challenges of the Retail Industry?</b></h2>\r\n<p>Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central (BC) addresses several complex challenges faced by the retail industry. Here’s how it helps: \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Inventory Management \r\n</b></h3><p>BC provides real-time stock monitoring, automated reordering, and predictive insights to maintain optimal inventory levels without overstocking or incurring extra costs. \r\n</p><h3><b>2. Sales Forecasting \r\n</b></h3><p>Robust analytics and reporting tools allow retailers to evaluate past sales data and predict <a href=\"https://www.askattest.com/blog/articles/retail-trends\" target=\"_blank\">upcoming retail trends</a> which assists in making effective sales strategies.</p><h3><b>3. Customer Relationship Management (CRM) \r\n</b></h3><p>Integrated CRM with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 CRM</a> features help track customer interactions, segment the customer base, and personalize marketing efforts which enhances overall customer experience.</p><h3><b>4. Supply Chain Management \r\n</b></h3><p>BC streamlines operations from supplier to customer with automated ordering, transit tracking, and supplier performance analytics using <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</a>.</p><p>Besides these challenges, retailers can connect Business Central with Shopify, which is an all-encompassing e-commerce platform. This integration simplifies operations, strengthens the supply chain, and boosts revenue. Here’s how BC can be integrated with Shopify: \r\n</p><h2><b>What is the Process for Integrating Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central with Shopify? \r\n</b></h2><p>When you <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/shopify-integration-with-business-central/\">integrate Dynamics 365 Business Central with Shopify</a>, it simplifies your business processes and provides a unified view of your operations. Here are the steps to get started: \r\n</p><p><b>1. Prerequisites \r\n</b></p><ul><li><b>For Shopify:</b> You’ll need a Shopify account and an online store. If you’re new to Shopify, learn how to create an account and configure settings. \r\n</li><li><b>For Business Central:</b> Ensure that the Shopify Connector app is installed. It’s preinstalled for new sign-ups and trials. Make sure users have the necessary permissions (covered by the Shopify – Admin (SHPFY – ADMIN) permission set). \r\n</li></ul><p><b>2. Install the Dynamics 365 Business Central App \r\n</b></p><ul><li>If you’re using an existing Business Central instance, this step is optional. \r\n</li><li>Find the Dynamics 365 Business Central app on the Shopify AppStore. \r\n</li><li>Sign in to your Shopify account and select your online shop. \r\n</li><li>Review privacy and permissions, then install the app. You’ll find it in the Apps section on the Shopify admin page. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>3. Connect Business Central to Shopify \r\n</b></p><ul><li>In Business Central, choose the Shopify Shop icon and create a new connection. \r\n</li><li>Enter a code (e.g., “Furniture” or “Coffee”) and the Shopify URL (format: https://{shop}.myshopify.com/). \r\n</li><li>Turn on the Enabled toggle and accept the terms. \r\n</li><li>Sign in to your Shopify account if prompted. \r\n</li><li>Review privacy terms and permissions, then choose Install App. \r\n</li></ul><p>That’s it! You’ll now have a seamless integration between Business Central and Shopify. For more details, check out the official guide. \r\n</p><h2><b>Why Consider Dynamics 365 Business Central App for Shopify? \r\n</b></h2><p>There are several reasons to consider the Dynamics 365 Business Central app for Shopify: \r\n</p><p><b>1. Two-way Synchronization \r\n</b></p><p>The app synchronizes inventory levels, customer data, orders, and fulfillment information between Shopify and Business Central. This eliminates manual data entry and reduces the risk of errors. \r\n</p><p><b>2. Centralized Management \r\n</b></p><p>Manage all your sales channels (including Shopify) from within Business Central. This provides a holistic view of your business and simplifies operations. \r\n</p><p><b>3. Improved Inventory Control \r\n</b></p><ul><li><b>Real-time Inventory Visibility:  \r\n</b></li></ul><p>Always have accurate stock levels across your Shopify store and Business Central. This helps avoid overselling and ensures you have enough inventory to fulfill orders. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Better Demand Forecasting:  \r\n</b></li></ul><p>Business Central\'s analytics can help predict future sales trends, which allows you to optimize your inventory management and avoid stockouts. \r\n</p><p><b>4. Enhanced Customer Experience \r\n</b></p><ul><li><b>Accurate Order Fulfillment:  \r\n</b></li></ul><p>With synchronized data, you can fulfill orders efficiently and provide accurate delivery estimates to your customers. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Improved Customer Management:  \r\n</b></li></ul><p>Consolidate customer information from Shopify into Business Central which allows for better customer service and targeted marketing campaigns. \r\n</p><p>Overall, the Dynamics 365 Business Central app for Shopify is a powerful tool for businesses that aim to streamline operations, improve inventory control, and enhance the customer experience. If you\'re a growing Shopify business and seeking a more robust back-end system, this integration is worth exploring. \r\n</p><h2><b>How Can Dynamics Square Help with Business Central for the Retail Industry? \r\n</b></h2><p>Dynamics Square is a leading <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\">Dynamics 365 implementation</a> partner in the United States. We have rendered services to some top organizations, including the retail industry. If you are looking forward to maximizing your growth with Microsoft Dynamics 365 solutions, then look no further than us.</p><p>In conclusion, Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central is revolutionizing the <a href=\"https://www.azilen.com/blog/custom-retail-software-development/\" target=\"_blank\">retail software development</a> industry by providing a comprehensive ERP solution that streamlines operations, enhances decision-making, and improves customer experiences.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;As retail businesses continue to face operational challenges in a competitive marketplace, adopting these solutions is crucial for future success.</p><p>Whether it’s handling inventory, forecasting sales, building customer relationships, or ensuring an efficient supply chain, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Business Central</a> offers tailored features to empower retail businesses.</p><p>So, if you’re running a retail business, you can consider implementing Business Central to bring efficiency and growth into your business.</p><p>If you need help, you can email us at <a href=\"mailto: arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\"><b>arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</b></a> or call us at <a href=\"tel: +12818990865\" target=\"_blank\"><b>+1 281 899 0865</b></a>.</p>', 'Business Central for Retail Industry: Build a Resilient Business', 'business central for retail industry', 'Strengthen your retail business with Business Central, offering tools to enhance resilience, streamline operations, and improve customer experience.', 'business central for retail industry,retail for dynamics 365 business central,retail for business central,microsoft dynamics 365 business central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1804659513352383.jpg', 'Arish Siddiqui', 'arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/business-central-for-retail-industry/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Business Central for Retail Industry: Build a Resilient Business\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Strengthen your retail business with Business Central, offering tools to enhance resilience, streamline operations, and improve customer experience.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1804657067698801.Business Central for Retail Industry.jpg\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Arish Siddiqui\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Arish-Siddiqui/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-07-15\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-07-15\"\r\n}', '[]', '08:24:10pm', '2024-07-15', '10 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2026-02-10 03:24:10'),
(219, 'Streamline Your Discrete Manufacturing with Business Central', 'discrete-manufacturing-with-business-central', 'Business central', 'business-central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1804824263880589.png', 'Discrete manufacturing is the process of producing individual items. These items include cars, furniture, toys, cell phones, and aircraft.', '<p>Discrete manufacturing is the process of producing individual items. These items include cars, furniture, toys, cell phones, and aircraft. Unlike process manufacturing, where goods are undifferentiated, such as oil, natural gas, and salt, discrete manufacturing produces clearly identified completed goods.</p><p>One can count and monitor these objects as separate entities. Usually, the procedure results in the final product by means of several parts, components, and sub-assembly techniques.</p><p>Through real-time insights, consistent departmental collaboration, and the unification of essential operations, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> optimizes discrete manufacturing processes. \r\n</p><p>Manufacturing businesses heavily rely on ERPs like Business Central to streamline their operations.  \r\n</p><p>The global market for industrial software, in terms of revenue, is likely to reach $46.6 billion by 2029 from its current valuation of $21.5 billion in 2024, at a CAGR of 16.7%. (<b>Source:</b> <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.marketsandmarkets.com/Market-Reports/industrial-software-market-27555137.html\" target=\"_blank\">Markets and Markets</a>) \r\n</p><h2><b>Key Details of Discrete Manufacturing in Business Central \r\n</b></h2><p>The powerful all-in-one <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft ERP Solution</a>, D365 Business Central, can help to simplify discrete and process manufacturing operations. Here are some key functions in Business Central that can help with discrete manufacturing: \r\n</p><h3><b>1.	Cost Tracking</b></h3><p>Business Central lets you monitor expenses throughout your manufacturing process. Whether you bring raw materials from different purchase orders or keep an inventory of semi-manufactured components, you will have consolidated data to confidently price your goods and guarantee the intended margin. \r\n</p><h3><b>2.	Bill of Materials (BOM)</b></h3><p>Specifying the components required for every product, you can create and oversee BOMs. BOMs support accurate manufacturing and effective resource allocation. \r\n</p><h3><b>3.	Routing and Operations</b></h3><p>Specify manufacturing routes involving labor, machines, and work centers as well as processes. This guarantees a seamless flow from raw resources to completed products. \r\n</p><h3><b>4.	Resource Management</b></h3><p>Whether tools, labor, or machinery, distribute resources effectively. Business Central facilitates the optimum utilization of resources. \r\n</p><h3><b>5.	Production Order Statuses</b></h3><p>Track manufacturing orders from development through completion. At any point in time, you will know the status of every order. \r\n</p><p>It is important to bear in mind that Business Central offers the necessary tools and features to power up your business operations and drive growth in your organization. \r\n</p><h2><b>What Challenges does Discrete Manufacturing Face and How Can Business Central Address Them? \r\n</b></h2><p>Discrete manufacturing faces several challenges and addressing them effectively is crucial for operational excellence. Here are some common challenges: \r\n</p><p>Achieving operational excellence, the ultimate manufacturing goal depends on successfully resolving various issues that discrete manufacturing presents. Here are some common operational challenges: \r\n</p><h3><b>1.	Complex Product Processes</b></h3><p>Intricate production techniques used in discrete manufacturing can cause operations to lag. By combining several elements, from order processing to the shop floor, Business Central simplifies processes, hence enhancing transparency and automation. \r\n</p><h3><b>2.	Supply Chain Disruptions</b></h3><p>Optimized <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\">supply chain management</a> is absolutely vital. By giving real-time access to inventory, demand, and supplier performance, Business Central aids in better decision-making. \r\n</p><h3><b>3.	Cost Control</b></h3><p>One never-ending challenge is keeping quality while controlling expenses. To maximize expenditure, Business Central provides budgeting, cost tracking, and financial management solutions. \r\n</p><h3><b>4.	Regulatory Compliance</b></h3><p>One must adhere to industry standards and rules. Business Central ensures this by automating compliance checks and reporting. \r\n</p><h3><b>5.	Technology Adoption</b></h3><p>Connecting modern solutions with legacy systems can be difficult. However, Business Central helps bridge this gap by allowing us to link modern processes with technologies already in use. \r\n</p><h3><b>6.	Inventory Management</b></h3><p>Effective <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/inventory-management/\">inventory management</a> is essential as it helps us avoid situations like overstocking or stockouts. Business Central lets you properly manage inventory with features like inventory control, demand forecasting, and reorder point management. \r\n</p><h3><b>7.	Operations Management</b></h3><p>With tools including serialization, lot tracking, production routing, and work centers, Business Central provides means to track and monitor production. This helps to maximize operations, increase efficiency, and maintain seamless running of manufacturing lines. \r\n</p><h3><b>8.	Reporting and KPI Tracking</b></h3><p>To understand your production performance, Business Central provides dashboards and reporting tools. Business Central allows you to easily track key performance indicators (KPIs) including on-time delivery rates, quality control measures, and production output. \r\n</p><h3><b>9. Enhanced Planning and Scheduling</b></h3><p>Features for sophisticated planning and scheduling are available in Business Central. It can be applied for demand forecasting, capacity planning, and manufacturing order scheduling. This enhances general control over the manufacturing process and visibility. \r\n</p><p>Business Central solves these problems mostly by means of flawless integration, automation, and strong features catered to specific requirements in discrete production.</p><h2><b style=\"color: rgb(50, 57, 63); font-size: 2rem;\">Implementation Process for Dynamics 365 Business Central</b></h2><p>Usually, implementing Business Central consists of these steps: \r\n</p><ol><li><b>Assessment and Planning:</b> A consultant will evaluate your present manufacturing techniques and point out areas that need improvement. Then, given your specific requirements and budget, they will create a strategy for implementing Business Central. \r\n</li><li><b>Data Migration:</b> Your current data related to products, inventories, customer records, and so on will be moved to Business Central. \r\n</li><li><b>Configuration and Customization:</b> Business Central can be tailored to fit your requirements via configuration and customization. This can call for tailoring dashboards, reporting, and processes. \r\n</li><li><b>Training and Go-Live:</b> Your staff will receive training to be able to adapt to Business Central. The system will be launched once the training is finished, so you can start using it for your manufacturing activities. \r\n</li></ol><p><b>Additional Tips: \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Think about collaborating with a <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-business-central-implementation/\">Dynamics 365 Business Central implementation</a> partner with a background in working with discrete manufacturers. \r\n</li><li>Clearly state your company goals and objectives before beginning the implementation process. \r\n</li><li>Engage key stakeholders from several departments all through the implementation phase. \r\n</li></ul><p>Effective implementation of Microsoft Dynamics Business Central will help discrete manufacturers to improve efficiency, productivity, and overall business performance.</p>\r\n<p></p><blockquote style=\"text-align: justify;\"><b><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"\">Reach out to Dynamics Square for smooth and successful implementation of Dynamics 365 Business Central and avail yourself of the maximum benefits. Schedule a free call now!</a></b></blockquote><p></p>\r\n<h2>How Can Dynamics Square Help You Streamline Your Manufacturing Operations?</h2>\r\n<p>Dynamics Square, your trusted <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics partner</a>, with over 12 years of experience and 150+ expert consultants, can help you simplify your complicated manufacturing business and create room for new opportunities. Including tailored system customizations, we have the tools and infrastructure required to implement a successful and efficient Dynamics 365 deployment. \r\n</p><p>Our manufacturing experts can offer a sustainable solution for a better future since they grasp the current situation of the manufacturing sector. Irrespective of the complexity of your production requirements, we are just a phone call away. \r\n</p><p>Should you need any assistance, please contact us at <b><a href=\"mailto: arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a></b> or give us a call at <a href=\"tel: +12818990865\" target=\"_blank\"><b>+1 281 899 0865</b></a>.</p><h3><b>Also Read:&nbsp;</b></h3><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/sustainability-with-dynamics-365-for-manufacturing/\" target=\"_blank\">How Supply Chain Can Bring Sustainability With Dynamics 365 for Manufacturing</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/warehouse-management-in-dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\" target=\"_blank\">Warehouse Management in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</a></p><p><a href=\"/dynamics-gp-to-business-central-migration/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics GP to Business Central Migration</a></p>', 'Streamline Your Discrete Manufacturing with Business Central', 'discrete manufacturing with business central', 'Enhance your discrete manufacturing processes with Business Central, streamlining production, improving efficiency, and boosting overall productivity.', 'business central discrete manufacturing,discrete manufacturing in dynamics 365 business central,dynamics 365 business central,business central implementation', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1804824263882756.png', 'Vivek Gururani', 'vivek.gururani@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/discrete-manufacturing-with-business-central/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Streamline Your Discrete Manufacturing with Business Central\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Enhance your discrete manufacturing processes with Business Central, streamlining production, improving efficiency, and boosting overall productivity.\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1804824190845851.Discrete Manufacturing with Business Central.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Person\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Vivek Gururani\",\r\n    \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/author/Vivek-Gururani/\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"Dynamics Square USA\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/img/dynamics_square-logo.svg\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"2024-07-17\",\r\n  \"dateModified\": \"2024-07-17\"\r\n}', NULL, '01:51:35pm', '2024-07-17', '7 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 13:51:35'),
(220, 'Maximize Technician Productivity with Dynamics 365 Field Service', 'maximize-technician-productivity-with-dynamics-365-field-service', 'Microsoft Cloud', 'microsoft-cloud', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1805374396969412.png', 'Enhance operational efficiency with Microsoft Dynamics 365 Field Service. Optimize technician productivity and service delivery seamlessly.', '<p>Designed to empower field service experts by simplifying the whole process, Microsoft Dynamics 365 Field Service is an end-to-end solution. It can streamline practically all facets of Field Service, </p><p>including predictive maintenance, remote support, auto-scheduling and technician dispatching, and real-time tracking.</p><p>\r\n \r\n</p><p>Let\'s start with some fascinating facts about the Microsoft Dynamics 365 Field Service before we get into the specifics: (Source: <a href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics-365/blog/business-leader/2024/02/05/forrester-study-finds-346-roi-when-modernizing-service-operations-with-dynamics-365-field-service/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft</a>)</p><p>\r\n \r\n</p><ul><li>346% ROI over 3 years\r\n \r\n</li><li>14% boost in Field worker productivity\r\n \r\n</li><li>Less than 6 months to pay back.\r\n \r\n</li></ul><p>Now, let\'s investigate all there is to know about Dynamics 365 Field Service. It is like having a reliable friend for your service operations.\r\n \r\n</p><h2><b>Dynamics 365 Field Service: At a Glance\r\n \r\n</b></h2><h3><b>What is Dynamics 365 Field Service?\r\n \r\n</b></h3><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-field-service/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Field Service</a> is an application that helps organizations deliver onsite service to customer locations. It’s like having a digital key tool for your field technicians.\r\n \r\n</li><li>How does it work? Well, it combines workflow automation, scheduling algorithms, and mobility to set up your mobile workers for success when they’re out there fixing things at customer sites.  \r\n \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>Why Should You Care?\r\n \r\n</b></h3><p>Because it’s all about efficiency! With Dynamics 365 Field Service, you can:</p><p>  \r\n \r\n</p><p></p><ul></ul><p></p><ul><li><b>Improve first-time fix rates:</b> Get it right the first time, every time, which simply implies the amount of time (in percentage) a service issue was resolved on the first visit to a customer.\r\n \r\n</li><li><b>Complete more service calls: </b>Your technicians will be like speedy superheroes.\r\n \r\n</li><li><b>Manage follow-up work:</b> And maybe even upsell or cross-sell while you’re at it.\r\n \r\n</li><li><b>Reduce travel time and wear and tear: </b>Less wear on the service vehicles while using Resource Schedule Optimization (RSO) to cut down on overall travel time.  \r\n \r\n</li><li><b>Organize and track customer issues: </b>No more lost sticky notes as the work orders feature can do all that.\r\n \r\n</li><li><b>Keep customers informed:</b> Check accurate arrival times and updates.  \r\n \r\n</li><li><b>Schedule visits conveniently: </b>Because nobody likes a surprise visit from the repair person.\r\n \r\n</li><li><b>Prevent equipment downtime: </b>Through smart preventive maintenance.\r\n \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>Who’s Using It?\r\n \r\n</b></h3><p>Let’s peek at some scenarios:</p><p></p><p></p><ul></ul><p></p><ul><li><b>Manufacturing: </b>Companies that sell and maintain equipment, such as medical devices or industrial machinery.\r\n \r\n</li><li><b>Utilities: </b>Fiber optic cable companies dispatching tech to fix outages.\r\n \r\n</li><li><b>Healthcare: </b>In-home healthcare providers scheduling and dispatching care workers.\r\n \r\n</li><li><b>Equipment maintenance:</b> Facilities managers handling heating and cooling repairs.\r\n \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>Key Capabilities:\r\n \r\n</b></h3><ul><li><b>Work Orders:</b> Define what needs fixing, especially at customer locations.\r\n \r\n</li><li><b>Scheduling and Dispatch:</b> Manage resources, visualize appointments, and optimize schedules.\r\n \r\n</li><li><b>Communication Tools:</b> Keep everyone in the loop—agents, techs, and customers.\r\n \r\n</li><li><b>Mobile App: </b>Guides techs through changes and service tasks.\r\n \r\n</li><li><b>Asset Management: </b>Keep track of equipment and service history.\r\n \r\n</li><li><b>Preventive Maintenance: </b>Auto-generate recurring maintenance appointments.\r\n \r\n</li><li><b>Inventory and Billing: </b>Manage stock, invoices, and returns.\r\n \r\n</li></ul><p>So, whether you’re fixing copiers, fiber optics, or lousy network signals, Dynamics 365 Field Service has your back!</p><p>\r\n \r\n</p><blockquote style=\"\"><b><i><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\">Reach out to Dynamics Square to squeeze out the full potential of Dynamics 365 Field Service. Refer to Dynamics Square White paper for a complete understanding of the role of AI in the growth of businesses.</a></i></b></blockquote><h2><b>What are the Advantages of Dynamics 365 Field Service?\r\n \r\n</b></h2><p>Dynamics 365 Field Service is similar to having a dependable companion for your service operations. Now let\'s dissect their advantages:\r\n \r\n</p><h3><b>1.    Improved Customer Service:</b></h3><p>Imagine a customer reports a problem; your field technician arrives like a service superhero. They have all the pertinent information in their hands with Dynamics 365 Field Service—that is, past service history, and equipment specifics. Thus, the outcome, issues are fixed more quickly, and consumers believe they are receiving VIP service.</p><p>\r\n \r\n</p><h3><b>2.         Optimized Employee Time:  \r\n \r\n</b></h3><p>Time is money, hence optimized employee time is like money. Dynamics 365 Field Service, then, lets your field techs maximize every minute. They get even predictive maintenance notifications, optimized routes, and real-time instructions. They are like navigational giants; no more meandering about lost or scratching their heads. This underscores the critical <a href=\"https://myhours.com/articles/the-importance-of-time-management\" target=\"_blank\">importance of time management</a> in field operations, ensuring that each task is executed efficiently and promptly.</p><p>\r\n \r\n</p><h3><b>3.         Reduced Costs:  \r\n \r\n</b></h3><p>Imagine a world in which documentation does not proliferate like rabbits, therefore lowering costs. Dynamics 365 Field Service digitizes everything, including large forms, work orders, and inventory control. Reduced manual data entering results in fewer mistakes, less annoyance, and less expense.</p><p>\r\n \r\n</p><h3><b>4.         Data Integration Magic:  \r\n \r\n</b></h3><p>Dynamics 365 runs nicely with others. It functions as the social butterfly of corporate applications. Your field service app exchanges data for greater coordination and cooperation when it interacts with other Dynamics 365 apps, such as Sales or Customer Service. This will let you have a 360-degree perspective of your customer.</p><p>\r\n \r\n</p><h3><b>5.         Service Level Agreement (SLA) Mastery:  \r\n \r\n</b></h3><p>SLAs are like making legal promises to your clients. Dynamics 365 Field Service tracks them as a conscientious librarian would. It guarantees that your techs maintain the general balance of the service sector, fix issues inside specified windows, and meet response times.</p><p>\r\n \r\n</p><p>So, there you have it—a glimpse into the magical world of Dynamics 365 Field Service. Just contact Dynamics Square if you want more specifics or wish to go deeper.</p><p>\r\n \r\n</p><h2><b>How does Copilot in Dynamics 365 Field Service work?\r\n \r\n</b></h2><p>Copilot in Dynamics 365 Field Service is an AI-powered assistant designed to enhance productivity and efficiency for frontline workers, dispatchers, and service managers. Here are some key features and functionalities:</p><p>\r\n \r\n</p><h3><b>1.         Summarizing Information:  \r\n \r\n</b></h3><p>Copilot allows customers to rapidly catch up on recent changes and updates by summarizing specifics about service accounts and work orders.<br></p><p>\r\n \r\n</p><h3><b>2.         Natural Language Interaction:  \r\n \r\n</b></h3><p>Users can interact with Copilot using natural language, either through text or voice commands. This makes it easy to get information or perform tasks without needing to navigate through multiple screens.<br></p><p></p><h3><b>3.              Work Order Management:  \r\n \r\n</b></h3><p>The Copilot assists in creating, viewing, and <a href=\"https://www.fieldpromax.com/blog/how-to-create-and-manage-work-orders\" target=\"_blank\">managing work orders</a>. It can automatically fill in essential details, making the process faster and reducing the chances of errors.<br></p><p></p><h3><b>4.       Scheduling Recommendations:  \r\n \r\n</b></h3><p>The AI provides scheduling recommendations, helping to optimize the allocation of resources and ensuring that tasks are completed efficiently.<br></p><p></p><h3><b>5.              Mobile Integration:  \r\n \r\n</b></h3><p>In the Field Service mobile app, Copilot can help summarize and update work orders based on user input, enhancing the mobile experience for technicians on the go.<br></p><p></p><h3><b>6. Predefined Prompts:  \r\n \r\n</b></h3><p>Copilot comes with predefined prompts to help users get the most out of its capabilities, such as listing work orders for a specific service account or identifying who is booked for a particular work order.<br></p><p>\r\n \r\n</p><p>Overall, Copilot aims to streamline operations, reduce administrative burdens, and improve the overall efficiency of field service operations.</p><p>\r\n \r\n</p><p>Ultimately, companies looking to improve their <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://www.fieldpromax.com/blog/common-challenges-in-field-service-management/\" target=\"_blank\">field service management</a> will find great value in Microsoft Dynamics 365 Field Service. Through IoT integration, it provides effective work order </p><p>administration, enhanced resource optimization, and proactive maintenance addressing the many needs of modern companies.</p><p>\r\n \r\n</p><h2><b>How can Dynamics Square help you with Dynamics 365 Field Service?</b></h2><p>\r\n \r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics Square</a> is a well-known Microsoft Dynamics 365 implementation partner in the USA. Our team of more than 150 seasoned consultants guarantees seamless implementation of Dynamics </p><p>365 Field Service to empower your field executives and improve your field service experience.</p><p>\r\n \r\n</p><p>Our professionals can evaluate your business needs and situation and propose the best feasible solution to get the most advantages. </p><p>Should you want assistance, kindly get in touch via phone at <a href=\"tel:+1\" 281=\"\" 899=\"\" 0865=\"\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a> or by email at <a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a>.&nbsp;</p><p><b>Also Read:</b></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/role-of-microsoft-cloud-for-manufacturing/\" target=\"_blank\">The Role of Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing in Empowering Businesses</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/manufacturing-in-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"background-color: white; font-family: sans-serif; font-weight: 400;\">Harness the Power of Manufacturing in Business Central</a><br></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/warehouse-management-in-dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\" target=\"_blank\">Warehouse Management in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/dynamics-365-telecommunication-accelerator/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Telecommunication Accelerator: A Powerful Solution for the Telecom Industry</a></p>', 'Maximize Technician Productivity with Dynamics 365 Field Service', 'Dynamics 365 Field Service', 'Enhance operational efficiency with Microsoft Dynamics 365 Field Service. Optimize technician productivity and service delivery seamlessly.', 'Microsoft Dynamics 365,Dynamics 365 Field Service', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1805374396973704.png', 'Samar Malik', 'samar.malik@dynamicssquare.com', '{\r\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n  \"@type\": \"BlogPosting\",\r\n  \"mainEntityOfPage\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n    \"@id\": \"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/maximize-technician-productivity-with-dynamics-365-field-service/\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"headline\": \"Maximize Technician Productivity with Dynamics 365 Field Service\",\r\n  \"image\": \"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1805374396969412.png\",  \r\n  \"author\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"\",\r\n    \"name\": \"\"\r\n  },  \r\n  \"publisher\": {\r\n    \"@type\": \"Organization\",\r\n    \"name\": \"\",\r\n    \"logo\": {\r\n      \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n      \"url\": \"\"\r\n    }\r\n  },\r\n  \"datePublished\": \"\"\r\n}', '[]', '02:35:29pm', '2024-07-23', '8 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2026-02-20 21:35:29');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(221, 'Ensure Quality and Compliance with Business Central Process Manufacturing', 'quality-and-compliance-with-business-central-process-manufacturing', 'Business central', 'business-central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1805441900349289.png', 'Achieve superior quality and regulatory compliance in Business Central Process Manufacturing with our expert solutions and innovative approaches.', '<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The world of process manufacturing, where raw materials become necessary goods, such as chemicals, energy, and food comprise, comprises one of the complex calculations, exact measurements, and stringent rules.<br></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">The key elements of success in process manufacturing are maintaining constant quality, reducing waste, and guaranteeing environmental responsibility. Managing these complexities, nevertheless, can be full of challenges. Business Central in Dynamics 365 suite is an efficacious ERP (Enterprise Resource Planning) that enables effective operation management for companies. \r\n</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">According to the Forrester Study, businesses achieved 172% ROI with Business Central over 3 years. (Source: <a href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-in/dynamics-365/products/business-central\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft</a>) \r\n</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">When it comes to process manufacturing, Business Central offers essential features to streamline and optimize various aspects of the production process. \r\n</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Regarding process manufacturing, Business Central provides the necessary tools to maximize several facets of the production process and simplify several elements of it. \r\n</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">This post covers information on how process manufacturers can find <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> to be a game-changer. We shall discuss the challenges this sector faces, including adhering to always changing rules and ensuring product consistency during significant volume runs.  \r\n</p><h2 style=\"text-align: left;\">How Can Business Central Strengthen Process Manufacturing? \r\n</h2><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Dynamics 365 Business Central offers a strong toolkit to handle various challenges. Discover how this ERP can streamline processes by:  \r\n</p><h3><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Simplifying Regulatory Compliance</li></ul></h3><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Automated tasks and current documentation help you stay on top of complicated regulations and say goodbye to manual processes. \r\n</p><h3><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Ensuring Consistent Quality</li></ul></h3><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Using real-time manufacturing data and integrating quality control systems will help you find and fix disparities before they affect your bottom line. \r\n</p><h3><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Optimizing Production For Efficiency</li></ul></h3><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Reducing waste by means of smart inventory control and efficient manufacturing techniques helps to maximize production. \r\n</p><h3><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Promoting Sustainable Practices</li></ul></h3><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Business Central offers critical insights into the use of raw materials and energy consumption to encourage sustainable practices. \r\n</p><h3><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Enhancing Supply Chain Transparency</li></ul></h3><p style=\"text-align: left;\">It involves using real-time data on supplier performance and inventory levels which offers a complete view of your supply chain with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</a>.</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Whether you are a seasoned process manufacturer or just starting out, Dynamics 365 Business Central can enable you to take control of your operations to help you achieve higher productivity and guarantee the quality and sustainability of your goods.  \r\n</p><blockquote style=\"text-align: left;\"><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>Reach out to Dynamics Square to configure the process manufacturing in Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management.  </i></b></a></blockquote><h3></h3><h2 style=\"text-align: left;\">Challenges of Process Manufacturing \r\n</h2><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Process manufacturing, where raw resources are turned into products like food goods, fuels, or chemicals, poses several challenges. Some key challenges are listed below, and Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central helps to solve them: \r\n</p><h3><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Strict Regulations</li></ul></h3><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Process manufacturers generally deal with food items or hazardous materials, so they must strictly follow complicated and always-changing rules. \r\n</p><h3><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Product Consistency</li></ul></h3><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Maintaining constant quality throughout extended production runs is absolutely vital, however, variables in equipment or temperature fluctuations might lead to deviations. \r\n</p><h3><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Waste Reduction</li></ul></h3><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Reducing wastage of raw materials during manufacturing increases efficiency and lowers expenses. Still, mistakes in measurements, leaks, or spills could result in waste. \r\n</p><h3><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Environmental Impact</li></ul></h3><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Owing to energy consumption and possible waste in process manufacturing, industry can have a major environmental impact. Sustainable practices are vital. \r\n</p><h3><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Supply Chain Transparency</li></ul></h3><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Quality control and potential recalls depend on knowing the source and flow of materials across the intricate supply chain. \r\n</p><h2 style=\"text-align: left;\">How Dynamics 365 Business Central Can Help</h2><h3><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Regulation Compliance</li></ul></h3><p style=\"text-align: left;\">The solution can handle regulatory needs, including leveraging <a href=\"https://www.scrut.io/soc-2/beginners-guide\" target=\"_blank\">SOC 2 compliance automation software</a> to ensure everything is up-to-date, track documentation for audits, and streamline processes.</p><h3><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Quality Control</li></ul></h3><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Dynamics 365 Business Central can connect with systems of quality control. Real-time production data monitoring helps you to see possible discrepancies and act fast to correct them. \r\n</p><h3><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Production Efficiency</li></ul></h3><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Inventory control and production efficiency are important areas the platform can optimize. This allows you to minimize waste by ensuring you have the correct quantity of supplies on hand. \r\n</p><h3><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Sustainability Features</li></ul></h3><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Dynamics 365 allows you to monitor raw material use and energy consumption. This information lets manufacturers spot areas that need to be worked upon and apply environmentally friendly methods. \r\n</p><h3><ul><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Supply Chain Visibility</li></ul></h3><p style=\"text-align: left;\">You get supply chain visibility via real-time data on inventory levels and supplier performance. This transparency all across the supply chain facilitates traceability and possible recall control. \r\n</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">With the help of Dynamics 365 Business Central, process manufacturers can have a centralized platform to simplify operations, guarantee quality control, navigate regulations, and reach higher sustainability. \r\n</p><h2 style=\"text-align: left;\">How to Configure Process Manufacturing in Dynamics 365 Business Central Management? \r\n</h2><p style=\"text-align: left;\">To configure process manufacturing in Microsoft Business Central, you need to set up production resources, bills of material, routings, machine centers, and work centers. Here\'s a broad summary of the actions you might take: \r\n</p><ol><li style=\"text-align: left;\">On the <b>Manufacturing Setup</b> page, set the manufacturing features which includes choosing planning parameters and specifying shop floor work hours. \r\n</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>Create Shop Calendars</b> to define a normal working week, including starting and finishing times for every workday and corresponding work shifts. \r\n</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>Set Up Work Centers and Machine Centers</b> to arrange production resource requirements and set of fixed values. \r\n</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>Create Routings</b> to arrange manufacturing activities in the necessary sequence and assign them to work or machine centers with suitable work times. \r\n</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>Create Production BOMs</b> to organize production components or subassemblies under a produced parent item. \r\n</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Work With <b>Manufacturing Batch Units of Measure</b> to make sure, that when things are stocked in one unit of measure but manufactured in another, the right component quantity is always accessible. \r\n</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>Work With Production Families</b> to define families of production items with similar manufacturing processes. \r\n</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">Use standard tasks to <b>Set Up Standard Routing Lines</b>, therefore streamlining the routing creation. \r\n</li><li style=\"text-align: left;\">If necessary, <b>Subcontract Manufacturing</b> will help to depict the operations of subcontracted manufacturers. \r\n</li></ol><p style=\"text-align: left;\">For detailed instructions and further information, you can refer to the comprehensive guides provided by Microsoft on configuring production processes in Business Central. These resources will walk you through each step of the setup process and provide additional context and details for each task. Remember to also check the system requirements and ensure that you have the necessary permissions to make these configurations. \r\n</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">You can refer to the thorough recommendations by Microsoft on <a href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics365/business-central/production-configure-production-processes\" target=\"_blank\">configuring production processes</a> in Business Central. These resources will help you through every stage of the setup process and offer further background and specifics for every task.  \r\n</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Besides, you can also get in touch with a recognized <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-business-central-implementation/\" target=\"_blank\">Business Central implementation</a> to get assistance. \r\n</p><h2 style=\"text-align: left;\">How Can Dynamics Square Help You with the Configuration? \r\n</h2><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Dynamics Square, a reputed <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 implementation</a> partner in the USA, has all the resources to ensure great success in your Business Central deployment. We have a group of experts who understand the nuances of Process Manufacturing inside out. Through careful analysis of your company\'s needs, they will guarantee you the maximum benefits. \r\n</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\">Having more than 12 years of experience, we’ve been instrumental in helping our clients achieve unprecedented growth and revenue. Should you run across any issues, please do not hesitate to email the address <a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a> or call <a href=\"tel:+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a>.&nbsp;</p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>Also Read:</b></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/manufacturing-in-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\">Harness the Power of Manufacturing in Business Central</a></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/what-is-manufacturing-erp-software/\" target=\"_blank\">What Is Manufacturing ERP Software? Benefits, Features, And Importance</a></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/manufacturers-choosing-dynamics-365-to-solve-business-challenges/\" target=\"_blank\">Why are Manufacturers Choosing Dynamics 365 to Solve Business Challenges?</a></p><p style=\"text-align: left;\"><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/role-of-microsoft-cloud-for-manufacturing/\" target=\"_blank\">The Role of Microsoft Cloud for Manufacturing in Empowering Businesses</a></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Quality & Compliance in Business Central Process Manufacturing', 'Business Central Process Manufacturing', 'Achieve superior quality and regulatory compliance in Business Central Process Manufacturing with our expert solutions and innovative approaches.', 'Business Central Process Manufacturing,Business Central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1805441900352875.png', 'Samar Malik', 'samar.malik@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '09:19:26pm', '2024-07-24', '9 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-04-14 21:19:26'),
(222, 'Step-By-Step Guide to Process Vendor Payments in Dynamics 365 Business Central', 'process-vendor-payments-in-dynamics-365-business-central', 'Business central', 'business-central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1806619276389275.how to process vendor payments in dynamics 365 business central.png', 'Learn how to efficiently process vendor payments in Dynamics 365 Business Central with our step-by-step guide, ensuring accuracy and streamlining your financial operations.', '<p>Maintaining a good rapport with vendors and guaranteeing seamless business operations depends on effective vendor payment processing. Strong features within <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> help companies manage their finances and vendor interactions, thereby simplifying this procedure.<br></p><p>This article lists how to efficiently handle vendor payments in Dynamics 365 Business Central to help you optimize your payment processes. \r\n</p><h2><b>Dynamics 365 Business Central: A Quick Brief \r\n</b></h2><p>Designed as a complete business management solution, Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central helps small and medium-sized companies simplify their operations, sales, customer support, and finances. With its all-encompassing features, Business Central Dynamics 365 helps companies to more effectively handle their financial operations, including payments to vendors. \r\n</p><h2><b>Processing Vendor Payments: The Step-by-Step Process \r\n</b></h2><p>Processing vendor payments is a crucial step in the Accounts Payable module after posting vendor invoices. Dynamics 365 Business Central offers a dedicated interface to streamline this process. This guide will walk you through the steps to process Accounts Payable (AP) payments. \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Go to Payment Journals \r\n</b></h3><p>Once the Business Central home screen loads up, select “<b>Cash Management</b>” and go to “<b>Payment Journals</b>.” If the Cash Management option is not available, use the search function to find “<b>Payment Journals</b>.” \r\n</p><h3><b>2. Select or Create Batches \r\n</b></h3><p>In the Payment Journals window, you can select an existing batch or create a new one. Batches help to group and manage different kinds of entries, facilitating multiple users to post vendor payments without overlapping transactions. Business Central provides three default batches: \r\n</p><ul><li><b>CASH \r\n</b></li><li><b>GENERAL \r\n</b></li><li><b>PMT REG \r\n</b></li></ul><p>To edit a batch, click “<b>Edit List</b>” to change the name, description, and default Bal. Account Type/No. To create a new batch, click “<b>New</b>” and fill in a new name and description. \r\n</p><p><b>Note: \r\n</b></p><p>To save time, default the “<b>Bal. Account Type</b>,” “<b>Bal. Account No</b>.,” and “<b>No. Series</b>” columns in the Payment Journal. This allows these fields to auto-populate for each transaction in the batch. \r\n</p><h3><b>3. Apply Payment Entries \r\n</b></h3><p>After setting up or selecting a batch, open it by clicking on the batch name. You can either manually enter your payment transactions or let Business Central automatically generate them. \r\n</p><p><b>Option 1: Manual Method \r\n</b></p><p>Ensure the following fields are correctly filled: \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Posting Date:</b> Work date or today’s date \r\n</li><li><b>Document Number: </b>Auto-generated by BC or manually entered \r\n</li><li><b>Document Type:</b> Payment \r\n</li><li><b>Account Type:</b> Vendor \r\n</li><li><b>Account Number:</b> Vendor number \r\n</li><li><b>Currency Code: </b>Leave empty if in local currency \r\n</li></ul><p>After entering the necessary information, click “<b>Home</b>” and then “<b>Apply Entries</b>” to apply your payment entry against posted invoices.  \r\n</p><p>Select the invoices by clicking the “<b>Applies-to ID</b>” column, then click “<b>Set Applies to ID.</b>” You can select multiple rows by clicking the three dots next to the first column, choosing “<b>Select More</b>,” specifying the desired rows, and then clicking “<b>Set Applies to ID</b>.” \r\n</p><p>Once the changes are applied, the amount column will populate automatically, and a checkmark in the Applied column will confirm that your payment entry has been applied. \r\n</p><p><b>Preview and Post \r\n</b></p><p>Preview the entry before posting to ensure the GL entry is correct. If everything looks good, post the entry and print the report if required. \r\n</p><p><b>Option 2: Automatic Method \r\n</b></p><p>For multiple payment entries, the manual option can be time-consuming. Use Business Central\'s auto option to save time. Click on “<b>Prepare</b>” and then “<b>Suggest Vendor Payments</b>.” \r\n</p><p><b>Suggest Vendor Payments Options: \r\n</b></p><ul><li><b>Last Payment Date:</b> Select the date on or after the due date of your posted invoices. \r\n</li><li><b>Summarize Per Vendor: </b>Consolidates multiple invoices for the same vendor into a single line. \r\n</li><li><b>Posting Date:</b> Enter the desired posting date for transactions. \r\n</li><li><b>New Doc. No. Per Line:</b> Activates a new document number for each line. \r\n</li><li><b>Account Type:</b> Set to “<b>Bank Account</b>” for vendor payments. \r\n</li><li><b>Account No.:</b> Select the appropriate bank account. \r\n</li><li><b>Bank Payment Type: </b>Choose between check or electronic payment. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>Note: \r\n</b></p><p>You can filter vendor entries based on various parameters, such as “<b>Vendor No</b>.” or “<b>Payment Method Code</b>,” to streamline recording payment entries. For advanced filtering options, seek assistance. \r\n</p><p>After entering the required information, click OK. Business Central will automatically generate payment lines and apply invoices against them, eliminating manual work. \r\n</p><p><b>Review and Post \r\n</b></p><p>Review the applied invoices for each payment line to ensure accuracy. Click “<b>Applies to Doc. No</b>.” and then the three dots or select the payment line and click “<b>Applied Entries</b>” to check the applied invoices. \r\n</p><p><b>Partial Payments: \r\n</b></p><p>To pay only a specific part of an invoice, use the “<b>Amount to Apply</b>” column to specify the desired amount. \r\n</p><p>Once reviewed, preview and post the entry. \r\n</p><p>By following these steps, you can efficiently process vendor payments in Dynamics 365 Business Central, ensuring accuracy and saving time. \r\n</p><blockquote><b><i>Contact <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics Square</a>, a leading Microsoft Gold partner in the USA, for the implementation of Business Central. Schedule a free consultation now! \r\n</i></b></blockquote><h2><b>Vendor Payment Processing Best Practices \r\n</b></h2><p>Following are the recommended practices that will help Dynamics 365 Business Central to guarantee accurate and effective vendor payment processing: \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Regular Reconciliation: \r\n</b></h3><ul><li>To guarantee accuracy, routinely match vendor records with your own. \r\n</li><li>Automate this process using the \"<b>Vendor Reconciliation</b>\" feature within Dynamics 365 Business Central. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>2. Automating Payment Workflows: \r\n</b></h3><ul><li>Using workflow automation will help to simplify the approval and payment process. \r\n</li><li>Create hierarchies for approvals and notifications to guarantee prompt payments and approvals. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>3. Monitoring Cash Flow: \r\n</b></h3><ul><li>Use the \"<b>Cash Flow Forecast</b>\" feature to track your cash flow and ensure you have enough for vendor payments. \r\n</li><li>Plan your payments to keep good cash flow and stay clear of liquidity problems. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>4. Vendor Communication: \r\n</b></h3><ul><li>Maintain open and clear communication with vendors on payment terms, due dates, and any disparities. \r\n</li><li>Track and control vendor interactions in Dynamics 365 Business Central with its \"<b>Vendor Management</b>\" features. \r\n</li></ul><h2><b>Integrating Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance \r\n</b></h2><p>Integrating Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance with Business Central Dynamics 365 can improve your operations of vendor payments even further. Advanced financial management tools offered by Dynamics 365 Finance, including budgeting, financial reporting, and consolidation, can help supplement vendor payment capabilities in Business Central. \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Enhanced Financial Reporting: \r\n</b></h3><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Finance</a> has strong financial reporting features that give a closer understanding of your financial situation. \r\n</li><li>View your financial situation holistically by combining these reports with Business Central\'s vendor payment data. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>2. Advanced Budgeting and Planning: \r\n</b></h3><ul><li>Using Dynamics 365 Finance\'s advanced budgeting and planning capabilities will help you to precisely estimate vendor payment needs. \r\n</li><li>Ensure financial stability by aligning your budget with vendor payment plans. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>3. Consolidation and Compliance: \r\n</b></h3><ul><li>MS Dynamics 365 Finance supports financial consolidation and adherence to many accounting standards. \r\n</li><li>Integrate this functionality with Business Central to ensure compliance in your vendor payment processes. \r\n</li></ul><p>In summary, maintaining solid supplier relationships and guaranteeing seamless business operations depend on the effective handling of vendor payments. From configuring payment systems to handling electronic payments and vendor credits, Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central offers thorough tools to simplify this process. Following best practices and using the interface with Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance can help companies maximize their vendor payment processes and improve financial management.  \r\n</p><p>By using these techniques, you will maximize Dynamics 365 Business Central, and guarantee correct and timely vendor payments, which as a result, improves your whole financial procedures. Dynamics 365 Business Central can help your business expand and satisfy your needs regardless of the volume of vendor transactions you handle—small or large. \r\n</p><h2><b>Choose Dynamics Square for Business Central Implementation \r\n</b></h2><p>With more than 12 years of experience, Dynamics Square is a leading <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 implementation partner</a> in the USA. We have a team of expert consultants who can minutely analyze your business requirements to suggest the most suitable D365 solution. Not only this, but we can also tailor these solutions to accommodate your unique business requirements. \r\n</p><p>If you want any assistance, please call us at <a href=\"tel:+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a> or send an email to <a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a>.&nbsp;</p><p><b>Also Read:</b></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/dynamics-365-finance-an-overview/\" target=\"_blank\">What is Dynamics 365 Finance? An Overview</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/quality-and-compliance-with-business-central-process-manufacturing/\" target=\"_blank\">Ensure Quality and Compliance with Business Central Process Manufacturing</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/discrete-manufacturing-with-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\">Streamline Your Discrete Manufacturing with Business Central</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/business-central-for-retail-industry/\" target=\"_blank\">Business Central for Retail Industry: Build a Resilient Business</a></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Vendor Payments in Dynamics 365 Business Central (2026)', 'vendor payments in Dynamics 365 Business Central', 'Discover how to process vendor payments in Dynamics 365 Business Central with our guide for efficient and accurate financial management.', 'Dynamics 365 Business Central,vendor payments,microsoft dynamics partner', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1806619276389279.how to process vendor payments in dynamics 365 business central.png', 'Samar Malik', 'samar.malik@dynamicssquare.com', '.', '[]', '02:03:14pm', '2024-08-06', '9 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2026-01-02 21:03:14'),
(223, 'A Guide to Reporting Tools for Dynamics 365 Business Central', 'reporting-tools-for-dynamics-365-business-central', 'Business central', 'business-central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1806710830980322.png', 'Explore top reporting tools for Dynamics 365 Business Central. Learn how to enhance your data analysis, gain insights, and improve decision-making effectively.', '<p>In the data-driven world of today, successful business management depends on the capability to derive useful insights from enormous volumes of data. <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central</a> (D365 BC), in this regard, is a useful ERP that combines several business operations into one, cohesive system with strong reporting capabilities.<br></p><p>This blog looks at the several reporting tools available with Dynamics 365 Business Central and demonstrates how companies may use them to make smart decisions and spur growth. \r\n</p><h2><b>Reporting Needs in Business Central \r\n</b></h2><p>Every business produces a lot of data every day covering operational transactions, sales performance, financial transactions, and more. Several key aspects like strategic planning, operational effectiveness, and performance monitoring depend on meaningful reporting from this unprocessed data. \r\n</p><h2><b>Types of Reports Businesses Need \r\n</b></h2><ol><li><b>Financial Reports: </b>These include balance sheets, income statements, cash flow statements, and financial ratios. \r\n</li><li><b>Operational Reports:</b> These comprise production schedules, inventory levels, and supply chain analytics. \r\n</li><li><b>Sales Reports:</b> These reports include sales forecasts, customer orders, and revenue analysis. \r\n</li><li><b>Human Resources Reports:</b> These consist of employee performance, payroll summaries, and workforce planning. \r\n</li></ol><h2><b>Key Benefits of Effective Reporting \r\n</b></h2><ol><li><b>Accuracy: </b>Guarantees that the data for decision-making is reliable. \r\n</li><li><b>Timeliness:</b> Provides up-to-date information needed for quick decisions. \r\n</li><li><b>Customization: </b>Tailors reports to specific business needs and benchmarks. \r\n</li><li><b>Accessibility: </b>Helps stakeholders to get information readily. \r\n</li></ol><h2><b>Integrated Reporting Tools within Dynamics 365 Business Central \r\n</b></h2><p>Dynamics 365 Business Central comes integrated with a suite of various reporting capabilities meant to satisfy a range of business needs. \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Business Central Reports \r\n</b></h3><p>D365 BC provides a broad spectrum of basic reports covering fundamental areas of business operations. Direct access to these reports lets users change layouts, add fields, and apply filters to satisfy particular requirements straight within the system. \r\n</p><p><b>Options for Customization: \r\n</b></p><ul><li><b>Report Layout Designer:</b> Personalize reports without requiring great technical knowledge. \r\n</li><li><b>Filters and Parameters: </b>Use filters and parameters to narrow down data to concentrate on particular dates, departments, or criteria. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>2. Financial Reporting \r\n</b></h3><p>Formerly known as account schedules, financial reporting in D365 BC is a powerful tool for financial reporting and analysis. They let customers create tailored financial statements and do thorough financial data analysis. \r\n</p><p><b>Purpose and Use Cases: \r\n</b></p><ul><li><b>Custom Financial Statements: </b>Create custom balance sheets, income statements, and cash flow reports. \r\n</li><li><b>Comparative Analysis: </b>Examine actuals in line with budgets or past performance. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>3. Analysis Views \r\n</b></h3><p>Analysis Views in D365 BC offer a versatile means to examine data across several angles without compromising the central data structure. \r\n</p><p><b>Purpose and Use Cases: \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Ad hoc querying and multi-dimensional analysis. \r\n</li><li>Monitoring performance across several departments or time periods. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>Advanced Reporting Tools \r\n</b></h3><p>For organizations looking for more sophisticated reporting capabilities, Dynamics 365 Business Central connects easily with various advanced tools. \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Power BI Integration \r\n</b></h3><p>Microsoft\'s business analytics tool, Power BI, offers interactive visuals and business intelligence features. Combining D365 BC with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\" target=\"_blank\">Power BI software</a> opens advanced data visualization and more thorough analytical insights. \r\n</p><h3><b>Advantages of Incorporating Power BI: \r\n</b></h3><ul><li><b>Interactive Dashboards: </b>Create dynamic, interactive dashboards that use real-time data to provide insights. \r\n</li><li><b>Advanced Analytics: </b>Utilize predictive analytics and machine learning to project trends and discover patterns.  \r\n</li><li><b>Data Sharing: </b>Share dashboards and reports all throughout the organization with ease. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>Examples of Advanced Visualizations and Dashboards: \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Sales performance dashboards with capabilities to provide in-depth insights. \r\n</li><li>Dashboards showing financial health with important financial ratios and trends. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>2. Microsoft Excel Integration \r\n</b></h3><p>Microsoft Excel is still a somewhat popularly used tool for reporting and data analysis. The integration of Microsoft Excel with Dynamics 365 Business Central lets users export data and generate customized reports. \r\n</p><p><b>Exporting Data to Excel: \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Simply export data from any D365 BC list or report into Excel for further analysis. \r\n</li><li>With direct access to Business Central data sources, you can maintain consistency and integrity of the exported data. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>Using Excel for Custom Reports: \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Create thorough reports using formulas, pivot tables, and charts within Microsoft Excel. \r\n</li><li>Use Excel\'s data refresh features connected to D365 BC to automate data changes.</li></ul><p><i>If you\'re looking to strengthen your skills, you can explore this <a href=\"https://www.goskills.com/course/learn-excel-tutorial\" target=\"_blank\">comprehensive Excel tutorial</a> to improve your ability to create accurate and efficient reports.</i></p><h3><b>3. Microsoft Copilot in Business Central \r\n</b></h3><p>Copilot in Dynamics 365 Business Centre uses artificial intelligence capabilities to simplify data analysis and then display it in a presentable form, hence improving reporting. It automates routine processes, offers predictive analytics, and provides real-time insights, to allow you to make data-driven decisions.  \r\n</p><p>Copilot easily generates thorough reports and simplifies difficult searches using natural language processing, therefore enhancing general business intelligence and operational effectiveness. \r\n</p><blockquote><b><i><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/white-papers/micorosoft-copilot-for-transformation-in-your-business/\" target=\"_blank\">Integrated inside Business Central, Microsoft Copilot is a powerful AI-assisting tool that can help you streamline processes across several roles. Download our freshly released white paper—Microsoft Copilot: The Catalyst for Transformation in Your Business—to learn more about it. Grab your copy for free, now!</a> \r\n</i></b></blockquote><h2><b>Third-Party Reporting Solutions \r\n</b></h2><p>Apart from the integrated and advanced reporting tools, various third-party solutions further expand the reporting capabilities of Dynamics 365 Business Central. \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Jet Reports \r\n</b></h3><p>One of the popular reporting and business intelligence tools, Jet Reports easily connects with D365 BC. It offers quick, adaptable reporting and analytics straight inside Microsoft Excel. \r\n</p><p><b>Key benefits:</b></p><ul><li><b>Excel-based Reporting: </b>Design reports in Microsoft Excel utilizing known tools and functions. \r\n</li><li><b>Real-time Data:</b> Access real-time data from D365 BC for real-time reporting. \r\n</li><li><b>Pre-built Templates:</b> For standard financial and operational reports, make use of pre-built templates. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>2. Zetadocs \r\n</b></h3><p>Zetadocs provides reporting and document management tools catered for Dynamics 365 Business Central. It improves reporting capabilities by means of document process simplification and integration with reports. \r\n</p><p><b>Key benefits:</b></p><ul><li><b>Automated Document Capture: </b>Automatically capture and save documents linked to transactions in D365 BC. \r\n</li><li><b>Custom Reporting: </b>Generate reports that include linked documents for comprehensive analysis. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>3. SQL Server Reporting Services (SSRS) \r\n</b></h3><p>Microsoft developed a server-based report generation technology called SQL Server Reporting Services (SSRS). For Dynamics 365 Business Central, it lets users create, run, and control reports. \r\n</p><p><b>Key benefits: \r\n</b></p><ul><li><b>Complex Report Design:</b> Make detailed reports with lots of formatting choices. \r\n</li><li><b>Web-based Access:</b> Deploy reports on the web for easy access and sharing. \r\n</li><li><b>Interactive Reports:</b> Include interactive features such as drill-down, sorting, and filtering. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>4. PowerApps and Microsoft Power Platform \r\n</b></h3><p>Microsoft Power Platform, including PowerApps, lets organizations create bespoke apps that can easily integrate with Dynamics 365 Business Central. These applications can include customized reporting tools. \r\n</p><p><b>Key benefits:</b></p><ul><li><b>Custom Applications:</b> Create apps that smoothly interact with D365 BC and handle particular business demands. \r\n</li><li><b>Improved Reporting:</b> Within PowerApps, create bespoke reports and dashboards. \r\n</li><li><b>Automation:</b> Use Power Automate to design workflows that automatically generate and distribute reports. \r\n</li></ul><h2><b>Best Practices for Effective Reporting \r\n</b></h2><p>Following best practices for efficient reporting will help organizations realize the advantages of reporting tools in Dynamics 365 Business Central. \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Define Key Metrics and KPIs \r\n</b></h3><p>List the main performance indicators and metrics that complement your business objectives. This guarantees that reports offer pertinent and practical insights. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Determine What to Measure: </b>Pay heed to metrics that impact business performance and decision-making. \r\n</li><li><b>Aligning Reports with Business Goals:</b> Make sure operational targets and strategic goals are reflected in reports. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>2. Data Accuracy and Consistency \r\n</b></h3><p>Reliable reporting depends on consistent and accurate data. Put in place systems to guarantee data integrity by means of frequent audits and reviews. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Ensuring Data Quality:</b> Verify data input and fix disparities right away to guarantee data quality. \r\n</li><li><b>Consistent Audits and Checks:</b> Plan frequent data evaluations and reports to ensure correctness. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>3. User Training and Adoption \r\n</b></h3><p>Adoption and correct application of reporting tools by users determine effective reporting. Give thorough instruction and encourage the use of these tools across the organization. \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Importance of Training Users:</b> Provide users with the required knowledge and skills to use reporting tools effectively. \r\n</li><li><b>Encourage Adoption of Reporting Tools:</b> Foster a culture of data-driven decision-making by promoting the use of reporting tools. \r\n</li></ul><p>Making smart decisions and corporate performance depend on accurate reporting. From built-in options to sophisticated integrations and third-party solutions, Dynamics 365 Business Central has a strong spectrum of reporting capabilities. Organizations can transform by using these reporting tools and adhering to best practices.</p><p><b style=\"color: rgb(50, 57, 63); font-size: 2rem;\">How Can Dynamics Square Help You Leverage Reporting Tools for Dynamics 365 Business Central?</b></p><p>Dynamics Square has been a reputed <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 implementation partner</a> in the USA for more than 12 years. We have all the resources to ensure successful <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/dynamics-365-business-central-implementation/\" target=\"_blank\">Business Central implementation</a>.  \r\n</p><p>Our team consists of professionals who grasp the subtleties of businesses inside out. By means of meticulous examination of your business\'s requirements, they will configure Business Central. \r\n</p><p>If you run across any problems, send us an email at <a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a> or simply call at <a href=\"tel:+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a>.&nbsp;</p><p><b>Also Read:</b></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/how-to-generate-interactive-reports-in-power-bi/\" target=\"_blank\">How to Generate Interactive Reports in Power BI?</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/why-your-business-needs-power-bi/\" target=\"_blank\">Why Businesses Need to Invest in Power BI – A Business Intelligence Tool</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/how-to-clean-irrelevant-data-in-power-bi-and-ways-to-transform-the-data/\" target=\"_blank\">Why it is Important to Clean Data in Power BI? How to clean and transform the data?</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/copilot-for-power-bi/\" target=\"_blank\">Copilot for Power BI: Take Productivity to the Next Level</a></p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Reporting Tools for Dynamics 365 Business Central (2026)', 'Dynamics 365 Business Central', 'Explore top reporting tools for Dynamics 365 Business Central to enhance data analysis and improve decision-making.', 'Dynamics 365 Business Central,reporting tools,business central', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1806710830982915.png', 'Samar Malik', 'samar.malik@dynamicssquare.com', '.', '[]', '02:02:52pm', '2024-08-07', '11 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2026-01-02 21:02:52');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(224, 'An Insight into Asset Management in Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations', 'asset-management-in-dynamics-365-finance-and-operations', 'Microsoft Dynamics 365', 'microsoft-dynamics-365', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1806819829204787.png', 'Optimize asset management with Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations. Track and manage assets efficiently throughout their lifecycle for better control and performance.', '<p>In the field of contemporary business, operational performance and financial efficiency depend mostly on good asset management. As technology develops quickly, companies are looking for more sophisticated solutions to handle their assets.<br></p><p>Check out this fact to understand how companies are investing in advanced solutions to manage their assets: \r\n</p><p>For the duration of 2024-2031, the market for fixed asset management software is likely to hit USD 19.54 billion by 2031 at a CAGR of 10.1% which was evaluated at USD 8.43 billion in 2023. (Source: <a href=\"https://www.verifiedmarketresearch.com/product/fixed-asset-management-software-market/\" target=\"_blank\">Verified Market Research</a>) \r\n</p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance-operations/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance &amp; Operations</a> (D365 F&amp;O) is one such really effective business solution that is comprised of a comprehensive asset management solution. After Microsoft split this solution into two—Dynamics 365 Finance and Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management (formerly Operations), the asset management module now comes in the latter solution. \r\n</p><p>Asset management in <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</a> provides a strong asset management solution meant to simplify and improve asset handling procedures.  \r\n</p><p>In this blog, we will discuss how asset management in Dynamics 365 can revolutionize your company operations by stressing its key benefits, capabilities, and best practices for implementation. \r\n</p><h2><b>What is Asset Management in Dynamics 365? \r\n</b></h2><p>In Dynamics 365, asset management is the methodical approach within the D365 F&amp;O system that lets companies monitor, control, and optimize their assets all through their lifetime. This encompasses all, from acquisition and implementation to maintenance and disposal. \r\n</p><p>Besides, it helps to maintain and maximize the value of physical and tangible assets. Asset management is included in the supply chain and financial management modules of Dynamics 365 which helps provide a complete picture of asset performance and expenses associated with them. \r\n</p><h2><b>Benefits of Using Asset Management in Dynamics 365 \r\n</b></h2><p>Using an asset management system inside <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365</a> has many benefits that could greatly enhance company operations. \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Improved Asset Utilization \r\n</b></h3><p>The asset management system of Dynamics 365 helps businesses more precisely track and monitor assets’ performance and utilization. This leads to optimum utilization of resources as organizations can easily find unused assets and reallocate them, when necessary, therefore optimizing the general asset performance. \r\n</p><h3><b>2. Reduced Downtime and Maintenance Expenses \r\n</b></h3><p>Using predictive maintenance tools and automated scheduling will help companies drastically lower unnecessary downtime. The system\'s capacity to predict possible problems and plan preventative maintenance helps to reduce repair costs and increase asset lifetime. \r\n</p><h3><b>3. Improved Decision-making with Data-driven Insights \r\n</b></h3><p>Strong analytics and reporting tools found in Dynamics 365 give insightful analysis of asset performance and financial impact. This data-driven strategy helps companies to properly manage resources and strategize by means of informed decision-making. \r\n</p><h2><b>Key Features of Asset Management \r\n</b></h2><p>Several Key features within Dynamics 365 Finance &amp; Operations improve asset management capabilities. \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Tracking and Managing Assets \r\n</b></h3><p>Real-time asset tracking lets companies track assets\' location, condition, and status all through their lifetime. This visibility enhances asset management plans and helps to maintain accurate data. \r\n</p><h3><b>2. Maintenance Scheduling \r\n</b></h3><p>The system offers automated routine maintenance and repair scheduling. This guarantees regular servicing of assets, therefore preventing unplanned breakdowns and prolonging their useful life. \r\n</p><h3><b>3. Work Order Management \r\n</b></h3><p>The all-inclusive work order management system in Dynamics 365 simplifies the process of creating, tracking, and managing work orders. This function guarantees correct and quick completion of maintenance tasks, hence improving efficiency. \r\n</p><h3><b>Integration with Other Modules \r\n</b></h3><p>The asset management module easily integrates with other Dynamics 365 modules including finance and supply chain management. This integration guarantees consistent and easily available asset data across several operations, therefore enhancing the overall operational coherence. \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Reporting and Analytics \r\n</b></h3><p>Analytics and reporting tools offer a thorough understanding of asset performance, expenses, and usage. Customizable reports and dashboards help companies to make data-driven decisions, perform trend analysis, and identify areas for improvement. \r\n</p><h3><b>2. Mobile Access \r\n</b></h3><p>Dynamics 365 lets users track and control assets from anywhere by means of mobile access to asset management tools. This adaptability improves productivity and guarantees that asset information is up to date. \r\n</p><blockquote><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>Optimize your asset management with Dynamics Square. Experience seamless integration and expert guidance for optimal efficiency. Reach out now to transform your asset management strategy! </i></b></a></blockquote><h2><b>How to Implement Asset Management in Dynamics 365? \r\n</b></h2><p>To implement asset management in Dynamics 365 comprises key steps, best practices, and common challenges along with ways to overcome them: \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Step Involved in Setting Up Asset Management \r\n</b></h3><ul><li><b>Define Objectives: </b>Start by stating your goals and requirements for asset management. Find out what you want the system to accomplish, perhaps better tracking abilities and/or reduced maintenance expenses. \r\n</li><li><b>Configure the System: </b>Set up the asset management module in Dynamics 365 in a way that aligns with your company\'s operations. This covers the specification of asset types, maintenance plans, and reporting criteria. \r\n</li><li><b>Import Asset Data: </b>Import existing asset data into the system to ensure a complete and accurate <a href=\"https://thectoclub.com/tools/best-asset-management-software/\" target=\"_blank\">asset inventory</a>. \r\n</li><li><b>Train Users: </b>Staff members should receive training on properly using the asset management tools. This will assist in guaranteeing user acceptance and maximize the advantages of the solution. \r\n</li><li><b>Monitor and Adjust:</b> After deployment, keep an eye on the functioning of the system and make necessary adjustments to improve its efficiency and handle any issues.  \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>2. Best Practices for Implementation \r\n</b></h3><ul><li><b>Involve Stakeholders: </b>Involve important stakeholders throughout the process of implementation to make sure the system satisfies their demands and wins their acceptance. \r\n</li><li><b>Start Small:</b> Think of testing the system on a smaller scale under a pilot phase before full implementation. \r\n</li><li><b>Regularly Update: </b>Maintaining the system\'s efficacy and relevance requires constant updating with the most recent features and enhancements. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>3. Common Challenges and How to Overcome Them \r\n</b></h3><ul><li><b>Resistance to Change: </b>Clearly communicate the advantages of the new system and offer sufficient training to help employees easily adapt to it. \r\n</li><li><b>Data Migration Issues: </b>Before importing asset data, ensure complete data cleansing and validation to avoid discrepancies. \r\n</li><li><b>Integration Complexities:</b> Work with professionals to control integrations between different modules and systems to guarantee flawless data flow and functionality. \r\n</li></ul><h2><b>Tips for Optimizing Asset Management \r\n</b></h2><p>Think about the following optimization tips to properly use Dynamics 365 asset management: \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Regular Maintenance and Inspections \r\n</b></h3><p>Create a routine maintenance schedule and perform frequent inspections to maintain assets in an optimal state. Proactive maintenance increases asset lifetime and helps avoid unanticipated breakdowns. \r\n</p><h3><b>2. Leveraging Data Analytics for Predictive Maintenance \r\n</b></h3><p>Predict potential problems and plan maintenance before they develop with the data analytics tools in Dynamics 365. This method can help to lower maintenance expenses and downtime. \r\n</p><h3><b>3. Training Staff and Ensuring User Adoption \r\n</b></h3><p>Proper training guarantees that every user of the asset management system is competent in using the system. This improves user adoption which is critical for maximizing the advantages of the system and reaching your asset management goals. \r\n</p><p>In summary, features like real-time tracking, automatic maintenance scheduling, and advanced analytics provide Dynamics 365 deliver the tools required to maximize asset utilization, lower costs, and improve decision-making.</p><p>Additionally, integrate <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 CRM</a> to enhance customer relationships and drive even greater value from your Dynamics 365 investment.</p><p> \r\n</p><h2><b>Partner with Dynamics Square for Customized Dynamics 365 Asset Management Solution \r\n</b></h2><p>Leveraging the capabilities of Dynamics 365 asset management becomes important when companies intend to increase their operational efficiency.  \r\n</p><p>If you would want a closer look at how Dynamics 365 might revolutionize your asset management systems, think about scheduling a demo or looking through other Microsoft Dynamics 365 resources. For that, you can get in touch with us. We are Dynamics Square, a renowned <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 implementation partner</a> in the USA with over 12 years of experience and a team of expert consultants. \r\n</p><p>Unlock the full potential of your assets and propel your company ahead with Dynamics 365 solutions. \r\n</p><p>Schedule a free consultation now!&nbsp;</p><p><b>Also Read:</b></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/maximize-technician-productivity-with-dynamics-365-field-service/\" target=\"_blank\">Maximize Technician Productivity with Dynamics 365 Field Service</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/what-is-dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management: What Is It?</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/manufacturers-choosing-dynamics-365-to-solve-business-challenges/\" target=\"_blank\">Why are Manufacturers Choosing Dynamics 365 to Solve Business Challenges?</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/how-can-dynamics-365-erp-help-textile-equipment-manufacturers/\" target=\"_blank\">How Can Dynamics 365 ERPs Help Textile Equipment Manufacturers?</a></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Asset Management in Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations', 'Asset Management', 'Optimize asset management with Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations. Track and control assets efficiently throughout their lifecycle.', 'Asset Management,Dynamics 365 finance and operations', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1806819829207772.png', 'Samar Malik', 'samar.malik@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '11:46:10am', '2024-08-08', '9 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2025-04-30 11:46:10'),
(225, 'Difference Between Transfer Journal and Transfer Order: D365 F&O', 'difference-between-transfer-journal-and-transfer-order', 'Microsoft Dynamics 365', 'microsoft-dynamics-365', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1806826705884879.png', 'Discover the key differences between Transfer Journal and Transfer Order. Learn how each process impacts inventory management and business operations.', '<p>In Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations (D365 F&amp;O), knowing the difference between a transfer journal and a Transfer Order is crucial when handling inventories. Although they seem to be related, these two features serve separate purposes and meet different needs.<br></p><p>This write-up explores the nuances of transfer journals and transfer orders, explaining their differences and uses inside D365 F&amp;O.  \r\n</p><h2><b>1. Overview of Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations \r\n</b></h2><p>Designed to maximize business processes, <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance-operations/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations</a> is a complete enterprise resource planning (ERP) tool. Among its many capabilities are supply chain management, inventory control, and financial management. Within the field of inventory control, the correct and effective movement of products is mostly dependent on Transfer Journals and Transfer Orders. \r\n</p><p>Let’s learn about them, one by one. \r\n</p><h2><b>2. What is a Transfer Journal? \r\n</b></h2><p>One simple tool for internal inventory movement in D365 Finance and Operations is a transfer journal. It lets organizations move goods between several sites inside the same warehouse or between closely spaced warehouses without including thorough tracking or shipping documents.  \r\n</p><p>Transfer journals are perfect for regular inventory changes and internal relocations because of their simplicity. \r\n</p><h3><b>Scenarios for Transfer Journals: \r\n</b></h3><ul><li><b>Internal Reorganization:</b> Transfer Journals allow an organization to shift goods from one bin location to another inside the same warehouse when it needs to rearrange its warehouse layout. This simplifies the maintenance of an accurate record of inventory locations free from the complexity of shipping documentation. \r\n</li><li><b>Correcting Mistakes:</b> A Transfer Journal allows one to rapidly rectify mistakes in items received with erroneous tracking numbers or at the wrong location. Businesses can keep exact traceability by moving goods between tracking dimensions, such as batch or serial numbers. \r\n</li><li><b>Close Proximity Transfers: </b>Transfer Journals help to streamline the process while goods are being moved between two geographically close warehouses. This simplifies the transfer procedure by removing the necessity for thorough tracking and documentation for delivery. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>How to Create and Process a Transfer Journal? \r\n</b></h3><p>Creating and processing a Transfer Journal in D365 Finance and Operations involves a few straightforward steps: \r\n</p><ul><li>Navigate to Inventory Management &gt; Journal entries &gt; Items &gt; Transfer. \r\n</li><li>Create a new journal by clicking \"<b>New</b>\". Add the required information including the journal name, description, site, and warehouse. \r\n</li><li>Enter the item number, quantity, from site, to site, from warehouse, and to warehouse to add the items you wish to transfer. \r\n</li><li>Validate the journal to look for mistakes. Post the journal once validated to complete the transfer. This will change the levels of inventory in the designated sites. \r\n</li><li>Navigate to Inventory management &gt; Inquiries and reports &gt; Journals &gt; Item transactions to review the transfer specifics. To read the specifics, choose the journal you posted and click \"<b>Transactions</b>\". \r\n</li></ul><blockquote><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>Get Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations implemented by a top Microsoft Gold partner in the USA—Dynamics Square. Schedule a free consultation now! </i></b></a></blockquote><h2><b>3. What is a Transfer Order? \r\n</b></h2><p>A transfer order in D365 Finance and Operations is designed as a completed tool for moving stocks between warehouses or sites where thorough tracking and shipping paperwork are needed.  \r\n</p><p>Transfer orders are appropriate for circumstances whereby objects must be tracked throughout travel since they offer more control and visibility over the transfer process. \r\n</p><h3><b>Scenarios for Transfer Orders: \r\n</b></h3><ul><li><b>Long-Distance Transfers: </b>Transfer Orders guarantee that goods are being traced all through the transportation process when goods are being moved between warehouses that are far apart. Maintaining inventory accuracy depends on tracking, shipping, and receiving documents, hence this covers all aspects. \r\n</li><li><b>Shipping Documentation:</b> Transfer orders are utilized when shipment documentation is needed to go along with the items. This is crucial for giving customers comprehensive shipment data and following shipping laws. \r\n</li><li><b>Warehouse Management Processes:</b> Transfer Orders fit very well in settings where warehouse staff members handle picking, packing, shipping, and receiving items. They guarantee that every stage of the transfer process is recorded and tracked. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>How to Create and Process a Transfer Order? \r\n</b></h3><p>Creating and processing a Transfer Order in D365 Finance and Operations involves several detailed steps: \r\n</p><ul><li>Visit Inventory Management &gt; Outbound orders &gt; Transfer Order to navigate. \r\n</li><li>Click \"<b>New</b>\" to draft a fresh transfer order. Now go into the \"<b>from</b>\" and \"<b>to</b>\" warehouses. \r\n</li><li>Enter the item number and quantity to add the items you wish to move. \r\n</li><li>Go to Inventory management &gt; Periodic &gt; Release transfer order picking. Click \"<b>OK</b>,\" then enter the transfer order number. Should the \"<b>Deduct released for picking</b>\" checkbox be chosen, the system will automatically deduct the pertinent quantity from the on-hand inventory. \r\n</li><li>Go return to your transfer order and click \"<b>Ship</b>\" in the Action Pane. Check the quantity and product; then, click \"<b>OK</b>\" to post the shipment. \r\n</li><li>Go to Inventory management &gt; Inbound orders &gt; Transfer order. Choose the transfer order then click \"<b>Receive</b>\" on the Action Pane. Check the quantity and product; then, to finish the receipt, click \"<b>OK</b>.\" \r\n</li></ul><h2><b>4. Key Differences Between Transfer Journals and Transfer Orders \r\n</b></h2><h3><b>Complexity and Application \r\n</b></h3><ul><li><b>Transfer Journals:</b> Simple and flexible, transfer journals fit for internal relocation, error correction, and close proximity transfers. \r\n</li><li><b>Transfer Orders: </b>These are more complicated, suited for long-distance transfers, needing shipping documents, and interacting with warehouse management systems. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>Tracking and Documentation \r\n</b></h3><ul><li><b>Transfer Journals:</b> Minimal tracking and no need for shipping documentation. Ideal for internal transfers where detailed tracking is unnecessary. \r\n</li><li><b>Transfer Orders:</b> Detailed tracking with shipping and receiving documentation. Ensures visibility and control over the transfer process. \r\n</li></ul><h3><b>Inventory Impact \r\n</b></h3><ul><li><b>Transfer Journals: </b>Inventory movements are recorded without offsetting costs. Suitable for internal adjustments and corrections. \r\n</li><li><b>Transfer Orders:</b> Inventory and its value are tracked throughout the transfer process, with potential impacts on costing methods like moving or weighted average. \r\n</li></ul><h2><b>5. Practical Considerations \r\n</b></h2><h3><b>Choosing the Right Tool \r\n</b></h3><p>Selecting between a transfer journal and a transfer order depends on the specific requirements of the transfer. For routine internal adjustments or transfers between nearby locations, transfer journals are efficient and straightforward. For transfers involving longer distances or requiring detailed tracking and documentation, transfer orders are the better choice. \r\n</p><h3><b>Implementation and Training \r\n</b></h3><p>Leveraging the full possibilities of both transfer journals and transfer orders depends on correct implementation and training. Reducing mistakes and optimizing inventory management will depend on warehouse personnel and inventory managers knowing when and how to apply each tool. \r\n</p><p>Transfer journals and transfer orders are absolutely essential tools for inventory control in Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations. Transfer Orders give thorough tracking and documentation for long-distance moves, while transfer journals provide simplicity and adaptability for internal relocations. Effective and accurate inventory management in D365 F&amp;O depends on an awareness of the differences and suitable applications for every tool. </p><p>Using these features will help businesses to keep accurate inventory records, simplify processes, and guarantee shipping rule compliance. Integrating these capabilities with <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics ERP</a> and&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a> further enhances customer interactions and overall operational efficiency.</p><h2><b>Choose Dynamics Square for D365 Finance and Operations Implementation  \r\n</b></h2><p>Dynamics Square, a leading <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 implementation partner</a> in the USA with more than 12 years of experience, ensures successful implementation of D365 F&amp;O. Our expert consultants have helped numerous organizations by carefully examining their business needs and recommending the most appropriate business solutions. Not only this but we can also customize these solutions to fit your particular business needs.  \r\n</p><p>If you require any help, call us at <a href=\"tel:+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a> or simply send us an email at <a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a>.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><b>Also Read:</b></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/top-15-erp-systems-for-small-businesses/\" target=\"_blank\">Top 15 ERP Systems for Small Businesses</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/copilot-in-dynamics-365-finance-and-operations/\" target=\"_blank\">How Copilot in Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations Boost Efficiency</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/dynamics-365-business-central-vs-finance-supply-chain/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Business Central Vs D365 Finance &amp; Supply Chain Management</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/microsoft-dynamics-365-erp-for-smes/\" target=\"_blank\">What products does Microsoft Dynamics 365 ERP offer to SMBs?</a></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Difference Between Transfer Journal and Transfer Order (2025)', 'Difference Between Transfer Journal and Transfer Order', 'Explore the key differences between Transfer Journal and Transfer Order and how they impact inventory management and operations.', 'dynamics 365 finance and operations,transfer journal,transfer order', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1806826705887251.png', 'Samar Malik', 'samar.malik@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '06:46:53pm', '2024-08-08', '8 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-12-18 18:46:53'),
(226, 'How to Integrate Microsoft Power Platform with Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations', 'how-to-integrate-microsoft-power-platform-with-dynamics-365-finance-and-operations', 'Integration', 'integration', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1806914523302666.How to Integrate Microsoft Power Platform with Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations.png', 'Unlock the potential of Power Platform with Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations. Streamline processes, enhance data insights, and drive business efficiency seamlessly.', '<p><a href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/power-platform/blog/2024/04/18/how-microsoft-power-platform-is-driving-real-world-impact-march-customer-success-stories/\" target=\"_blank\">With 33 million monthly active users</a>, Microsoft Power Platform has completely changed how companies handle data analysis, process automation, and solution development. When combined with Dynamics 365 Finance &amp; Operations, now formally called Dynamics 365 Finance &amp; Supply Chain Management, it opens a fresh world of opportunities for improving business insight and efficiency.<br></p><p>This thorough guide will examine how to optimize the components of the Power Platform to enhance <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365-finance-operations/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 Finance &amp; Operations</a>. \r\n</p><h2><b>Development of a Data-Driven Culture \r\n</b></h2><p>Organizations, in the digital era of today, are more determined to build a culture that understands the value of data-driven decision-making. This change not only emphasizes the importance of data accessibility but also enables teams to properly utilize it. These initiatives support the mission of transforming business operations digitally, which helps companies use data for optimizing operations, customer involvement, and overall efficiency. \r\n</p><p>Digital transformation lets companies improve internal processes, streamline operations, and engage customers in more significant ways. Companies can improve their ability to control data, automate processes, and get meaningful insights by using Microsoft Power Platform, hence advancing their digital transformation path. \r\n</p><h2><b>Microsoft Power Platform: At a Glance \r\n</b></h2><p>The Microsoft Power Platform comprises tools meant to empower users with superior capabilities for data analysis, application development, and process automation. There are five components to the platform: \r\n</p><ol><li><b><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-bi/\" target=\"_blank\">Power BI</a>:</b> It possesses strong business intelligence and analytics features that let users generate interactive reports and dashboards with real-time data access. \r\n</li><li><b><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-apps/\" target=\"_blank\">Power Apps</a>:</b> It lets users create unique apps with little coding by using both canvas and model-driven app types to handle certain business demands. \r\n</li><li><b><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-automate/\" target=\"_blank\">Power Automate</a>:</b> It helps to streamline processes and increase productivity by allowing the automation of repetitive actions and procedures across different applications and services. \r\n</li><li><b><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-power-virtual-agents/\" target=\"_blank\">Power Virtual Agents</a>:</b> Users of Power Virtual Agents can design intelligent chatbots that improve client interactions and automatically answer frequently asked questions. \r\n</li><li><b>Power Pages:</b> It lets customers design external-facing webpages for gathering or presenting data from Dynamics 365 and Power Apps. \r\n</li></ol><p>Dataverse, formerly known as the Common Data Service (CDS), links these elements by aggregating data from many sources to offer a consistent picture and support advanced analytics and automation. \r\n</p><blockquote><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\"><b><i>Contact Dynamics Square to extend the capabilities of your Microsoft Dynamics 365 for Finance and Operations by integrating Power Platform. Schedule a free call now! </i></b></a></blockquote><h2><b>Steps to Integrate Power Platform with Dynamics 365 Finance &amp; Operations \r\n</b></h2><p>Speaking of Power Platform integration possibilities, some of the popular options include: \r\n</p><ol><li>With a new Microsoft Dataverse instance \r\n</li><li>With an existing Microsoft Dataverse instance \r\n</li><li>Dual-write setup from Lifecycle Services \r\n</li></ol><p>Here we shall elaborate on connecting finance and operations apps with a new Microsoft Dataverse instance. \r\n</p><h2><b>Connecting Finance and Operations Apps with a New Microsoft Dataverse Instance \r\n</b></h2><p>Administrators utilizing Microsoft Dynamics Lifecycle Services are discovering that many features today call for setting up a connection to Dataverse via Power Platform Integration. Setting up and linking a Dataverse instance is simple for users who have not yet embraced Dataverse for low-code applications, services, or other <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 apps</a>.  \r\n</p><p>The steps below lead you through the process of essentially merging your financial and operations apps environment with a new Dataverse instance into a single logical environment. \r\n</p><h3><b>1. Choose Setup on the Power Platform Integration Tab \r\n</b></h3><p>Use the Power Platform Integration FastTab by first navigating to your sandbox or production environment in Lifecycle Services. Should the Setup button be accessible, you can now set your Dataverse connection configuration. \r\n</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1806895898024878.Screenshot of the Power Platform Integration FastTab..png\" style=\"width: 1344px;\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align: center; \">(Source: Microsoft)<br></p><h3 style=\"text-align: left;\"><b>2. Setup Dataverse using a Template \r\n</b></h3><p>Select a template in the Power Platform Integration Setup dialog box to add Dataverse to your initial Power Platform environment. Leave the \"Use a different Power Platform Environment\" choice selected as No. See the section on linking finance and operations apps with an existing Dataverse instance if you require to connect to one already in use. \r\n</p><p><b>Available templates include:</b></p><ol><li><b>Dynamics 365 Standard:</b> Not including application maps for dual-write, it enables add-ins, virtual entities, business events, and dual-write components. \r\n</li><li><b>Dynamics 365 Standard with Dual-write: </b>Adds all standard template capabilities plus application maps for dual-write. \r\n</li><li><b>Project Operations:</b> This template comprises all capabilities of the Dynamics 365 Standard with a Dual-write template together with solutions required for customers with a Dynamics 365 Project Operations license. \r\n</li><li><b>Choose a template:</b> next, click Setup and check Agree. \r\n</li></ol><h3><b>3. Confirm Your Action \r\n</b></h3><p>A dialog box with a warning message that the connection process is irreversible will show up. Like applying a platform upgrade to your environment, this action cannot be undone once finished. Start by typing your name into the dialog box. \r\n</p><p><img src=\"https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/gallary/1806895888743357.Screenshot of the Setup Power Platform Integration - This can\'t be reversed dialog box..png\" style=\"width: 1344px;\"><br></p><p style=\"text-align: center; \">(Source: Microsoft) \r\n</p><h3><b>4. Wait for Provisioning to Finish \r\n</b></h3><p>Usually, the provision of the new Dataverse instance takes a few minutes. You may have a little downtime during this period when the X++ runtime identifies a new connection to Dataverse. While Dataverse is being integrated, the environment will show as \"<b>Preparing</b>\" in the Power Platform admin area. \r\n</p><p><b>Important Notes: \r\n</b></p><ol><li><b>Irreversibility: </b>Connecting a finance and operations apps environment to a Dataverse instance is a one-way process. If you need to delete the Dataverse instance later, refer to the guide on deleting environments with Power Platform Integration enabled. \r\n</li><li><b>Prerequisites: </b>Ensure you have at least 1 GB of Microsoft Power Platform database storage available. Validate the governance policy of your tenant in the Power Platform admin center and ensure the user performing the setup has the necessary roles and licenses. \r\n</li></ol><p><b>Recommended Guidelines: \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Choose \"<b>Yes</b>\" for the \"<b>Use a different Power Platform Environment</b>\" option in Step 2 in case you already have a Dataverse instance and wish to link it with your finance and operations environment. \r\n</li><li>To keep a 1:1 mapping, treat your operations environment and Power Platform environment as one entity across lifecycle operations. \r\n</li><li>Following these guidelines will help you to combine your operations and financial apps environment with Dataverse so unleashing features like add-ins, dual-write, virtual entities, and business events for optimum functionality. \r\n</li></ul><p>In summary, integrating Microsoft Power Platform with Dynamics 365 Finance &amp; Operations creates a lot of opportunities for custom application development, process automation, and data-based deeper insights. Businesses can improve their operations, interact with customers more successfully, and forward their digital transformation initiatives by using the capabilities of Power Platform.</p><p>Leverage <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-crm/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics CRM</a>&nbsp;and <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics ERP</a> alongside these tools to further enhance customer engagement and streamline your business processes.</p><p> \r\n</p><h2><b>Partner with Dynamics Square for Successful Power Platform Implementation \r\n</b></h2><p>Please contact us if you have any concerns or require help integrating Power Platform and Dynamics 365 Finance &amp; Operations. We are Dynamics Square, a reputed <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/our-services/dynamics-365-implementation-services/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365 implementation partner</a> in the USA for over 12 years now.  \r\n</p><p>With the help of the team of expert consultants, we perform a deep analysis of your business and tailor Dynamics 365 solutions as per your specific requirements. \r\n</p><p>You can simply send an email to <a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a> or give us a call at <a href=\"tel:+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a> if you need any help.&nbsp;</p><p><b>Also Read:</b></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/asset-management-in-dynamics-365-finance-and-operations/\" target=\"_blank\">An Insight into Asset Management in Dynamics 365 Finance &amp; Operations</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/copilot-in-dynamics-365-finance-and-operations/\" target=\"_blank\">How Copilot in Dynamics 365 Finance and Operations Boost Efficiency</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/power-apps-with-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\">How Power Apps with Business Central Integration Works?</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/blog/power-automate-with-business-central/\" target=\"_blank\">Power Automate with Business Central: Amp Up Your Business with Automated Solutions</a></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p>', 'Microsoft Power Platform with Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations', 'Power Platform with Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations', 'Enhance business efficiency with Power Platform and Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations. Streamline processes and gain powerful data insights.', 'power platform,dynamics finance and operations,dynamics 365 f&o', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1806914523302670.How to Integrate Microsoft Power Platform with Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations.png', 'Samar Malik', 'samar.malik@dynamicssquare.com', NULL, NULL, '04:16:42pm', '2024-08-09', '9 mins read', 0, 1, NULL, '2024-09-12 16:16:42');
