INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `title_slug`, `category`, `category_slug`, `image`, `short_description`, `description`, `meta_title`, `meta_keyword`, `meta_description`, `meta_tags`, `meta_image`, `author`, `author_email`, `additional_script`, `additional_multiscript`, `publish_time`, `publish_date`, `read_time`, `rank`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(313, 'ERP for Process Manufacturing: Mastering Complexity, Ensuring Quality, Driving Innovation', 'erp-for-process-manufacturing', 'ERP', 'erp', 'https://blognew.dynamicssquare.com/upload/blog/1833803080272181.ERP for Process Manufacturing.jpg', 'ERP for Process Manufacturing streamlines production, inventory, compliance, and quality control, ensuring efficiency and traceability in batch operations.', '<p>In the high-stakes world of process manufacturing where precision, compliance, and consistency are non-negotiable ERP for process manufacturing has evolved from back-office tools into mission-critical platforms. </p><p>Whether you\'re blending chemicals, refining oil, brewing beverages, or producing pharmaceuticals, the complexity of managing formulas, batch traceability, regulatory standards, and fluctuating raw material costs demands more than spreadsheets and siloed systems.</p><p>ERP tailored for process manufacturing isn\'t just about streamlining operations. It’s about enabling agility, ensuring quality, and driving innovation in an industry where a single deviation can mean millions in losses or a failed audit.  \r\n</p><p>This article explores how modern ERP solutions are transforming process manufacturing by integrating production, quality control, compliance, and supply chain management into a unified digital backbone. \r\n</p><h2>What is Process Manufacturing ERP Software? \r\n</h2><p>ERP for process manufacturing is a specialized type of ERP system designed to support the unique needs of process manufacturing industries such as food and beverage, chemicals, pharmaceuticals, cosmetics, and oil &amp; gas. These industries rely on formulas or recipes rather than discrete parts, and they often deal with variables like weight, volume, potency, and shelf life.  \r\n</p><h2>Top 3 ERPs for Process Manufacturing \r\n</h2><p>Unlike discrete manufacturing, process manufacturing deals with ingredients, recipes, and batches, demanding industry-specific functionalities like lot tracking, quality control, and regulatory reporting. </p><p>Here’s a curated list of the best ERP for process manufacturing that can help streamline operations and drive growth. \r\n</p><p>Whether you\'re in food and beverage, chemicals, pharmaceuticals, or cosmetics, these solutions are designed to streamline production, enhance compliance, and drive business growth. \r\n</p><h3>1. Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management \r\n</h3><p><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/dynamics-365-supply-chain-management/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management</a> is a powerful, cloud-based ERP A powerful, cloud-based ERP software for process manufacturing, Dynamics 365 offers end-to-end visibility and control over production. Its features in demand forecasting, compliance, and batch scheduling make it one of the best ERP for process manufacturing businesses focused on scalability and agility. \r\n</p><h3>2. BatchMaster ERP \r\n</h3><p>Built exclusively for process industries, BatchMaster ERP provides strong capabilities in formula management, batch processing, and regulatory compliance. It\'s a top contender among ERP software for the process manufacturing due to its deep industry alignment. \r\n</p><h3>4. SYSPRO ERP \r\n</h3><p>SYSPRO offers IoT and AI integration with robust batch and lot control, supporting traceability in food, beverage, and chemical manufacturing. It\'s ideal for companies seeking a flexible ERP for process manufacturing with modern capabilities. \r\n</p><h2>What are the Challenges of Process Manufacturing and how can ERP Resolve them? \r\n</h2><p>Process manufacturing, which is common in industries such as chemicals, food and beverage, and pharmaceuticals, faces a unique set of challenges because of its reliance on formulas, continuous production, and strict regulatory requirements. </p><p>Here\'s a breakdown of the key challenges and how ERP systems help resolve them: \r\n</p><h3>Challenges in Process Manufacturing \r\n</h3><h4>1. Complex Formula and Recipe Management \r\n</h4><ul><li>Managing multiple versions of formulas with precise measurements and scalability is difficult. \r\n</li><li>Adjustments for potency, yield, or substitutions must be tracked accurately. \r\n</li></ul><h4>2. Regulatory Compliance \r\n</h4><ul><li>Industries must comply with strict regulations (e.g., FDA, GMP, OSHA). \r\n</li><li>Requires detailed documentation, traceability, and audit trails. \r\n</li></ul><h4>3. Batch Traceability and Quality Control \r\n</h4><ul><li>Tracking raw materials through production to finished goods is essential. \r\n</li><li>Ensuring consistent quality across batches is critical. \r\n</li></ul><h4>4. Inventory and Shelf-Life Management \r\n</h4><ul><li>Managing perishable or hazardous materials with expiration dates. \r\n</li><li>Avoiding stockouts or overstocking sensitive materials. \r\n</li></ul><h4>5. Production Scheduling and Yield Variability \r\n</h4><ul><li>Continuous or batch production must be scheduled efficiently. \r\n</li><li>Yield can vary due to raw material quality or process conditions. \r\n</li></ul><h4>6. Cost Control and Waste Reduction \r\n</h4><ul><li>Monitoring production costs and minimizing waste is vital for profitability. \r\n</li><li>Requires real-time data on material usage and process efficiency. \r\n</li></ul><h3>The right ERP software for process manufacturing resolves these through</h3><h4>1. Advanced Formula Management \r\n</h4><p>ERP systems like <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-365/\" target=\"_blank\">Dynamics 365</a> and BatchMaster offer version-controlled formula management with scalability and substitution tracking. \r\n</p><h4>2. Built-in Compliance Tools \r\n</h4><p>ERPs provide documentation, electronic signatures, and audit trails to meet regulatory standards. \r\n</p><h4>3. End-to-End Traceability \r\n</h4><p>Track ingredients from supplier to finished product, enabling fast recalls and quality assurance. \r\n</p><h4>4. Inventory Optimization \r\n</h4><p>Real-time inventory tracking with alerts for expiration, reordering, and hazardous material handling. \r\n</p><h4>5. Smart Scheduling and Planning \r\n</h4><p>AI-driven production planning tools optimize batch sizes, reduce downtime, and adjust for yield variability. \r\n</p><h4>6. Cost and Waste Analytics \r\n</h4><p>Integrated analytics help monitor costs, identify inefficiencies, and reduce material waste. \r\n</p><h2>How to choose the right ERP for process manufacturing? \r\n</h2><p>Choosing the right ERP system for process manufacturing involves a strategic evaluation of your business needs, industry requirements, and long-term goals. Here’s a step-by-step guide to help you make an informed decision: \r\n</p><h4>1. Identify Your Business Requirements \r\n</h4><ul><li>Define your core processes: formula management, batch production, compliance, etc. \r\n</li><li>List challenges in your current system (e.g., lack of traceability, manual data entry). \r\n</li><li>Consider scalability for future growth. \r\n</li></ul><h4>2. Prioritize Industry-Specific Features \r\n</h4><ul><li>Look for ERPs to process manufacturing (e.g., batch control, lot traceability). \r\n</li><li>Ensure support for regulatory compliance (FDA, GMP, OSHA, etc.). \r\n</li><li>Evaluate quality control and recall management capabilities. \r\n</li></ul><h4>3. Evaluate Integration and Compatibility \r\n</h4><ul><li>Check whether the ERP integrates with your existing tools (e.g., CRM, MES, lab systems). \r\n</li><li>Consider compatibility with your preferred deployment model (cloud, on-premise, hybrid). \r\n</li></ul><h4>4. Assess Usability and Training Needs \r\n</h4><ul><li>Choose a system with an intuitive interface and role-based dashboards. \r\n</li><li>Evaluate the vendor’s training, onboarding, and support services. \r\n</li></ul><h4>5. Analyze Total Cost of Ownership (TCO) \r\n</h4><ul><li>Include licensing, implementation, training, maintenance, and upgrade costs. \r\n</li><li>Compare cloud subscription vs. on-premise licensing models. \r\n</li></ul><h4>6. Request Demos and References \r\n</h4><ul><li>Ask for a live demo tailored to your industry and processes. \r\n</li><li>Speak with existing customers in your sector to understand real-world performance. \r\n</li></ul><h4>7. Consider Vendor Reputation and Roadmap \r\n</h4><ul><li>Research the vendor’s experience in process manufacturing. \r\n</li><li>Review their product roadmap and commitment to innovation (AI, IoT, analytics).</li></ul><h2>How does Dynamics 365 help with batch and formula management?</h2><p>Dynamics 365 offers robust support for batch production, which is essential for process industries where products are manufactured in lots rather than discrete units. \r\n</p><p><b>Key Features: \r\n</b></p><p><b>1. Formula Management</b>: Instead of Bills of Materials (BOMs), process manufacturing uses formulas that define ingredients, quantities, and versions. These formulas can include: \r\n</p><ul><li>Active ingredients \r\n</li><li>Fillers \r\n</li><li>Co-products and by-products \r\n</li><li>Potency and yield adjustments \r\n</li></ul><p><b>2. Batch Orders:</b> These are the process manufacturing equivalent of production orders. They allow: \r\n</p><ul><li>Scheduling and tracking of batch jobs \r\n</li><li>Linking to specific formulas and routes \r\n</li><li>Real-time consumption and output tracking \r\n</li></ul><p><b>3. Scalable Batching: </b>Formulas can be scaled based on batch size, and the system automatically adjusts ingredient quantities. \r\n</p><p><b>4. Potency Management:</b> Adjusts ingredient quantities based on actual potency (e.g., in pharmaceuticals or chemicals). \r\n</p><p><b>5. Batch Balancing: </b>Ensures the correct mix of ingredients to meet target specifications. \r\n</p><h2>Can Dynamics 365 manage co- and by-products?</h2><p>In process manufacturing, it’s common for a production process to yield co-products and by-products alongside the primary product. Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management has robust features to manage both, ensuring accurate costing, inventory tracking, and compliance. \r\n</p><p><b>Understanding Co-products and By-products \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Co-products are valuable secondary products intentionally produced alongside the main product. \r\n</li><li>By-products are unintended or less valuable outputs that may still have economic or disposal implications. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>How Dynamics 365 Handles Them \r\n</b></p><h4>1. Formula Management \r\n</h4><p>Dynamics 365 uses formulas instead of BOMs (Bills of Materials) for process manufacturing. \r\n</p><p><b>You can define a formula to include: \r\n</b></p><p>Primary product \r\n</p><ul><li>Co-products (e.g., multiple grades of oil from refining) \r\n</li><li>By-products (e.g., waste material or chemical residue) \r\n</li></ul><p><b>Example: \r\n</b></p><p>You’re producing refined soybean oil: \r\n</p><ul><li>Primary Product: Refined Soybean Oil \r\n</li><li>Co-product: Soy Lecithin (used in food additives) \r\n</li><li>By-product: Soybean Hulls (used as animal feed or discarded) \r\n</li></ul><p>You can set up the formula to include all three, with defined quantities and cost allocations. \r\n</p><h4>2. Cost Allocation \r\n</h4><ul><li>You can assign a cost allocation percentage to each output. \r\n</li><li>Dynamics 365 distributes the cost of raw materials and processing accordingly. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>Example: \r\n</b></p><ul><li>70% of the cost to Refined Soybean Oil \r\n</li><li>25% to Soy Lecithin \r\n</li><li>5% to Soybean Hulls \r\n</li></ul><p>This ensures accurate financial reporting and inventory valuation. \r\n</p><h4>3. Inventory Tracking \r\n</h4><p>All outputs (main, co-products, by-products) are tracked in inventory. \r\n</p><p><b>You can define whether a by-product is: \r\n</b></p><ul><li>Kept and sold \r\n</li><li>Disposed of \r\n</li><li>Recycled into another process \r\n</li></ul><p><b>Example</b>: \r\n</p><p>If a by-product like steam is reused in heating another process, you can track it as an internal transfer rather than waste. \r\n</p><h4>4. Production Orders and Reporting \r\n</h4><p>When a production order is executed, the system records: \r\n</p><ul><li>Consumption of raw materials \r\n</li><li>Yield of the main product \r\n</li><li>Generated co-products and by-products \r\n</li></ul><p>This helps with yield analysis, waste reduction, and efficiency improvement. \r\n</p><h4>5. Compliance and Documentation \r\n</h4><p>For industries like pharmaceuticals or chemicals, co-products and by-products need to be documented for regulatory compliance. \r\n</p><p>Dynamics 365 supports batch tracking, traceability, and quality inspections for each output. \r\n</p><blockquote><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Ready to streamline your manufacturing operations? Connect with Dynamics Square for industry-ready ERP solutions built for process efficiency. </b></a></blockquote><h2>How does Dynamics 365 support quality control and traceability<span style=\"font-size: 2rem;\">?</span></h2><p>Quality and traceability are quite important in regulated industries like food, pharma, and chemicals. Dynamics 365 provides comprehensive tools: \r\n</p><h4>1. Quality Control</h4><ul><li><b>Quality Orders</b>: Automatically triggered based on events (e.g., goods receipt, production completion). \r\n</li><li><b>Test Groups and Test Variables</b>: Define specific tests (e.g., pH, viscosity, temperature) and acceptable ranges. \r\n</li><li><b>Non-conformance Management</b>: Tracks deviations and initiates corrective actions. \r\n</li><li><b>Quality Associations</b>: Link quality checks to specific processes or items. \r\n</li></ul><h4>2. Traceability</h4><ul><li><b>Lot and Batch Tracking</b>: Every item can be tracked by batch number, with full visibility from raw material to finished product. \r\n</li><li><b>Forward and Backward Traceability</b>: Enables quick identification of affected products in case of recalls. \r\n</li><li><b>Electronic Batch Records (EBR)</b>: Maintains digital records of production and quality data for compliance. \r\n</li></ul><h4>3. Integration with IoT and AI</h4><ul><li>Real-time monitoring of production parameters \r\n</li><li>Predictive quality analytics using Azure AI and Machine Learning \r\n</li></ul><h2>How can you manage shelf life and lot tracking with Dynamics 365?</h2><p>Dynamics 365 SCM provides comprehensive tools for managing perishable inventory, which is critical in industries like food, pharmaceuticals, and chemicals. \r\n</p><p><b>Key Capabilities</b></p><h4>1. Shelf Life Management</h4><ul><li>Define shelf life per product or per batch. \r\n</li><li>Automatically calculate expiration dates based on manufacturing or receipt date. \r\n</li><li>Use first-expired-first-out (FEFO) picking strategies to minimize waste. \r\n</li></ul><h4>2. Expiration Date Control</h4><ul><li>Set minimum shelf life requirements for sales, transfers, or production. \r\n</li><li>Block usage of expired inventory through blocking rules. \r\n</li></ul><h4>3. Lot Tracking</h4><ul><li>Assign and track lot numbers (batch numbers) throughout the supply chain. \r\n</li><li>Enable full traceability from raw materials to finished goods. \r\n</li><li>Support lot inheritance, where finished goods inherit lot attributes from raw materials. \r\n</li></ul><h4>4. Inventory Statuses: \r\n</h4><ul><li>Use inventory statuses (e.g., available, quarantined, expired) to control usability. \r\n</li></ul><h2>What AI tools does Dynamics 365 offer for forecasting?</h2><p>Dynamics 365 integrates with Azure AI, Machine Learning, and Power BI to deliver intelligent insights across operations. \r\n</p><h4>1. Predictive Maintenance</h4><ul><li>IoT Integration: Connects with IoT sensors to monitor equipment health in real time. \r\n</li><li>Azure Machine Learning Models: Predict equipment failures based on historical and sensor data. \r\n</li><li>Maintenance Scheduling: Automatically triggers maintenance work orders before failures occur. \r\n</li></ul><h4>2. Demand Forecasting</h4><ul><li>Built-in Forecasting Models.</li><li>Uses historical sales, seasonality, and trends. \r\n</li><li>Supports statistical models like exponential smoothing and ARIMA. \r\n</li></ul><h4>3. AI-Enhanced Forecasting</h4><ul><li>Integrates with Azure AI to improve forecast accuracy. \r\n</li><li>Incorporates external data (e.g., weather, market trends) for better predictions. \r\n</li></ul><h4>4. Power BI Dashboards</h4><ul><li>Visualize forecasts, variances, and KPIs. \r\n</li><li>Enable drill-down analysis for planners and executives. \r\n</li></ul><h2>Role of PIM module in Dynamics 365 in managing recipes and formulations</h2><p>In Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management (SCM), the Product Information Management (PIM) module plays a major role in managing recipes and formulations, especially for industries like food and beverage, pharmaceuticals, chemicals, and cosmetics, where precise control over ingredients and production processes is essential. \r\n</p><p>Here’s a rundown of how PIM supports recipe and formulation management: \r\n</p><h4>1. Centralized Control of Product Data \r\n</h4><p>The PIM module acts as the single source of truth for all product-related information, including raw materials, semi-finished goods, and finished products. For recipe-based manufacturing, this means: \r\n</p><ul><li>Defining product variants based on formulation needs (e.g., different flavors, concentrations, or packaging). \r\n</li><li>Managing ingredient specifications, including physical and chemical properties, allergens, and regulatory data. \r\n</li></ul><p>This centralized approach ensures consistency and compliance across all departments and production sites. \r\n</p><h4>2. Recipe and Formula Management \r\n</h4><p>In industries where formulations are critical, PIM integrates with the Process Manufacturing capabilities of Dynamics 365 SCM to manage: \r\n</p><ul><li><b>Formulas</b>: These are the equivalent of Bills of Materials (BOMs) but tailored for process manufacturing. They define the quantities and proportions of ingredients used. \r\n</li><li><b>Co-products and by-products</b>: PIM allows you to define expected outputs beyond the main product, which is essential in chemical or food production. \r\n</li><li><b>Scalable formulas</b>: Formulas can be scaled based on batch size, ensuring flexibility in production planning. \r\n</li></ul><h4>3. Precision and Compliance \r\n</h4><ul><li>PIM supports unit of measure conversions, yield calculations, and loss factors, which are vital for accurate recipe execution. It also helps ensure: \r\n</li><li>Regulatory compliance by tracking restricted substances or allergens. \r\n</li><li>Labeling accuracy by linking product data with packaging and nutritional information. \r\n</li></ul><h4>4. Version Control and Change Management \r\n</h4><p>Formulations often evolve due to R&amp;D, cost optimization, or regulatory updates. PIM supports: \r\n</p><ul><li>Versioning of formulas and recipes, allowing you to track changes over time. \r\n</li><li>Approval workflows to ensure that only validated formulations are used in production. \r\n</li></ul><p>This ensures traceability and reduces the risk of errors or non-compliance. \r\n</p><h4>5. Integration with Other Modules \r\n</h4><p>PIM doesn’t work in isolation. It integrates seamlessly with: \r\n</p><ul><li>Production control for recipe execution on the shop floor. \r\n</li><li>Quality management for testing and validation of ingredients and finished goods. \r\n</li><li>Inventory and procurement to ensure the right ingredients are available when needed. \r\n</li></ul><p>Finally, the PIM module in Dynamics 365 SCM is foundational for managing recipes and formulations. It ensures that product data is accurate, compliant, and production-ready supporting both operational efficiency and regulatory requirements. \r\n</p><blockquote><a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/contact-us/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Looking to implement the best ERP for process manufacturing? Connect with Dynamics Square for a free consultation and explore how tailored solutions can transform your production operations. </b></a></blockquote><h2>What ERP features are needed for process vs. discrete manufacturing?</h2><p>Process and discrete manufacturing have fundamentally different production models, which shape their ERP needs:</p><table class=\"table table-bordered\"><tbody><tr><td><b>Feature</b></td><td><b>Process Manufacturing</b></td><td><b>Discrete Manufacturing</b></td></tr><tr><td>Production Type</td><td>Continuous or batch-based</td><td>Unit-based, assembly line</td></tr><tr><td>Inputs</td><td>Ingredients, formulas</td><td>Components, parts</td></tr><tr><td>Outputs</td><td>Bulk products, co/by-products</td><td>Finished goods, subassemblies</td></tr><tr><td>Routing</td><td>Often flexible, yield-based</td><td>Fixed steps, BOM-driven</td></tr><tr><td>Inventory Tracking</td><td>Lot/batch tracking, shelf life<br>\r\n</td><td>Serial numbers, part tracking</td></tr><tr><td>ERP Needs</td><td>Formula management, potency, traceability compliance</td><td>BOMs, routings, work centers, MRP</td></tr><tr><td>Industries</td><td>Food, pharma, chemicals</td><td>Automotive, electronics, machinery</td></tr></tbody></table><p><b>ERP Implications:</b></p><p>Process Manufacturing requires formula-based planning, potency adjustments, and regulatory compliance tools.  \r\n</p><p>Discrete manufacturing focuses more on 	assembly logic, serial tracking, and engineering change management.  \r\n</p><h2>What are some real-world examples that suggest the powerful impact on Dynamics ERP for process manufacturers? \r\n</h2><p>Here are some compelling real-world examples that highlight the powerful impact of <a href=\"https://www.dynamicssquare.com/products/microsoft-dynamics-erp/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Dynamics ERP</a> in process manufacturing: \r\n</p><p><b>1. ChemTreat (Water Treatment Chemicals) <i>(<a href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics-365/blog/business-leader/2022/02/17/dynamics-365-drives-improvement-in-manufacturing-supply-chains/\" target=\"_blank\">Source</a>) \r\n</i></b></p><p><b>Industry</b>: Chemical Process Manufacturing \r\n</p><p><b>Solution</b>: Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management \r\n</p><p><b>Impact</b>: \r\n</p><ul><li>Replaced a heavily customized legacy system with a modern, cloud-based ERP. \r\n</li><li>Gained real-time supply chain visibility to proactively address raw material shortages. \r\n</li><li>Improved planning and execution processes across the business. \r\n</li><li>Created a foundation for broader digital transformation initiatives. \r\n</li></ul><p><b>2. The Simply Good Foods Company (Packaged Foods – Atkins &amp; Quest)<i> (<a href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics-365/blog/business-leader/2022/04/14/dynamics-365-breathes-composability-into-enterprise-resource-planning-modernization/\" target=\"_blank\">Source</a>) \r\n</i></b></p><p><b>Industry</b>: Food &amp; Beverage Manufacturing \r\n</p><p><b>Solution</b>: Dynamics 365 Supply Chain &amp; Finance \r\n</p><p><b>Impact</b>: \r\n</p><ul><li>Standardized operations across merged entities without sacrificing reporting independence. \r\n</li><li>Improved order processing productivity and master data consistency. \r\n</li><li>Enabled greater logistics efficiency through third-party logistics integration. \r\n</li><li>Strengthened operational scalability and customer-facing consistency. \r\n</li></ul><h2>Ready to Transform Your Process Manufacturing Operations? \r\n</h2><p>If you\'re looking for a powerful, flexible, and industry-ready ERP solution, Microsoft Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management is a top-tier choice for process manufacturers. With advanced capabilities in batch management, traceability, production planning, quality control, and compliance, Dynamics 365 is purpose-built to help you stay competitive and resilient in a dynamic market. \r\n</p><p>Whether you\'re scaling production, managing compliance, or minimizing waste, choosing the right ERP software for process manufacturing is critical. A modern, cloud-enabled ERP for process manufacturing platform like Dynamics 365 empowers your business to thrive in a complex regulatory and production environment. \r\n</p><p>At Dynamics Square, we specialize in helping process manufacturers like you implement and optimize Dynamics 365 to unlock greater efficiency, transparency, and profitability. From system assessment and planning to deployment, customization, and support we guide you in every step of the way. \r\n</p><h3>Why Choose Dynamics Square? \r\n</h3><ul><li>Microsoft-certified Dynamics 365 experts \r\n</li><li>Deep domain expertise in process manufacturing \r\n</li><li>Seamless migration and integration services \r\n</li><li>Ongoing support and training \r\n</li></ul><p>Let’s take your operations to the next level. \r\n</p><p>Get in touch today for a free consultation or personalized demo of Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management tailored to your manufacturing needs. \r\n</p><p>If you need any help, please don\'t hesitate to contact us by phone at <a href=\"tel:+1 281 899 0865\" target=\"_blank\">+1 281 899 0865</a> or by email at <a href=\"mailto:arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com\" target=\"_blank\">arish.siddiqui@dynamicssquare.com</a>.</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p> \r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\n